 Bookmark Horticulture Student Asst. Conner 2 G/R34661P CAES-Horticulture Grad/Research/Student/Temp Individual will assist with the field, seed processing, laboratory and greenhouse activities. Crucial field activities include data collection and harvesting along with other miscellaneous duties. Additional duties will involve helping with seed processing shelling, data collection, organizing) and greenhouse work (plant cultivation and crossing) when needed. Laboratory activities include condu... View Details Bookmark Graphic Designer S15711P Athletics-Creative Services Staff This position is responsible for assisting the Creative Services department’s efforts in creating a digital identity strategy that includes graphic and motion graphic design, visual identity, digital and social media strategy. The Graphic Designer will fulfill requests from many different areas, including Athletic Communications, Marketing and Recruiting, while adhering to and assisting in the ... View Details Bookmark Medical Records Associate S15319P VetMed-VTH Admin Services Staff This position provides customer service to all clients of the Medical Records Department. Primary responsibilities include: attaching documentation to patient records; answering and routing phone calls, emails and faxes in a timely manner; processing records requests, and other duties as assigned. This position will assist the VTH Business information systems manager in providing first level su... View Details Bookmark BUILDING SERVICES WORKER, LEAD S15705P FMD-Svcs-Blding Svcs Staff The Building Services Worker Lead is a key position within Facilities Management Division’s Building Services unit. Reporting directly to a Manager, this position will be responsible for day to day management of custodial operations within an assigned building or collection of buildings. The Building Services Worker Lead directly supervises crews approximately 6 to 10 employees who are responsi... View Details Bookmark Bus Operations Supervisor S15547P Auxiliary Transit Opera Staff 09/17/2026 This position is responsible for providing supervision for the daily operation of the campus transit system. This work involves both direct and indirect oversight of bus operators on routes and during pre/post trip inspections. This position gives support to drivers by communicating and providing guidance to address the needs of bus operators. In addition, this position is also responsible for ... View Details Bookmark Program Coordinator II S15708P PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt Staff The Program Coordinator II supports the Defense Community Resilience Program (DCRP) through project coordination, operational support, stakeholder engagement, and administrative management. The position assists with planning and tracking project activities, coordinating internal and external partners, preparing reports and project materials, supporting proposal development, and monitoring proje... View Details Bookmark Associate Director of Network and Data Center Operations S15699P EITS-Data Ctr Ops Staff This position manages the Data Center Operations, Facilities Management, Cellular, and Network Operations teams.  This position will also assist in infrastructure projects as needed to complete any related projects and delivery of services. View Details Bookmark HOUSEKEEPER S15707P PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel Staff This position provides cleaning services primarily in hotel guest rooms. The housekeeper is responsible for responding to all guest requests appropriately, identifying and notifying appropriate parties of any maintenance issues, and maintaining accurate records of work performed and time spent. Housekeeper maintains their cart with the proper cleaning supplies, amenities, and linens. Housekeepe... View Details Bookmark Senior Director, Marketing and Communications S15690P COE-Communications Office Staff The Senior Director of Marketing and Communications provides strategic leadership and vision for the College’s marketing and communications enterprise. This role is responsible for developing and executing a comprehensive, data-driven communications and marketing strategy that advances the College’s mission, strengthens its brand, and ensures integrated, consistent messaging across all platform... View Details Bookmark Student Worker-Medical Equipment Assistant G/R34653P VetMed-VTH Administration Grad/Research/Student/Temp Position will complete various tasks and projects throughout the Veterinary Teaching Hospital as assigned by the Medical Equipment Manager to include assisting with inventory management, repairs, and preventative maintenance of the Veterinary Teaching Hospital medical equipment. View Details Bookmark Long County 4-H Agent F2785P CAES-Southeast District CES Faculty This position will provide educational programming in the County. This position will also provide management and oversight of the County 4-H Program in cooperation with other staff members. The County 4-H Program is robust and provides a wide variety of educational opportunities for youth. This position will work cooperatively with county 4-H staff and provide oversight, management, and support... View Details Bookmark IT Professional Assistant S15703P EITS-Client Services Staff Builds and maintains computer lab images for lab and staff computers. Ensures that the labs and client computers operate within established departmental policy and procedural guidelines. Develops and maintains EITS desktop standards and procedures. Provides client technical support on Windows and Apple hardware in addition to software products. Provides technical support on supported mobile dev... View Details Bookmark Administrative Assistant II S15700P CAES-Southeast District CES Staff This position is responsible for the processing of travel authorizations, training registrations, and reminders, as well as reviewing monthly bank reconciliation reports. Additionally, it involves managing equipment inventory and surplus, overseeing copier maintenance, and processing payment requests. The position offers administrative assistance to the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) a... View Details Bookmark Undergraduate Research Assistant Leaf Phenotyping G/R34649P Warnell-Research Grad/Research/Student/Temp Seeking a motivated student to assist with leaf phenotyping and processing, organizing laboratory equipment and supplies, labeling and maintaining leaf samples, and keeping accurate records of sample collection and measurements. This position provides hands-on experience in forest genetics, tree physiology, and laboratory research. View Details Bookmark Tift County EFNEP Program Assistant S15692P CAES-Southwest District CES Staff This position is based in Tift County. This position is responsible for paraprofessional work with County Extension Agents in a Food and Nutrition Education program for limited resource clients. Work is performed under general supervision. View Details Bookmark Senior Creative Design Specialist S15698P DAR-Communications Staff 09/10/2026 This position reports to the Creative Director and plays a key role in advancing and stewarding the visual identity of Development and Alumni Relations (DAR). The role works closely with other Creative Design Specialists within the Development and Alumni Relations Communications department (DARCOMM) and, when applicable, Creative Team student staff.This position is responsible for the planning,... View Details Bookmark Photojournalist Assistant G/R34648P CAES-Comm & Marketing Grad/Research/Student/Temp The student photojournalist will work in the Office of Marketing and Communications (OMC) within the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES), supporting the creation of visual content that enhances storytelling across digital and print platforms. This position offers the opportunity to capture and curate engaging photography, assist with content repurposing and visual adaptati... View Details Bookmark Parking Compliance Monitor S13507P Auxiliary Parking Compliance Staff This position is responsible for the enforcement of parking regulations and operational policies in campus lots and structures. View Details Bookmark Career Consultant S15670P DAR-Career Center Staff The Career Consultant serves as the primary career services liaison to assigned colleges or schools at the University of Georgia. This role acts as a critical link between the Career Center and the college, serving as a resource for students, employers, and faculty on career planning, industry trends, and professional development. Internally, the Career Consultant advocates for the college’s ca... View Details Bookmark Communications Director S15696P PSO-Sea Grant Program Staff The Communications Director serves on the Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant leadership team, providing strategic direction for the unit’s communications program and contributing to organizational planning and decision-making. Reporting directly to the Director, this position oversees all aspects of communications operations, including the development and implementation of internal and exte... View Details Bookmark Lead Financial Aid Advisor, Client Services S15702P VPI-Student Financial Aid Staff Provides leadership to and routinely assists Financial Aid Advisors and support staff in accomplishing their daily responsibilities. Serves as authority for satisfactory academic progress appeals and manages reports on potential changes in student eligibility. Advises students and parents regarding federal, state and institutional aid in an accurate and efficient manner, and assists with relate... View Details Bookmark Laboratory Technician I S15695P VetMed-Poultry Diagnos & Rsch Staff Position is located in the PDRC Diagnostic Laboratory and deals with formalin fixed tissues from the poultry industry and requires laboratory skills that promote turn-around time for diagnostic test and research results. View Details Bookmark Post-Doctoral Associate AD-Rains G/R34629P CAES-Entomology Grad/Research/Student/Temp The Post-Doctoral Associate will coordinate, conduct, and publish original research to advance precision agriculture technologies, including farm application systems, weed management, cotton harvesting practices, and autonomous navigation of intelligent multi-purpose rovers. Responsibilities include designing and executing field and laboratory studies, developing and evaluating innovative techn... View Details Bookmark Student Assistant - Dr. Dunn G/R34614P CAES-Food Science & Technology Grad/Research/Student/Temp Undergraduate Laboratory work for Dr. Dunn’s lab. View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 … 24 25 Next Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
