    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "University of Georgia Staff: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:www.ugajobsearch.com,2005:/postings/all_jobs University of Georgia Staff: All Jobs 2026-09-03T09:32:10-04:00 https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478446 2026-04-22T17:20:49-04:00 2026-06-24T12:10:55-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator – Wahsega <div>This job is a temporary Environmental Educator at Wahsega 4-H Center located in Dahlonega, Georgia. The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include life and earth science, ecology, team building, outdoor skills, and living history. Other responsibilities include animal care, maintenance of teaching areas and resources, facilities, grounds, and support of general operations of the facility.</div> CAES-Wahsega https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483824 2026-05-18T16:13:59-04:00 2026-05-18T16:14:01-04:00 Part-Time Athens-Clarke County Extension 4-H Program Assistant <div>The County Extension Program Assistant position will perform duties necessary to assist the county extension agents in the day-to-day conduct of programs. Duties will include answering phone calls and helping 4-H and Agricultural assignments.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478565 2026-04-22T17:29:44-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:44-04:00 Work Study Student (NE) VPI-Service Learning https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492098 2026-07-08T15:47:04-04:00 2026-07-08T15:47:05-04:00 Veterinary Assistant - Ophthalmology <div>This position will give assistance to the senior veterinary technicians and veterinary staff on the care of ill or injured client-owned animals brought to the Veterinary Teaching Hospital in the hopes of recovery.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Anim Spc Srvc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478655 2026-04-22T17:36:54-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:55-04:00 Temporary Skilled Crafts/Trade <div>This is a position of trust. This is a full-time temporary position working in Receiving and Mail Services. Responsibilities include assisting with the processing of university’s mail and distributing goods delivered to the university.</div> FD-Mail & Receiving Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496773 2026-07-29T15:05:12-04:00 2026-07-29T15:05:13-04:00 Research Funding Administrator <div>Reporting to the Joint Director of the CCRC/CMM, the Research Funding Administrator is a senior-level grants management professional overseeing pre-award administration for the Complex Carbohydrate Research Center and the Center for Molecular Medicine (Centers), which receive over $20M per year in external funding. Supported by one or more Grants Specialists, this position manages the full grant lifecycle, tracks progress, and provides updates to faculty.<br><br></div><div>The role also serves as a liaison with the Office of Sponsored Projects and funding agencies, while supporting faculty in proposal development and award administration. In addition, the Research Funding Administrator represents the Centers on institutional committees and must demonstrate strong communication skills and the ability to meet strict deadlines.<br><br></div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477976 2026-04-21T18:16:44-04:00 2026-04-21T18:16:45-04:00 Research Technician - Grass Genomes (Devos Lab) This Research Technician position works as part of a dynamic team on the genetics of grasses.  In addition to laboratory research, the post-holder will assist with planting, maintaining, and harvesting of greenhouse and field experiments.  The Devos Lab consists of a multinational team of graduate students and post-docs working under the supervision of and with people of different cultural backgrounds.   Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in next-generation library preparation.  This position is grant-funded for five (5) years.  While the continuation of funding and employment is anticipated, it is not guaranteed. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503814 2026-09-01T08:07:28-04:00 2026-09-01T08:07:29-04:00 Grants Professional Intern <div>This student intern position works with Auxiliary Services in Finance and Administration at UGA and provides Experiential Learning credit.<br><br>The Grants Professional Intern will support the identification, evaluation, and development of grant opportunities for UGA Auxiliary Services. This includes conducting prospect research, summarizing funding opportunities, drafting proposal sections, preparing supporting documentation, and maintaining organized grant files. The intern will work closely with the Grants Professional and Auxiliary unit partners to help ensure accurate, timely, and competitive grant submissions.</div> Auxiliary Finance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500117 2026-08-14T10:20:36-04:00 2026-08-14T10:20:36-04:00 Accounts Receivable and Payables Specialist <div>This position provides accounting support within the Accounts Receivable and Payables functions, performing responsibilities such as processing invoices, billing, account monitoring, transactions, aging, reconciliations, customer service, and maintaining compliance with university policies and financial controls. This role requires attention to detail, accuracy in transaction processing, and the ability to collaborate with internal and external stakeholders.</div> Auxiliary Finance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478393 2026-04-22T17:16:50-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:50-04:00 Temporary Service Worker - Con't Ed (Cain) <div>Room set-up and room clean up; office support such as copying, faxing, making conference disks, word-processing; managing storage space; supporting transportation need in our workshops; providing A-V support in some cases; and supporting our catering operation.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478830 2026-04-22T17:50:24-04:00 2026-08-20T10:46:24-04:00 grounds keeper-nonstudent <div>Maintain the grounds and commons areas for Athletic facilities.</div> Athletics-Grounds https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502386 2026-08-25T09:18:21-04:00 2026-08-25T09:18:22-04:00 Program Coordinator <div>The Program Coordinator provides advanced administrative, operational, and programmatic support for the School's research and outreach missions. The position serves as the primary administrative coordinator supporting the Associate Dean for Research and provides operational support to the Associate Dean for Outreach. Approximately 80% of the position's effort supports research administration, faculty support, strategic planning, assessment, reporting, and special projects under the direction of the Associate Dean for Research, while 20% supports outreach planning, communications, data collection, reporting, continuing education activities, and operational initiatives under the direction of the Associate Dean for Outreach.<br><br></div><div>The incumbent performs and oversees a broad range of administrative functions and business processes that support faculty, staff, students, research programs, outreach initiatives, and School leadership. Responsibilities include project coordination, systems administration, reporting and assessment activities, strategic planning support, faculty evaluation support, database management, communications, stakeholder engagement, space planning, and operational process development.<br><br></div><div>The position administers and maintains reporting systems and operational databases supporting research and outreach activities, including faculty productivity reporting, outreach activity reporting, continuing education administration, research program reporting, and assessment systems used for leadership decision making. The incumbent exercises substantial independent judgment in managing projects, coordinating stakeholders, solving operational problems, implementing administrative procedures, and recommending process improvements that advance School objectives.<br><br></div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478514 2026-04-22T17:24:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:36-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Zhang Lab 1 <div>The Isakson Center for Neurological Disease Research Zhang Lab is seeking 2 Postdoctoral Research Associates.<strong> </strong>The research in the laboratory of Dr. Hui Zhang focuses on elucidation of mechanisms underlying Parkinson’s disease at the molecular, cellular and circuit level. Motivated applicants with a Ph.D. in Neuroscience or related field are encouraged to apply. The successful candidates will be responsible for independent design and execution of experiments as well as data analysis, interpretation and communication of results.</div> VetMed-Isakson CNDR https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488214 2026-06-12T08:22:39-04:00 2026-06-12T08:22:40-04:00 Liberty County 4-H Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the County. This position will also provide management and oversight of the County 4-H Program in cooperation with other staff members. The County 4-H Program is robust and provides a wide variety of educational opportunities for youth. This position will work cooperatively with county 4-H staff and provide oversight, management, and support of the 4-H program. As necessary, deliver 4-H programming in a variety of settings including in-school, afterschool, and through participation in state and district events. This position utilizes the expertise of and works closely with advisory groups, community leaders, public officials and representatives of intended audiences to analyze data, identifies needs, and assists in developing educational programs.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478613 2026-04-22T17:32:57-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:58-04:00 Temporary Skilled Crafts/Trades - Granade This position will assist with the maintenance on the main campus grounds. Work includes planting flower beds and shrubs/trees, mowing grass, spraying pesticides, and trimming shrubs. CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494820 2026-07-21T11:45:17-04:00 2026-07-21T11:45:18-04:00 Food Service Worker I (Late Night) <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477821 2026-04-21T17:57:55-04:00 2026-04-21T17:57:56-04:00 Agricultural Specialist <div>This position reports directly to the Senior Farm Manager in the Animal and Dairy Science Department (ADS) and ultimately to the Head of ADS. The principal duties of the position include, but are not limited to: providing day-to-day operational support under the direction of the Sr. Farm Manager of the beef cattle, dairy, sheep, swine and equine operations; direct involvement in forage production, facility maintenance and repairs; equipment operation, maintenance and repair; working with faculty and farm staff to ensure that the research, teaching and extension missions are accomplished.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478750 2026-04-22T17:42:12-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:13-04:00 Genetics Laboratory Assistant <div>The Shamblin lab seeks laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample processing, DNA extractions, and data calling for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate students and the lab manager with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, skin, fin clips, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing for fish and wildlife species of conservation concern. This position will also assist the PI with data calling with microsatellite and sequencing projects. Sample archiving and general laboratory maintenance are expected.&nbsp;<em>Candidates should be available to work 30-40 hours weekly if not taking classes or 15-20 hours weekly if taking classes during the summer. Please make your summer availability clear in your cover letter</em></div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498396 2026-08-06T11:07:41-04:00 2026-08-06T11:07:42-04:00 Research Technician <div>The position provides research support to the stone fruit rootstock breeding program at the USDA-ARS Fruit and Tree Nut research Lab located at Byron, GA. The role will participate in the planning, design, and implementation of laboratory, greenhouse, and field experiments designed to manage rootstock breeding germplasm, breeding nurseries, and field trials. In addition, the position will supervise undergraduate students and part-time workers, responsibilities include managing a variety of field, greenhouse, and laboratory experiments at or near Byron. More specific duties include breeding nursery maintenance, plant propagation, data collection, equipment maintenance and operation, application of insectices/pesticies using spray equipment, data entry, and program support. This position will report to the principal investigator (Dario Chavez, Ph.D.) and coordinate research with onsite researcher (Jeekin Lau, Ph.D.).<br><br><strong>This is a grant-funded position with continued employment beyond 08/31/2029 based on the needs of the project as well as available funding and satisfactory job performance and progress.</strong></div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478120 2026-04-21T18:34:56-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:56-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The individual is expected to develop a comprehensive beef research and Extension program in the successful candidate's area(s) of expertise, but emphasis will be placed on the ability to develop an internationally recognized Extension and research program. This faculty member will be expected to supervise graduate students and interns.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504291 2026-09-03T09:32:10-04:00 2026-09-03T09:32:10-04:00 Administrative Assistant II <div>This position is responsible for the processing of travel authorizations, training registrations, and reminders, as well as reviewing monthly bank reconciliation reports. Additionally, it involves managing equipment inventory and surplus, overseeing copier maintenance, and processing payment requests. The position offers administrative assistance to the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) and Family &amp; Consumer Sciences (FACS) Program Development Coordinators, while also supporting other district personnel such as District Area Agents as required.<br><br>This position will work effectively without immediate supervision and work as a member of the SE District Cooperative Extension team.</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500851 2026-08-18T12:32:23-04:00 2026-08-18T12:32:24-04:00 Administrative Assistant to Associate Dean and the Assistant Dean for Academic Affairs <div>The position provides administrative support for the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Assistant Dean of Academic Affairs, and other members of the academic program staff in the Warnell School and reports to the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477755 2026-04-21T17:31:38-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:39-04:00 Sous Chef <div>This position will be a highly skilled food preparation worker who will assist the chef in the preparation of a wide variety of meats, fish, starches, casseroles, breads, vegetables and desserts. Knowledge and skills in food quality, food safety and food preparation will be needed. A person in this position will work with very limited supervision and may lead other employees to complete assigned tasks.</div> Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478711 2026-04-22T17:40:16-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:16-04:00 Production Student Assistant <div>At the Performing Arts Center, student production assistants help to play a vital role in making sure our world-class events and performances run smoothly from set-up, to showtime, to strike. The tasks of the job are varied, and every shift is a little different. Some things you may be doing include…<br>-Setting up lighting<br>-Setting up microphones and speakers<br>-Focusing lights<br>-Assisting with artist entrances/exits<br>-Running spotlights<br>-Laying dance flooring<br>-Artist security<br>and much more!</div> SRVPAA-Performing Arts https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497571 2026-08-03T14:46:18-04:00 2026-08-03T14:46:18-04:00 Student Manager - Women's Basketball Athletics-Women's Basketball https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478058 2026-04-21T18:29:14-04:00 2026-04-21T18:29:15-04:00 Wayne County Agriculture & Natural Resources Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) area in Wayne County providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods. Wayne County has a rich history of an extraordinary Ag Row Crop and Forestry program. County stakeholders rely heavily on the County Agent. Homeowners also depend on the Agent’s expertise to provide training and programming to the citizens of the community. Tended acres are covered with cotton, peanuts, tobacco, corn, turf, pine trees and pasture. <br><br>This position involves frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are necessary. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br><a href=\"http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm\"><strong>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</strong></a></div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504113 2026-09-02T09:30:53-04:00 2026-09-02T09:30:54-04:00 Plant Pathology Research Technician (C. Oliveira) <div>The Research Technician will primarily support industry-sponsored and research field trials by assisting with planting, fungicide applications, disease assessments, harvesting, data entry in ARM, and keeping trial reports current. The position will also assist with purchasing, inventory management, laboratory organization, maintenance of fungal isolate collections, and greenhouse and laboratory activities as needed. The technician will follow UGA policies and procedures, participate in lab meetings and scientific discussions, and work with industry partners, other UGA programs, and members of the Peanut and Pecan Pathology Lab to support ongoing research activities. The technician will contribute to research projects through data collection, analysis, and presentation of findings under the guidance of faculty and senior research personnel.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500486 2026-08-17T12:04:39-04:00 2026-08-17T12:04:39-04:00 Farm Manager - BREC Alapaha <div>The farm manager at the Blueberry Research and Education Center (BREC)-Alapaha is responsible for the day-to-day operations of the BREC – Alapaha. This includes but is not limited to management of farm operations that include tillage/bedding, planting, scouting, pest protection, scouting irrigation, frost/freeze protection, harvesting, post-harvest disposition of fruit, etc. The farm manager will be responsible for the day-to-day operation of the blueberry research enterprise at the BREC-Alapaha. This includes working closely with the BREC superintendent and faculty, extension specialists, etc. to implement and manage complex research protocols to ensure that research and extension faculty, students, etc. receive the highest possible level of support on this farm for their programs. The farm manager will be responsible for the daily upkeep, maintenance and appearance of the equipment, facilities and grounds that are associated with the BREC-Alapaha. The farm manager will provide daily supervision to UGA staff who work at BREC-Alapaha and will report to the BREC superintendent. This position serves as the primary PCard holder for BREC- Alapaha.</div> CAES-Blueberry Farm https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478416 2026-04-22T17:19:57-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:57-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate AD - Dutta-06 <div>The post-doctoral research associate will work on identifying diverse thiosulfinate tolerance gene cluster in bacterial pathogens affecting Alliums. This position will functionally validate these clusters and assess their role in tolerating thiosulfinate in vitro and in vivo. Opportunities are also available to study molecular docking and identify suitable candidates that will made bacteria sensitive to thiosulfinates in Alliums. The incumbent will take a leadership role in data collection, data analysis, and compiling manuscripts for publication in appropriate journals. This position will work closely with different key industry stakeholders, and could be involved in supervising undergraduates. The incumbent will also present results at local and national conferences.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480031 2026-04-29T11:23:08-04:00 2026-04-29T11:23:09-04:00 Zone Mechanic I (Electrical) <div>The position will assist in facilities maintenance, construction, and general upkeep of physical properties. This position is responsible for troubleshooting non-complex facilities problems and providing preventive, corrective, and predictive solutions for such problems routinely. This position is responsible for reporting information to management concerning the changing conditions of the University’s facilities and equipment in assigned areas, as well as making recommendations for improvements and upgrades to facilities. This position will be a first responder to trouble calls and emergent needs. Secondary responsibilities of this position include maintaining appropriate documentation and maintenance records, personal timekeeping records, and summarizing actions in writing. This position performs other related duties incidental to the work described herein. This position receives instruction and direct supervision from senior technicians, shop managers, and Operations and Maintenance Leadership.</div> FMD-O&M-Off Campus Zone https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478538 2026-04-22T17:25:59-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:59-04:00 Athletic Subject Tutor - Non-Student Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490679 2026-06-29T15:34:01-04:00 2026-06-29T15:34:01-04:00 Communications & Public Relations Coordinator <div>Manages the communications and public relations for the Skidaway Institute of Oceanography. Responsibilities include media relations, development of printed and digital media, full editorial responsibility for the website and the Skidaway Campus Notes, and interfacing with Skidaway faculty, staff, administration, campus partners, and general public.</div> VPR-Skidaway Inst Oceanography https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478632 2026-04-22T17:34:00-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:01-04:00 Stu Asst - Altizer <div>The Altizer Lab in the Odum School of Ecology at UGA seeks to hire an undergraduate student&nbsp; to assist with ongoing research projects focused on interactions between animals and their parasites, including:&nbsp; (1)&nbsp; Tracking parasites in monarch butterflies using citizen science data, (2) Experimental studies of host-parasite interactions in monarch butterflies, (3) studies of animal behavior and diet as relates to parasite infection. Students will help to collect and enter data, set up laboratory experiments, perform greenhouse work, and communicate with citizen scientists. Students should be comfortable handling plants and insects, data entry, and with basic microscopy. Attention to detail and adherence to sterile procedures are essential. Interested students are expected to work 8-12 hours per week during the academic year and 10-20 hours during the summer months, with the opportunity to continue work beyond the current academic term. We especially encourage freshman and sophomores interested in working beyond the current academic year to apply.&nbsp;</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495884 2026-07-24T20:52:42-04:00 2026-07-24T20:52:42-04:00 Carpenter <div>Reporting to the Director of Lands and Facilities, the Maintenance Technician/Carpenter is a full-time professional staff position. The Maintenance Technician/Carpenter performs skilled work in the construction, repair, and maintenance of wooden and wood substitute items and structures. Also, performs duties in the general repair and maintenance of buildings and university facilities. Strong customer service skills and working independently with little supervision is needed.</div> VPR-Skidaway Inst Oceanography https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477860 2026-04-21T18:00:13-04:00 2026-04-21T18:00:14-04:00 Research Professional-Nankar <div>This position will have significant responsibility and involvement in the design, management, and interpretation of field research trials within the Department of Horticulture’s Vegetable Breeding Program. The successful candidate will oversee vegetable breeding field and greenhouse research. Responsibilities include independently planning, supervising, and conducting experiments, maintaining detailed crop management records, collecting and analyzing data. PCARD</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503253 2026-08-27T15:57:16-04:00 2026-08-27T15:57:17-04:00 Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs <div><strong>POSITION IS ONLY OPEN TO CURRENT FACULTY MEMBERS IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA.</strong><br><br>The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Programs (ADUP) in the College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) is a key member of the Dean’s staff and plays an important leadership role in the college. The ADUP collaborates with the Dean on planning College strategic initiatives, goals and action steps for undergraduate programs and strategies to attain these goals. The ADUP provides administrative leadership and oversight of the CVM’s undergraduate programs, including curriculum development and improvement; advising; enrollment management; student success and progress programs and student affairs; institutional assessment and improvement; human resources and faculty development, including summative and formative performance appraisals; budget and finance development and management related to instruction and Undergraduate Student Affairs; and facilities planning and management.<br><br></div><div>The ADUP is expected to collaborate with the Dean, Associate Deans, Department Heads, faculty, and staff to develop effective support for teaching and active learning experiences. The ADUP oversees and coordinates review of all curricular elements in the college’s undergraduate programming and ensure effective use of instructional and office support to attain College and University goals.<br><br></div><div>The ADUP is responsible for addressing student grievances; issues and problems; provides leadership for any undergraduate assessment or accreditation needs; and coordinates timely completion of requisite reports for the college, university, system, or other regulatory body. The ADUP serves as the Dean’s liaison to various educational related committees and events at the college and university levels and coordinates various awards and recognition opportunities associated with undergraduate education.<br><br></div><div>The ADUP also coordinates with university scheduling as well as the College’s Office of Academic Affairs and Graduate Affairs to ensure that instructional space and equipment for undergraduate programs are appropriate. Additionally, other duties will be assigned as needed.</div> VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499419 2026-08-11T18:32:33-04:00 2026-08-11T18:32:33-04:00 Skilled Trades Worker <div>The primary function of this position is to perform a variety of building maintenance tasks in and around the residence halls. This person works in a community housing approximately 1,200 student residents. The position performs duties necessary to uphold communication and customer service with a variety of peers, residents and other departmental stakeholders; performs periodic duties during weekend and holiday shifts and on-call operations to uphold the standards of care for a 24-hour, seven-day a week residential program. Must be available to work specified shift, with occasional additional shifts Saturday, Sunday, or after hours as needed.</div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478374 2026-04-22T17:16:16-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:16-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant - Huang <div>The graduate student in this position will work under supervision to support research activities, including performing laboratory experiments, conducting data analysis, laboratory maintenance and other activities specified by the professor.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478805 2026-04-22T17:46:45-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:46-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Brisbois <div>A postdoctoral research position is open for candidates with a Ph.D. in biomaterials or a closely related field, as well as a strong background and experience in the areas of: <strong><em>polymer chemistry; small molecule synthesis; biomaterials; controlled release/delivery; light, fiber optics, and photoactivated release; 3D printing; materials characterization; biomedical engineering; and materials and analytical chemistry. </em></strong>As a team member, the successful candidate will work on fast-paced and interdisciplinary projects, including fabricating and characterizing novel polymers, therapeutic controlled release, and testing them using <em>in vitro </em>and <em>in vivo </em>models for conducting cell/molecular biology and biocompatibility tests. Postdoctoral researcher candidates that are highly independent, self-driven, have excellent communication skills, and are motivated with a passion for research and are encouraged to apply. <br><br><strong>The initial appointment is full-time for one year, and the renewal is subject to satisfactory performance in year 1 and continued funding.&nbsp;</strong></div> ENGR-Chem Material & Biomed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504661 2026-09-04T15:51:56-04:00 2026-09-04T15:51:57-04:00 Guest Experience Coordinator - PART TIME <div>The Guest Experience Coordinator-Part-Time, is responsible for providing exceptional customer service to all visitors and enhancing the overall guest experience while visiting the garden. This incumbent serves as a source of accurate information about all aspects of the Gardens’ experience.</div> CAES-Coastal Botanical Gardens https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501624 2026-08-20T12:59:50-04:00 2026-08-20T12:59:51-04:00 Mystery Shopper <div>This position will perform mystery shops for Dining Services to evaluate current offerings, customer service levels, and quality for various units within Dining Services operating units. Attention to detail and the ability to professionally summarize/communicate the completed shop through online reporting. Shop assignments and online reporting need to be completed in a timely manner and as described in the program guidelines.</div> Auxiliary Dining Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478496 2026-04-22T17:24:03-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:03-04:00 Temporary Service Worker - Con't Ed (Cain) <div>Temporary, part-time worker.&nbsp; Duties will include data entry, providing reception and phone coverage, providing duplicates, handling fax and email communications.&nbsp; Helping staff with mailings, event planning, room set-up and clean-up, and other duties as needed. Driving will be a responsibility of the position.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486658 2026-06-03T09:32:57-04:00 2026-06-03T09:32:58-04:00 Cook I (Partial Year) <div><strong>This is a benefits eligible, partial year position, 9-11 months of each year. The selected candidate will be required to sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.</strong><br><br>Skilled cooking work in the preparation of foods for a cafeteria. Work involves the general preparation and cooking of a variety of foods, or the specialized preparations of meats and vegetables. Work involves responsibility of neatness and cleanliness in preparing food, and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Works under the supervision of a Cook 2 or Chef.</div> Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478582 2026-04-22T17:30:15-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:16-04:00 Temporary Field/Greenhouse Assistant To assist in field preparation, maintenance, mowing, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494008 2026-07-16T13:46:57-04:00 2026-07-16T13:46:57-04:00 Student Surgery Crew - LA <div>The Large Animal Emergency Surgery Assistant is utilized after-hours and on weekends to act as a circulating assistant in the Large Animal Surgery Department.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504317 2026-09-03T10:41:22-04:00 2026-09-03T10:41:22-04:00 Long County 4-H Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the County. This position will also provide management and oversight of the County 4-H Program in cooperation with other staff members. The County 4-H Program is robust and provides a wide variety of educational opportunities for youth. This position will work cooperatively with county 4-H staff and provide oversight, management, and support of the 4-H program. As necessary, deliver 4-H programming in a variety of settings including in-school, afterschool, and through participation in state and district events. This position utilizes the expertise of and works closely with advisory groups, community leaders, public officials and representatives of intended audiences to analyze data, identifies needs, and assists in developing educational programs.<br><br></div><div>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500862 2026-08-18T12:51:15-04:00 2026-08-18T12:51:16-04:00 Residence Hall Director <div>The primary function of this position is to create safe, comfortable, and thriving communities that foster a strong sense of belonging and focus on student learning. As an integral member of the team, Residence Hall Directors are full-time, exempt, live-in professionals who oversee one or more residence halls housing up to 1,000 residents. Special emphasis is placed on shaping the residential experience by facilitating the residential curriculum within their communities, as well as supervising various levels of student staff, advising student groups, and supporting desk operations. The incumbent will be an active and engaged member of the department who is committed to growth and high-quality work.</div> Housing-Resident Progs & Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478460 2026-04-22T17:22:20-04:00 2026-05-13T11:08:28-04:00 Building Services Worker - Rock Eagle - Temporary <div>This position performs manual custodial care of Rock Eagle 4-H Education Center cottages, buildings, and facilities. This includes cleaning and minor maintenance work throughout the center. Primary responsibility of the position is directed at the effective use of proper methods and materials in cleaning and caring for building areas and cottages. Individual works without close supervision and follows well established routines and procedures.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483975 2026-05-19T11:11:59-04:00 2026-05-19T11:11:59-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor of Risk Management and Insurance <div>The Department of Insurance, Legal Studies and Real Estate in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Risk Management and Insurance at the assistant or associate professor level, with an anticipated employment start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Insur, Legal, Real Est https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478567 2026-04-22T17:29:48-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:48-04:00 Student Assistant (NE) VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492249 2026-07-09T11:48:06-04:00 2026-07-09T11:48:07-04:00 Assignments Specialist <div>The Assignments Specialist provides front-facing customer service for University Housing and the Housing Assignments Office while managing various key processes related to the assignments processes. A person in this position supports a fast-paced office that has daily interaction with students, parents, staff, faculty and other stakeholders, often on matters of a confidential and sensitive nature. This individual also performs general duties associated with assignments and communication with the more than 9,000 students living in on-campus housing.</div> Housing-Admin Srvcs & Communic https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478664 2026-04-22T17:37:11-04:00 2026-04-22T17:37:11-04:00 Food Service Worker I - Jekyll Island - Temporary <div>Work involves routine food preparation, food service and cleaning the food service and eating areas. Employees work under direct supervision while involved in the preparation, serving and cleaning. Employee follows written and/or oral procedures and practices especially as related to safety and food safety. Employee implements procedures, methods, and activities developed by others. This position reports to the 4-H Dining Commons Manager.</div> CAES-Jekyll Island https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496846 2026-07-30T08:41:21-04:00 2026-07-30T08:41:21-04:00 Director of Golf Operations <div>Responsible for administrative, logistical, and daily operations of the Division I intercollegiate men’s and women’s golf programs. Assisting the coaching staff in the overall administration of the programs, including part-time payroll processing, budget development and management. Serve as the point of contact for travel-related logistics. Serve as the point of contact for the personal development program for student-athletes. Support the Head Coaches with the efficient and productive operation of the men’s and women’s golf programs.&nbsp;</div> Athletics-Women's Golf https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477986 2026-04-21T18:24:46-04:00 2026-04-21T18:24:47-04:00 Assistant Research Scientist <div>Research Scientist combining wet lab and computational approaches to analysis and understanding of protein structure and function. &nbsp;</div> VPR-Inst of Bioinformatics https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503831 2026-09-01T09:11:10-04:00 2026-09-01T09:11:10-04:00 LABORATORY TECHNICIAN II <div>This is a responsible technical position in the Infectious Diseases Laboratory (IDL) in the Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery in the College of Veterinary Medicine. The position will primarily require good general lab techniques and a willingness to learn new techniques are important. The use of aseptic techniques for sample handling, and processing are necessary. This position will require development and validation of neutralization assays, nucleic acid purification, amplification and running polymerase chain reaction (PCR) tests using a thermocycler and agarose gel and methods.&nbsp;</div> VetMed-SAMS Infect Disease Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500119 2026-08-14T10:30:04-04:00 2026-08-14T10:30:05-04:00 Sr. Payroll Coordinator <div>The Sr. Payroll Coordinator oversees payroll operations for Auxiliary Services, ensuring accurate, timely, and compliant payroll processing across multiple units. The role serves as the primary resource for approvals, escalations, and audit readiness; directly supervises the Auxiliary Payroll Coordinator; and partners with Auxiliary HR, central university payroll, and unit leadership to resolve issues, improve processes, and maintain strong internal controls.</div> Auxiliary Finance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478398 2026-04-22T17:19:26-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:27-04:00 Math Tutor Act as one-on-one or small group tutor for student-athletes enrolled in MATH, STAT, PHYS, CSCI, or other math related courses. Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478836 2026-04-22T17:50:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:36-04:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>This position is funded as part of the NSF Biofoundry project to develop large language models for biological sequence analysis. Specifically, the candidate will develop and fine tune protein language models for glycoenzyme classification, engineering and function prediction and work closely with other project personnel to test predictions generated from LLMs. The candidate will also provide written reports of project updates and develop course materials for user training.</div> Franklin-Biochemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502456 2026-08-25T11:46:44-04:00 2026-08-25T11:46:45-04:00 TBO Team Lead - Team 3 <div>The Terry Business Office Team Lead oversees and coordinates fiscal operations for assigned departments and units. The position has supervisory responsibility and serves as liaison between other Terry teams to facilitate effective workflow and operations. This role will focus on master’s programs and International Business for Terry. This includes the Full-Time MBA, Executive MBA, Professional MBA, Online MBA, Master of Science in Business Administration, and the programs coordinated by International Business. This position reports to the Terry Business Office under the leadership and supervision of the Administrative Financial Director. This role will receive guidance from the Unit Heads to ensure faculty, staff, and departmental needs are met.</div> Terry-Business Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478518 2026-04-22T17:24:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:44-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate-Ad-Nankar <div>- Lead plant breeding and pre-breeding research in START-UP SETTING since it is relatively new breeding program and it is TIME DEMANDING.<br>- Strong knowledge of breeding methods used in vegetable breeding.<br>- Handle and operate analytical biochemistry, molecular biology, and high-throughput phenotyping equipments and tools.<br>- Understand statistical principles and applications to be applied in breeding research.<br>- Excellent oral and written communication skills.<br>- Interest in collaborative research and ability to work in multicultural team.<br>- Obtain driving license and operate the vehicle.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488742 2026-06-16T15:18:25-04:00 2026-06-16T15:18:26-04:00 Digital Marketing & Social Media Coordinator <div>The Digital Marketing and Social Media Coordinator plays a key role in advancing the mission and visibility of the University of Georgia College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES). As part of the CAES Office of Marketing and Communications (OMC), this position helps shape how audiences experience and engage with the college online, transforming narratives about research, teaching, and Extension into compelling digital content that reflects the impact of Georgia’s No. 1 industry.<br><br>Reporting to the Digital Marketing and Social Media Manager, the Digital Marketing and Social Media Coordinator contributes to a collaborative team dedicated to elevating the college’s brand and strengthening connections with students, faculty, alumni, and partners. Through creative storytelling, strategic campaign management, and data-informed decision-making, this role supports initiatives that inspire pride, encourage engagement, and extend the reach of the college’s work across Georgia and beyond.</div> CAES-Comm & Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478615 2026-04-22T17:33:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:29-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate The focus of the position will be on spatial population dynamics, with an  emphasis on \r\nunderstanding how movement and resource selection influence survival. A secondary \r\nemphasis will be on development of power analysis tools in the R package 'unmarked'. Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494919 2026-07-21T15:27:25-04:00 2026-07-21T15:27:25-04:00 Research Technician I - Iron Horse <div>Assists farm manager with day to day operation of a 600 acre plant sciences research farm. Tasks include but are not limited to interacting with CAES Research Faculty, Staff and students on a regular basis, operating agricultural equipment, guidance systems, variable rate controllers, applying fertilizers, applying pesticides, land prep., soil sampling, general farm maintenance and repair, etc.</div> CAES-Campbell Rsch & Ed Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477824 2026-04-21T17:58:02-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:03-04:00 Housing Operations Manager - Rock Eagle 4-H Center The individual in this position is responsible for the direction of housekeeping services to all buildings at Rock Eagle 4-H Center.  The individual in this position hires, trains, and supervises regular full-time employees and part-time employees in the Housekeeping Department.  The individual must have effective communication skills in order to work with other department heads, guests, and employees in the department. \r\n\r\nthe individual in this position manages a department of 20 employees and must be willing to work weekends, evenings, and long days in order to have the 4-H Center ready for the arrival of guests.  Supervision includes the cleaning of guest quarters or cabins, cleaning buildings, providing conference setups, managing laundry, and ordering equipment and supplies. \r\n\r\nhttp://www.rockeagle4h.org/ CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478759 2026-04-22T17:42:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:29-04:00 Temporary Facilities Office Assistant <div>The Housing Department Facilities Office Assistant helps on-campus residents maintain the highest quality of life in their living space by expediting maintenance and building services work requests to get them resolved as quickly as possible. The office assistant also escorts contractors on campus for inspections and repair work.<br><br></div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498440 2026-08-06T12:34:32-04:00 2026-08-06T12:34:32-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>The postdoctoral researcher will lead laboratory experiments, analytical measurements, data interpretation, and computational analyses while coordinating closely with the Principal Investigator and student researchers. This position will ensure continuity across interconnected project activities, maintain rigorous quality assurance and reproducible data workflows, and accelerate completion of milestones. The postdoctoral researcher will also train and mentor graduate and undergraduate students, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration. This position is essential for timely and successful project completion.</div> Franklin-Geology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478127 2026-04-21T18:35:12-04:00 2026-04-21T18:35:13-04:00 Area Director-DeKalb <div>Would you like to have an impact on your community and make a difference? Are you committed to service? Are you a strategic thinker with strong business acumen and leadership experience? Do you excel at managing teams, analyzing complex business challenges, and driving results? The University of Georgia Small Business Development Center (SBDC) in Tucker, GA is seeking a highly motivated individual for a management-level, public service faculty position dedicated to helping Georgia businesses grow and prosper. We seek a skilled professional for a management-level, public service faculty position focused on business development and operational leadership, dedicated to helping Georgia businesses grow and prosper.<br><br></div><div>As an Area Director, you will apply your broad base of business knowledge to deliver high-impact consulting, training, and strategic guidance to small businesses across your assigned territory. Responsibilities also include managing the DeKalb SBDC territory and office personnel. This role requires strong analytical capabilities, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. You will lead the daily operations of the Tucker office, supervise, and ensure program excellence within the DeKalb County SBDC service area.<br><br></div><div>This position involves multi-county travel and offers the opportunity to apply your expertise in a dynamic, collaborative environment.<br><br></div><div>The salary is $95,000 with a comprehensive benefits package, including a defined benefits retirement plan.</div> PSO-Small Business Dev Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478593 2026-04-22T17:32:20-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:20-04:00 Temporary Research Technician The individual will manage research programs that determine fluxes in peanut, pecan, and other ecosystems. The individual will help plan, prepare, and monitor field data collection. The candidate will deploy instrumentation, and use computer programs to double check and process data; the individual will help prepare both technical and scientific reports and write-ups meant for numerous and various outlets. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494143 2026-07-17T08:26:42-04:00 2026-07-17T08:26:43-04:00 Communications & Content Specialist <div>The Communications &amp; Content Specialist advances UGA’s strategic communications priorities by serving as the embedded communications professional for the Innovation District while also contributing editorial and storytelling content to the Division of Marketing &amp; Communications’ institutional channels. The ideal candidate is a versatile communicator and strong writer who brings journalistic instincts, digital fluency, and the ability to navigate both unit-level and institution-wide priorities. This individual is equally comfortable building relationships across campus, identifying compelling stories, and creating content that engages various audiences while supporting the university’s reputation and strategic goals.</div> MarComm-Strategic Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477758 2026-04-21T17:31:44-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:45-04:00 Lab Manager <div>The Laboratory Manager position is a full-time role within the Brain Food Lab at the University of Georgia, directed by Dr. Shana Adise, PhD, focusing on neurocognitive development, obesity, and related outcomes in youth.<br><br></div><div>The primary responsibilities of the Lab Manager are multifaceted, serving as the operational and technical backbone of the lab. Key duties include data management and analysis (overseeing entry, cleaning, storage, and coding pipelines) and study coordination (managing participant recruitment, scheduling, and MRI scanning logistics). Additionally, the Lab Manager is responsible for supervision and training of research assistants, handling daily lab operations (inventory and ordering), managing regulatory compliance (IRB protocols), and providing general administrative and research support to the PI, such as assisting with grant reports.</div> FACS-Nutritional Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478715 2026-04-22T17:40:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:24-04:00 Student Assistant - Ogden <div>This position will help with all aspects of Dr. Ogden’s CEA breeding program. This will involve a combination of greenhouse, lab, and field work.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497719 2026-08-04T09:26:44-04:00 2026-08-04T09:26:44-04:00 OPERATIONS SPECIALIST I <div>This is the second in a series of three non-exempt Operations Specialist positions.<br>This is a specialized position that coordinates and performs aspects of the financial cycle. The purpose of this position is to process the University's financial operations as well as departmental operations.</div> FD-Accounts Payable https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478071 2026-04-21T18:29:45-04:00 2026-04-21T18:29:46-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Genetics, Genomics, & Tree Breeding <div>The Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources at the University of Georgia in Athens, GA invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Forest Genetics, Genomics and/or Tree Breeding at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, with research, instruction, and university and professional service expectations as part of a 9-month appointment. Potential areas of research may include: Forest genetics, genomics, tree breeding, genomic selection, and gene editing technologies to address the molecular genetic basis of perennial traits relevant to forest productivity, health, adaptation, wood quality, and value-added biomaterials. We are particularly interested in candidates who can build a collaborative research program with faculty in the Warnell School, across campus, and with research partners at regional, national, and international levels, employing these tools for forest health applications, conserving and restoring threatened forest tree species, and improving forest productivity.<br><br></div><div>Research responsibilities include development of an externally funded program that is recognized nationally and internationally. Teaching duties could include developing new undergraduate and graduate courses in Forest Genetics/Tree Improvement and Forest Biotechnology. Professional service includes serving on School/University committees and actively participating in professional/scientific societies.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504169 2026-09-02T12:03:31-04:00 2026-09-02T12:03:32-04:00 IT Professional Asst (PT) <div>The EITS Help Desk provides tier 1 support to University of Georgia Faculty, Staff, and Students on a variety of EITS products. These products include UGAMail, MyID, eLC, UGA and several other applications. This position will be a public facing support personnel. This will include engagement through phone, chats, tickets, and walk-ins.&nbsp;</div> EITS-Client Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500519 2026-08-17T13:10:07-04:00 2026-08-17T13:10:07-04:00 Manager - Volleyball Critical to the daily operations and success of our team. These individuals provide assistance with laundry, equipment care and maintenance, practice set-up & take down, and occasionally travel with teams and provide assistance in various ways on road trips. Athletics-Volleyball https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478420 2026-04-22T17:20:04-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:05-04:00 Student Assistant - Hunt <div>The unit seeks a conscientious, thorough, and careful student assistant to assist lab personnel with sample preparation and laboratory maintenance.<br><br></div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480162 2026-04-30T08:21:39-04:00 2026-04-30T08:21:40-04:00 Zone Mechanic I (Plumbing) <div>The position will assist in facilities maintenance, construction, and general upkeep of physical properties. This position is responsible for troubleshooting non-complex facilities problems and providing preventive, corrective, and predictive solutions for such problems routinely. This position is responsible for reporting information to management concerning the changing conditions of the University’s facilities and equipment in assigned areas, as well as making recommendations for improvements and upgrades to facilities. This position will be a first responder to trouble calls and emergent needs. Secondary responsibilities of this position include maintaining appropriate documentation and maintenance records, personal timekeeping records, and summarizing actions in writing. This position performs other related duties incidental to the work described herein. This position receives instruction and direct supervision from senior technicians, shop managers, and Operations and Maintenance Leadership.</div> FMD-O&M-East Zone Shop https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478540 2026-04-22T17:26:02-04:00 2026-04-22T17:26:03-04:00 Post Doc AC - Rains <div>1) development of training materials for advanced technology training for farmers, 2) developing weeding system using lasers and mechanical weeding and 3) improved post-processing handling of peanuts to reduce aflatoxin contamination.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490714 2026-06-30T09:28:00-04:00 2026-06-30T09:28:01-04:00 Director of Biosafety and Responsible Official <div>This position acts as the University Biosafety Officer as part of the research compliance infrastructure of the Office of the Vice President for Research. Overall responsibilities include the development, implementation and management of programs and policies relative to the University's compliance with biological safety; biohazardous materials security; and federal, state and local regulations governing all research involving biological materials, agents and toxins.<br><br>This position leads and manages the Office of Biosafety, including the management of the University Institutional Biosafety Committee. This position works closely with the USDA, the CDC, state and local authorities, and with professional organizations to assure that the university meets all regulatory requirements, minimizes environmental risks, and protects human health and the environment.<br><br>Responsibilities include but are not limited to supporting and consulting with the Institutional Biosafety Committee and the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee; safety oversight of research projects involving recombinant DNA, transgenic plants and animals; animal, plant and human pathogens and biological toxins; biological laboratory safety; oversight of biocontainment design, construction and commissioning; oversight on all aspects of biocontainment facility protocol development; oversight of annual verification of proper containment parameters for biocontainment facilities; consultation on the importation and interstate transport of regulated biological materials, and the shipment of regulated biological materials; blood borne pathogen exposure control program; biological safety cabinet certification program; the autoclave sterilization efficiency testing program; biohazardous materials security; employee, student, and public health programs; and support of the occupational health programs.<br><br>Training is a key component of this position, and the incumbent must be able to work closely with a very diverse community. This position is a primary source of leadership and guidance on biological and laboratory safety, as well as security and regulatory information, for the University. Use sound professional judgement in interpreting and executing biosafety regulations and policy. Ability to build and maintain relationships with a variety of stakeholders. Must have effective communication. This position is a full-time on-site role and requires on-call availability after hours for emergencies.</div> VPR-Biosafety https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478634 2026-04-22T17:34:04-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:05-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Switchgrass and Turfgrass Disease Management <div>The applicant will participate in switchgrass and turfgrass disease management by breeding for disease resistance and exploring for biocontrol agents. The applicant will work on identifying sources of disease resistance, carrying out functional analysis of gene expression, developing collections of plant pathogens and mycoparasites, studying pathogen population structure, and investigating parasite-pathogen-plant interactions. The candidate will work in collaboration with plant breeders, molecular biologist, plant pathologists and extension faculty. The candidate will help in drafting papers and grant proposals.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496317 2026-07-27T16:12:20-04:00 2026-07-27T16:12:20-04:00 Small Animal Emergency Front Desk, PRN <div>The primary responsibility for this position will be to assist the Emergency Critical Care team on setting appointments and receiving emergency patients during evenings, overnights, weekends and holidays. The ECC Vet Asst. will assist clients in delivering their pets to the ECC team which may include lifting/restraining and transporting into the ER. This position will also answer phones, set up appointments from local referring veterinarians, open patient charts in the hospital database system and process payments for services.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477871 2026-04-21T18:00:40-04:00 2026-04-21T18:00:40-04:00 Part Time Food Service Worker-Wahsega Work involves routine food preparation, food service and cleaning the food service and eating areas. Employees work under direct supervision while involved in preparation, serving and cleaning. Employee follows written and/or oral procedures and practices especially as related to safety and food safety. Employee implements procedures, methods and activities developed by others. This position reports to the 4-H Dining Commons Manager. CAES-Wahsega https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503316 2026-08-28T08:06:51-04:00 2026-08-28T08:06:52-04:00 4-H Paulding County AmeriCorps Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members will comply with AmeriCorps guidelines such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other trainings.<br>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members will log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499506 2026-08-12T10:45:31-04:00 2026-08-12T10:45:31-04:00 Manager Bulldog Print + Design <div>Provides strategic leadership and operational management for Bulldog Print + Design, overseeing all print production, customer service, business operations, staffing, and vendor management functions. Directs daily operations for digital print, wide-format, finishing, and related services to ensure high-quality production, efficient workflow, customer satisfaction, and compliance with University policies and procedures. Develops operational goals, manages departmental resources, and leads continuous improvement initiatives to support campus printing and design needs. Supervises professional and production staff and serves as the primary liaison between Bulldog Print + Design, University departments, external vendors, and administration.<br><br></div> FD-Bulldog Print & Design https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478376 2026-04-22T17:16:19-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:20-04:00 Temporary Lab Assistant - Plant Genetics <div>This position is needed to assist in the cleaning and processing of seed samples for various crops.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478807 2026-04-22T17:46:49-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:49-04:00 Facilities Office Assistant <div>The Housing Department Facilities Office Assistant helps on-campus residents maintain the highest quality of life in their living space by expediting maintenance and building services work requests to get them resolved as quickly as possible.</div><div><br><br></div> Housing-Facilities-Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501680 2026-08-20T14:54:08-04:00 2026-08-20T14:54:08-04:00 Foreign & International Law Librarian <div>The Foreign &amp; International Law Librarian provides specialized legal research, reference, instructional, and collection development support for the School of Law’s foreign, international, and comparative law programs. The position also supports faculty, students, journals, moot court teams, visiting scholars, and related centers; contributes to Law Library operations and strategic initiatives; instructs School of Law legal research courses; and participates in professional, scholarly, and service activities.</div> Law School-King Law Library https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478498 2026-04-22T17:24:06-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:06-04:00 Food Service Worker - Wahsega - Temporary <div>Work involves preparing and serving food and cleaning food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision, follow written and/or oral procedures and practices. Employee will implement these procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</div> CAES-Wahsega https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486776 2026-06-03T15:24:38-04:00 2026-06-03T15:24:38-04:00 Coordinator for Instructional Development <div>For full consideration, those wishing to apply for this position should submit application materials by July 4 ,2026.<br><br>The University of Georgia seeks an organized and thoughtful individual to join the Center for Teaching and Learning (CTL) as a Coordinator for Instructional Development. The CTL is a unit of the Office of Instruction, whose central mission is to provide university-wide leadership, collaboration, and support on matters related to instruction. This Coordinator for Instructional Development reports to the Senior Associate Director for Teaching and Learning, and collaborates with other CTL personnel. At the CTL, Coordinators work under the guidance of their supervisor to develop and execute plans and protocols for effective and efficient operations in their area. They manage and oversee the implementation of programs and services, coordinate and support external facing initiatives, cultivate and maintain relationships with individuals from campus partner units, provide training, consultations, and support for individuals across campus, collaborate with their CTL colleagues, and more.<br><br>The individual filling this position will join the CTL team in supporting instruction across all UGA schools and colleges. The instructional development services that may be included in this individual's portfolio could include project management and coordination, one-on-one teaching-related consultations, facilitation of mid-semester formative evaluations of teaching, execution of specific CTL programs, development of help resources for teaching and learning technology, and support for instructional use of our learning management system. There will also be an opportunity for this individual to teach at least once per year within our slate of graduate level teaching development courses.</div> VPI-Teaching & Learning Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502819 2026-08-26T11:32:08-04:00 2026-08-26T11:32:08-04:00 Business Manager <div>This is a highly responsible position that will assume primary responsibility for the business management activities of an assigned unit(s) within the College. This position manages and controls all accounting and budgetary functions for the department and may supervise student and/or staff positions. Responsibilities include but are not limited to posting financial transactions; reconciling accounts; coordinating with the CPH Post Award Office to manage grant accounts; working with the CPH HR Director on processing new hire personnel/paperwork; interpreting and executing UGA policies and procedures.</div> Public Health-Business Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478766 2026-04-22T17:43:31-04:00 2026-04-22T17:43:32-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Pickering Lab <div>Agentic AI is rapidly changing nearly every domain, from academia to industry. Agriculture is no different. These postdoctoral opportunity will look to research and build <em>agentic scientific AI systems</em> that can design, predict, and optimize agricultural outcomes—across crops, environments, and management regimes. We are seeking a Postdoctoral Associate to develop the next generation of <strong>Agentic AI for Agricultural Design and Prediction</strong>, spanning:</div><ul><li><strong>Genomics agents</strong> that assemble <em>AI-native genomic prediction and selection models</em> (e.g., DNA foundation-models, GNN/sequence architectures for breeding decisions, pangenomic models).</li><li><strong>Crop Growth Model agents</strong> that create <em>AI-native crop growth models</em>—including <strong>Bio-Informed Neural Networks (BINNs)</strong> and hybrid dynamical systems that fuse mechanistic constraints with large-scale data.</li><li><strong>Scientific agent workflows</strong> that can ingest literature + datasets, propose modeling choices, run experiments, quantify uncertainty, and iteratively improve models with human-in-the-loop evaluation.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>This role sits at the intersection of applied mathematics, machine learning, genomics, crop science, and dynamical systems, and will be carried out in a highly interdisciplinary team environment.<br><br><strong>Potential Focus Areas</strong></div><ol><li><strong>Agentic Genomics for Prediction &amp; Selection</strong>: Build agents that can automatically construct, evaluate, and adapt genomic/pangenomic/editing prediction pipelines (from raw genotypes/omics to breeding-value predictions), including modern representation learning and uncertainty-aware decision support.</li><li><strong>Agentic AI Crop Growth Models (AI-CGMs)</strong>: Develop hybrid modeling agents that learn <strong>AI-native CGMs</strong> (e.g., BINNs; constrained neural ODEs; spatiotemporal models) integrating genomics, phenomics, physiology, weather, soils, remote sensing, and management data.</li></ol><div><br><strong>What Success Looks Like (12–24 months)</strong></div><ul><li>A working agentic modeling stack demonstrated on at least one “end-to-end” crop use case (e.g., data → genomics predictions + AI-CGM → intervention suggestions with uncertainty).</li><li>Publications in top venues (ML for science, computational biology, agronomy/crop modeling) and public releases of code/benchmarks.</li><li>Clear pathways to stakeholder deployment (breeders, agronomists, extension, or industry R&amp;D).</li></ul> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498510 2026-08-06T14:44:38-04:00 2026-08-06T14:44:39-04:00 4-H Lamar County AmeriCorps Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting required impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members must comply with AmeriCorps requirements such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other required trainings.<br>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members are required to log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478185 2026-04-22T09:03:55-04:00 2026-04-22T09:03:56-04:00 Clay & Randolph Counties ANR Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) area by providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods. Randolph and Clay counties have a total combined Farm Gate Value of $85,021,527. Peanuts, small grains and forages are among the top agricultural commodities in these counties. Timber and forestry products comprise another large percentage of the Farm Gate Value.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478789 2026-04-22T17:44:12-04:00 2026-04-22T17:44:13-04:00 Temporary Technician (Lance) <div>This position is focused on working with a long term data set. The technician will organize a large data set, conduct quality control, and statistically analyze the data. In addition, the technician will write the methods and results and begin a literature review for the manuscript. Opportunities also exist to conduct some field work in support of other projects going on in the lab.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504449 2026-09-03T14:28:18-04:00 2026-09-03T14:28:18-04:00 Senior Director, Marketing and Communications <div>The Senior Director of Marketing and Communications provides strategic leadership and vision for the College’s marketing and communications enterprise. This role is responsible for developing and executing a comprehensive, data-driven communications and marketing strategy that advances the College’s mission, strengthens its brand, and ensures integrated, consistent messaging across all platforms and units.<br><br></div><div>This role oversees branding and messaging, directs the creation of high-impact marketing materials—including those supporting fundraising and development—and executes the communication strategy through publications, news releases, promotional pieces, and key relationships that elevate the College’s visibility. Additional responsibilities include supervising a team of six, guiding digital and media strategies, leveraging analytics to optimize web, social, and advertising performance, and fostering cross-functional collaboration to align College communications with university-wide initiatives.</div> COE-Communications Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501153 2026-08-19T09:10:31-04:00 2026-08-19T09:10:32-04:00 Student Supervisor Specialist I <div>Under the direction of the McBay Science Library User Services Desk Coordinator, the Student Supervisor Specialist I attends to library patron requests at the service desk as well as via phone and email with regard to the circulation of books, media, loanable technology, course reserves, and resource sharing materials; provides information about the library and its resources; and participates in hiring, training, and coordination of student employees.<br><br>Additional responsibilities include: processes materials, maintains accurate patron records, and adds item records as needed; handles specialized services including issuing borrowers’ cards, placing and clearing student registration holds, answering inquiries concerning library obligations and interpreting policies, rules, and regulations.<br><br>This position serves as the person in charge in the absence of the User Services Desk Coordinator or the Lead Student Supervisor.This position may also collaborate with Security at night and on the weekends and in cases of emergency situations.<br><br>Work is performed in a team environment under general supervision following established practices and procedures.<br><br>Work schedule is typically Tuesday-Saturday, 10am-7pm. Schedule is subject to change during breaks, intersession, and home football game days.</div> Libraries-Access Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478463 2026-04-22T17:22:25-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:25-04:00 Grounds Keeper - Rock Eagle - Temporary <div>Job duties will include, but are not limited to:<br>Mowing grass with zero turn, stand up, walk-behind and push-type lawnmowers. Weed-eating turf edges, large areas, hillsides, and lake edges. Edging curbs, roads, sidewalks, and other areas. Trimming trees, bushes, hedges, and other landscaped areas. Picking up, grinding limbs, and working with a Brush Bandit chipper, or similar equipment. Hand stacking rip-rap stone and other type landscaping rock. Spreading pine straw, wheat straw, and grass seed. Lining and painting football fields. Knowledge of proper use of chainsaws and other related equipment. Will climb onto roofs (using a ladder) to blow off roofs and clean gutters on all buildings. Spraying chemicals to control weeds, insects, etc. Assist with center trash collection, building set up and breakdowns as needed.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/484145 2026-05-20T10:37:52-04:00 2026-05-20T10:37:52-04:00 Clinical or Tenure Track Poultry Veterinarian <div>The Department of Population Health, Poultry Diagnostic and Research Center (PDRC), College of Veterinary Medicine at the University of Georgia is seeking a veterinarian to fill a vacant position in clinical poultry medicine. Responsibilities include clinical services to the poultry industry and major participation in the Master of Avian Medicine and the online Master of Avian Health and Medicine degree programs. The position will be either a non-tenure track clinical assistant or clinical associate professorship or a tenure track assistant or associate professorship depending on qualifications.<br><br>Rank, salary, and terms of appointment will be dependent upon qualifications and experience of the applicant.</div> VetMed-Poultry Diagnos & Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478569 2026-04-22T17:29:51-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:52-04:00 Student Assistant CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492478 2026-07-10T10:32:27-04:00 2026-07-10T10:32:29-04:00 University Registrar and Executive Director of Curriculum Management <div>This is a rare and substantively distinctive opportunity in the national registrar profession: the role combines the full scope of a flagship university registrar with direct responsibility for UGA's curriculum governance systems, the institutional infrastructure through which faculty-approved academic programs, courses, and degree requirements are managed, published, and implemented. The University Registrar and Executive Director of Curriculum Management (“University Registrar”) reports directly to the Vice President for Instruction and Senior Vice Provost for Academic Planning and serves on the VPI Leadership Team with the Vice Provost for Enrollment Management and two Associate Vice Presidents for Instruction. The University Registrar provides support and guidance to the Vice President for Instruction as needed in areas including, but not limited to, curriculum, student success initiatives, faculty governance, and academic program proposals. This role also represents the office on committees and inorganizations at the university, state, and national level. This role works collaboratively with other offices in managing enrollment, curricular issues, academic advising, class schedules, and classroom space management, which informs the Institution’s strategy and directs its best efforts in the successful attainment of students’ educational goals.</div><div>The University Registrar provides guidance to campus leadership concerning curriculum development and approval and resolution of student issues and is the liaison with the University System of Georgia (USG) concerning curriculum and the Chief Transfer Officer for the university serving on USG committees as needed. The University Registrar is responsible for supporting and implementing university and VPI student success initiatives including the recently launched new digital <a href=\"https://clr.uga.edu/content/index.html\"><strong>Comprehensive Learner Record</strong></a>, as well as the First-Year Odyssey Seminar and Double Dawgs program. The University Registrar oversees the development, implementation, and maintenance of student and curriculum systems. The University Registrar is a professional who with the goal of student success, collaborates across campus and appreciates the role of the University Registrar’s Office in the larger institutional context, is collaborative, able to engage various constituencies, and works to ensure everyone across the institution is part of conversations on student success. The University Registrar provides leadership, strategic planning, organization, and direction for all functional areas of the Office of the University Registrar and is responsible for the budget.</div> UHR-HR Search Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/18421 2018-02-22T16:54:57-05:00 2018-02-22T16:54:58-05:00 NBE_Hourly Project AFFIRM is seeking a part-time employee (19 hours/week) to assist with a study of transgender, transsexual, trans, nonbinary, gender non-conforming, and genderqueer Atlantans. COE-Counseling & Human Dev Svc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478670 2026-04-22T17:37:21-04:00 2026-04-22T17:37:21-04:00 Post Doctoral AD- Carver <div>A 2-year postdoctoral position focused on wildlife disease management is available in the Odum School of Ecology at the University of Georgia. The research will focus on the practical application and modelling of sarcoptic mange control in wildlife. The goals of the research are to: (1) work with stakeholders engaged in on-ground disease management problems; (2) advance a modeling framework to enhance alignment with the types and nuances of management undertaken in situ; and (3) produce data-informed management guidelines for select host species impacted by sarcoptic mange. The ideal applicant for this position will have a strong appreciation for the realities of on-ground wildlife disease management, and with the creativity to think innovatively in this space. The applicant will listen to, understand the nuances, and work with stakeholders engaged in disease management attempts, as well as willingness to gain first-hand experience. The applicant will be competent with modeling, but does not have to be a modeler per se, as practical cross-disciplinary skills are equally important for this research. The work is focused on sarcoptic mange and broadly around ideas presented in the below perspective from the Journal of Applied Ecology. The fundamentals of a modelling framework already exist, and this project would build out from that to be widely translational across mange host species (at least several specific examples), and ultimately have potential application to systems with similar transmission modes. Carver, S., A. Peters and S. A. Richards (2022). \"Model Integrated Disease Management to facilitate effective translatable solutions for wildlife disease issues.\" Journal of Applied Ecology 59(12): 2902-2910.</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496934 2026-07-30T13:18:07-04:00 2026-07-30T13:18:08-04:00 Associate Dean of College Operations <div><strong>YOU MUST HOLD A CURRENT FACULTY POSITION AT THE RANK OF PROFESSOR OR CLINICAL PROFESSOR IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA TO APPLY TO THIS POSITION.</strong><br><br>The Associate Dean for College Operations (ADCO) reports directly to the Dean and oversees the comprehensive management of the college’s physical and technical infrastructure, including: facilities, information technology, and safety and compliance policies, designed to support and advance the CVM’s tripartite mission of teaching, service, and research. As a senior administrator, the ADCO serves as a strategic advisor to the Dean and other college leaders, bridges the gap between academic/clinical missions and university logistics, and ensures the college is compliant with all university, state, and federal regulations, as well as veterinary accreditation standards.</div> VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477988 2026-04-21T18:24:51-04:00 2026-04-21T18:24:51-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor – Meat Science Extension and Teaching <div>Assistant or Associate Professor – Meat Science Extension and Teaching. This is a nine-month, tenure track or tenured appointment (65% Extension, 30% Teaching, 5% Service) with two months of summer salary (11.111% per month) guaranteed in the Department of Animal and Dairy Science (ADS, ads.caes.uga.edu) in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences at the University of Georgia (UGA). The position will be located at the UGA Athens Campus. It is expected to develop and provide leadership for a relevant nationally/internationally recognized meat science Extension and teaching program.<br><br></div><div><strong>Major Responsibilities</strong>: The individual is expected to develop and provide leadership for a relevant nationally/internationally recognized meats Extension program. Extension activities include interacting with industry, county agents, and other scientists to develop a state-of-the-art information/technology transfer program for the meat industry. This faculty member will serve as a resource on meat processing, fresh and processed meat production, and meat evaluation for the meat industry, 4-H and FFA meat judging coaches, and HACCP training, and is expected to develop or contribute to a comprehensive meat science curriculum to include topics in meat evaluation, fresh meats, and processed meats; advise undergraduate and graduate students; mentor students interested in industry work experiences/internships; lead students in extracurricular learning experiences; and provide guest lectures to support existing courses. The specific Extension and applied research program will be determined based on the successful candidate’s area(s) of expertise, but emphasis will be placed on the ability to develop an externally funded, applied research program. This faculty member will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in meat science, and a graduate course in their area of expertise within the department.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503850 2026-09-01T09:46:17-04:00 2026-09-01T09:46:18-04:00 Business Operations and Human Resources Manager <div>This position is a highly responsible managerial position which independently performs administrative functions by directing the planning, organizing and executing the day-to-day operations of the Institute for Bioinformatics (IOB).<br><br></div><div>This position has equal focus on financial operations, administration, and efforts to grow the Institute. The successful candidate will be able to develop department policy, programs and procedures and assist with grant/funding proposal development and organized training/symposia events. This position is responsible for preparation of accounting statements and reports and assisting administration in the preparation of more complex statements and reports. This position exercises judgment in maintenance of accounting procedures, provides consultation to IOB faculty and staff on accounting and sponsored programs policy and procedures, as well as consultations to employees and supervisors on human resources issues. This position is distinguished by the complexity and scope of issues, independence and discretion, and the degree of technical expertise to perform successfully. Independence and communication are key because the IOB Director (direct report) is located in a different building on campus and frequently travels.</div> VPR-Inst of Bioinformatics https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500139 2026-08-14T11:49:39-04:00 2026-08-14T11:49:40-04:00 Global Education Advisor II <div>The position is an integral part of a wide variety<strong> </strong>and vibrant group of international education professionals passionate about their contribution to the overall educational mission of UGA. The Global Education Advisor works with the staff of the Office of Global Engagement's Global Education office. The position implements procedures and policies, including risk management, pertaining to international student mobility; counsels students by providing technical guidance and problem resolution before, during and after programs overseas, including faculty-led study abroad, exchange, affiliate and consortia programs, University System study abroad, external offerings, work, internships, research, volunteer and service learning experiences; provides information to student in one-on-one and group formats via advising appointments, email, phone, social media, informational events, and publications; promotes international opportunities on UGA campus and beyond; assists with training student staff; and works closely with faculty and staff throughout campus involved with study abroad.</div> OGE-Global Education https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478401 2026-04-22T17:19:31-04:00 2026-06-29T16:32:44-04:00 Bus Operator (Temporary) Safe operation of buses on campus routes and occasional charters. Complete paperwork associated with assignments. Follow written and verbal instructions as given by supervisory personnel. Occasional bus washing and other non-driving tasks are needed from time to time. Will submit to drug and alcohol testing in accordance with the US Department of Transportation. Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478843 2026-04-22T17:51:40-04:00 2026-04-22T17:51:41-04:00 Auxillary Events and Outside Rentals Intern <div>This position is responsible for managing and supporting auxiliary events and outside rentals that generate revenue and maximize facility utilization beyond traditional athletic use. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: coordinating and executing sporting and non-sporting rental events; serving as the primary liaison for clients hosting hospitality events, tours, banquets, meetings, and special events; managing the event rental database and calendar; preparing and administering rental contracts and ensuring adherence to contractual, financial, and risk management guidelines; and providing on-site event oversight. The role works closely with internal departments to coordinate staffing, facility setup and breakdown, and operational support, while maintaining a strong focus on customer service, operational efficiency, and institutional standards. Additional responsibilities include assisting with reporting, documentation, and other administrative duties that support auxiliary event and facility operations.<br><br></div><div><br></div> Athletics-Event Management https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502616 2026-08-25T15:47:07-04:00 2026-08-25T15:47:08-04:00 Organizational Development and Change Management Consultant <div>The Organizational Development and Change Management Consultant, within the Division of University Human Resources (UHR) for the University of Georgia, structures and implements organizational development and change management strategies, facilitates stakeholder engagement, and partners across functional areas to ensure successful adoption of new systems, processes, and ways of working. As part of the Learning and Development department within UHR, this role plays a key role in aligning people, processes, and technology to enhance organizational effectiveness and long-term capabilities.<br><br></div><div>This senior role serves as an internal consultant for university leaders, departments, and HR partners to improve organizational effectiveness through change management, team development, leadership support, workforce education, and organizational assessment, with an initial focus on the implementation of a new Unified Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system. In partnership with UHR units and campus partners, this role supports successful ERP adoption by developing strategies for change, educating stakeholders, and aligning the workforce with new digital workflows and capabilities. This role focuses on minimizing resistance to change as well as developing training and implementation strategies to ensure the new technology improves overall efficiency.</div> UHR-Learning & Development https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478520 2026-04-22T17:25:27-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:28-04:00 Temporary Research Garden Assistant - Griffin <div>Plant and maintain annual flower beds. Water container gardens and around the Research and Education Garden. Mow grass when needed.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488831 2026-06-16T16:44:33-04:00 2026-06-16T16:44:34-04:00 Lab Tech-Medical Science II <div>This role is responsible for the organization and implementation of research projects including data collection, assay development, execution, and project management. These projects may entail laboratory and/or clinical research. Individuals in this position operate as part of a team of departmental technicians serving a large department of faculty researchers. Project specific duties will vary with individual principal investigator and project. This role’s primary responsibility is to work in the lab, although light animal work (restraint, medicating, assessing) may be required.</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478618 2026-04-22T17:33:35-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:35-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research - Bahri, Griffin Conduct laboratory, greenhouse and field work including making media, culturing fungi, extracting DNA, conducting PCR, planting seed, collecting data. CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494987 2026-07-21T17:07:20-04:00 2026-07-21T17:07:20-04:00 Associate Director of Education <div>The Associate Director of Education is a non-tenure-track Public Service Faculty position responsible for strategic leadership and operational oversight of the Marine Education Center and Aquarium. The role oversees daily operations, including supervision of faculty and staff, facilities, vessels, and vehicles, while ensuring compliance with institutional policies and effective budget administration.</div><div>This position serves on the Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant leadership team and leads the design, delivery, and evaluation of marine education and outreach programs aligned with unit priorities and National Sea Grant initiatives. The position fosters collaboration across university units, government agencies, and external stakeholders, and represents the organization at professional and public forums.</div><div>Additional responsibilities include guiding strategic planning, supporting development initiatives, securing external funding, and integrating education initiatives across multiple locations. The position requires demonstrated expertise in informal education leadership, program development, and team management, along with strong communication skills and a deep understanding of coastal and marine issues, particularly those relevant to Georgia’s coast.</div><div>This is an administrative, non-tenured public service faculty appointment in the public service faculty career ladder at the University of Georgia. The successful candidate will be appointed at the rank of Public Service Assistant Associate, or Senior Public Service Associate. For information about the requirements for each rank, please see Guidelines for Appointments and Promotion (<a href=\"http://outreach.uga.edu/policies/appointment-and-promotion-guidelines/\"><strong>http://outreach.uga.edu/policies/appointment-and-promotion-guidelines/</strong></a>).</div> PSO-Marine Extension Service https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477828 2026-04-21T17:58:11-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:12-04:00 Food Service Worker - Camp Jekyll, 4-H This role involves manual and semi-skilled routine work in the performance of food service duties. Employees apply skills and knowledge that are acquired through experience. This work involves the preparation and service of food and the cleaning and sanitation of equipment and facilities. Duties include cooking and preparing food, safety and sanitation techniques involving methods of maintaining high standards of cleanliness, food quality and presentation; and for assuring that patrons are served in a pleasant and courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained. This position reports to the 4-H Dining Commons Manager. CAES-Jekyll Island https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501736 2026-08-21T00:01:29-04:00 2026-08-21T00:01:30-04:00 Events Specialist <div>The Events Specialist position reports to the Assistant Director for the Gwinnett Campus and is responsible for providing logistical support for UGA and non-UGA educational activities (academic, continuing education, community, and corporate) on weekdays and Saturdays. This position serves as campus scheduler in the 25Live system and assists with the DSX door lock system.<br><br>This person coordinates UGA physical space maintenance and oversees physical set-up and arrangements for event needs. This position also assists the Assistant Director with planning and organizing on-campus events, conferences, trainings, and student events and orientations; provides IT/AV support for students, faculty, staff, and outside organizations utilizing space on the campus; and works closely with staff and faculty in academic departments, Public Service &amp; Outreach units, external partners, and vendors. This position is essential tothe campus's day-to-day operations, especially on Saturdays.</div> VPI-Gwinnett Graduate Programs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478500 2026-04-22T17:24:10-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:10-04:00 Lifeguard - Rock Eagle- Temporary <div>This is an “as needed” position responsible for monitoring the safety and wellbeing of guest as they use the pools at Rock Eagle.<br><br></div><ul><li>Rock Eagle pools are open based on group reservations. The pools are open sporadically and you will not have the same schedule week to week. You will receive your schedule 3 weeks in advance and will have 1 week to contact me with any conflicts.</li><li>Pools can be reserved any time from 8am-10pm</li><li>As a lifeguard your primary responsibility will be to supervise pool activity. In addition to lifeguarding, you will be responsible for obtaining the pool keys to open the pool and returning them at the end of your shift. You will be expected to keep the pool storage closets clean and organized. You may be asked to sweep off the pool deck or clean up trash around the pool before pool use.</li></ul> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486916 2026-06-04T12:26:11-04:00 2026-06-04T12:26:12-04:00 Research Associate II- Norris <div>Independently performs components of a research program as directed by a senior member of the research team. Involvement in designing certain aspects of research projects as needed. Independently conducts work complementary to the overall research objectives. Participate in training staff in laboratory procedures as needed.</div> VetMed-Vaccines & Immun Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478595 2026-04-22T17:32:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:25-04:00 Temporary Lab/Field Assistant Assist in running soil and water analysis and field sample collection. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494322 2026-07-17T13:54:23-04:00 2026-07-17T13:54:23-04:00 Supervision Coordinator – Limited Term <div>The Supervision Coordinator supports and coordinates the Elementary program in the Department of Educational Theory and Practice (ETAP) with an emphasis on university supervision and clinical practice. Ensures effective onboarding, assignment, support, and evaluation of university supervisors while maintaining compliance with ETAP, COE, and GAPSC guidance. Manages program documentation, systems, and partnerships to support high‑quality supervision experiences for teacher candidates.<br><br><strong><em>This position has a limited-term appointment, which is expected to end June 30, 2027.&nbsp; The position may be extended beyond the initial term, contingent upon continued funding.</em></strong></div> COE-Educational Theory & Pract https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477777 2026-04-21T17:34:02-04:00 2026-04-21T17:34:02-04:00 LVT - SA, 24/7 Care <div>The Licensed Veterinary Technician (LVT) position is responsible for providing animal nursing care within the Small Animal Emergency Critical Care unit of the Veterinary Teaching Hospital. This position is skilled in all facets of veterinary animal care regarding patient assessment, emergency triage procedures, surgery preparation and patient case management. This position involves handling patients in life threatening situations where the following duties involved in triage of accident patients includes: CPR, Collection of blood, urine by expression, cystocentesis or catheterization, Administration and application of anesthesia, drugs, fluids, medications and immunological agents by oral, parenteral and injectable routes and utilization of computer systems to enter and maintain medical record keeping. The LVT will need to professionally communicate with Veterinarians, students and fellow technicians concerning the affected workflow, time limitations and patient status and will maintain a positive attitude and calm demeanor throughout stressful situations.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Animal Emerg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478718 2026-04-22T17:40:28-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:29-04:00 Temporary Field/Lab Assistant - Mergoum <div>Help with the planting and harvesting of the wheat breeding nursery in North and South Georgia. Will also help with the upkeep of six greenhouses and preparing of seed to be replanted in field. Overnight trips and working 8 hours in the heat of the summer.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497775 2026-08-04T12:12:05-04:00 2026-08-04T12:12:06-04:00 Open Rank - Assistant, Associate or Full Professor <div>The University of Georgia announces an opening for a tenure track faculty member at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level in the Complex Carbohydrate Research Center (CCRC; www.ccrc.uga.edu) in the area of plant and/or microbial glycoscience. We seek outstanding scientists whose research complements or expands our existing strengths in the CCRC and fosters a team science atmosphere that can benefit from our cutting-edge NMR, Mass Spectrometry, Computational, and Structural Biology infrastructure. Successful candidates will have access to a robust graduate student training program (partially supported by an NIH training grant in Glycoscience), highly motivated undergraduate trainees, and the opportunity to participate in education at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, and will be expected to build or maintain a vibrant, extramurally-funded research program that leverages the highly collaborative research environment at the CCRC and UGA.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The CCRC is home to the DOE Center for Plant and Microbial Complex Carbohydrates, the NSF-funded BioF-GREAT BioFoundry, the Network for Advanced NMR (NAN), and the NIH-funded T32 Glycoscience Training Program. The CCRC also plays a leading role in the DOE-funded Center for Bioenergy Innovation (CBI) and is the home of GLYGEN, GLYCAM, and the leadership for the 5th edition of Essentials of Glycobiology. The above are national resources for the study of complex carbohydrates from plants, microbes, and animals and the successful candidate will be expected to utilize and expand such resources through collaborative research efforts.<br><br>An attractive start-up package with highly competitive conditions of employment will be offered.&nbsp;</div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478078 2026-04-21T18:30:58-04:00 2026-04-21T18:30:59-04:00 Lowndes County Ag & Natural Resources Agent <div>This County Extension Agent position is responsible for managing the Agricultural and Natural Resources program in the county. By providing educational opportunities in farm production, livestock, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods. Agriculture is diverse in Lowndes County with top commodities including citrus production, tobacco and miscellaneous nuts and fruits. With large metropolitan areas, Lowndes County depends on the Extension ANR agent for horticulture, turf, landscape industry, and homeowner calls as well as small farm enterprises and a Master Gardener program. It serves as a UGA Public Service Faculty. It is under the direction and leadership of the County Extension Coordinator and the Southwest District Extension Director.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br><a href=\"http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm\"><strong>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</strong></a></div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504181 2026-09-02T12:30:58-04:00 2026-09-02T12:30:59-04:00 Student Assistant - Dr. Dunn <div>Undergraduate Laboratory work for Dr. Dunn's lab.</div> CAES-Food Science & Technology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500612 2026-08-17T15:37:58-04:00 2026-08-17T15:37:59-04:00 Academic Records and Credentialing Coordinator <div>The Academic Records and Credentialing Coordinator supports and coordinates essential School of Medicine Registrar functions related to student registration, academic records, enrollment status, grades, graduation related process, and student credentialing across the MD program. The Coordinator manages credentialing workflows; supports students to ensure readiness for enrollment and entry to clinical sites; tracks completion of institutional and clinical site credentialing requirements; maintains accurate and confidential records; and serves as a primary contact related to academic records and credentialing for students and clinical partners. Success in the role requires exceptional accuracy, organization, discretion, customer service, and the ability to manage multiple time-sensitive processes across student cohorts, systems, and partner organizations.</div><div>The Coordinator reports to the Registrar for the School of Medicine, and works closely with other roles such as the Director of Medical Education, Assistant Dean for Clerkship Curriculum, Clerkship and Elective Coordinators, Clinical Site and Faculty Relations Coordinator, Clinical Skills and Simulation team, Community and Population Health team, and healthcare system partners. The Coordinator is ultimately responsible to the Associate Dean for Curriculum for the duties attached to the role.</div> SOM-UME https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478422 2026-04-22T17:20:08-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:08-04:00 Research Associate <div>This position will serve as a field-based project coordinator of a long-term research project focused on assessing white-tailed deer movements relative to flooding and chronic wasting disease (CWD) in northeastern Louisiana. The successful candidate will coordinate and conduct field research on-site in northeastern Louisiana, where CWD is established and of significant management concern to agencies and landowners. The candidate will be primarily responsible for coordinating and conducting field research that will involve capture of adult and juvenile white-tailed deer using various capture techniques (e.g., rocket nets, free darting), immobilization of captured animals, monitoring of captured animals via radio telemetry, investigating related mortality events, and running the day-to-day operations of a field crew including a technician and intermittent support from other personnel. The applicant will also assist in managing databases, summarizing data, and preparing technical reports and presentations to disseminate the results of the research. The candidate will serve as the primary point of contact for state agency personnel within the study area, as well as private landowners, and others with questions or concerns about the field research. Likewise, the candidate will serve as the liaison between field research activities and principal investigators in the Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources at the University of Georgia.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/481015 2026-05-05T09:41:31-04:00 2026-05-05T09:41:32-04:00 Law School Fellow <div>The Fellow will support the mission of the Jane W. Wilson Family Justice Clinic as determined by the Director including representing low-income victims of domestic violence and stalking in emergency protective order proceedings and other domestic relations matters, supervision of law students representing clients under the Student Practice Act, and community outreach and education. This is a 2-year position, with the second year dependent on performance and funding.</div> Law School-General https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478543 2026-04-22T17:26:07-04:00 2026-07-22T12:40:04-04:00 Grounds Keeper - Student <div>Maintain the grounds and commons areas for Athletic facilities.</div> Athletics-Grounds https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490729 2026-06-30T10:25:46-04:00 2026-06-30T10:25:47-04:00 Assistant Director, Equal Opportunity Office <div>The Assistant Director assists the Director in ensuring the University provides a fair and respectful environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors that is free from discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected categories. The Assistant Director conducts investigations of complaints of harassment, discrimination, and sexual misconduct. At the direction of the Director, the Assistant Director will assist in providing analysis and guidance with respect to all institutional compliance efforts with federal and state laws and regulations addressing discrimination and harassment as well as with University System of Georgia and UGA non-discrimination and anti-harassment policies, including the development of policies and procedures governing the reporting, investigation and adjudication of claims of discrimination, harassment, and sexual misconduct. The Assistant Director assists in educating the University community about discrimination and harassment.<br><br><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Law degree (JD) from an American Bar Association, accredited law school, and a member in good standing of a state bar association.</li><li>Two years of progressive experience in the legal or compliance field.</li></ul> EOO-Equal Opportunity Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478638 2026-04-22T17:34:11-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:12-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Terns <div>Perform NIH-funded research in the area of CRISPR and anti-CRISPR biology.</div> Franklin-Biochemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496399 2026-07-28T08:51:04-04:00 2026-07-28T08:51:04-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Crop Design <div>The University of Georgia invites applications for three open rank tenure-track faculty positions in Crop Design. This is part of a strategic cluster hire aimed at building world-leading capacity in rational crop redesign for climate resilience, yield, sustainability and profit. All positions will be part of a nascent Institute of Crop Design, and departmental homes will be determined by the successful candidate’s research foci and include Crop and Soil Sciences, Plant Pathology, and Horticulture. We seek candidates in three broad areas:</div><ol><li>Cutting-edge AI, machine-learning, and computational modeling in combination with quantitative genetics to enable predictive crop design. Priority areas include:<ol><li>AI-guided prediction of genome-editing outcomes and genotype-to-phenotype mapping</li><li>Design and optimization of synthetic genetic circuits using multi-omics integration</li><li>Development of digital-twin or in silico models for crop performance under stress</li><li>High-throughput computational frameworks for trait engineering in major crops</li></ol></li><li>Advanced Genome Engineering for Crops. This position will strengthen UGA’s synthetic biology capacity to engineer novel genetic circuits, metabolic pathways, and traits in agriculturally important species.<ol><li>Development of synthetic promoters, biosensors, orthogonal systems, or genetic circuits</li><li>Advanced genome-editing technologies (e.g., base/prime editing, multiplex CRISPR, large-scale knockouts)</li><li>Protein engineering at scale (e.g., high-throughput enzyme screening, AI-guided protein design)</li><li>Metabolic pathway refactoring and biosynthetic engineering in crops</li><li>High-throughput genetic engineering pipelines for trait improvement (yield, nutrient efficiency, stress tolerance, or bio-manufacturing)</li></ol></li><li>Integrative Crop Design and Translational Synthetic Biology. We seek an established leader who integrates AI, advanced genome engineering, genetics, and synthetic biology to redesign crops for sustainable, high-performance agriculture. Priority will be given to candidates with:<ol><li>A track record of large-scale genome design, synthetic chromosome engineering, or systems-level trait stacking</li><li>Experience translating fundamental discoveries into applied crop varieties or technologies</li><li>Expertise in building interdisciplinary teams that bridge AI, genetics, and genetic engineering</li><li>Vision for industry partnerships and real-world deployment of engineered crops</li></ol></li></ol><div>All position appointments are 75% research, 20% teaching, and 5% service.</div> CAES-Assoc Dean for Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477885 2026-04-21T18:04:02-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:03-04:00 LVT - Ophthalmology <div>As a member of the Ophthalmology service, you will be performing quality medicine at its highest levels and standards while running and maintaining advanced equipment associated with these procedures. Technicians in these positions are essential in the organization of the service and patient care, assisting with examinations, specimen collection, diagnostic procedures, treatments, anesthesia, and surgeries on small and large animals. Will be part of a team training and guiding fourth year veterinary students, interns and residents, as well as veterinary technician students on their path towards a professional career in veterinary medicine.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Anim Spc Srvc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503393 2026-08-28T10:38:11-04:00 2026-08-28T10:38:12-04:00 Temporary Technician (Beasley) <div>The selected candidate(s) will support several research efforts based out of the University of Georgia’s Savannah River Ecology Laboratory (SREL): 1) the development and field testing of lures to improve wild pig trapping efficiency, 2) the evaluation of Forward Looking Infrared (FLIR) thermal technology to improve the efficacy and efficiency of aerial removal operations, 3) estimation of wild pig populations using remote cameras, and 4) attaching GPS collars to elucidate the movement ecology of wild pigs. Opportunities also may exist to assist with research evaluating the spatial ecology and population dynamics of white-tailed deer. Primary duties will include collecting and processing data evaluating performance of wild pig attractants, operating remote camera arrays, assisting with data collection and logistical coordination for FLIR-guided aerial operations across study sites in the Southeast, wild pig capture and handling for attachment of GPS collars, and video/image processing.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499581 2026-08-12T13:20:56-04:00 2026-08-12T13:20:57-04:00 Executive Assistant <div>This incumbent provides executive-level support to the Dean of the Mary Frances Early College of Education and is responsible for efficient and effective management of the office. Administrative duties include managing the Dean’s correspondence and calendar, serving as liaison with internal and external constituents, anticipating and addressing needs of the Dean by using independent judgment. Responsibilities involve handling information that is sensitive, high-profile and confidential nature, such as personnel matters and donor information. Activities and decisions are highly complex and require significant independent action and judgment while adhering to institutional policies.</div> COE-Education Dean's Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478379 2026-04-22T17:16:24-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:25-04:00 Student Assistant - Mailhot <div>This is a part-time (up to 20 hours per week) position. The student will be working in the Variety Testing program performing seed lab activities and sometimes field work. This position will report to Dr. Danial Mailhot, Program Director.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478809 2026-04-22T17:46:52-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:53-04:00 Post -Doctoral Associate AD <div>The post-doctorial associate will participate in the Georgia CTSA Translational Workforce Development (TWD) project, working with the Georgia CTSA TWD Directors and faculty, BTSI Director, and UGA Georgia CTSA TWD faculty. The goal of the TWD project is to support career advancement of translational research professionals through a career navigation system (eMPACT, Empowering Purposeful Advancement of Careers and Training in the Research Workforce), and an online continuing education platform (TWD Course Catalog). The postdoctoral associate will work collaboratively to maintain, disseminate, evaluate, and improve eMPACT and TWD Course Catalog to promote personalized training and career advancement, workforce support and retention, and strategic development of training programs to meet the needs of health professionals. The postdoctoral associate will also manage inter-institutional collaboration and communication and other logistics related to end­ user interviews and surveys for the project. This may require regular visits to Emory University. It is expected that the associate will author and contribute to peer-reviewed research, outreach, publications and presentations.<br><br></div> VPR-Biomed & Health Sci Inst https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478620 2026-04-22T17:33:38-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:39-04:00 Night Auditor - Temporary The part-time night auditor will perform an audit of the business day’s transactions.  Audit duties include running all daily reports and checking for accuracy, auditing all payment types, completing all end-of-day reports, and rolling the date to the next business day.  The night auditor will also check in and check out guests, make and confirm reservations, answer all telephone calls and respond to guest requests, serve as manager on duty, enter maintenance work orders, prepare daily shift report, and attend meetings and training sessions.  As the manager on duty, the night auditor will learn the hotel’s fire, health, and safety regulations and be ready to implement these policies and procedures when needed. PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495029 2026-07-22T09:28:02-04:00 2026-07-22T09:28:03-04:00 IT Support Specialist <div>Provide technical support to the Ralston Institute faculty, staff, and students. This position reports to supervisory staff in the Office of Technology and Instructional Services. This includes assisting customers with all aspects of desktop support operations, providing support through telephone, email, Teams, and in-person. Responsible for documenting known problems and solutions in an internal ticketing system.</div> FACS-Ralston Institute https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477831 2026-04-21T17:58:18-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:18-04:00 Administrative Assistant II - Rock Eagle 4-H Center <div>The Administrative Assistant II supports the operations of the maintenance and housekeeping departments by providing high-level administrative and clerical assistance. This role ensures the smooth execution of daily activities, coordinates work orders, maintains records, and facilitates communication between departments to enhance operational efficiency.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502862 2026-08-26T13:30:23-04:00 2026-08-26T13:30:23-04:00 Banquet Captain <div>At the Georgia Center, the Banquet Captain assists the banquet team to create the optimal atmosphere for large events and meetings. The incumbent is responsible for event set-up, running events, helping direct banquet staff, along with maintenance; and the breakdown of meeting and banquet rooms according to department standards. Handling cash/credit cards may be required at times.</div> PSO-Cont Ed-Aux-Food Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478772 2026-04-22T17:43:42-04:00 2026-04-22T17:43:43-04:00 Conservation Genetics Lab and Greenhouse Technician <div>The technician will work with Dr. Bothwell, graduate students, and other research technicians to investigate how adaptations to drought and disease vary across southern pine species and genotypes (loblolly and longleaf). Primary responsibilities will include assisting with growing pine seedlings in the Whitehall Greenhouse, inoculating seedlings with the pathogen Lecanosticta acicola responsible for brown spot needle blight (BSNB), and conducting weekly surveys of disease severity and seedling health. They will also assist in collecting weekly digital scans of roots, and gain experience in using image analysis software to investigate how root architecture, growth, and morphology contribute to forest resilience to drought. They will also have the opportunity to gain experience using LICOR and pressure chambers to measure plant physiological traits (e.g., photosynthesis, stomatal conductance). Students may also develop a research project of their own related to the above study, which could become a Senior Thesis project.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498513 2026-08-06T14:45:03-04:00 2026-08-06T14:45:04-04:00 4-H Carroll County AmeriCorps Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting required impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members must comply with AmeriCorps requirements such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other required trainings.<br><br></div><div>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members are required to log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478224 2026-04-22T10:49:30-04:00 2026-04-22T10:49:31-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant (Lin) VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478792 2026-04-22T17:46:21-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:22-04:00 Facility Rental Assistant <div>The responsibilities of Facility Rental Assistant involve opening and closing facilities for events, overseeing weddings/receptions/meetings etc., assisting occasionally with set up/tear down of events, and interacting with catering and event support staff. Assistant will work both in-house and outside rental events.</div> PSO-State Botanic Garden of GA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504480 2026-09-03T15:57:16-04:00 2026-09-03T15:57:17-04:00 Associate Director of Network and Data Center Operations <div>This position manages the Data Center Operations, Facilities Management, Cellular, and Network Operations teams.&nbsp; This position will also assist in infrastructure projects as needed to complete any related projects and delivery of services.</div> EITS-Data Ctr Ops https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501218 2026-08-19T11:02:02-04:00 2026-08-19T11:02:02-04:00 COOK II <div>This position will be located at the Marine Education Center and Aquarium on Skidaway Island, near Savannah, Ga. The Center provides hands-on, feet-in approach to teaching marine science and coastal ecology field and laboratory education programs. Audience includes PK-12 students and teachers, summer campers, undergraduates, and the public.<br><br></div><div>UGA Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant are units of Public Service and Outreach at the University of Georgia, supporting Georgia’s short- and long-term prosperity.<br><br>This position serves as food prep and service worker for meals ( breakfast, lunch, and dinner) served to student and university groups (up to 80 individuals per meal) participating in education programs at the Marine Education Center and Aquarium. Adheres to set guidelines, policies, and time schedules set by direct supervisor, Chef Manager. Works with a professional and welcoming attitude and adheres to procedures on quality, portion control and presentation and excellent customer service.</div> PSO-Marine Extension Service https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478468 2026-04-22T17:22:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:33-04:00 Camden County 4-H Program Assistant, Part Time <div>The County Extension 4‐H Program Assistant is a para‐professional who works with County Extension Agents to deliver the 4‐H program in their assigned geographic area and performs duties necessary to assist the county extension agents in the day‐to‐day conduct of programs. This employee works cooperatively with all Extension faculty and staff where applicable and is administratively responsible to the County Extension Coordinator and the District Extension Director and programmatically responsible to an assigned County Extension 4‐H Agent.<br><br></div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/485052 2026-05-22T15:25:58-04:00 2026-05-22T15:25:58-04:00 Greene County Agriculture and Natural Resources Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the ANR area in Greene County. This will include managing the Agricultural &amp; Natural Resources program in Greene County by providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods.<br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478571 2026-04-22T17:29:55-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:55-04:00 Temporary Turfgrass Lab/Field Assistant, Griffin <div>Assist researchers with both lab and field experiments conducted on turfgrass, both on and off of the Griffin Campus.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492714 2026-07-10T16:27:28-04:00 2026-07-10T16:27:29-04:00 OPEN Rank - ST SX Emerg Surg 2026 <div>Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery at the College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, invites applications for a clinical (non-tenure) track faculty position in small animal soft animal tissue surgery at the rank of assistant or associate professor.<br><br>The major responsibilities for this position are to teach and provide service in soft tissue surgery in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, teach didactic and laboratory courses in soft tissue surgery to veterinary students, actively participate in training of surgical residents, and to develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. The surgeon filling this position will be responsible for approximately 36 weeks of clinical service. Approximately half of that time the surgeon filling this position will be responsible for daytime emergency and morning transfers on the urgent surgery Service, which also includes supporting the interventional radiology service, and serving as the backup for the standard soft tissue service. This service will be supported by a surgery house officer (resident or intern) and students or technicians. The other half of the time the surgeon will be responsible for participating in the standard appointment-based soft tissue surgery service. Responsibilities during the remaining 16 weeks include opportunities to teach lecture and laboratory courses in soft tissue surgery to veterinary students and the development of scholarly activity consistent with individual interest. Proportionate assignments for each area will be based on the interests of the candidate in conjunction with the missions of the Surgery program and the Department.<br><br>The service enjoys access to vanguard technology in diagnostic imaging, including a 64-slice CT scanner, 3.0 Tesla MRI, digital radiography, ultrasound, nuclear scintigraphy, and a dedicated interventional radiology suite. The Veterinary Teaching Hospital is a 300,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility opened in March 2015. Each specialty has its own dedicated rounds room. Faculty members’ offices and over 5,400 square feet of shared research space are located on the floor above the hospital.<br><br>For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications.&nbsp;</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/28056 2018-07-11T16:28:42-04:00 2018-07-11T16:28:42-04:00 Public Area Attendant This position is responsible for ensuring that all public areas of the Georgia Center remain clean and presentable at all times. PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478680 2026-04-22T17:38:52-04:00 2026-04-22T17:38:53-04:00 Student Assistant (1) - J. Thompson CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497119 2026-07-31T09:29:05-04:00 2026-07-31T09:29:05-04:00 Research Professional I <div>The SMART Pharmacology laboratory (Department of VetMed-Precision One Health) studies how drugs act across biological scales, combining patient-derived organoid models with quantitative pharmacology to advance precision therapeutics for animals and people. The incumbent will keep equipment in proper working order, maintain inventory, prepare stocks and buffers, order supplies, and ensure overall lab organization and safety compliance. They may also maintain and generate animal-derived cell cultures (2D cell lines and 3D organoids). This employee should be very organized and have good communication skills. All work will adhere to standard laboratory practices. Responsibilities may also include data collection, analysis, and interpretation, and presenting research findings to other staff. This will be a one-year term position, with potential for renewal based on performance and availability of funding.</div> VetMed-Precision One Health https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477991 2026-04-21T18:24:57-04:00 2026-04-21T18:24:58-04:00 Business Consultant-Macon <div>Join an environment that has been named by Georgia Trend as a “Best Place to Work”. Our team consist of a well-respected and collaborative group of professionals committed to using their areas of expertise to enhance the economic well-being of the small business community. As a trusted Business Consultant, you will enjoy applying your knowledge to help small business clients reach their goals by providing a wide range of educational and consulting services. We are looking for trusted consultants who have a passion to serve and a desire to make a positive impact in the small business community.<br><br>A Small Business Development Center (SBDC) Business Consultant is a public service faculty position responsible for providing counseling and delivering programs to individuals, businesses, communities, organizations, and other public agencies in their assigned geographic territory. This charge requires a broad base of business knowledge, excellent analytical skills, and the ability to effectively manage multiple projects simultaneously. These duties require the integration of business theory and practice, thus necessitating professional development activities. This position is located in Macon, Georgia. Multi-county travel is required.<br><br>Salary is $80,000 and an excellent benefits package including a defined benefits retirement plan.</div> PSO-Small Business Dev Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503869 2026-09-01T10:45:59-04:00 2026-09-01T10:46:00-04:00 Broadcast Engineer <div>Serve as the primary on-site engineer for UGA Athletics originated broadcasts, SEC Network broadcasts, and video board shows. Responsible for the care, maintenance, and use of the Athletic Association’s Control Rooms at Sanford Stadium and remote broadcast locations, while ensuring proper use of all video equipment, and the video infrastructure connecting the various athletic venues.&nbsp;</div> Athletics-New Media https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500159 2026-08-14T12:27:21-04:00 2026-08-14T12:27:22-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor <div>The J. M. Tull School of Accounting in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant or associate professor rank with primary teaching and research interests in the auditing area. The position will begin in the fall of 2027 with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Tull Sch of Accounting https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478403 2026-04-22T17:19:35-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:35-04:00 Van Operator (Temporary) <div>Transport passengers with registered disabilities in an accessible van to and from various campus locations in accordance with applicable laws and department procedures. Assist passengers entering and exiting the vehicle as necessary. Inspect vehicle before, during, and after shift to ensure vehicle is in proper operating condition. Complete necessary paperwork, including time sheets and vehicle condition reports. Operates other vehicle equipment such as electronic AVL equipment and wheelchair ramps. Applicants submit to drug and alcohol testing by the US Department of Transportation.&nbsp;</div> Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478873 2026-04-23T09:24:06-04:00 2026-04-23T09:24:06-04:00 Part-Time Quitman County Extension Administrative Assistant <div>This County Extension position (part-time – 16 hours/week) in Quitman County will be the primary contact with the public, greet clients, distribute resources, and handle clerical and QuickBooks financial management duties. This role is crucial to the management of the office and success in serving the citizens of the county. This role will be the \"face\" of UGA Extension to the residents in the county.</div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502715 2026-08-26T09:11:54-04:00 2026-08-26T09:11:55-04:00 Trade Shop Apprentice <div>Reporting to the Technical Trades Manager, the Trade Shop Apprentice supports the maintenance, repair, and improvement of University Housing facilities while developing practical skills across multiple skilled trades. Working alongside and under the guidance of HVAC/Refrigeration Mechanics, Electricians, Masons, Painters, and other experienced trades professionals, the apprentice gains hands-on experience and progressively develops the knowledge and technical proficiency needed to perform assigned work with greater independence.<br><br></div><div>This position works in a community housing approximately 9,000 student residents. This position provides a high-level of customer service with a variety of peers, residents and other departmental stakeholders. To uphold the standard of care for a 24-hour, seven-day a week residential program, this position performs periodic duties during weekends and holidays, and it participates in on-call operations.</div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478522 2026-04-22T17:25:31-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:31-04:00 Temporary Turfgrass Assistant - FRS <div>This position is needed provide assistance with the maintenance of Turfgrass Research Field on the UGA Griffin Campus.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/489276 2026-06-22T11:45:57-04:00 2026-06-22T11:45:57-04:00 Research Associate IV - Data Strategy <div>This senior-level position within the Carl Vinson Institute of Government supports the Institute’s growing portfolio of data strategy, governance, organizational improvement, and applied research initiatives for higher education, government, and public sector partners. The position serves as an accomplished and experienced professional researcher who conducts significant applied research and technical assistance activities and may serve as a senior collaborator or co-investigator on funded projects and multi-disciplinary initiatives under the general guidance of Institute leadership.<br><br>The role provides strategic consultation and technical assistance related to enterprise data strategy, organizational data management, analytics, governance practices, and operational effectiveness. The position collaborates with campus leaders, technical professionals, and partner organizations to support data-informed decision-making, strengthen organizational processes, and advance strategic initiatives. Responsibilities include project leadership, partner engagement, applied research support, strategic consultation, training development and delivery, and collaboration across cross-functional teams and external stakeholders. The role also contributes to the continued growth and sustainability of the Institute’s technical assistance, applied research, and professional development services related to data strategy and governance.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478381 2026-04-22T17:16:28-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:28-04:00 Student Assistant - Czarnota <div>This position will assist faculty and staff with greenhouse, research and field plots. As well as help with extension and teaching activities. This position will work both indoors and outdoors with minimum supervision. There will also be some work in a greenhouse environment. Duties may also include intermittent out-of-town travel to research plots. Computer experience with word processing, spread sheet, and graphics software is a plus.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478813 2026-04-22T17:49:46-04:00 2026-04-22T17:49:47-04:00 Student Assistant - Golf Maintenance The role of a golf course maintenance employee is to assist with the daily maintenance and preparation of the golf course in order to provide the best possible playing conditions to the patrons of the UGA Golf Course. Auxiliary University Golf Cour https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501876 2026-08-21T10:50:22-04:00 2026-08-21T10:50:22-04:00 IT Manager <div>This is a specialized, highly responsible position with a broad understanding of information technologies in the modern enterprise environment. The position plans, implements and develops information technology strategies for Grady College. The position also designed information systems by setting parameters that include budgetary decisions as well as manages implementation of large, complex technology projects. Tactically, the person in the position will be capable of triaging technical issues, reconciling competing priorities, communicating effectively demonstrating exceptional customer service, exhibiting the capacity to independently research, assess and adapt to changing technologies and supervise a staff of IT professionals.</div> Grady-Information Tech Service https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478504 2026-04-22T17:24:17-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:18-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator – Rock Eagle <div>This job is a temporary Environmental Educator at Rock Eagle 4-H Center located in Eatonton, Georgia. The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include life and earth science, ecology, team building, outdoor skills, and living history. Other responsibilities include animal care, maintenance of teaching areas and resources, facilities, grounds, and support of general operations of the facility.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487320 2026-06-08T11:01:16-04:00 2026-06-08T11:01:17-04:00 Director for Enrollment and Student Affairs <div>The Director for Enrollment and Student Affairs serves as a senior administrative leader responsible for the strategic direction, development, and oversight of enrollment management and student affairs functions for the University of Georgia School of Nursing. This role leads the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of services and programs that support student recruitment, admissions, retention, progression, and the overall student experience.<br><br></div><div>Reporting directly to the Founding Dean, the Director provides leadership in building a high-performing, student-centered infrastructure during the school’s formative years. The position is responsible for establishing and leading core functional areas, including admissions, enrollment management, academic advising, and student affairs, and for developing staff and systems to support a growing School of Nursing.<br><br></div> SON-Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478599 2026-04-22T17:32:31-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:32-04:00 Graduate Assistant Warnell-USGS/GA F & W Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494459 2026-07-20T09:28:57-04:00 2026-07-20T09:28:57-04:00 OUA Budgets and Capital Expenditures Business Professional (Limited-Term) <div>This position provides secondary support to the Manager OUA Budgets and Capital Expenditures for procurement, contracting, and financial transactions related to OUA planning, design, and construction projects; on average, this is around $900M per year. The employee will understand UGA, BOR, and GSFIC policies, processes, and procedures, and be able to understand the larger vision while also following through on precise details. The position requires the ability to communicate well, be customer service oriented, and interact with OUA Project Managers as well as business managers across campus, procurement, legal affairs, and BOR Real Estate and Facilities staff, etc. The employee will obtain chartstrings and document fund sources, reconcile budgets, and/or assist with reconciling complex budgets with multiple and varied funding sources and spend down requirements. The employee will process various financial transactions and resolve related issues. <br><br><strong>This position has a limited appointment term, which is expected to end two years after the start date. This appointment may be extended if the volume &amp; complexity of projects continue to be high.</strong></div> F&A-University Architects https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477804 2026-04-21T17:50:25-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:25-04:00 RESEARCH PROFESSIONAL I Technical and professional responsibilities associated with this position include field and laboratory research and diagnostics related to wildlife health. Included will be both the supervision of others doing this work and active participation in completing these tasks. Also included, is the supervisory responsibility of field and laboratory equipment maintenance (equipment and supplies) and assuring that all safety and regulatory requirements are met. Precise records are required. Assistance in planning and selection of sampling and diagnostic approaches related to research projects and diagnostic samples, including assistance with both grant and manuscript preparation, also will be required. Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478720 2026-04-22T17:40:32-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:32-04:00 Temporary Technician (Lance) <div>This is a technician position at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory (SREL). The incumbent(s) is/are responsible for assisting current University of Georgia graduate students with field and laboratory research. The technician will be assisting with ecotoxicological research on amphibians and/or snakes, which will require trapping and handling in the field, setting up and maintaining mesocosm experiments, data collection/entry, and assisting with the metal analysis of tissues. The technician will also assist with some other ongoing projects such as amphibian population monitoring to include collection and analysis of environmental DNA, reviewing camera trap footage, and acoustic recording device files.<br><br></div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497836 2026-08-04T14:50:33-04:00 2026-08-04T14:50:33-04:00 Business Manager I <div>This position works in two main areas: Managing post-award financial accounting for faculty in the department and assisting the department Business Manager II for a variety of specialized accounting, administrative and customer service functions. Activities and decisions are varied in nature, with independent action, excellent judgement, confidential treatment, and professional demeanor. This role serves as the primary contact for questions regarding financial policies and procedures, travel related questions, and reimbursement requests.<br><br>The position is responsible for accurate data entry and will process financial transactions including travel authorizations and reimbursements, expense reports, UGAMart procurement requisitions, invoice payments, payment requests, journal vouchers and cash deposits in an efficient and accurate manner. Unusual cases or questionable matters are resolved with this position’s supervisor. This position will assist faculty and staff located on the UGA Athens campus as well as personnel in other areas of Georgia. Staff members are expected to demonstrate flexibility with scheduling to ensure the office will remain open and operational during normal business hours and to provide assistance to others to meet broader departmental needs as needed.<br><br>This position will work under the direct supervision of the Business Manager II and will work closely with the Department Head.</div> FACS-Human Devel & Family Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478084 2026-04-21T18:31:13-04:00 2026-04-21T18:31:14-04:00 Dodge County ANR Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) area in the county providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods. County stakeholders rely heavily on the County Agent. Homeowners and Master Gardner Volunteers also depend on the Agent’s expertise to provide training and programming to the citizens of the community. Top commodities in the county are cotton, timber and peanuts.<br><br></div><div>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504206 2026-09-02T13:49:55-04:00 2026-09-02T13:49:55-04:00 Laboratory Technician I <div>Position is located in the PDRC Diagnostic Laboratory and deals with formalin fixed tissues from the poultry industry and requires laboratory skills that promote turn-around time for diagnostic test and research results.</div> VetMed-Poultry Diagnos & Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500635 2026-08-17T16:05:42-04:00 2026-08-17T16:05:43-04:00 Private Lands Engineer - IRIS (Virginia) <div>The University of Georgia (UGA) is seeking applications for a <strong>Private Lands Engineer</strong> (Water Resources) to support implementation of the Working Lands for Wildlife (WLFW) Aquatics Connectivity Framework. This project is a collaboration between UGA and the USDA Natural Resources Conservation Service (NRCS) WLFW program. This position will serve as a key implementation lead and primary point of contact for the Regional WLFW Southern Waters Framework in Virginia, will be responsible for developing and implementing multi agency and NRCS workshops within the state, will engage in regional coordination aligned with broader program goals, and will serve as a key engineering resource for Virginia NRCS state leadership.<br><br></div><div>Through the Farm Bill, NRCS provides technical and financial assistance to farmers, ranchers, and forestland owners/managers who voluntarily undertake conservation practices on working lands. WLFW systematically targets conservation efforts to enhance wildlife habitat on agricultural landscapes while improving agricultural and forest productivity. Hellbenders face many threats from conventional agricultural practices that lead to loss of forested riparian habitat and degraded water quality from sedimentation and pollutants.<br><br>This high-level Staff position will be under the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS), at the College of Engineering’s School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering (ECAM). The successful incumbent(s) will join a multidisciplinary team of engineers, scientists and designers at the University of Georgia who are engaged in collaborations between IRIS and the USDA, other universities, and private sector partners. These projects are highly specialized due to the incorporation of natural infrastructure systems and nature-based solutions.<br><br>The successful incumbent will collaborate in an interdisciplinary environment and will lead, conceptualize and implement high-quality and high-impact engineering research and/or design projects through extensive knowledge and experience of environmental/civil engineering (or related discipline) for successful project delivery. <br><br>A successful applicant must be a licensed Professional Engineer in Virginia or demonstrate sufficient experience and education to obtain licensure.<del><br></del><br><strong>This position will be based out of Virginia, in the Abingdon area. Daily duties will be conducted remotely, in the NRCS field office, and on project sites throughout the area. </strong><br><br><strong>This is a grant-funded position. Continuation of employment is contingent upon the continuation of funding sources. </strong><br><br></div> ENGR-Resilient Infrast Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478424 2026-04-22T17:20:11-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:12-04:00 Temporary Food Service Worker - Burton 4-H Center <ul><li>Work involves routine food preparation, food service and cleaning the food service and eating areas.</li><li>Employees work under direct supervision while involved in the preparation, serving and cleaning.</li><li>Employee follows written and/or oral procedures and practices especially as related to safety and food safety.</li><li>Employee implements procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</li><li>This position reports to the 4-H Dining Commons Manager.</li></ul> CAES-Burton 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/481253 2026-05-05T16:53:17-04:00 2026-05-05T16:53:18-04:00 Open rank - Internal Medicine Faculty <div>The College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, invites applications for clinical track (non-tenure track), tenure track, or tenured faculty positions in small animal internal medicine at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor.<br><br>The major responsibilities for this position are to teach and provide service in small animal internal medicine in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, teach didactic and laboratory courses related to internal medicine topics to veterinary students, actively participate in the training of residents and interns, and develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. Proportionate assignments for each area will be based on the candidate's interests in conjunction with the missions of the internal medicine program and the Department. The service enjoys access to vanguard technology, including an endoscopy suite with a complement of endoscopic equipment, Ho:YAG laser, electrosurgical resectoscope, a new Somatom Definition Edge 128 slice CT by Siemens, 3.0 Tesla MRI, digital radiography, ultrasound, nuclear scintigraphy, full laboratory support, and a dedicated interventional radiology suite with a ceiling mounted Canon Alphenix c-arm. The Veterinary Teaching Hospital is a 300,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility where each specialty has its own dedicated rounds room.<br><br>For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant's experience and qualifications.</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478548 2026-04-22T17:26:16-04:00 2026-04-22T17:26:17-04:00 Developing Pathways Intern <div>Previous coursework in environment or natural resource management preferred.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490957 2026-07-01T10:33:26-04:00 2026-07-01T10:33:26-04:00 Animal Caretaker <div>This work involves the cleaning and maintenance of patient facilities in the Vet Teaching Hospital. This includes removing manure and soiled shavings/bedding in patient stalls and kennels. Discharged patient stalls are also cleaned and disinfected. In specific areas of the hospital, floors are swept vacuumed and hosed clean. New patient stalls are prepared as directed by Lead Caretaker or Supervisor. Various other facilities of the hospital in both large and small animal are also cleaned and maintained on a regular basis. Assistance is also given to DVM's, Technicians, and Students where appropriate and requested.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478640 2026-04-22T17:34:15-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:15-04:00 Ruter - Technician <div>This position supports Dr. John Ruter’s ornamental plant breeding and development program, as well as assists with teaching and/or Extension duties as required. The position is grant funded and employment past one year will be dependent upon additional funding.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496422 2026-07-28T10:53:24-04:00 2026-07-28T10:53:25-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>The Jing Li Lab (https://jinglilab.com) in the Department of Chemistry at the University of Georgia is seeking two highly motivated postdoctoral researchers to join our team. These are fully funded positions focused on applying molecular dynamics simulations, computational biophysics, and artificial intelligence–based approaches to investigate the molecular mechanisms and pharmacology of ion channels and membrane transporters.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidates will study how structural and functional alterations in these membrane proteins contribute to human disease and will help develop computational strategies for therapeutic discovery and drug design.<br><br></div><div>Our group provides a collaborative, team-oriented research environment with extensive opportunities for scientific mentorship, interdisciplinary collaboration, professional development, and career advancement.</div> Franklin-Chemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477893 2026-04-21T18:04:21-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:22-04:00 Baker <div>This is skilled work in baking pastries and bread in a dining hall, snack bar, cafeteria, or campus eateries. Work involves responsibility for baking a variety of pastries and bread and for assuring proper quality and quantity. Duties may include supervision and/or instruction of food service workers assigned to assist in baking activities and in cleaning equipment and facilities. Assignments are determined from menus and the employee has some judgement in applying baking skills and knowledge. Work is normally performed under the supervision of a food service supervisor and is reviewed for quality, economy and volume of output.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503496 2026-08-28T14:50:25-04:00 2026-08-28T14:50:26-04:00 Academic Advisor I <div>The Academic Advisor I position within UGA’s College of Engineering supports incoming and current Engineering undergraduate students in their academic pursuits. The <strong>Academic Advisor I </strong>position:<br><br></div><ul><li>Effectively facilitates one-on-one advising sessions with students pursuing majors within the College of Engineering.</li><li>Understands requirements, policies, procedures, and the use of student-facing technologies (Degree Works, SAGE, Athena, etc.).</li><li>Provides general support related to student decision-making, exploration, and development.</li><li>Makes basic referrals based on individual students’ situations, needs, and interests.</li><li>Considers students’ degree progress, interests, and abilities when providing advisement to students</li><li>Demonstrates professionalism and clarity in communications to students, staff, faculty, and others within and outside the college.</li><li>Maintains accurate records by following policies and procedures instituted by the college.</li><li>Demonstrates knowledge of university and degree requirements</li><li>Understands basic advising practice and how it is related to some aspects of student development.</li><li>Engages effectively with members of the home unit or department</li></ul><div><br></div><div>As an ENGR advisor, you will play a vital role in supporting students with various professional and academic experiences.</div><div><br></div><div>The Advisor I role will involve understanding the unique challenges and needs of these groups, offering guidance, and fostering an inclusive environment that enhances their academic and personal success. The Academic Advisor I will provide tailored resources and advocacy to help students navigate their educational journeys and reach their goals.<br><br></div><div>The primary function of all Academic Advisor positions in the College of Engineering is to administer student support to enrolled and prospective students while working collaboratively with other Academic Advisors and staff throughout the College of Engineering and across campus. In addition, Academic Advisors must stay abreast of current degree program procedures, policies, and curriculum requirements and of UGA-wide policies and procedures for UGA employees and Academic Advisors specifically. College of Engineering Academic Advisors will follow all UGA Academic Advising Services requirements and are encouraged to continue their professional learning through their learning and development resources and best practices.</div><div>The College of Engineering offers BS, MS, and PhD degree programs through four schools – School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering, School of Computing, School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, and School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering. For further details on our offered degrees and programs, please visit <a href=\"https://engineering.uga.edu/degrees-programs/\"><strong>https://engineering.uga.edu/degrees-programs/</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>The College of Engineering is a rapidly growing Engineering college at a flagship public university. Since its founding in 2012, UGA’s College of Engineering has added multiple new degree programs, increased its enrollment to over 2,700 undergraduate and 300 graduate students, employs over 200 Faculty, Staff and Post-Doctoral Associates, and has had a 300% increase in research funding in the last 5 years.<br><br></div><div>This position will report directly to the College of Engineering Director of Advising and is expected to manage a caseload of approximately 275-305 advisees. The Academic Advisor I position will work with other Academic Advisor I, II, and III Advisors, both independently and collaboratively as part of the college Advising team.</div> ENGR-Experiential Prg & Outrea https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499704 2026-08-12T16:28:39-04:00 2026-08-12T16:28:40-04:00 Director of Student Affairs <div>The Director of Student Affairs provides leadership and support for law students by promoting student success, well-being, and engagement throughout their academic experience. This position serves as a primary resource for students facing personal, academic, financial, or health-related challenges and coordinates access to university support services and accommodations. The Director oversees the administration of student accommodations, supervises staff, and advises student organizations. The role also manages the law school's mentorship program, fostering meaningful connections among students, alumni, faculty, and legal professionals. Additionally, the Director plans and executes student orientation programs and supports key community-building and ceremonial events.</div> Law School-General https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478622 2026-04-22T17:33:42-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:42-04:00 IT Assistant  Summer Student  #2 This position is need for summer to help with helpdesk support, website edits, and various projects. OGE-Assoc Provost's Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495103 2026-07-22T12:23:39-04:00 2026-07-22T12:23:40-04:00 4-H Burke County AmeriCorps State Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps State member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members should comply with AmeriCorps guidelines such as monthly reporting, monthly webinars, and other trainings.<br><br></div><div>This posting is for a part-time member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members will log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477835 2026-04-21T17:58:27-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:28-04:00 Trades Helper - Rock Eagle 4-H Center <div>This is semi-skilled work assisting skilled workers in the performance of duties related to electrical, plumbing, air conditioning, heating, and other building trades work.<br><br>This position includes managing two pool areas including pool chemicals, trash pick-up across the center, cleaning culverts, pressure washing, window cleaning, waxing and mopping floors, responding to work orders, and assisting other team members across the center.<br><br>This position includes obtaining a Certified Pool Operator (CPO) certification. This includes servicing pumps, maintaining and repairing pool systems, and cleaning pools.<br><br>This position will be a member of the maintenance department. All maintenance team members assist with responding to work orders, general maintenance, and assisting with emergency repairs across the 4-H center.<br><br>Hours will vary with groups on center. Evening and weekend rotations are required.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503020 2026-08-26T16:19:45-04:00 2026-08-26T16:19:45-04:00 Histology Technician <div>This position will be based in the Histology Lab of the Department of Pathology in the College of Veterinary Medicine. The main responsibilities will include routine histology to include trimming diagnostic lab biopsy cases. In addition, this position will serve as a backup for the Necropsy Lab in the Athens Veterinary Diagnostic Lab.</div> VetMed-Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478781 2026-04-22T17:43:58-04:00 2026-04-22T17:43:58-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate – Vilgalys Evolutionary Immunogenomics Lab <div>The Evolutionary Immunogenomics Lab (PI: Dr. Tauras Vilgalys) at the University of Georgia, Department of Genetics is looking for a highly motivated and independent individual to work as a Postdoctoral Associate.<br><br></div><div>Our goal is to discover how natural populations resist infectious diseases and use those insights to improve human health. Projects in the lab combine high throughput functional genomics, bioinformatics, and <em>in vitro </em>experimental systems to address questions related to primate evolution, host-pathogen evolution, and gene-by-environment interactions. The successful candidate will contribute to project design and pursue projects that integrate functional, evolutionary, and/or immuno-genomic approaches.<br><br></div><div>This position is for a post-PhD trainee preparing for a research scientist career path. The planned position will provide a transition to career independence through the development of professional skills; supervision by senior scientist incorporating individual development plan in support of training goals and those of faculty mentor; and publication of research findings/scholarship during postdoc appointment period. For appropriate projects, the candidate may have the opportunity to mentor junior scientists in the lab.</div><div><br><br></div> Franklin-Genetics https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498691 2026-08-07T13:49:17-04:00 2026-08-07T13:49:18-04:00 Application Analyst Principal <div>This is a senior level position for a highly experienced and technical lead. They will be supporting the Student Information Services (SIS) team, a division of Enterprise Information Technology Services) EITS. It is a senior level application administration and implementation position which will support current system administration tasks, maintenance and troubleshooting, as well as provide analysis, development, integration and implementation of new systems pertaining to the Student Information Systems.</div> EITS-App Admin & Reporting https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478360 2026-04-22T17:14:43-04:00 2026-08-06T16:39:06-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator – Fortson <div>This job is a temporary Environmental Educator at Fortson 4-H Center located in Hampton, Georgia. The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include life and earth science, ecology, team building, outdoor skills, and living history. Other responsibilities include animal care, maintenance of teaching areas and resources, facilities, grounds, and support of general operations of the facility.</div> CAES-Fortson 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478794 2026-04-22T17:46:25-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:26-04:00 Turfgrass Field/Lab Assist - Waltz Assist researchers with both lab and field experiments conducted on turfgrass, both on and off of the UGA Griffin Campus. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504495 2026-09-03T17:02:55-04:00 2026-09-03T17:02:56-04:00 Bus Operations Supervisor <div>This position is responsible for providing supervision for the daily operation of the campus transit system. This work involves both direct and indirect oversight of bus operators on routes and during pre/post trip inspections. This position gives support to drivers by communicating and providing guidance to address the needs of bus operators. In addition, this position is also responsible for performing administrative task to include payroll review/approval and providing back-up support for the Transit Dispatcher in their absence. On occasion, this position may operate buses on routes and special charters. Applicants submit to drug and alcohol testing by the US Department of Transportation.</div> Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501250 2026-08-19T12:10:11-04:00 2026-08-19T12:10:12-04:00 Houseperson <div>This position is responsible for supporting housekeepers and laundry personnel. Responsibilities include stocking housekeeping closets with linen and supplies, delivering linen and supplies to housekeepers, and removing dirty linens and trash from hotel rooms. This position also assists with laundry responsibilities such as sorting, washing, drying, and folding linen and towels. This position is responsible for providing outstanding customer service and contributing to the success of the housekeeping team.</div> PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478475 2026-04-22T17:22:45-04:00 2026-06-03T13:44:19-04:00 Food Service Worker - Rock Eagle - Temporary <div>Work involves preparing and serving food and cleaning food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision, follow written and/or oral procedures and practices. Employee will implement these procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/485248 2026-05-26T13:54:58-04:00 2026-06-24T12:24:30-04:00 Crop & Soil Sciences- Student Assistant 2-Grey <div>Individual will assist in lab experiments, prepare for upcoming experiments, keep lab areas, and greenhouses clean and organized. Will also assist with field experiments, assist technician and graduate student where needed. Full time work available during the summer months. Shifts start at 7AM for work most days and occasionally 6AM for out of town travel to Plains and Griffin so punctuality is important.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478573 2026-04-22T17:29:58-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:59-04:00 Temporary researcher This is a field researcher position who will assist with the trapping, telemetry monitoring, and sampling of various mammals.  Work will be conducted in various field conditions and be subject to various climate factors (High temps, cold temps, rain, etc.) VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493111 2026-07-14T09:02:39-04:00 2026-08-12T11:45:34-04:00 Assistant Research Scientist <div>The University of Georgia’s Center for Applied Isotope Studies (CAIS) seeks an Analytical Chemist at the rank of Assistant Research Scientist to support the Lab for Environmental Analysis. This renewable 12-month position will lead the commissioning and operation of a new hybrid triple quadrupole/linear ion trap LC-MS/MS system and develop analytical services for a diverse client base spanning environmental science, ecology, agriculture, archaeology, forensics, biomedical research, and related fields.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will conduct chemical analyses, develop and validate analytical methods, manage client projects, supervise students, and contribute to laboratory operations, budgeting, and service development. Responsibilities include sample preparation, data analysis, report preparation, client communication, and maintaining advanced chromatographic and mass spectrometric instrumentation. The appointee is also expected to pursue collaborative research, secure external funding, and publish in peer-reviewed journals.</div> VPR-Ctr Applied Isotope Study https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/30398 2018-08-17T14:27:26-04:00 2018-08-17T14:27:27-04:00 Temporary Administrative Work-Based Learning Program AY 2018-2019 Provides administrative support to LLED faculty and staff including, but not limited to, creating and maintaining office supply inventory, assisting Office Manager with equipment inventory, copying/scanning, overseeing office space signage, supporting social media, and other general reception duties such as answering phones, greeting visitors, and organizing mail. Some special project work with faculty included. COE-Language & Literacy Educ https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478682 2026-04-22T17:38:56-04:00 2026-04-22T17:38:56-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Woodson <div>The Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS) and the Department of Geology at the University of Georgia are hiring for a 1-year, renewable (for a maximum of 4 total years) postdoctoral research position.<br><br>The successful candidate will develop a regional groundwater model for southeast and coastal Georgia and run future climate and development scenarios. The postdoc will be under the direct supervision of Brock Woodson (College of Engineering) and Adam Milewski (Department of Agricultural and Applied Economics), and but will work with the broader team including the project sponsor to develop application scenarios and high-resolution site-specific models for areas of interest.<br><br>The successful incumbent will work with an interdisciplinary team of engineers, geologists and other scientists and practitioners to co-develop and implement research on the economic, ecological, and social related to groundwater along the Georgia coastal region. The successful candidate will collaborate in disciplinary and interdisciplinary academic publications, policy briefings, and outreach activities. This is a research position with duties related to the project needs and the mentoring/supervision of graduate and undergraduate students.<br><br></div> ENGR-Resilient Infrast Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497350 2026-07-31T15:08:22-04:00 2026-07-31T15:08:22-04:00 Business Manager <div><br>The Business Manager supports the daily financial and administrative operations of the College of Environment and Design Business Office. This position is responsible for processing and monitoring financial transactions, maintaining accurate financial records, assisting faculty and staff with business-related procedures, and ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures.<br><br></div><div>The position performs a variety of operational and administrative business functions, including grant pre- and post-award administration, payment processing, account reconciliation, procurement support, payroll reconciliation assistance, and financial record maintenance. The Business Manager serves as a resource to faculty, staff, and students regarding routine financial and administrative matters and works collaboratively with the Assistant Financial Director to support efficient business office operations.<br><br></div><div>This role exercises independent judgment in managing assigned tasks and resolving routine operational issues while escalating complex financial or policy matters to the Assistant Financial Director as appropriate.</div> CED-Business Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477994 2026-04-21T18:25:06-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:06-04:00 Assistant Research Scientist <div>Assistant Research Scientist position in CCRC's National Glycoscience Resources Laboratory.<br><br></div><ul><li>Conduct research for development of new tools and method for structural characterization of glycoproteins and polysaccharides using a of MS, HPLC, HPAEC or NMR techniques and subsequently publish and obtain independent funding.</li><li>Write and edit manuscripts and reviewers on topics in glycoscience to increase the publication output.</li><li>Supervise laboratory technicians, postdocs and research professions in service and research projects that includes characterization of glycoconjugates with collaboration from investigators from outside of UGA.</li><li>Write detailed comprehensive reports on data produced in the laboratory on structural, characterization of polysaccharides and glycoproteins.</li><li>Review reports produced by other laboratory members for accuracy and high quality so that the data can be used in a manuscript publication.</li><li>Teach and organize on the hands-on and virtual training courses offered by the CCRC on glycoconjuagtes with participants from universities, research institutes and government agencies.</li><li>Help organize workshops and tutorials on topics in glycoscience.</li></ul> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503945 2026-09-01T13:49:30-04:00 2026-09-01T13:49:31-04:00 Life Science Technician (Lance) <div>Assist with field and laboratory based studies of amphibian and reptile ecotoxicology, population ecology, and conservation.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500195 2026-08-14T13:42:32-04:00 2026-08-14T13:42:32-04:00 Softball Manager Athletics-Softball https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478406 2026-04-22T17:19:40-04:00 2026-08-27T17:07:44-04:00 Compliance Monitor (Temporary) <div>Parking Event Staff are the front line personal for greeting, engaging, and interacting with all patrons entering and exiting the parking areas. The position will assist patrons with parking and transportation needs for special events within and around the University of Georgia-Athens Campus. Work with a team to create a safe environment for patrons to arrive/depart University events.&nbsp;</div> Auxiliary Parking Compliance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478915 2026-04-23T11:45:08-04:00 2026-04-23T11:45:10-04:00 Strategic Engagement and Grants Specialist <div>The Strategic Engagement and Grants Specialist will play a crucial role in supporting all Public Service and Outreach (PSO) units by identifying and pursuing high-value funding opportunities, convening interdisciplinary teams, and enhancing proposal competitiveness. This role integrates strategic engagement with grants development by proactively scanning agency priorities, analyzing funding trends, and leading and shaping collaborative proposal development efforts.</div><div>This role serves as a key advisor to project teams and operates with a high degree of independence, guiding teams through reviewer criteria and scoring considerations, and building strong partnerships across PSO, academic units, community organizations, and external agencies. The Specialist establishes efficient proposal processes, supports project ideation, coordinates structured proposal enhancement activities such as peer review and mock panels, and provides training on best practices across the grant lifecycle.</div><div>The position ensures that PSO’s external funding strategy aligns with broader university priorities and contributes to improving proposal development processes and funding outcomes across PSO, strengthening the impact of outreach initiatives.</div> PSO-VP Public Serv & Outreach https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502738 2026-08-26T09:51:16-04:00 2026-08-26T09:51:17-04:00 Fox Squirrel Research Technician <div>The University of Georgia, Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources (<a href=\"http://warnell.uga.edu/)\"><strong>http://warnell.uga.edu/)</strong></a> and The Jones Center at Ichauway (<a href=\"https://www.jonesctr.org/)\"><strong>https://www.jonesctr.org/)</strong></a> are offering seasonal positions conducting camera trap surveys of fox squirrels in Georgia. The positions begin in mid-December 2026 and will end at the end of May 2026. The employees will assist with a camera trapping study to estimate fox squirrel abundance and habitat use at multiple locations across the state. Activities will include, but are not limited to, setting, and maintaining 200 wildlife camera traps and organizing and processing camera trap data, as well as conducting vegetation surveys at camera locations. Lodging and a field vehicle will be provided.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478524 2026-04-22T17:25:34-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:35-04:00 Temporary Tech Parapro - Li Lab A temporary/lab research position is needed to work in the soybean research lab to take agronomic notes, collect data, and harvest soybean research plots in the field. This position will work in the seed lab to weigh and clean samples, thresh individual plants, and prepare seed for spring planting. CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/489497 2026-06-23T12:03:52-04:00 2026-06-23T12:03:53-04:00 Sports Nutrition Student Worker Assist Sports Nutritionists with providing nutrition services for UGA Olympic Sports. This will include different areas of food service and food management, education, and outreach as it relates to collegiate sports nutrition within the guidelines of the NCAA and compliance rules at UGA. Athletics-Olympic Nutrition https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503580 2026-08-31T10:01:32-04:00 2026-08-31T10:01:33-04:00 Temporary Accountant <div>Involves the accurate and timely completion of reports and invoices and processing of awards and modifications under the terms of the various contracts, grants and agreements awarded to the university. The position will interpret, establish, and maintain award files and government documents pertaining to post-award administration of grants and contracts.</div> FD-SPA Post Award Accounting https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499762 2026-08-13T10:02:25-04:00 2026-08-13T10:02:25-04:00 WUGA Digital Coordinator <div>The Digital Coordinator is responsible for expanding the organization's reach, relevance, and impact across digital platforms while strengthening audience habits and engagement. This position serves as the primary driver of digital storytelling, content distribution, audience development, and digital product growth, ensuring that the organization's journalism and programming reach audiences where they increasingly consume media.<br><br></div><div>The role focuses on attracting and retaining new listeners and supporters, increasing daily engagement through newsletters, podcasts, social media, photo, video, and web content. Working collaboratively with newsroom, programming, and central Marketing &amp; Communications staff, this position creates and repurposes existing content into compelling digital experiences that execute strategic opportunities for audience growth.</div> MarComm-WUGA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478384 2026-04-22T17:16:34-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:34-04:00 Student Assistant <div>Student assistant position.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478817 2026-04-22T17:49:56-04:00 2026-04-22T17:49:56-04:00 Equestrian - Building Services Work daily with horses at the UGA Equestrian barn and help to clean and maintain the area and animals. Athletics-Equestrian https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501960 2026-08-21T15:14:01-04:00 2026-08-21T15:14:01-04:00 IC Instructional Coach <div>This position will be responsible for online coaching, vetting lesson plans, and creating exemplar lesson plans to support the instructional conversation professional learning community.</div> COE-Research & Graduate Educ https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478506 2026-04-22T17:24:21-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:21-04:00 Temporary Turfgrass Lab/Field Assistant - Walt <div>This position will assist researchers with both lab and field experiments conducted on turfgrass on the Griffin Campus as well as off-site areas.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487636 2026-06-09T09:39:59-04:00 2026-06-09T09:40:00-04:00 Jasper County Administrative Assistant <div>This Jasper County Extension position is a non-exempt professional staff role within UGA Cooperative Extension responsible for handling the many resources offered by the Extension office. A level of independent judgment is necessary to effectively carry out the duties of the job and the incumbent is expected to manage administrative duties by developing techniques and procedures as appropriate. This role works cooperatively with all Extension faculty and staff where applicable and is administratively responsible to the County Extension Coordinator.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478603 2026-04-22T17:32:38-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:39-04:00 Temporary Lab/Field Assistant (EARTH) To assist and learn in breeding, harvesting, collecting data, and research operation. The learning objective is for the intern to work in experiments preparations and in field/greenhouse operations. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494782 2026-07-21T11:18:17-04:00 2026-07-21T11:18:17-04:00 Food Service Worker II This is manual and semi-skilled work in the performance of advanced food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for limited supervision over subordinate food service workers engaged in serving foods and cleaning facilities for limited food preparation tasks and for related food service duties that are more advanced and responsible than the duties of Food Service Worker I. Employees of this class apply limited skills and knowledge that are acquired through experience. Duties include responsibility for instructing subordinate food service workers in dining hall techniques and methods; for maintaining high standards of cleanliness; and for assuring that patrons are served in a pleasant and courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained. Auxiliary Oglethorpe https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477807 2026-04-21T17:50:31-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:32-04:00 Senior Research Associate - Metropolitan Human-Wildlife Conflicts <div>Managing human-wildlife interactions in urbanized environments is an increasing concern for wildlife management agencies. Although suburban and urban environments provide important habitat for wildlife, the high density of people increases the probability of negative human-wildlife interactions (e.g., vehicle collisions with deer, damage to personal property by wildlife, harm to pets, anthropogenic food conditioning of wildlife). Suburban and urban residents may have limited knowledge of wildlife or how to mitigate potential conflicts with wildlife. Moreover, suburban and urban residents may be unaware that state wildlife agencies have the expertise to assist them in managing potential conflicts with wildlife.<br><br>The successful candidate will conduct a human dimensions study in the metropolitan Atlanta (metro-Atlanta) region to determine the following:<br>1. Metro-Atlanta residents’ level of wildlife tolerance, and determinants of wildlife tolerance, e.g. attitudes, beliefs, risk concerns, pet ownership, socio-demographics;<br>2. Perceived positive and negative impacts of wildlife, and whether certain wildlife species tend to be liked or disliked;<br>3. Residents’ knowledge of appropriate actions to mitigate human-wildlife conflicts, and their willingness to engage in these actions;&nbsp;<br>4. Residents’ prior awareness of Georgia Department of Natural Resources (GADNR), and their level of trust in GADNR; and<br>5. How residents would prefer to receive information about living with wildlife.<br><br></div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478723 2026-04-22T17:40:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:37-04:00 Northern Bobwhite Field Technicians (2)-GA <div><strong>Position Summary</strong> | Seeking Research Technicians to assist with Northern Bobwhite trapping, radio-telemetry tracking, and nest checking of Northern Bobwhite as well as other associated fieldwork as part of larger experimental studies. Data entry, equipment maintenance, and other duties requested by supervisors. Selected individuals will also gain numerous opportunities to interact directly with the Georgia DNR. Employees will be working with minimal supervision on site and should be comfortable working independently. Previous experience with radio-telemetry is desired. Knowledge of and experience with Microsoft Excel, databases, and ArcGIS is desired. Applicants should be comfortable occasionally working alone after dark.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498029 2026-08-05T10:04:50-04:00 2026-08-05T10:04:50-04:00 ASST SYSTEM ADMINISTRATOR <div>This position is responsible for supporting the use of computing devices across all of the various units within the Office of Research. Areas of responsibility include but are not limited to: desktop support (Windows/Mac), device imaging, printer management, device inventory, device management via Intune/Addigy, device troubleshooting, user management (AD and Entra), network/IP management, and conference room support.<br><br>This position requires completion of specified certifications within the first two years of hire for employees who do not already possess them, with department support available.</div> VPR-Research IT https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478094 2026-04-21T18:31:37-04:00 2026-04-21T18:31:38-04:00 Hall County 4-H & Youth Development Agent <div>This position will be responsible for managing the 4-H &amp; Youth Development programming in Hall County by providing educational opportunities for youth in 4-H club meetings, coordinating local activities, and preparing youth for project and judging events.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and Adult Clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504257 2026-09-02T16:26:08-04:00 2026-09-02T16:26:09-04:00 Communications Director <div>The Communications Director serves on the Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant leadership team, providing strategic direction for the unit’s communications program and contributing to organizational planning and decision-making. Reporting directly to the Director, this position oversees all aspects of communications operations, including the development and implementation of internal and external communication strategies, policies, processes and priorities that enhance the visibility and impact of the unit’s research, education and extension programs. The position supervises two full-time communications professionals and regularly mentors undergraduate and graduate students while collaborating with leadership, faculty, staff, partners and stakeholders to develop products, resources and communications materials that support coastal communities. Responsibilities include managing the creation of print, digital and multimedia content; overseeing website, social media, publication and media relations efforts; providing communications training and support for staff, students and partners; and promoting events and fundraising initiatives that advance the mission of Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant.</div> PSO-Sea Grant Program https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500676 2026-08-17T22:30:59-04:00 2026-08-17T22:30:59-04:00 Baker I <div>This is skilled work in baking pastries and bread in a dining hall, snack bar, cafeteria, or campus eateries. Work involves responsibility for baking a variety of pastries and bread and for assuring proper quality and quantity. Duties may include supervision and/or instruction of food service workers assigned to assist in baking activities and in cleaning equipment and facilities. Assignments are determined from menus and the employee has some judgment in applying baking skills, and knowledge. Work is normally performed under the supervision of a food service supervisor and is reviewed for quality, economy, and volume of output.</div> Auxiliary Village Summit https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478432 2026-04-22T17:20:23-04:00 2026-05-26T15:34:51-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator – Burton <div>This is a temporary Environmental Educator position at Burton 4-H Center located on Tybee Island, Georgia. The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include a focus on coastal ecology, life science, earth science and marine science. Other responsibilities include animal care, lead staff duties, general support of overall center operations.</div> CAES-Burton 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/481806 2026-05-07T17:43:07-04:00 2026-05-07T17:43:08-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The postdoctoral research associate assists Dr. Ahn with activities related to the Translational Core. This includes literature reviews, assistance in message development, assistance with the virtual reality development and user testing, preparation for the annual workshop, VR Demo Day, and the VR-integrated training package, as well as other Translational Core activities, under Dr. Ahn’s supervision. The postdoctoral researcher will also help develop drafts of white papers, request for proposals, and annual reports from the Translational Core. Translational science will be a key aspect of this position and the postdoc will be involved in the various translational communication efforts that arise from the CHARTER project. This may involve social media content generation, dissemination, community events, and liaison efforts with community partners. Day to day operations and management of the CACHE center space will also be required, which includes administrative duties such as IRB protocol drafting and submission, hardware maintenance, repairs, software updates, and administering demos for visitors. The position will also involve the drafting of peer-reviewed manuscripts to be presented at conferences and peer-reviewed journals in related fields.</div> VPR-Owens Inst Behavioral Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478552 2026-04-22T17:26:48-04:00 2026-05-04T16:23:52-04:00 Research Technician - Chavez <div>This is a temporary position that will be responsible for assisting and supporting the Associate Professor of Horticulture with applied research and extension programs.</div><ul><li>Assist with setting up and overseeing field trials, greenhouse, and laboratory applied research in cooperation with industry and CAES faculty.</li><li>Perform greenhouse maintenance and any additional activities as needed, including but not limited to potting media, planting, fertilization, and irrigation.</li><li>Collect data from field, greenhouse, and laboratory studies and subject this data to appropriate statistical analyses.</li><li>Applied research will involve outdoor field studies and work in greenhouses.</li><li>Maintain and accurately keep an inventory of supplies, chemicals, and pesticides for the program while making sure the program PI stays in full compliance with UGA, EPD, and EPA regulations governing the storage and usage of these materials.</li></ul> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491183 2026-07-02T10:54:53-04:00 2026-07-02T10:54:53-04:00 Plant Nematology Lab Student Assistant – Mitchum Lab <div>The Plant Nematology Lab Assistant position will support laboratory and greenhouse research related to plant diseases and the biology of their causal agents under the direction of a faculty member and/or lab manager/post-docs/graduate students. Duties include, but are not limited to, planting and processing of plants for screening for nematode resistance, including labeling tags, packaging and germination of seed, harvesting seed, filling pots with soil, soaking and processing roots for nematode analysis; assisting with plant and/or nematode care by watering of plants in greenhouses and growth chambers, including short periods on a rotational basis during assigned weekends; assisting with lab maintenance and chores, including washing and sterilize pots, stocking supplies, cleaning the lab, disposing of plant material; assisting with prepping, steaming, and disposal of soil.</div> CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478643 2026-04-22T17:34:20-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:21-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate AD - West & Lourenco <div>The University of Georgia Microbiome Research group is seeking a motivated and hardworking postdoctoral fellow to support and develop novel approaches to collect, analyze, and interpret human microbiome data to better understand the healthy and diseased microbiome. Our group seeks to understand how the microbiome, particularly the gastrointestinal system, changes between diverse individuals spanning multiple age groups, sexes, ethnicities, and other key population demographics. We are also interested in how the microbiome changes in acute and chronic disease and injury states in conditions such as stroke, traumatic brain injury, diabetes, and cancer and how they correlate with condition severity and prognosis.</div><div><br></div><div>Experience in the use of the programming language Python, as well as Python software such as QIIME and QIIME2. In addition, experience using R, including packages such as Phyloseq, DESeq2, ANCOM, and/or PICRUSt. Experience with software and pipelines important for analyzing shotgun sequencing data, metatranscriptomics, proteomics, and/or metabolomics. Familiarity with statistical analyses using linear, mixed, and non-linear models, as well as non-parametric data in order to analyze large data sets.</div><div><br></div><div>The candidate will work primarily in the field of metagenomics and metatranscriptomics; however, summarizing and analyzing other type of large datasets (such as population demographics) is desirable.</div><div><br></div><div>The successful candidate will work under the direction of Drs. Jeferson Lourenco (https://animaldairy.uga.edu/people/faculty/jeferson-lourenco.html) and Franklin West (<a href=\"https://site.caes.uga.edu/tnrrl/\"><strong>https://site.caes.uga.edu/tnrrl/</strong></a> and https://westlaboratory.org). The UGA Microbiome Research group lead by Drs. Lourenco and West is a highly collaborative team that works with academic, industry, and government partners nationally and internationally. Their research is also highly interdisciplinary and often includes working with microbiologist, nutritionist, clinicians, and other allied health industry experts. Drs. Lourenco and West are committed to the short- and long-term professional development of lab members and will work with the candidate in supporting their career goals.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496491 2026-07-28T13:55:48-04:00 2026-07-28T13:55:48-04:00 Veterinary Assistant II- Field Services/Therio <div>The primary purpose of the Field Services/Theriogenology Veterinary Assistant is to assist the theriogenology and Field Services department with daily in-house and on-site appointments, maintain and stock the necessary equipment to conduct the theriogenology service, and assist with maintaining records and charges for the theriogenology and field service department as appropriate. Handling/restraint of large animals. (Primarily horses/cows, but may include sheep, pigs, goats, and camelids). The assistant is needed to safely handle all temperaments of horses. This includes handling for lameness exams (jogging/lunging), procedures, standing surgeries, radiology/bone scan, neuro exams and stallion collection.<br>Other duties include assisting LVT’s/Clinicians/Students/Client Support Coordinator in any capacity as needed for patient care, general housekeeping/stocking/stall maintenance, animal/sample transport, anesthetic induction/recovery, and utilization of VetView/Cubex (the hospital's medical records software and medication dispensing).</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477896 2026-04-21T18:04:28-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:29-04:00 Asst Golf Course Superintendent <div>This is a highly responsible professional that is managing 18 holes on a golf course, putting green, and surrounding areas. There are 200 acres of property within this person’s supervisory responsibilities. This includes building maintenance, environmental/safety regulation and compliance, and organization of events, etc. This individual also has budgetary responsibilities, such as maintaining the annual budget for building use and facilities maintenance. Above all, this incumbent is responsible for the general supervision and maintenance of the course as well as the maintenance of the crew, which consists of approximately 5-8 full-time staff and 10-20 part-time student employees.</div> Auxiliary University Golf Cour https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478526 2026-04-22T17:25:37-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:38-04:00 Forestry Technician USFWS <div>Positions will be located on various National Wildlife Refuges in the Southeast region. Potential Refuge locations may include (but not limited to): Carolina Sandhills NWR in McBee, SC; St. Marks NWR in St. Marks, FL; Okeefenokee NWR in Folkston, GA; Piedmont NWR in Round Oak, GA; Lower Suwanee NWR in Chiefland, FL; Noxubee NWR near Starkville, MS; and, Clarks River in Kentucky. Primary duties include collecting baseline forest habitat data, cruising &amp; marking timber to enhance wildlife habitat, and assisting with timber sale administration. Other duties may involve invasive plant control and monitoring of wildlife and habitat responses to various forest management treatments. A wide variety of wildlife management activities may also be incorporated depending upon refuge needs and objectives.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/489661 2026-06-24T09:58:28-04:00 2026-06-24T09:58:29-04:00 Student Assistant- Dining Hall Locations <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in a dining hall. Work involves responsibility for preparing and serving foods, cleaning facilities, and providing customer service.</div> Auxiliary Dining Board Plan Op https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478624 2026-04-22T17:33:46-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:46-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate - Gaertig The postdoctoral researcher will\r\nstudy Hpo1, its interactions with other patterning proteins and its localization using super-resolution and\r\nimmunogold electron microscopy Franklin-Cellular Biology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495399 2026-07-23T11:15:16-04:00 2026-07-23T11:15:17-04:00 Assistant Dean for Education <div>The Assistant Dean for Education serves as the Ivester School of Nursing’s academic leader for educational programs and clinical track faculty, reporting directly to the Dean. This position provides strategic and operational leadership for the development, implementation, systematic evaluation, and continuous quality improvement of all degree programs. The Assistant Dean for Education is a key partner to the Dean in advancing the school’s educational mission and its commitment to developing a highly prepared nursing workforce for Georgia and beyond.</div> SON-Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477844 2026-04-21T17:58:48-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:49-04:00 STEAMFITTER This is skilled steam fitting and welding work at the journeyman level, primarily involved with the operation, maintenance, troubleshooting and repair of campus steam distribution system, system components and building steam powered equipment. Most work performed on equipment both inside and outside of buildings buildings. Additionally, work involves pipe fitting and welding in support of steam system and equipment work as well as other general welding work in support of other shop maintenance activities. FMD-O&M-Welding Shop https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503085 2026-08-27T09:14:51-04:00 2026-08-27T09:14:52-04:00 Sr. Associate Dean of Strategic Initiatives and Faculty Success <div><strong>POSITION IS ONLY OPEN TO CURRENT FACULTY MEMBERS IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA.</strong><br><br>The Senior Associate Dean for Strategic Initiatives and Faculty Success reports directly to the Dean and oversees the development and implementation of strategic initiatives, such as our Rural Healthcare, Clinician Retention Initiatives, and building projects. The Senior Associate Dean works with the College leadership and staff to promote the College and serve as a liaison to various College stakeholders, including alumni, donors, the legislature, and College Advisory Board. In addition, this individual will provide leadership and oversight on issues and initiatives related to Faculty Affairs, including hiring; career development (e.g., onboarding, advancement, promotion, and/or tenure); conflict management; and other faculty-centered issues.</div> VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498780 2026-08-07T16:37:49-04:00 2026-08-07T16:37:49-04:00 Hall County EFNEP Program Assistant <div>This position is based in Hall County and is responsible for paraprofessional work under the supervision and direction of County Extension Agents/Supervisors. This incumbent provides paraprofessional work with County Extension Educator/Agents in a food and nutrition education program. Plans, organizes, schedules, and conducts nutrition and food safety classes for limited resource clients. Prepares and conducts food demonstrations for group classes. Work is performed under general supervision.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478365 2026-04-22T17:15:59-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:00-04:00 Temporary Administrative - Griffin Campus, Young Scholars <div>This position will provide critical administrative support for the Young Scholars program during the summer of 2022. The person selected for the position will serve as the group facilitator and chaperone during all YSP related activities, including but not limited to: group workshops and training sessions, field trips to UGA Athens and other scientific research facilities, and final presentation sessions. This person will also serve as a direct contact for the students and will meet with students on a weekly basis to monitor their progress throughout the duration of the program. This person will also help coordinate workshops, handle travel arrangements, prepare and distribute documents to support program activities, and provide administrative and clerical support to local YSP coordinator.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478796 2026-04-22T17:46:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:30-04:00 Student Assistant - Li Lab Student assistant in Dr. Zenglu Li's lab. CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504504 2026-09-04T08:07:33-04:00 2026-09-04T08:07:34-04:00 Medical Records Associate <div>This position provides customer service to all clients of the Medical Records Department. Primary responsibilities include: attaching documentation to patient records; answering and routing phone calls, emails and faxes in a timely manner; processing records requests, and other duties as assigned. This position will assist the VTH Business information systems manager in providing first level support for end users of Vetview and Instinct applications such as login issues and basic functionality.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501274 2026-08-19T13:36:35-04:00 2026-08-19T13:36:36-04:00 Computer Operations Tech II <div>This position involves activities of an assigned shift of personnel engaged in the operation and monitoring of data center facilities and related infrastructure equipment, such as HVAC, electrical grid, emergency backup UPS and generator systems, water/leak detection equipment, security and fire suppression systems, as well as research and enterprise servers, core networking services, and related services and equipment. Assist with installing server racks, cabinets, servers, storage devices, and network devices. Responsibilities include planning, scheduling, and coordinating those activities; the resolution of complex error situations with and without additional technical or supervisory assistance; making recommendations regarding new or improved service routines and production schedules. Work is performed alongside other shift personnel and subject to review by the Operations and Infrastructure leadership through conferences and evaluation of results obtained.&nbsp;</div> EITS-Data Ctr Ops https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478481 2026-04-22T17:22:56-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:57-04:00 Academic Services Intern <div>University of Georgia, a Division I member of the Southeastern Conference is currently seeking applications for the position of Academic Services Intern. The position is an 11-month appointment beginning in July 2026 and ending in May 2027.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/485992 2026-05-29T13:15:08-04:00 2026-05-29T13:15:09-04:00 Northern Bobwhite Field Technician-TX <div>We are seeking 2 technicians to assist with Northern Bobwhite research on public and private lands in Texas. Typical duties involve but are not limited to: Capturing and handling wild bobwhite, daily animal husbandry of captive bobwhites, radio-telemetry, clearing and baiting trap sites, building walk-in funnel cage traps, data entry, equipment maintenance, and other various duties. The selected individuals will interact with the Texas Department of Parks and Wildlife staff, and private property managers/owners. Employees will be working with minimal supervision and should be comfortable working independently during daytime and nighttime hours, in adverse weather conditions, and where venomous snakes are found. Previous experience with bird handling and radio-telemetry is desired. Hiking ~5-10 miles per day, lift 50 lbs, and comfortable working in tight quarters for several hours at a time.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478575 2026-04-22T17:30:03-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:04-04:00 Temporary Lab/Field Assistant Sample collection, DNA extraction, gel electrophoresis, PCR, help maintain plants in greenhouse/field. CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493195 2026-07-14T12:27:32-04:00 2026-07-14T12:27:32-04:00 Area Director-Atlanta <div>Would you like to have an impact on your community and make a difference? Are you committed to service? Are you a strategic thinker with strong business acumen and leadership experience? Do you excel at managing teams, analyzing complex business challenges, and driving results? The University of Georgia Small Business Development Center located in Atlanta, GA is seeking a highly motivated, highly skilled professional for a management-level, public service faculty position dedicated to helping Georgia businesses grow and prosper, focused on business development and operational leadership. Responsibilities also include managing the Atlanta SBDC territory and office personnel.<br><br>As an Area Director, you will apply your broad base of business knowledge to deliver high-impact consulting, training, and strategic guidance to small businesses across your assigned territory. This role requires strong analytical capabilities, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. You will lead the daily operations of the Atlanta office, supervise staff, and ensure program excellence within the Atlanta SBDC service area.<br><br>This position involves multi-county travel and offers the opportunity to apply your expertise in a dynamic, collaborative environment.<br><br></div><div>The salary is $100,000 with a generous, comprehensive benefits package, including a defined benefits retirement plan.</div> PSO-Small Business Dev Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477376 2026-04-20T14:19:52-04:00 2026-04-20T14:19:52-04:00 Research Professional <div>Objectives of the PERSEUS project include developing a forest management simulation model that combines spatial data, forest growth and yield projections, and forest harvest scheduling assumptions to simulate forest management activities at broad scales of the eastern United States. The Research Professional I will work with colleagues in the Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources, as well as the Institute for Artificial Intelligence at the University of Georgia, and similar colleagues from Purdue University and the University of Maine, to accomplish the data development and modeling goals associated with these objectives.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478689 2026-04-22T17:39:08-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:09-04:00 Forest Business Research Intern <div>The Forest Business and Operations team at the Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources is searching for 3 undergraduate students to conduct research related to forest business. Interns will assist graduate students, professors, and staff with field data collection during summer 2025. Field data collection will include measurements of soil, trees, and timber harvesting machines. Interested students should be current undergraduates with an interest in applied forestry and field data collection. The internship is open to all forestry and natural resources majors.<br><br>The successful candidates will work in a team setting. Day-to-day activities would consist of travel, field data collection and analysis around timber harvest sites, and other duties as assigned. The position will be based in Athens, GA and most data collection will be conducted in Georgia and surrounding states. Some overnight travel to nearby states may be needed, but all travel expenses will be covered. These positions provide a great opportunity to explore new areas of the state, meet forestry professionals, and become familiar with general forestry practices.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497448 2026-08-03T10:28:59-04:00 2026-08-03T10:29:00-04:00 Plumber <div>This is skilled technical work at a journeyman level involving operating, installing, maintaining, troubleshooting and repairing: plumbing systems and components, steam and hot water boiler equipment, other gas-fired equipment and fire protection systems. This includes systems in building as well as utility service: water, sanitary sewer, storm sewer and gas distribution systems.</div> FMD-O&M-Struct Maint&Projects https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478002 2026-04-21T18:25:25-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:26-04:00 Assistant/Associate Research Scientist for Advancing Circular Bioeconomy Systems <div>The College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES) at the University of Georgia seeks to recruit an Assistant or Associate Research Scientist to work on the Circular Bioeconomy Systems (CBS) initiative. This is a non-tenured track position with 95% research and 5% service responsibility.<br><br>The position will be housed in the UGA CAES; however, the incumbent will be expected to work closely with faculty in the multidisciplinary teams from Colleges/Schools of Engineering, Forestry and Natural Resources, Arts and Sciences, Family and Consumer Sciences, and others. The candidate is expected to maintain an internationally renowned research program that produces and publishes work recognized and used by researchers and stakeholders around the world. The incumbent will report to the office of the CAES Associate Dean of Research.<br><br>The incumbent will coordinate and draft proposals for external funding to support the CBS initiative. Although this position is predominantly a research appointment, the person will interact with undergraduate/graduate students and stakeholders, and contribute to teaching and outreach mission of the University.&nbsp;</div> CAES-Assoc Dean for Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504022 2026-09-01T15:33:59-04:00 2026-09-01T15:34:00-04:00 Student Assistant - Facilities BSW <div>The Building Service Worker II performs manual work in a variety of cleaning and related duties in the University Health Center (UHC), including exam rooms, restrooms, conference rooms, and offices. The work of this position involves the performance of cleaning in an assigned building area. The primary responsibility of this position is the effective use of proper methods and materials in cleaning and caring for building areas and equipment. This individual works under close supervision and follows well established routines, procedures, and infection control standards.</div> UHC-Facilities Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500209 2026-08-14T14:15:46-04:00 2026-08-14T14:15:47-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>The Tsui Lab in the Center for Molecular Medicine at the University of Georgia is seeking to recruit a highly motivated postdoc to join our new team in studying the role of glycosylation in cell-cell communication. Multiple projects on elucidating the genetic regulatory network of glycosylation, deorphanizing human lectins, and investigating specific contributions of glycan-lectin interactions in neuroinflammation are available.</div><div>The projects will primarily use cultured cells in a BSL2 environment along with CRISPR screens, flow cytometry, microscopy, genomics, and glycoproteomics. The postdoctoral researcher will be expected to design, perform, and document experiments as well as disseminate their work through conferences and published manuscripts. In addition, the postdoctoral researcher will be expected to provide scientific leadership within the lab by mentoring graduate and undergraduate students.</div> VPR-Ctr for Molecular Medicine https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478409 2026-04-22T17:19:46-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:46-04:00 Deer Research Technician <div>Technicians will assist a master’s student with data collection this fall. Data collection will be conducted with captive deer at the Whitehall Deer Research Facility in Athens, GA. The research project investigates the interaction between white-tailed deer and residential fences to reduce deer-fence conflicts. More specifically, data collected during this position will attempt to describe the jumping abilities of white-tailed deer from a biomechanical perspective. Technicians will assist the graduate student with jumping trials in which deer will attempt to cross vertical barriers while being recorded by an array of high-speed cameras. Primary responsibilities will include moving deer throughout the facility, assisting the master’s student with data collection, and any necessary preparation/concluding activities. Technicians are expected to work outdoors for several hours, which may include early mornings or late evenings.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479222 2026-04-24T11:20:40-04:00 2026-04-24T11:20:40-04:00 Horticulture Student Assistant-Sugimoto 2 <div>The successful applicant will be responsible for assisting fruit and vegetable quality to extend shelf-life and agricultural product development through field, laboratory, and storage-based research. The incumbent will assist in sample preparation in the lab and data collection for produce quality-related analyses. The role also includes to upkeep of laboratory space and requires data entry. All tasks will be performed under the direction and supervision of the lab manager.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478650 2026-04-22T17:36:45-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:45-04:00 Canteen Worker - Rock Eagle This is a summer time position responsible for stocking shelves, pricing inventory, operating a cash register/credit card machine, checking and filling vending machines, operating concession area, receiving and handling merchandise. CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496641 2026-07-29T09:20:21-04:00 2026-07-29T09:20:22-04:00 Carpenter <div>This is manual work at the journeyman level in both rough and finished carpentry. Work involves the construction and maintenance of structural woodwork, other woodwork involving the use of standard carpenter tools and power-driven woodworking machinery, and the building and repair of structures of brick, tile, stone, and similar materials. Assignments are normally made orally or in the form of sketches or blueprints. Work is inspected for satisfactory compliance with instructions, although routine repairs are usually made independently without supervision or review.<br><br></div> FMD-O&M-Struct Maint&Projects https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477903 2026-04-21T18:04:46-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:47-04:00 GRANTS OFFICER I <div>Sponsored Projects Administration, Pre-Award, is the central pre-award or sponsored projects office at the University of Georgia. The office manages an extensive portfolio of awards/proposals. Work is considered highly professional and technical, involving the review and processing of research and other types of grant proposals, negotiation of awards and contracts, and a variety of post-award non-financial administrative duties (no-cost extensions, amendments, compliances, problem-solving, etc.) This position serves on the contract team. The successful candidate will join several other research administrators in SPA and manage the high-level desk with the most complicated sponsors, contracts, and internal/external authorities. In addition to the current workload, the Grants Officer I serves as a mentor and helps train others in SPA. Due to the breadth of knowledge and experience, rarely need assistance with the most complicated sponsors/issues. Consistently demonstrates an ability to independently manage work queue, honor deadlines and performance metric expectations, resolve issues, and consistently demonstrate SPA Customer Service Standards. The employee will independently negotiate contracts and will possess signatory authority to bind the University to terms and conditions.</div> VPR-SPA Pre-Award https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503593 2026-08-31T10:26:57-04:00 2026-08-31T10:26:57-04:00 University Budget Analyst <div>This position provide will provide support for Schools, Colleges, Divisions and Units on campus along with support for the department heads and staff within the Budget Division. The incumbent will serve as the backup to the Budget Specialist which requires detailed analysis, data preparation and reporting. The focus and nature of this position requires professionalism, strong customer service and communication skills, exceptional organizational and time management skills, and attention to detail. In addition, this position deals with matters of a highly confidential nature.</div> FD-Budgets https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499793 2026-08-13T11:00:18-04:00 2026-08-13T11:00:19-04:00 Football Creative Services - Student Worker <div>This position will work with the Football Creative Services department to conceive, design and produce high quality digital and social content for UGA Football.</div> Athletics-Football https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478386 2026-04-22T17:16:37-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:38-04:00 Student Assistant - Esseili <div>This position will provide laboratory support to researchers.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478823 2026-04-22T17:50:09-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:09-04:00 Infectious Disease Forecasting Postdoctoral Position <div>The CEID Postdoctoral Scholar will serve as a scientist-in-residence, working on research projects with the CEID Infectious Disease Forecasting Working Group. Scholars will write scholarly articles and seek to publish research findings in academic journals. Research will also be shared to CEID members during workshops and other events, and to the greater scientific community through presentation at external conferences when appropriate. The selected individual(s) will have access to world class faculty and research scientists and an assigned faculty mentor, technical support for computational projects, and the opportunity to participate in CEID activities including workshops, seminars, collaborative projects and working groups. CEID Postdoctoral Scholars will either take a leadership role in an existing working group, or form a new working group(s) based on research areas of interest to the individual and other CEID members.</div> Ecology-Ctr Ecol of Infec Dis https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502024 2026-08-24T00:01:33-04:00 2026-08-24T00:01:34-04:00 Student Laboratory Assistant - Zock 2 <div>Upkeeping laboratory cleanliness, laboratory glassware, instrument training, calibration, and maintenance, dataset creation.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478508 2026-04-22T17:24:24-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:25-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant - Vines <div>This position will support a turfgrass breeding program by assisting with field maintenance, sample collection, laboratory processing, data entry, and preliminary data analysis. The individual will gain research experience and professional development with the potential to continue as a graduate student in the fall semester.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487860 2026-06-10T07:50:01-04:00 2026-06-10T14:40:27-04:00 Class Checker - Non-Student Assistant <div>As an Athletics Class Checker, your duties will include the following:</div><div>• Monitoring the daily attendance and promptness of a diverse group of student-athletes.<br>• Communicating regularly with Athletics Staff Members to ensure accountability.<br>• Logging detailed reports to inform Academic Counselors/Staff of daily occurrences.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478605 2026-04-22T17:32:42-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:43-04:00 Temporary Lab/Field Assistant Assist in maintaining plants in field and greenhouse conditions, as well as helping collect experimental data. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494790 2026-07-21T11:23:18-04:00 2026-07-21T11:23:18-04:00 Food Service Worker I (Partial Year) <div>*This is a benefits eligible, partial year position (9-11 months of the year) August 1st thru May 10th of each year. The selected candidate will need to sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.*&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary Village Summit https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477809 2026-04-21T17:50:37-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:37-04:00 COVID-19 Diagnostic Technician <div>This technician is responsible for planning, coordinating and executing the performance of all Molecular Diagnostic test procedures for the diagnosis and treatment of bacterial, viral and fungal diseases of animals.</div> VetMed-Athens Diagnostic Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478726 2026-04-22T17:40:42-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:43-04:00 Georgia 4-H Camp Counselor <div>This job is a Camp Counselor in the Georgia 4-H Summer camping program, located at one of five 4-H Facilities across the state. Counselors are expected to create a safe and fun environment for campers to participate in experiential learning and recreational opportunities, primarily in an outdoor, natural setting. Counselors also plan and produce entertainment opportunities for campers and work to coordinate these activities with UGA Cooperative Extension Staff and other Center staff.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498051 2026-08-05T10:28:41-04:00 2026-08-05T10:28:42-04:00 Administrative Associate II <div>The Administrative Associate II provides centralized financial and administrative operations support for the Executive Education unit. This role is responsible for managing transactional business processes including accounts receivable and payable coordination, vendor management, contract processing, faculty compensation coordination, inventory management, and financial documentation related to program delivery.<br><br>Working closely with the Executive Director, Director of Operations &amp; Learner Experience, and program delivery staff, the Administrative Associate II ensures that financial and operational processes are executed accurately, consistently, and in alignment with University of Georgia and Terry College policies.<br><br>The role serves as the primary liaison between Executive Education and the Terry College Business Office for financial transactions, contract processing, and financial documentation related to program operations. By centralizing these functions, the Administrative Associate enables program delivery staff and leadership to focus on growth, program development, and client engagement.</div> Terry-Executive Education https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478104 2026-04-21T18:34:17-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:18-04:00 Open Rank <div>The Athens Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory (AVDL), College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, Athens, GA invites applications for a full-time Veterinary Microbiologist with a keen interest in and enthusiasm for diagnostic microbiology and molecular biology. This is a twelve-month faculty position and can be either clinical (non-tenure) or tenure track with appointment at the level of assistant, associate, or full professor in a fully accredited diagnostic laboratory and NAHLN member.<br><br>This position will oversee bacteriology, mycology, and molecular biology sections of the AVDL as the Section Head of Microbiology. This position will also be in charge of the Research &amp; Development initiatives of the AVDL. This position would collaborate with faculty within and outside the AVDL toward developing new assay platforms and methodologies, and expanding our services. The AVDL is a fully accredited diagnostic laboratory by the Association of American Veterinary Laboratory Diagnosticians, that is also a member of the National Animal Health Laboratory Network. The laboratory provides services for veterinarians in the State of Georgia and beyond, and the UGA Veterinary Teaching Hospital. The AVDL performs more than 130,000 tests from more than 53,000 case submissions per year that include specimens from a wide variety of species such as dogs, cats, horses, pigs. small and large ruminants, New World camelids, and occasionally other animal species such as birds, reptiles, etc. The position will have emphasis on diagnostic service, and applied research toward development and validation of novel diagnostic assays and platforms. Teaching opportunities for the successful candidate include graduate, professional and undergraduate level courses offered by the Department of Infectious Diseases and/or Department of Pathology.<br><br>The percent commitment for this position would include up to 40% research, 50% diagnostic service, and 10% teaching /scholarly activities. Salary, rank, and terms of appointment will be dependent upon the qualifications and experience of the applicant.</div> VetMed-Infectious Diseases https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504269 2026-09-03T07:52:31-04:00 2026-09-03T07:52:32-04:00 Parking Compliance Monitor <div>This position is responsible for the enforcement of parking regulations and operational policies in campus lots and structures.</div> Auxiliary Parking Compliance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500737 2026-08-18T09:53:26-04:00 2026-08-18T09:53:27-04:00 Rural Development Fellow <div>The Rural Development Fellow will assist on a wide variety of economic development, workforce development, and community development technical assistance projects. This fellowship will last approximately 32 weeks. The purpose of this fellowship is to support the organization’s active project portfolio especially in rural Georgia through project coordination, administrative work, and project research. The position may assist with supporting client meetings and events outside the office. This position will serve a critical role in supporting several annual events including Georgia’s Workforce Conference, PROPEL Kick off/forum and PROPEL Ramble. Core tasks will include event support, meeting documentation, stakeholder interviews, applied research, report writing, and other administrative tasks as needed.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478438 2026-04-22T17:20:34-04:00 2026-05-01T13:51:12-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant - Joseph <div>This position is needed to support the Entomology department as a part of Dr. Joseph's research program with Turf and Ornamentals in Georgia. This position will assist the supervising faculty with research projects.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/482990 2026-05-13T15:40:31-04:00 2026-05-13T15:40:32-04:00 Horticulture Student Assistant -4 Deltsidis <div>Will perform a variety of duties involved in the research projects and activities of Dr. Deltsidis’ research program such as fruit and vegetable crop harvesting, postharvest experiments, sample preparation in the lab, and produce quality-related analyses. Upkeep of laboratory space and data entry are also part of this position. All tasks will be performed under the direction and supervision of the lab manager.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478556 2026-04-22T17:29:27-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:28-04:00 Student Employee This position is responsible for milking cows and feeding calves at the University of Georgia Teaching Dairy. This position is only open to students enrolled at a college/university. The cows are milked twice a day and the calves get fed twice a day as well. The job may also include completing chores around the farm that are necessary to help the farm run successfully, such as grounds maintenance, putting out hay, vaccinations, timed AI shots and cattle movements. CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491734 2026-07-07T09:00:51-04:00 2026-07-07T09:00:51-04:00 4-H Monroe County AmeriCorps Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members will comply with AmeriCorps guidelines such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other trainings.</div><div>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members will log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500334 2026-08-17T08:26:26-04:00 2026-08-17T08:26:27-04:00 ADS Student Assistant Beef 4 <div>The Student Research Assistant supports and assists with daily research operations under the supervision of the Senior Farm Manager. This position works closely with research technicians, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers to support team objectives and contribute to research outcomes.<br><br>Responsibilities include following established research and animal care protocols, assisting with data collection and recordkeeping, supporting project implementation, and helping maintain research facilities and equipment.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478411 2026-04-22T17:19:49-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:49-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate AD <div>The post-doctoral researcher will work on a variety of projects in quantitative genetics and genomics, ranging from practical to theoretical, will develop novel methods to be applied in animal breeding and genetics, and perform analyses in fish data .</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479829 2026-04-28T14:46:54-04:00 2026-04-28T14:46:55-04:00 Part-time Food Service Worker - Rock Eagle <div>Work involves preparing and serving food and cleaning food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision, follow written and/or oral procedures and practices. Employee will implement these procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478530 2026-04-22T17:25:45-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:45-04:00 Federal Work Study - Soil & Water Lab <div>A part-time student technician (federal work-study) to work in the soil and water lab within the Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources beginning Fall 2023. Responsibilities consist primarily of laboratory and data entry components, with possibilities for occasional field work.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490218 2026-06-26T06:54:43-04:00 2026-06-26T06:54:44-04:00 CONSTRUCTION WORKER I <div>This an entry level position whose main emphasis is to support and assist skilled tradesmen in day to day construction activities. The work will be supervised by a foreman and to a lesser degree by the skilled workers being assisted. Support and assistance includes helping to form and place concrete, potholing utilities and serving as a spotter during excavation, assisting in backfill, grading, asphalt placement and other jobsite activities. Also maintaining barricades, signage and performing traffic control. It includes using hand tools and small machinery such as cutoff saws, jackhammers, tamps and drills. It also includes performing any other duties as needed. In addition, this position will report during inclement weather to assist with downed tree removal and snow and ice removal.<br><br></div> FMD-Grounds-Construction https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478626 2026-04-22T17:33:50-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:50-04:00 Post Doc Research Associate Burg Lab <div>The postdoctoral associate will conduct research on a pre-specified project as well as ones of their own design and publish that research. The postdoc will take on senior responsibilities like research mentoring, grant writing, and publishing. Primary responsibilities will include management and implementation of tissue engineering studies in the Harbor Lights Laboratory. A research leader with background in biomaterials and cell biology is needed in order to manage coordinate the day-to-day research activities in the laboratory.&nbsp;<br><br></div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495590 2026-07-23T16:36:30-04:00 2026-07-23T16:36:30-04:00 Maintenance Assistant <div>The primary purpose of this position is to lend assistance to skilled trade and maintenance workers with the installation, maintenance and repair of machinery, electrical and/or electronic components found within Housing facilities.</div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477850 2026-04-21T17:59:49-04:00 2026-04-21T17:59:50-04:00 Part-Time Food Service Worker - Burton 4-H Center <div>This position is based on the Burton 4-H Center on Tybee Island (http://georgia4h.org/4-h-centers/burton-4-h-center/). Work involves food preparation, serving, and cleaning the food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision while involved in preparation of food, serving, and cleaning.</div> CAES-Burton 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503105 2026-08-27T10:58:28-04:00 2026-08-27T10:58:29-04:00 Res Assc-Social Science IV <div>This senior-level position, within the Government Services and Research Division’s Local Government Unit, supports the Institute’s diverse portfolio of applied research and technical assistance work addressing local government operations, organizational effectiveness, staffing analyses, and financial studies. This position conducts significant applied research and technical assistance while serving as senior collaborator and managing complex public sector initiatives under the general guidance of faculty and project leadership.<br><br>The role drives substantive aspects of project execution, including research design, qualitative and quantitative analysis, data interpretation, and the creation of final deliverables. To ensure seamless project planning and continuity across multiple concurrent initiatives, the position collaborates closely with faculty, research professionals, local government officials, and external stakeholders.<br><br>This role requires a high degree of professional judgment, independent analytical thinking, and the ability to translate complex research into actionable recommendations for local government clients. Additional responsibilities include contributing to proposal development, supporting project coordination, facilitating stakeholder engagement, and driving the continued growth and effectiveness of the Local Government Unit’s applied research and technical assistance services.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498928 2026-08-10T12:23:52-04:00 2026-08-10T12:23:52-04:00 Part-Time Advanced Practice Practitioner - Dermatology <div>The part-time Nurse Practitioner for Dermatology plays a key role within Medical Services and reports to the Primary Care Lead Physician. This position’s primary responsibility is to provide comprehensive, age-appropriate dermatologic care, including assessment, diagnosis, treatment, prevention, and patient education for eligible members of the University Community at the University of Georgia Health Center. In collaboration with primary care clinicians, specialty providers, nursing staff, and other Health Center personnel, this role also serves as a dermatologic resource in both consultative and referral capacities.</div> UHC-Medical Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478368 2026-04-22T17:16:05-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:05-04:00 Temporary Lab/Field Research - Chavez This position will work both indoors and outdoors doing primarily field and laboratory work for peach, blueberry and grape research projects. Fieldwork includes, but is not limited to, helping to plant, maintain, harvest and process field studies. Work in the field and greenhouse will be done in hot conditions. Laboratory work includes, but is not limited to, processing samples, dissection, extraction, and others.  The employee receives specific work instructions at the beginning of each new task and the work is closely supervised until the employee is capable of consistently performing the task. CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478798 2026-04-22T17:46:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:33-04:00 Temporary Field/Summer Assistant - Raymer <div>To assist in field preparation, maintenance, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504559 2026-09-04T10:37:41-04:00 2026-09-04T10:37:41-04:00 Horticulture Student Asst. Conner 2 <div>Individual will assist with the field, seed processing, laboratory and greenhouse activities. Crucial field activities include data collection and harvesting along with other miscellaneous duties. Additional duties will involve helping with seed processing shelling, data collection, organizing) and greenhouse work (plant cultivation and crossing) when needed. Laboratory activities include conducting polymerase chain reaction for marker-assisted selection. Individual will work as a part of a team.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501313 2026-08-19T14:22:14-04:00 2026-08-19T14:22:14-04:00 Senior Event Coordinator <div>The Event Planner is responsible for planning, coordinating, and overseeing complex meetings, conferences, and special events from initial planning through on-site execution. The individual serves as the primary liaison for clients, managing event logistics, vendor coordination, catering, lodging, technical services, staffing, and security needs to ensure a successful event experience. Responsibilities include negotiating contracts, preparing and managing budgets, monitoring conference center expenditures, and ensuring accurate billing for all event-related charges.<br><br>The position involves building and maintaining strong relationships with clients, vendors, and stakeholders while providing exceptional customer service.</div> CAES-Tifton Conf Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478490 2026-04-22T17:23:52-04:00 2026-04-22T17:23:53-04:00 Postdoc Nibbelink This postdoc will coordinate and execute our work with the US Army Corps of Engineers (USACE) to develop a framework and geospatial tool(s) for the prioritization of landscape elements with respect to the potential to use natural infrastructure solutions for flood risk reduction in addition to water quality, habitat, and other social benefits in the context of engineering decision making and civil works projects. This process will allow stakeholders to visualize and prioritize geographic areas where natural infrastructure solutions might maximize multiple ecosystem services. The postdoc will coordinate team members (faculty, students, USACE partners, international partners), review literature, build a conceptual model, collect and manage spatial data, conduct analyses, build an initial version of a prioritization tool, and write reports/articles for various outlets. Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486079 2026-05-29T16:14:29-04:00 2026-05-29T16:14:29-04:00 Grants Coordinator III <div>This is a highly responsible professional Staff position working with College of Engineering Faculty and the Office for Sponsored Programs, involving the submission and approval of external funding applications. This position will primarily work with faculty in development, preparation, and review of proposals for external funding, as well as submit proposals to sponsors within DLSA limits, and coordinate submission of proposals outside DLSA limits with College of Engineering Grants Coordinators and/or SPA.<br><br>This position will serve as a Decentralized Limited Signatory Authority (DLSA) and is expected to complete the necessary certification for a phase-2 DLSA within the first 3 months of employment.<br><br>This position will serve as a resource to the College of Engineering and investigators in administration of sponsored projects.</div> ENGR-Research & Grad Studies https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478577 2026-04-22T17:30:06-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:07-04:00 Student Assistant Franklin-Psychology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493306 2026-07-14T14:48:08-04:00 2026-07-14T14:48:08-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Journalism and the University of Georgia’s Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in journalism to begin in August 2027.&nbsp;<br><br>The department and college have a collegial and productive culture of research and teaching, engaged students, and promote a supportive environment for individual growth.&nbsp;<br><br>The successful candidate must be able to teach effectively in our journalism curriculum at the undergraduate and graduate levels and in our college-wide Ph.D. program, and regularly publish peer-reviewed research in our field. Mentoring graduate students and service to the college is also expected. The effort allocation for the position is 50% teaching, 45% research, and 5% service.</div> Grady-Journalism Department https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477480 2026-04-20T16:54:29-04:00 2026-04-20T16:54:29-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>The Wells Lab, in the Complex Carbohydrate Research Center at the University of Georgia, is seeking a motivated <strong>Biochemist/Cell Biologist</strong> to explore the <strong>O-Mannose pathway</strong> and its role in <strong>Congenital Muscular Dystrophy (CMD)</strong>. This position is part of a robust research program funded by the <strong>NIH</strong>, <strong>NSF (BioFoundry)</strong>, and the <strong>Michael J. Fox Foundation</strong>. You will bridge glycobiology and functional genomics, focusing on how defective O-mannosylation leads to muscle and neural phenotypes in a highly collaborative, well-funded environment.<br><br></div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478700 2026-04-22T17:39:28-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:29-04:00 The Oglethorpe Echo Ad Sales <div>&nbsp;The right candidate will be paid $12.50 an hour for 10 hours a week (hours include commute time). Duties include selling print and digital ads for The Echo, a 151-year old weekly newspaper in Oglethorpe County, and its special sections. Other duties include delivering weekly papers to local businesses and maintaining established business relationships with contacts, creating monthly house ads, selling print and digitals, helping to create feature pages and ad campaigns alongside the business and marketing managers, and other duties as assigned. To assist the business and marketing managers at The Oglethorpe Echo.<br><br><br></div> Grady-Journalism Department https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497467 2026-08-03T11:19:00-04:00 2026-08-03T11:19:00-04:00 Communications Specialist <div>This role splits time between the Office of Instruction (OVPI) and the Office of Service-Learning (OSL), reporting jointly to OVPI’s Director of Communications and the OSL Director. The communications specialist plans, coordinates, writes, and edits a wide variety of content to promote the university's broader instructional and service-learning missions. Working closely with campus units, internal stakeholders, and other communications staff, this position coordinates content production and aligns messaging with the division's overall communications strategy.<br><br></div> VPI-VP of Instruction https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478008 2026-04-21T18:25:39-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:41-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the level of Assistant Professor. We seek an individual who will build and maintain a strong extramurally-funded research program in the area of pharmaceutical and biomedical sciences, such as AI drug discovery, cancer biology, medicinal chemistry, pharmacology, or pharmacokinetics. The successful candidate will complement and build upon the Department’s existing research strengths, which include active programs in chemical biology, pharmacology and pharmaceutics, cancer biology, and infectious diseases.<br><br><strong>Research Areas of Interest</strong>&nbsp;</div><div>Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>AI/computational drug discovery&nbsp;</li><li>Computational or virtual drug screening&nbsp;</li><li>Chemical biology&nbsp;</li><li>Pharmacology&nbsp;</li><li>Immunology&nbsp;</li><li>Cancer biology&nbsp;</li><li>Drug formulation or drug delivery&nbsp;</li><li>Medicinal chemistry&nbsp;</li><li>Toxicology&nbsp;</li><li>Systems biology&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br>The Department offers a competitive salary, excellent laboratory space, and a generous start-up package to support the successful candidate’s research program.&nbsp;</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504088 2026-09-01T17:12:15-04:00 2026-09-01T17:12:16-04:00 Mental Health Case Manager <div>The Mental Health Case Manager is an essential member of the Integrated Care Team and will provide appropriate and individualized case management to students and eligible partners. This position manages the referral and tracking of clients sent to other clinics within the UHC, discharged to the community, and/or transferred to a higher level of care. The Mental Health Case Manager will help obtain past and ongoing treatment records and be an active member of the Case Disposition Team. The Mental Health Case Manager will also provide primary, secondary, and tertiary services to eligible members of the UGA community, within the UHC mental health care scope of service. These services may include group, individual, crisis interventions, outreach, and consultation. Licensed Clinicians provide mental health evaluations, formulation of conceptualization, diagnoses, treatment plans, and crisis intervention. Services are delivered in accordance with UHC/CAPS policies and procedures.</div> UHC-Counseling & Psych Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491830 2026-07-07T12:37:46-04:00 2026-07-07T12:37:47-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - SUN <div>This position in the Department of Plant Pathology will conduct cutting-edge research on the molecular biology and genetics of plant RNA viruses. Current research focuses on understanding host responses to vascular invading viruses.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478652 2026-04-22T17:36:48-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:49-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate AD <div>The post-doctoral researcher will work on a variety of projects in quantitative genetics and genomics, ranging from practical to theoretical, will develop novel methods to be applied in animal breeding and genetics, and perform analyses in fish data .</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496669 2026-07-29T10:55:32-04:00 2026-07-29T10:55:33-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Management Information Systems in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for one or more full-time tenure-track faculty position(s) at the assistant professor level. The position(s) will begin fall semester 2027, with an anticipated employment start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Mgmt Information Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477916 2026-04-21T18:06:03-04:00 2026-04-21T18:06:04-04:00 Research Tech III-Tarleton <div>Research Tech position in moderate sized, highly dynamic, and productive research lab working in immunity to human parasitic infections using primarily mouse models. Specific duties will vary with the project but may include maintenance of cultured cells and parasites, performance of in vitro and in vivo tests for the effectiveness of antiparasite drugs, plasmid construction, CRISPR screening, immunological assays (Luminex, Flow Cytometry), tissue preparation, and microscopy. Many opportunities will exist for developing a diverse skill set and for gaining experience and independence in designing and executing research experiments and protocols. A successful candidate will be able to prioritize work duties and manage the details of experiment execution. A successful applicant will be willing to work with mice and human pathogens.</div> VPR-Center Trop Emerg Glob Dis https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503609 2026-08-31T11:35:37-04:00 2026-08-31T11:35:38-04:00 Building Services Worker II <div>The Building Services Worker II duties are inclusive of those of the BSW I; sweeps, dust mop, wet mop, dusts, high dusts, light floor care. Cleans windows, window sills, walls, furniture, and other equipment in and around university buildings and grounds. Collects and removes bulk quantities of trash and recyclables. Secures and unlocks university buildings. Delivers, receives, and transports miscellaneous supplies and materials to and from various buildings. Performs cleaning and disinfection on surfaces such as: glass, windows, doors, electrical switches, Venetian blinds, and other building related equipment in classrooms, restrooms, administrative buildings, recreational and fitness building, laboratories, medical clinics, etc. Maintains adequate supplies in restrooms and janitorial closets. May be needed to perform bodily fluid clean-up or specialized viral/bacterial disinfection. Performs minor light bulb replacement from an 8' ladder.<br><br>In addition, the BSWII performs floor care with large specialized floor care equipment: carpet cleaning and extraction, strip / wax / burnish floors, refinish wood floors, etc. Responsible to the safe operation and operator level maintenance of assigned equipment. Responsible for building walk-through inspections on weekly basis, assist with equipment inspections of building cleaning machine and tools, and the submission of building and/or equipment inspection form to lead/supervisor.</div> FMD-Svcs-Blding Svcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500055 2026-08-13T17:32:11-04:00 2026-08-13T17:32:12-04:00 Open Rank - Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor <div>The University of Georgia’s Victoria Kay Ivester School of Nursing invites applications for an open-rank, non-tenure-track clinical faculty position at the Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor level. Rank will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will contribute to the development and launch of UGA’s new School of Nursing and its prelicensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing program. Primary responsibilities include teaching across didactic, laboratory, simulation, and clinical settings; maintaining clinical expertise; engaging in educational and/or clinical scholarship; and contributing to service within the School, University, profession, and broader community. The faculty member will also have opportunities to help shape curriculum, establish innovative teaching practices, develop strong clinical partnerships, and build the culture and academic foundation of a new nursing school.<br><br></div><div>This position supports the School’s mission to prepare future nurses through excellence in teaching, evidence-based practice, innovation, and meaningful engagement with clinical and community partners. This clinical-track appointment is not eligible for tenure.</div> SON-Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478389 2026-04-22T17:16:42-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:43-04:00 Student Assistant - Cain <div>Must be able to work independently, have excellent problem-solving skills, and good interpersonal and customer service skills. Duties will include data entry, providing reception and phone coverage, providing duplicates, handling fax and email communications. Help staff with mailings, event planning, room set-up, and other duties as needed.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478825 2026-04-22T17:50:13-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:14-04:00 Event Management and Facilities Intern <div>Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: hiring and supervising student staff, on-site event management of selected sports, scheduling staff for various athletic events, assisting full-time facility staff with set-up/break down of home athletic events, contacting visiting teams and officials, creating and/or updating athletic operations manuals, coordinating and guiding tours of Athletic Association facilities, managing special events and rentals, assisting staff with facility maintenance and projects and performing day-to-day-office duties.</div> Athletics-Event Management https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502234 2026-08-24T14:41:39-04:00 2026-08-24T14:41:39-04:00 Director of Gift and Estate Planning <div>Reporting to the Senior Director of Gift &amp; Estate Planning in the Division of Development &amp; Alumni Relations, the Director of Gift &amp; Estate Planning is critical to University of Georgia’s efforts to identify and cultivate private support across all schools, colleges, and units on campus. The position is responsible for independently managing a portfolio of donors and prospects capable of making significant planned gifts. This position contributes directly to university-wide fundraising goals and is one of the key efforts to raise private funds that support student career preparation, scholarships, faculty support, research, innovation, public service and outreach, facility renovations as well as unrestricted money. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>This position focuses on managing a pipeline of deferred major gifts by establishing annual goals for individual donor prospects and advising development partners within schools, colleges, and units on planned giving strategy. The position works collaboratively with UGA Foundation trustees and other key volunteers as needed on university-wide and unit-based planned giving efforts.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Director of Gift &amp; Estate Planning also serves as the liaison and subject-matter expert to other development officers across campus and therefore is critical to the central development team’s ability to support cross-campus collaboration and strategy development for prospects and donors capable of major gifts ($50k+).</div><div><br></div> DAR-Gift & Estate Planning https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478510 2026-04-22T17:24:28-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:28-04:00 Turfgrass Field Assistant <div>This position will assist Turfgrass researchers with field experiments conducted on turfgrass on the UGA Griffin Campus.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487984 2026-06-10T15:14:51-04:00 2026-07-23T15:49:10-04:00 Culinary Server for Georgia Football - Student Assistant <div>The server will assist the Culinary Service Manager in executing front of the house service for Georgia Football. This person will need to follow proper cleaning and sanitation procedures as well as multitask. They will also be responsible for stocking front of house, which includes but is not limited to various fueling stations, food service lines and tabletops.</div> Athletics-Football Nutrition https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478608 2026-04-22T17:32:48-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:49-04:00 Student Bus Detailer This position is responsible for the end-of-day transportation fleet detailing that supports Campus Transit Operations. Auxiliary Transit Maint https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494816 2026-07-21T11:42:39-04:00 2026-07-21T11:42:40-04:00 Food Service Worker I <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477811 2026-04-21T17:50:41-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:42-04:00 Research Assistant/Tech <div>Assist graduate students, professor, and laboratory coordinator with various research projects that are ongoing in the laboratory and in the field. This will entail field collecting of insect samples, correct preparation and preservation of specimens, sorting insects in the lab, cleaning and maintain field equipment, data entry, and microscope work. This is a limited term position and is contingent on funding. Position will end September 2022.&nbsp;</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478736 2026-04-22T17:41:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:41:48-04:00 Sustainability Research Assistant (Wood Value Chains) <div>Our project aims to gain novel actionable insights about how industrial structure, business-society interactions and forest ecosystems shape outlook of development of sustainable wood-based sector in two heavily forested and industrialized regions; US southeast and Nordics facing emerging environmental and economic disruptions. The student will support data collection and methodological development to generate insights into the sustainability impacts and potential of wood use, with a focus on the U.S. and the U.S. Southeast.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498094 2026-08-05T11:52:54-04:00 2026-08-05T11:52:54-04:00 Ticket Office Student Assistant <div>This position is responsible for answering phones, assisting customers in person at the Butts-Mehre ticket window, and occasional email correspondence with current and prospective ticket buyers. Assisting the Director and Assistant Director of Ticket Operations with various projects including, but not limited to, season and single game ticket allocations, fulfilling ticket requests, and mailing ticket orders. Additional responsibilities will include Paciolan ticketing system proficiency, customer record confidentiality, familiarity with athletic venues and parking regulations, and StubHub integration support.</div> Athletics-Ticket Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478113 2026-04-21T18:34:38-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:39-04:00 Open Rank in Counseling Psychology <div>We are seeking an exceptional and experienced candidate for an open-rank, tenure-track position in the Counseling Psychology doctoral (APA accredited) and Mental Health Counseling master’s (MPCAC accredited) programs in the Department of Counseling and Human Development Services at the University of Georgia to begin August 1, 2026. Specifically, we seek a candidate whose program of work demonstrates innovation, inclusive excellence, and interdisciplinarity to continually enhance research and teaching excellence for our doctoral and master’s students as well as advances our department’s goals and aligns with the Mary Frances Early College of Education’s mission.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong> for this position include: 1) teaching core graduate courses in counseling psychology, mental health counseling; 2) providing clinical supervision of field experiences in counseling psychology and mental health counseling; 3) conducting research that is relevant to the field of counseling psychology; 4) advising doctoral students and serving on dissertation committees; and 5) contributing service to university, college, departmental, and program committees, to professional associations, and to local, national, and/or international communities. The MFE COE recognizes that the scholarly work of faculty often includes the integration of teaching, research, and service.</div> COE-Counseling & Human Dev Svc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504286 2026-09-03T09:23:35-04:00 2026-09-03T09:23:36-04:00 Senior Creative Design Specialist <div>This position reports to the Creative Director and plays a key role in advancing and stewarding the visual identity of Development and Alumni Relations (DAR). The role works closely with other Creative Design Specialists within the Development and Alumni Relations Communications department (DARCOMM) and, when applicable, Creative Team student staff.</div><div>This position is responsible for the planning, development, and execution of graphic design solutions supporting clients and units within DAR. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, consulting with clients and developing and implementing designs through multiple communication mediums (e.g., web, social media platforms, digital advertising, signage, promotional marks, promotional merchandise, and print products such as mailers, invitations, and magazines). Responsibilities also include contributing to the development and execution of divisional marketing and communication strategies, as well as overseeing promotional merchandise vendor relationships and leading merchandise innovation efforts.&nbsp;</div><div>This position ensures all design work complies with the visual identity and branding of the University of Georgia and the Division of Development and Alumni Relations and requires independent initiative in supporting the university visual identity and trademark approval process. This includes collaborating with other Creative Design Specialists and the Creative Director to interpret, apply, and support implementation of branding standards and visual identity guidelines to ensure a cohesive brand presence across everything produced in the division. In addition, this position identifies opportunities and recommends new communication strategies and creative tactics that enhance the effectiveness of DAR communications.</div><div>This position is critical in helping DAR create and implement a consistent, branded communication plan, contributing to key communication initiatives and milestones, helping strengthen the quality, innovation, and effectiveness of DAR’s outreach to alumni and donors.</div> DAR-Communications https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500801 2026-08-18T11:27:01-04:00 2026-08-18T11:27:02-04:00 Peanut Research Technician- Tifton Campus <div>The Research Technician position will be under the Assistant Dean's office based at the University of Georgia Tifton Campus; however, frequent travel to research farms and off-site locations throughout Georgia's peanut production regions will be necessary to support breeding and variety evaluation activities. At appointment, the person in this position will assist with research that focuses on all aspects of peanut production. The primary focus of current research projects is to support peanut breeding and agronomic programs and initiatives. This position will also provide assistance, as needed, to other research areas related to peanut improvement and production. This role will involve collaborating with and assisting researchers, graduate students, technicians, and student workers to achieve program objectives and support ongoing research activities.</div><div><br>General responsibilities will include routine field maintenance such as cultivation, spraying, fertilization, irrigation, and other crop management activities necessary for successful field research. Additional duties will include tissue sampling, data collection in field and laboratory settings, plot establishment and maintenance, plant and plot harvesting, peanut grading and shelling, seed packaging and inventory management, planting, and operation of research equipment.</div> CAES-Tifton Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478440 2026-04-22T17:20:38-04:00 2026-05-20T12:26:18-04:00 Temporary Field Assistant - Pritchard <div>This position will provide assistance in establishing new turf plots, maintaining existing research plots and greenhouse research.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483236 2026-05-14T14:44:57-04:00 2026-05-14T14:44:57-04:00 Limited Term Lecturer <div>The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences (PBS) at the University of Georgia invites applications for three limited-term (one-year) full-time (9-month) Lecturer positions. This appointment is primarily focused on supporting the instructional mission of the department by contributing to teaching in the undergraduate and PharmD programs, particularly in areas related to pharmaceutical and biomedical sciences. Please refer to our curriculum at <a href=\"https://rx.uga.edu/academic-programs/bachelor-of-science-2/\"><strong>https://rx.uga.edu/academic-programs/bachelor-of-science-2/</strong></a> for additional details.</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478558 2026-04-22T17:29:31-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:32-04:00 Compliance Monitor (Student) <div>Enforcement of parking regulations and operational policies in campus lots and structures. Strong, professional customer service.</div> Auxiliary Parking Compliance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504097 2026-09-02T08:26:38-04:00 2026-09-02T08:26:38-04:00 Community Partnerships Coordinator <div>The Office of Service-Learning (OSL) is looking for an energetic, conscientious, and self-directed professional to coordinate and expand an after-school literacy and sports coaching program. The successful candidate will have a unique professional opportunity to provide essential leadership for expanding a community after-school program that can serve as a model throughout the state to enrich literacy instruction and provide increased access to youth sports programs.<br><br></div><div>The mission of the University of Georgia Office of Service-Learning is to support academic service-learning and community engagement initiatives that enhance student learning, support engaged scholarship, and address community needs. The OSL is a jointly supported unit of Public Service and Outreach and the Office of Instruction.<br><br></div><div>The OSL serves as a hub for campus and community collaborations and works with over 100 community partners each year. The program coordinator will engage with and provide support for school-based partnerships. This full-time position will report to the assistant director for community partnerships in the Office of Service-Learning.<br><br></div><div>Primary responsibilities include the following key activities:</div><ul><li>Coordinating all aspects of after-school program.</li><li>supervising graduate assistant and Lead Success Coaches</li><li>Managing student workers.</li><li>Facilitating UGA service-learning projects and recruiting UGA student volunteers.</li><li>Developing and delivering training and preparation for UGA students involved in the after-school program.</li><li>Working with internal and external partners to evaluate program success.</li></ul><div><br><br></div> VPI-Service Learning https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500355 2026-08-17T09:08:51-04:00 2026-08-17T09:08:52-04:00 DeKalb County Program Assistant - EFNEP <div>This position is based in DeKalb County. This position is responsible paraprofessional work with County Extension Agents in a food and nutrition education program for limited resource clients. The employee will exhibit qualities of independent judgment. Work is performed under general supervision.<br><br>Job duties include planning, organizing, scheduling, and conducting nutrition and food safety classes for limited resource clients, including youth and adults, under supervision of County Extension Agent. Job duties also include assisting the County Extension Agent by researching and providing information requested by clients.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478413 2026-04-22T17:19:52-04:00 2026-08-17T14:01:00-04:00 Temporary Laboratory Assistant <div>The position of laboratory assistant will support client projects by doing work to support project completion. This work includes conducting laboratory and microbiology analysis, and also conducting product and process tests. The work includes completion of test documentation and report writing.</div> CAES-Food Prod Inno & Comm Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479838 2026-04-28T15:07:27-04:00 2026-04-28T15:07:28-04:00 Part-time Food Service Worker - Rock Eagle <div>Work involves preparing and serving food and cleaning food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision, follow written and/or oral procedures and practices. Employee will implement these procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478533 2026-04-22T17:25:50-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:50-04:00 Student Assistant (PIL) <div><em>Duties and Responsibilities will depend on the interests and talents of the successful applicant, but may include writing reports or articles about the work of the lab, assisting with the creation of training materials for in-country partners, designing graphics, conducting literature reviews or creating other research products, completing logistical tasks necessary for team meetings and travel, or other duties necessary for lab operations.</em></div> CAES-Peanut Innovation Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490462 2026-06-26T17:09:05-04:00 2026-06-26T17:09:06-04:00 AI Research Facilitator <div>The Georgia Advanced Computing Resource Center (GACRC), a division of Enterprise Information Technology Services at the University of Georgia, seeks to establish an <strong><em>AI Research Facilitator</em></strong> position to support the University’s rapidly expanding needs in artificial intelligence and data-driven research. The GACRC provides advanced computing and research storage services to more than 500 research groups, and recent multimillion-dollar investments in GPU-accelerated infrastructure have positioned UGA to support leading-edge AI research across disciplines.</div><div>Over the past three years, the University has undertaken the Presidential Interdisciplinary Faculty Hiring Initiative in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, bringing approximately 70 new faculty hires to campus. At the same time, existing faculty across the sciences, social sciences, humanities, arts, and professional programs are increasingly incorporating AI and machine learning into their research portfolios. To fully realize the potential of these rapidly growing AI-driven initiatives, UGA must provide specialized, human-centered research support that complements its advanced computing investments. The AI Research Facilitator will play a central role in enabling faculty to effectively leverage AI methodologies, accelerating research impact across the institution.</div> EITS-Research Computing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478629 2026-04-22T17:33:55-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:56-04:00 Student Assistant (NE) CAES-Ag Leadership, Ed & Comm https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495627 2026-07-24T09:24:12-04:00 2026-07-24T09:24:13-04:00 Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provosts <div>This position provides administrative support to the Office of the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost and serves as an integral member of the staff support team. The position provides primary administrative support for the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs and the Vice Provost for Academic and Community Engagement. Working collaboratively with other staff, this position helps ensure efficient and effective service delivery within the Provost’s Office. The position routinely handles confidential matters and must exercise sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism.</div> SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477853 2026-04-21T17:59:56-04:00 2026-04-21T17:59:57-04:00 Phlebotomist - Shape IV <div>The primary responsibility of the Phlebotomist is collecting and processing blood samples (e.g., centrifuging in the field, performing aliquots onsite) as well as proper labeling, adherence to biosafety procedures and transporting samples safely. Phlebotomist also collects bio-marker data (e.g., blood pressure, height, weight, hip/waist measures). Other duties include obtaining informed consent and completing all visit paperwork.</div> VPR-Center for Family Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503161 2026-08-27T13:10:13-04:00 2026-08-27T13:10:13-04:00 Office Manager <div>The Office Manager in the Office of Special Events is responsible for coordinating and managing the administrative activities of the office and providing administrative support to members of the Special Events staff. This position processes invoices and payments, manages office leases and contracts, supports human resources activities, orders supplies, maintains office inventories and assets, and assists with budget-related functions.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>This position interacts with a variety of external callers, visitors, and internal contacts at all levels of the organization. Independent judgment is required to plan, prioritize, and organize a varied workload while managing multiple responsibilities and deadlines. This position is essential to the mission of the department by providing excellent customer service to constituents and supporting the operation of a highly organized and productive unit.</div> DAR-Office of Special Events https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499263 2026-08-11T11:55:32-04:00 2026-08-11T11:55:33-04:00 Student Worker Assistant <div>Tsai lab in Davison Life Sciences is looking for student assistants to help with general upkeep and running of a plant genomics research laboratory. Tasks include washing glassware, plant tissue processing and disposal, stocking supplies, general cleaning, and preparation of common reagents. Preferred schedule is 3 hours/day, 3-5 days/week, which can include some weekend shifts.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478371 2026-04-22T17:16:10-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:10-04:00 Temporary Field Assistant - Plant Genetics <div>This part-time position is needed to assist with vegetable curation. This position will assist with harvesting fruit from various vegetable crops in the field and greenhouse; extracting seed from the harvested fruit; cleaning and packaging of seed, and miscellaneous duties as assigned.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478800 2026-04-22T17:46:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:37-04:00 Student Research Assistant - Nematology (2) <div>This position involves sorting and recording nematode plant and soil samples that received from our clients, filling of 100cc beakers with soil, extracting plant-parasitic nematodes from samples, accurately entering nematode assay results into a database system, washing glassware, discarding of leftover soil and plant samples, keeping the lab neat and clean, and if necessary, sterilizing glassware, remaining out-of-state soil samples and other related materials in an autoclave. In addition to processing nematode diagnostic samples, incumbent would work on various greenhouse and field research projects on the management of plant-parasitic nematodes associated with different crops. Specifically, incumbent would maintain both greenhouse and field experiments, apply treatments, and may travel to layout trials and record relevant data.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504644 2026-09-04T14:05:24-04:00 2026-09-04T14:05:24-04:00 Digital Marketing Strategist <div>The Digital Marketing Strategist is a member of the Odum School’s communications team and reports to the Communications Director. This position plans and produces content for social media and other digital platforms, including managing the social media content calendar, drafting and editing copy and graphics, capturing photos and videos as needed, and supporting integrated marketing campaigns.<br><br></div><div>The position oversees Odum School accounts (Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook and Blue Sky) and River Basin Center (RBC) accounts (Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook), tracking and reporting analytics and assisting in setting benchmarks. This position will spend 80% time on Odum School and 20% time on RBC social media.<br><br></div><div>This position collaborates with faculty, staff, students, alumni and campus partners to identify storytelling opportunities and translate complex academic programs, research and outreach activities into engaging communications. They will participate in ongoing content strategy sessions with communications team members and are expected to provide ideas and produce original content. There is room for growth in developing paid social media strategies to support School/Center initiatives, and this position will play a significant role in leading those efforts.</div><div><br>Success in this role requires strong writing and storytelling skills, creativity, organization, attention to detail, and the ability to plan and execute digital communications that build engagement, highlight student experiences, and strengthen the Odum and RBC brands.</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501437 2026-08-19T17:07:50-04:00 2026-08-26T10:34:25-04:00 Academic Services Professional/Co-Director <div>The Academic Services Professional supports student success and timely degree completion through academic advising, program administration, and student services. This position differs from Academic Services Paraprofessional roles in its higher level of autonomy, leadership responsibilities, and strategic decision-making.<br><br></div><div>Reporting directly to the Senior Associate Dean for Academic Programs and Graduate Education, this position provides leadership and oversight for undergraduate advising across the college. Responsibilities include coordinating advising staff for all undergraduate programs, directly supporting two Lead Academic Advisors and providing indirect supervision to 8-10 Academic Advisors. The role also oversees advising office operations, leads strategic initiatives for the Mary Frances Early College of Education, manages budget development and related fiscal responsibilities, serves on committees, supports the Office of Academic Programs, and performs other duties as assigned.</div> COE-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478493 2026-04-22T17:23:57-04:00 2026-04-22T17:23:58-04:00 Hort Rubio-Ames PhD Grad Student <div>The Small Fruit Research and Extension Lab is seeking a resourceful and motivated individual interested in Horticulture, especially blueberry production and management to fill 1 PhD research assistantship in the Department of Horticulture at the University of Georgia’s Tifton campus.&nbsp; Potential research topics are flexible but will have a general focus on blueberry production and cultural management practices (fertilization, pruning, and water management), and alternative blueberry production systems. The candidate chosen for the position will have the opportunity to cultivate the necessary skills in the field as well as gain outreach and extension experiences, and overall professional development relevant to future careers in the industry and academia.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486604 2026-06-02T16:17:51-04:00 2026-06-02T16:17:52-04:00 FoodPro Assistant Manager <div>Reporting to the FoodPro Manager, the primary function of the FoodPro Assistant Manager will be to perform daily invoice entry and product maintenance within FoodPro. Under the supervision of the FoodPro Manager, the FoodPro Assistant Manager will also provide support and guidance to units on daily activities needed for inventory and invoicing. These include developing/maintaining SOPs for receiving product from external vendors, transferring goods between Dining locations, taking weekly inventory and report analysis to ensure all units are operating at the highest level for current and future fiscal and production weeks. Responsibilities also include serving as the back-up to the FoodPro Manager. Will also serve as backup for POS Manager as needed. Provide training and support to all units on the process of receiving goods to and/or from respective units. Work with user to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro. Work to establish inventory, schedule cycle, and special event menus. Work to promote the use and enhance the FoodPro program. Work with Dining Service staff in all areas to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro.</div> Auxiliary Central Storage https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478579 2026-04-22T17:30:10-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:10-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate AD This position in the Department of Plant Pathology will work on antifungal resistance monitoring of human pathogens in agricultural environments. Projects include development of assays for the rapid molecular detection of azole-resistant strains of Aspergillus fumigatus in environmental samples, identification of environments conducive to azole resistance development, and identifying fitness costs of azole resistance in fungi in agricultural environments. CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493692 2026-07-15T15:29:57-04:00 2026-07-15T15:29:57-04:00 Large Animal Client Services Coordinator <div>The Large Animal Client Services Coordinator provides professional, high-quality customer service and administrative support for the Large Animal Teaching Hospital. This position is responsible for checking in clients and patients, scheduling appointments, and ensuring all client, patient, and potential referring veterinarian information is accurate and complete prior to and during each visit. The coordinator verifies ownership, billing party and record requirements, facilitates communication between clients and clinicians, and ensures a seamless client experience. This role supports both the clinical and operational missions of the Large Animal Teaching Hospital by maintaining accuracy, professionalism, and efficacy in all client service functions.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477747 2026-04-21T17:31:21-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:22-04:00 Dining Services Repair Technician <div>This position is responsible for troubleshooting and repairing commercial kitchen equipment, performing general building maintenance task and preventative maintenance for equipment and dining facilities. General maintenance task will consist of performing a variety of physical labor task at variable rates to include plumbing, electrical work, painting, wall covering, low-grade construction, etc. This position will be assigned work order task daily by the Maintenance Foreman and provide status updates on the completion of task by providing and maintaining service reports. If needed, this position will be responsible for submitting work orders to the Facilities Management Division (FMD) for maintenance task beyond the scope of the work for the position.</div> Auxiliary Dining Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478703 2026-04-22T17:39:34-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:35-04:00 Student Assistant- Monfort <div>Assist lead scientist and technician in the planting, data collection, and harvesting of peanut agronomy research plots. Specific duties include but are not limited to the following: data collection, data entry, plot stake labeling, cleaning and filling sprayers, plot maintenance and plot photography. Many duties will be conducted in the early morning (6 am) so punctuality is expected.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497478 2026-08-03T11:52:08-04:00 2026-08-03T11:52:08-04:00 Greenhouse Tsai Lab Student Assistant <div>The Tsai Lab in the Warnell School of Forestry at UGA (<a href=\"https://www.aspendb.org/)\"><strong>https://www.aspendb.org/)</strong></a> is looking for a part-time student worker to help maintain experimental trees in their field and research greenhouses. The student assistant will work with our greenhouse research technician to inspect, weed, trim and maintain experimental plants, apply biocontrol and fertilizer, and assist with a variety of other greenhouse maintenance tasks (cleaning, composting, watering). Preferred schedule is 3 hours/day, 3-5 days/week, plus at least one weekend shift (2-4 pm) per month. Please include in your cover letter your available hours and desired number of hours/week you'd like to work.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478011 2026-04-21T18:25:48-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:49-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the level of Assistant Professor. We seek an individual who will build and maintain a strong, extramurally funded research program in any area of pharmaceutical and biomedical sciences, such as Pharmacology; Immunology, Medicinal Chemistry with experience in high-throughput screening; Systems Biology, and Cancer Biology. The successful candidate will complement and build upon the Department’s existing research strengths, which include active programs in chemical biology, pharmacology and pharmaceutics, cancer biology, and infectious diseases.<br><br><strong>Research Areas of Interest</strong>&nbsp;</div><div>Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>AI/computational drug discovery&nbsp;</li><li>Computational or virtual drug screening&nbsp;</li><li>Chemical biology&nbsp;</li><li>Pharmacology&nbsp;</li><li>Immunology&nbsp;</li><li>Cancer biology&nbsp;</li><li>Drug formulation or drug delivery&nbsp;</li><li>Medicinal chemistry&nbsp;</li><li>Toxicology&nbsp;</li><li>Systems biology&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br>The Department offers a competitive salary, excellent laboratory space, and a generous start-up package to support the successful candidate’s research program.&nbsp;</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478560 2026-04-22T17:29:35-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:36-04:00 International Centers Student Ambassador This student will help advertise and recruite from classrooms. This student will work at open house and talk to students about what to expect while attending Study Away programs at the UGA International Centers. The students are scheduled at Tate Center tables during selected hours to promote and answer questions from other students  about the three Centers and their programs. OGE-International Centers https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492060 2026-07-08T14:34:05-04:00 2026-07-08T14:34:06-04:00 Executive Assistant- Asst. Dean's Office-Tifton <div>This position provides administrative support to the Assistant Dean of the Tifton Campus by compiling information and preparing reports, handling information requests and performing relevant administrative support functions. The incumbent works closely with the Assistant Dean to ensure smooth operation of the Tifton Campus and the departments located on it and will act on behalf of the Assistant Dean as delegated. Specific duties include, but are not limited to handling confidential or sensitive information discreetly, scheduling appointments, creating agendas for meetings, assisting with campus events, handling multiple phone calls, taking minutes at meetings and composing correspondence of a routine nature. This position involves a great deal of organizational skill to keep the office running smoothly, as well as communication skills needed to professionally interact with all levels of University administrators, faculty, staff, agricultural and political groups, and the public.</div> CAES-Tifton Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478654 2026-04-22T17:36:53-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:53-04:00 Temporary Technical Paraprofessional - Missaoui Lab <div>A Temporary Tech. Parapro. will assist with projects and tasks in laboratory, greenhouse, field and office. Employee will be assigned various tasks throughout the year depending upon availability, skill set, and program needs. We conduct research at multiple locations. Travel to farms and facilities will be required to perform some duties. Individual needs to be detail oriented, accept instruction, and willing to work in various environments. Work well with others.</div> CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496684 2026-07-29T11:14:29-04:00 2026-07-29T11:14:30-04:00 Assistant Program Director – Internal Medicine Residency Program <div>The University of Georgia School of Medicine is seeking a dynamic, innovative academic medical educator with outstanding interpersonal and communication skills to join the leadership team of the three-year categorical Internal Medicine Residency Program in Athens, Georgia, as an Assistant Program Director. This position offers significant opportunities for professional development, leadership growth, and advancement in medical education.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Program Director will assist the Program Director in the administration and operation of the Internal Medicine Residency Program, with a particular focus on Quality Improvement and Patient Safety. The role includes instructional, clinical, scholarly, and administrative responsibilities. In addition, the individual will serve as the Medical Director of the resident continuity clinic, Community Internal Medicine of Athens (CIMA), overseeing clinic operations and providing teaching and supervision for Internal Medicine residents.<br><br></div><div>This is a non-tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor, commensurate with qualifications and experience.</div> SOM-GME https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477942 2026-04-21T18:07:03-04:00 2026-04-21T18:07:04-04:00 Director of Broadcast Technologies/Chief Engineer <div>The Director of Broadcast Technologies/Chief Engineer will lead all technical and engineering operations for Georgia Athletics to deliver first‑class broadcast experiences. The role provides hands‑on and supervisory responsibility for installation, maintenance, and operation of control‑room and venue‑specific broadcast systems - with emphasis on linear and streaming television and in‑venue videoboards, including all football events. This position oversees all control rooms and remote broadcast equipment, technical personnel, and vendor relationships, collaborating with network and large‑screen personnel to deliver productions for UGAAA and SEC Broadcast Partners. The Director of Broadcast Technologies ensures the seamless transmission of high‑quality audio and video signals across baseband and IP paths, manages complex signal flows during live productions, and executes in fast‑paced live environments.&nbsp;</div> Athletics-New Media https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503719 2026-08-31T14:57:51-04:00 2026-08-31T14:57:52-04:00 Director of Spirit <div>Coordinate all spirit team practices and annual tryout at the end of spring semester. Coordinate travel and attend all required home and some post-season competitions.&nbsp; Coordinate all youth and college prep clinics and manage recruiting efforts for potential spirit members. Track academics of all team members to ensure compliance. Coordinate strength and conditioning and training schedule. Create and maintain spirit budget. Handle all mascot operations including casting, invoicing and overall supervision of appearances. Handle inventory for spirit program and maintenance of mascot uniforms.</div> Athletics-External Operations https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500112 2026-08-14T09:57:13-04:00 2026-08-14T09:57:14-04:00 Business Intelligence Analyst–Student Success <div>Reporting to the Assistant to the Vice President for Student Affairs, the Business Intelligence Analyst – Student Success serves as the primary analytics and business intelligence professional for the Division of Student Affairs. This position develops predictive models, dashboards, visualizations, and analytical products that support strategic intelligence, organizational effectiveness, and evidence-informed decision-making across the division.<br><br></div><div>Working closely with the Office of Institutional Research and campus partners, the Business Intelligence Analyst integrates data from multiple institutional systems to identify trends, forecast outcomes, and evaluate factors influencing student engagement, wellbeing, retention, progression, and graduation. The position provides actionable insights, executive reporting, and student success analyses that inform divisional priorities, resource allocation, and continuous improvement efforts.</div> VPSA-VP for Student Affairs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478392 2026-04-22T17:16:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:48-04:00 Camera survey technician <div>Worker will tag infrared trail camera photos to species and tagging deer photos to sex, age, and unique identifying markers. Both duties will assist a deer research project funded by the Arkansas Game and Fish Commission investigating population-level impacts of Chronic Wasting Disease of white-tailed deer in northwestern Arkansas.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478827 2026-04-22T17:50:18-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:18-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate - Kner <div>This Postdoctoral Associate (“Postdoc”) will work on developing novel structured-illumination microscopy systems for a variety of biomedical applications.</div> ENGR-Electrical & Computer https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502370 2026-08-25T08:35:41-04:00 2026-08-25T08:35:41-04:00 Underwriting and Traffic Coordinator <div>The Underwriting and Traffic Coordinator manages underwriting sales and administration, revenue operations, content production, and traffic systems to support the delivery of underwriting and promotional messaging. This position also writes, records, and produces underwriting and public service announcements and manages program and traffic logs to ensure accurate scheduling and compliance. The coordinator collaborates with consultants, clients, business and station staff to support efficient station operations.</div> MarComm-WUGA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478513 2026-04-22T17:24:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:34-04:00 Temporary Research Technician - dev Kumar <div>This position will provide laboratory support to researchers in a microbiology lab. The position will be responsible for assisting with experiments and preparing regents and media. This position will also help in the general housekeeping of laboratory supplies and instruments.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488160 2026-06-11T14:04:26-04:00 2026-06-11T14:04:27-04:00 Cook I <div>Skilled cooking work in the preparation of foods for a Dining Commons. Work involves the general preparation and cooking of a variety of foods, or the specialized preparations of meats and vegetables. Work involves responsibility of neatness and cleanliness in preparing food, and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Works under the supervision of a Cook 2 or Chef.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478611 2026-04-22T17:32:53-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:54-04:00 Temporary Service Worker (Cain) Temporary, part-time worker is expected to work independently, have excellent problem-solving skills, and good interpersonal and customer service skills.\r\nDuties will include data entry, providing reception and phone coverage, providing duplicates, handling fax and email communications. Helping staff with mailings, event planning, room set-up and clean-up, and other duties as needed. CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494819 2026-07-21T11:44:13-04:00 2026-07-21T11:44:14-04:00 Food Service Worker I (Partial Year) <div><strong>*This is a benefits eligible, partial year position (9-10 months of the year) August through May of each year. The selected candidate will be required to sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date. *</strong><br><br>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477820 2026-04-21T17:57:53-04:00 2026-04-21T17:57:54-04:00 Registered Veterinary Technician <div>The primary purpose and function of the Veterinary Technician is to support veterinarians in teaching veterinary students clinical skills including technical skills and animal care.</div> VetMed-Academic Affairs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478745 2026-04-22T17:42:03-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:05-04:00 Forestry Technician Internship <div>Positions will be located on various National Wildlife Refuges in the Southeast region. Potential Refuge locations may include (but not limited to): Carolina Sandhills NWR in McBee, SC; St. Marks NWR in St. Marks, FL; Okeefenokee NWR in Folkston, GA; Piedmont NWR in Round Oak, GA; Lower Suwanee NWR in Chiefland, FL; Noxubee NWR near Starkville, MS; and, Clarks River in Kentucky. Primary duties include collecting baseline forest habitat data, cruising &amp; marking timber to enhance wildlife habitat, and assisting with timber sale administration. Other duties may involve invasive plant control and monitoring of wildlife and habitat responses to various forest management treatments. A wide variety of wildlife management activities may also be incorporated depending upon refuge needs and objectives. Approximate duration will be 13 weeks between mid-May – mid August. Start day may be flexible to accommodate students needing to complete the May forestry camp before beginning work. Positions are full-time temporary with 40-hours of work per week. Students wishing to receive internship credit may need to complete an internship agreement or practicum agreement and enroll in the appropriate course.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498229 2026-08-05T15:41:29-04:00 2026-08-05T15:41:30-04:00 Department Head of Human Development and Family Science <div>The College of Family and Consumer Sciences (FACS) at the University of Georgia (UGA) is seeking applications for the Department Head of Human Development and Family Science (HDFS).<br><br>The Department Head will inspire an expansive vision for the future and effectively interact with constituencies associated with academia, government, industry, and alumni, as well as faculty, staff, and students. Central to the department head’s leadership is the promotion of policies and everyday practices that address the needs of communities. This position requires strong leadership capabilities and the ability to foster success in research, service, and development funding. It is expected that the successful candidate will lead the faculty and its programs to a higher level of excellence.<br><br>The Department Head reports directly to the Dean of the College of Family and Consumer Sciences with annual reviews and third year administrative reviews informed by the faculty of the unit. The Department Head is a member of a College leadership team committed to the integration of the missions of research, instruction, and extension and outreach in a research land-grant institution.</div><div>The position is a nine-month academic year appointment with administrative and summer month salary supplement while serving as Department Head. Time allocation is 60-70% administration,30-40% research or teaching, and 5% service, to be determined based on the interests and strengths of the candidate and fit with the needs of the unit at the time of hire.</div> UHR-HR Search Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478118 2026-04-21T18:34:50-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:51-04:00 Clinical Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track position at the level of Clinical Assistant Professor. We seek an individual who will teach in the areas of Biotechnology, Pharmaceutics/Compounding &amp; Formulation, Pharmacogenomics, Pharmacokinetics/Pharmacodynamics, Pharmaceutics/ Drug Delivery, and other pharmaceutics-related courses. The successful candidate will complement and build upon the Department’s existing research strengths, which include active programs in chemical biology, pharmacology and pharmaceutics, cancer biology, and infectious diseases.</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504288 2026-09-03T09:27:39-04:00 2026-09-03T09:27:40-04:00 Undergraduate Research Assistant Leaf Phenotyping <div>Seeking a motivated student to assist with leaf phenotyping and processing, organizing laboratory equipment and supplies, labeling and maintaining leaf samples, and keeping accurate records of sample collection and measurements. This position provides hands-on experience in forest genetics, tree physiology, and laboratory research.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500840 2026-08-18T12:09:33-04:00 2026-08-18T12:09:33-04:00 Professional Support Coordinator (Partial Year) <div>Provides administrative, organizational, and outreach support to promote and represent the organization and brand as a socially responsible force internally and in the community. Assists with administrative tasks, supports events, provides management/logistical research projects, and supports grant development.<br><br>This is a partial-year position aligned with the academic year calendar.&nbsp;</div> COE-Latino Achv&Success in Ed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478444 2026-04-22T17:20:45-04:00 2026-05-20T16:32:15-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator – Camp Jekyll <div>This job is a temporary Environmental Educator at Camp Jekyll, located on Jekyll Island, Georgia. The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include life and earth science, ecology, and marine science. Other responsibilities include animal care, maintenance of teaching areas and resources, facilities, grounds, and support of general operations of the facility.</div> CAES-Jekyll Island https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483696 2026-05-18T11:16:34-04:00 2026-05-18T11:16:34-04:00 Glider Lab Technician (PT3) <div>Responsibilities will include assisting with various aspects of operations of autonomous underwater vehicles as needed, including preparation, testing, deployment/recovery, and examination of the data. There may also be the opportunity to contribute to other components of field research, depending on experience, interest, and project needs. Training on the use and operation of gliders and other AUVs will be provided by the principal investigator.</div> VPR-Skidaway Inst Oceanography https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478709 2026-04-22T17:40:13-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:13-04:00 Student Assistant - FMD <div>The student will be working in the Facilities Management Division performing mail room work and providing customer service. This involves tasks like sorting mail, processing outgoing mail (including applying postage), handling package tracking, and maintaining accurate records.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497538 2026-08-03T13:46:28-04:00 2026-08-03T13:46:29-04:00 Grantsmanship Development Professional <div>Under the direction of the Director in the Office for Strategic Research Development, perform professional level duties related to the development of research grant writing ability and knowledge (“grantsmanship”) across the University of Georgia’s research enterprise. This includes working intensively with individual faculty to develop grant proposals and instruct them in grantsmanship. It also includes developing and delivering grantsmanship workshops and other outreach activities. This position requires experience working closely with academic faculty; knowledge of research grant proposal development; and superior writing, editing, and proofreading ability.</div> VPR-Strategic Rsch Dev https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478037 2026-04-21T18:27:24-04:00 2026-04-21T18:27:25-04:00 Assistant Professor - Row Crop Entomologist <div>The Department of Entomology (https://ent.uga.edu) at the University of Georgia (UGA) invites applications for a tenure-track position (9 months) in row crop integrated pest management (IPM) with emphasis on cotton at the Assistant Professor rank. The position is budgeted at 65% research, 30% Extension, and 5% service.&nbsp; We seek candidates with expertise in IPM and expertise and/or interest in sustainable production of row crops.<br><br>The successful candidate will be expected to develop a nationally recognized research and extension program supported by competitive external funding, to publish high impact research, and to effectively mentor graduate/undergraduate students. A collaborative and multidisciplinary approach to solving important problems within the cotton industry that strengthens and complements the current programs in the department and college is expected. Multistate and international collaborations are also encouraged. Cooperative projects with the UGA Cotton Team and multistate collaborations are encouraged. Extension responsibilities will include communicating effectively with row crop producers, extension agents, and other stakeholders to translate research results using traditional and digital media. The successful candidate is expected to be active in departmental and university service, professional activities, and outreach. Anticipated start date is August 3, 2026.<br><br>This position is located in the Department of Entomology, UGA-Tifton Campus, Tifton, Georgia. The UGA-Tifton campus is home to 90 scientists and more than 400 support staff across 9 departments in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences. On-campus resources include office, laboratory, greenhouse and rearing space, multiple research farms, and required agricultural machinery.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504111 2026-09-02T09:10:30-04:00 2026-09-02T09:10:30-04:00 Grand Farm Support Technician <div>Assists Farm Manager with day-to-day operation of the UGA Grand Farm. Tasks include but are not limited to operating agricultural equipment, guidance systems, variable rate controllers, applying fertilizers, applying pesticides, land prep., soil sampling, general farm maintenance and repair, data collection, etc.</div> CAES-Grand Farm https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500405 2026-08-17T10:26:52-04:00 2026-08-17T10:26:53-04:00 Research Professional - Missouri <div>The Gamebird and Managed Ecosystems (GAME) Lab is seeking a Research Professional to serve as a project field research leader on a Northern Bobwhite project near Columbia or Kirksville, MO. The project will examine bobwhite ecology and restoration efforts on private lands in Missouri. The successful incumbent will work with landowners and other research staff to coordinate research activities. This incumbent will lead seasonal field technicians in field data collection. Work will involve quail trapping and radio-tagging, tracking birds via radio telemetry, vegetation surveys, data entry and management, and other duties as assigned. This position will involve working non-typical hours, with morning and nighttime work needed at different times of the year. This candidate may also assist with hiring seasonal employees. This position has a limited term appointment term which is expected to end 2 years after start date. The position may be extended beyond the initial term, contingent upon continued funding.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478415 2026-04-22T17:19:55-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:56-04:00 FWS Lab Assistant <div>Student will assist with research projects on plant pathogenic fungi.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480015 2026-04-29T10:58:21-04:00 2026-04-29T10:58:22-04:00 HVAC Refrigeration Mechanic <div>This is a skilled technical work at the journeyman level involving operating, installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing building HVAC systems and components, including but not limited to chillers, air handlers, terminal units, water coils, pumps, valves, motor starters, and other related equipment. (Systems are primarily central air handling type with hydronic heating and cooling units). This position serves primarily to make repairs, corrections, and perform routine preventive maintenance on electrical, HVAC, and other mechanical equipment; make repairs to general building facilities, including, but not limited to, general carpentry repairs, repairs to ceiling and floor coverings, doors, windows, and furniture; perform minor paint and patch work. The person serving in this position can demonstrate an ability to engage and complete basic repairs and tasks independently. Complete and/or assist in the completion of minor service requests as needed. Solicit the advice of shop personnel in specific trades as needed; refer more complex and time-consuming items to shop personnel; assist in repairs if necessary.</div> FMD-O&M-HSC Zone Shop https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478537 2026-04-22T17:25:57-04:00 2026-05-26T15:01:43-04:00 Athletic Subject Tutor - Student Assistant Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490543 2026-06-29T09:20:31-04:00 2026-06-29T09:20:31-04:00 Faculty Affairs Assistant <div>The Faculty Affairs Assistant provides administrative and operational support for faculty-related processes at the college level. This role serves as a primary point of contact for faculty appointments, reappointments, promotions, tenure, leaves, evaluations, and compliance with institutional policies. The position ensures accurate recordkeeping, timely processing of actions, and effective coordination between the unit, central faculty affairs, human resources, and academic leadership.</div><div>This position also provides executive-level support to the Senior Associate Dean of Faculty Success and Strategic Initiatives in the College of Veterinary Medicine on a wide range of administrative duties including tracking, prioritizing, and managing the Associate Dean’s workflow; acting as liaison between the Associate Dean and other entities on- and off-campus; and anticipating and addressing the needs of the Associate Dean by using independent judgment while working under pressure and maintaining a professional demeanor. Many responsibilities are of a sensitive, confidential and high-profile nature, which include personnel matters. The scope of this position within the College involves seven diverse academic departments, a Veterinary Teaching Hospital and several Diagnostic Laboratories as well as College-wide overarching Faculty Affairs.</div> VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478631 2026-04-22T17:33:58-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:59-04:00 Necropsy Student Assistant <div>This position provides basic assistance for the diagnostic necropsy service to the Veterinary Teaching Hospital and clients of the Athens Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory.</div> VetMed-Athens Diagnostic Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495833 2026-07-24T16:19:12-04:00 2026-07-24T16:19:13-04:00 Grants Coordinator II <div>Assist faculty, graduate students and/or staff in development, preparation, and review of proposals for external funding.Submit proposals to sponsors within DLSA limits. Coordinate submission of proposals outside DLSA limits with CVM Grants Coordinators and/or SPA. Serve as a resource to CVM Business Managers and investigators in administration of sponsored projects. Interpret, clarify and document diverse sponsor requirements.</div> VetMed-Research & Graduate Aff https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477859 2026-04-21T18:00:10-04:00 2026-04-21T18:00:12-04:00 Farm Operations Professional I - Chavez (2) <div>This position directs the day-to-day management of farm operations, encompassing planting, irrigation, and harvesting to provide essential research support for the stone fruit and pecan research projects at the USDA-ARS Fruit and Tree Nut research Lab located at Byron, GA. The incumbent will manage the various phases of the research projects by performing largely independent farming duties within pecan and peach orchard settings. Key technical duties include the operation of farm tractors (greater than or equal to 50 horsepower) with associated implements/attachments and other heavy equipment, pesticide sprayer calibration and application, mowing, planting, and harvesting, and equipment repair. The role involves coordination and collaboration with faculty and project leaders on the design and implementation of field experiments. This position will modify and execute field experiments to maintain the uniform conditions of the research study. Specific technical management tasks involve scouting orchards for disease and pest issues, monitoring plant and soil nutrient levels, managing applications and pesticide planning, and maintaining and monitoring irrigation systems. The incumbent will be responsible for creating detailed schedules for planting, irrigation, spraying, fertilizing, pruning, training, and planting orchards. This position will assist in the hiring, training, and direct supervision of seasonal workers and staff, ensuring efficient execution of all farm and research-related tasks.<br><br><strong>This is a grant-funded position with continued employment beyond 08/31/2026 based on the needs of the project as well as available funding and satisfactory job performance and progress.</strong></div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503207 2026-08-27T15:11:49-04:00 2026-08-27T15:11:50-04:00 Student Assistant Histo <div>Position is responsible for trimming representative sections of samples for IDL accessions, and maintaining cleanliness and organization of the Pathology Grossing Lab, the Grinding Room, and the Histology Lab.</div> VetMed-Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499418 2026-08-11T18:28:46-04:00 2026-08-11T18:28:47-04:00 Coordinator for Residential Education and Leadership <div>Reporting to the Assistant Director for Academic Initiatives &amp; Student Leadership, the primary function of this position is to create safe and comfortable communities that have a focus on student learning. Special emphasis is given in autonomously leading programmatic and student leadership initiatives, advising student groups and the supervision of graduate residents. The successful candidate will be an active and engaging member of the department and prepared to oversee a student leadership program for 8500 residential students. The Coordinator for Residential Education and Leadership is an integral part of the team and is a full-time professional staff position.</div> Housing-Resident Progs & Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478373 2026-04-22T17:16:14-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:14-04:00 Graduate Assistant - Jespersen <div>Graduate Assistantship.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478804 2026-04-22T17:46:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:44-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Handa <div>This postdoctoral research position is open for candidates with a Ph.D. in biomaterials or a closely related field, as well as a strong background and experience in the fields of <em>polymer science, biomaterials, 3D printing, controlled release/delivery, microbiology, antimicrobial testing, hemocompatibility, tissue engineering, microfluidics, bioengineering, biochemistry, and chemistry</em>.<br> <br>As a team member, the successful candidate will work on fast-paced and interdisciplinary projects, including fabricating and characterizing novel polymers, therapeutic controlled release, and testing them using <em>in vitro </em>and <em>in vivo </em>models for conducting cell/molecular biology and biocompatibility tests. Postdoctoral researcher candidates that are highly independent, self-driven, have excellent communication skills, and are motivated with a passion for research and are encouraged to apply. <br><br><strong>The initial appointment is full-time for one year, and the possibility of renewal is subject to satisfactory performance in year 1 and continued funding.</strong></div> ENGR-Chem Material & Biomed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504652 2026-09-04T15:03:02-04:00 2026-09-04T15:03:02-04:00 Assistant Director of Development <div>The Assistant Director of Development serves as a frontline fundraiser for the University of Georgia School of Medicine and is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding philanthropic support for the School's fundraising priorities. Reporting to the Senior Director of Development, the position manages a portfolio of donors and prospects across the philanthropic continuum, with a primary emphasis on leadership annual giving donors capable of making gifts between $1,500 and $50,000. The Assistant Director also identifies and cultivates individuals with major and planned giving potential and, when appropriate, solicits and stewards these gifts in collaboration with the Senior Director of Development.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Director builds relationships with alumni, grateful patients when appropriate, physicians, foundations, corporations, community partners, and friends of the School of Medicine whose philanthropic interests align with advancing student scholarships, faculty excellence, biomedical research, educational innovation, and initiatives that improve healthcare throughout Georgia. The position coordinates annual giving initiatives, including Dawg Day of Giving and other annual fundraising campaigns, and develops targeted fundraising and donor engagement projects designed to increase donor participation, retention, and leadership annual giving. Frequent travel throughout Georgia and the Southeastern United States is expected, with occasional travel beyond the region as needed.</div> SOM-Operations https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501539 2026-08-20T10:53:24-04:00 2026-08-20T10:53:25-04:00 Business Analyst <div>The Business Analyst provides leadership for the Bursar and Treasury Services Division using data analytic skills to support business decisions and deployment of enterprise-level solutions to the University’s information systems. The analyst uses queries along with other analytic reporting tools to provide useful reporting metrics that will help management identify processes in need of improvement, make recommendations, and respond to outside questions. This role performs duties including gathering, documenting, and analyzing business processes and coordinating with functional, cross-functional, and technical teams to develop, test, and implement projects, APIs and data feeds related to Banner, PeopleSoft, and other Third-Party Systems such as TouchNet. The Business Analyst assists with assessing and testing upcoming system upgrade releases and patches. The Business Analyst creates project plans, coordinates and leads project meetings, ensures project documentation is up to date, and manages tasks related to projects. Additionally, the Business Analyst prepares specifications for developers, coordinates testing with functional stakeholders on campus, functionally approves migrations and upgrades in non-production and production instances, and assists with determining the training materials needed for upgrades and projects. The Business Analyst supports the development of operational reports related to existing processes and projects. In addition, the Business Analyst supports the division with special projects or processing tasks as needed.</div> FD-Student Account Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478495 2026-04-22T17:24:01-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:01-04:00 Ruter Student Assistant #3 <div>The University of Georgia Department of Horticulture is seeking applicants as student workers with responsibility of operational management of field and container production of ornamental nursery crops along with supporting greenhouse and laboratory operations. Recruits will work to support an ornamental plant breeding program located at the Durham Horticulture Farm in Watkinsville, GA. The initial start date for this position is 3/1/2022 and continuation of the positions are contingent upon future funding.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486657 2026-06-03T09:23:47-04:00 2026-06-03T09:23:47-04:00 Business Operations Professional II <div>This Business Operations Professional serves as a strategic business partner to the Institute, providing comprehensive financial management of organizational accounts through a deep understanding of the Institute’s mission, operations, and the specific business needs of our divisions. This role applies advanced knowledge of financial accounting and public budgeting within the context of higher education and public service to support sound decision-making and operational effectiveness.<br><br>Acting as an internal consultant on fiscal affairs, financial management, and budget strategy, this position advises faculty, staff, and leadership on budgeting, budget management, and financial planning. Responsibilities include monitoring personal services and operating expenditures in relation to budgets and actuals, as well as overseeing sub-awards, contracts, and other outsourced services.<br><br>Using advanced financial expertise, the Business Operations Professional ensures all transactions comply with Institute of Government guidelines, University of Georgia policies, and Board of Regents policies. The role leads the development and production of complex financial reports and maintains accurate financial data and records within internal financial management systems (currently QuickBooks and related document management systems) to support transparency and informed decision-making.<br><br>The Business Operations Professional ensures proper administration of all related agreements, including compliance with applicable local, state, and federal laws. Regular financial analysis and reporting are conducted using internal systems, and accounts are routinely reconciled against university records to ensure accuracy and integrity.<br><br>Supporting business operations across multiple divisions, this position ensures financial coverage aligns with organizational priorities. The Business Operations Professional provides professional oversight of fiscal affairs, reinforces best practices in financial management, and serves as a trusted advisor and resource to faculty, staff, and Institute of Government leadership regarding financial operations and account management.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478581 2026-04-22T17:30:13-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:14-04:00 Temporary Technician Perform laboratory processes and well as various filed work. VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493949 2026-07-16T13:01:37-04:00 2026-07-16T13:01:38-04:00 4-H Franklin County AmeriCorps State Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members will comply with AmeriCorps guidelines such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other trainings.<br><br></div><div>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members will log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477752 2026-04-21T17:31:32-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:33-04:00 PMRC Field Crew Member <div>This position implements the installation, maintenance, treatment, measurement, and documentation of research field plots of a large, regional, forestry field research program from Virginia to Florida to East Texas. The individual in this position follows study work plans and established protocols in executing tasks. The individual works as part of a crew and independently. Task completion often requires the individual to solve problems regarding scheduling, safety, quality, and methods. The individual contributes to improvement in work processes through critical observation and trial and error. The employee interprets results of efforts (e.g. tree measurements, plot layout, efficiency of effort) for reasonableness, accuracy, and process quality and makes modifications as warranted.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500853 2026-08-18T12:38:35-04:00 2026-08-18T12:38:36-04:00 Student Writer <div>The student writer will work in the Office of Marketing and Communications (OMC) within the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES), assisting in the dissemination of news and information about the college to the campus and news media. This position offers the opportunity to develop internal announcements within CAES and UGA Cooperative Extension, review and creatively adapt research publications to produce clear, engaging, and accessible content for a general audience. Writing will be shared across multiple channels, including the CAES Field Report, Almanac magazine and other CAES and UGA communication platforms. Writing includes media releases, web content, research stories, faculty and student profiles, and feature stories.<br><br>The ideal candidate is available to work 10-15 hours per week. The hours are flexible and will be structured around class schedules and related deadlines.<br><br><br></div> CAES-Comm & Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478457 2026-04-22T17:22:15-04:00 2026-05-28T11:01:33-04:00 Academic Mentor <div>Assist student-athletes in their academic endeavors by providing supplemental support.<br>Academic mentors to meet with student-athletes weekly during regularly scheduled sessions to foster academic independence and encourage self-regulated learning. Pay is $15 per 1-hour mentor session.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483918 2026-05-19T10:13:09-04:00 2026-05-19T10:13:10-04:00 Elbert County Agriculture and Natural Resources Agent <div>This position will manage the Agricultural &amp; Natural Resources program in Elbert County by providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br></div><div>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478566 2026-04-22T17:29:45-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:46-04:00 LAB/RESEARCH ASSISTANT VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492246 2026-07-09T11:47:03-04:00 2026-07-09T11:47:04-04:00 Assignments Coordinator <div>The assignments coordinator is primarily responsible for coordinating assignments for more than 9,000 current students living in the residence halls, apartments, and at the Health Sciences Campus with considerable independence. The person in this position provides functional leadership regarding significant and crucial processes relating to the assignments processes and demonstrates expertise and experience in the management of these complex processes. The staff member in this position carries out work with a high level of independent judgement and autonomy.</div> Housing-Admin Srvcs & Communic https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478661 2026-04-22T17:37:05-04:00 2026-04-22T17:37:05-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The postdoctoral scholar will join 2, NIH-funded grants that evaluates the efficacy of a novel cognitive training intervention for improving emotion regulation ability in schizophrenia. The grant uses fMRI as a key outcome measure. The postdoctoral fellow who will be responsible for supervising clinical diagnostic interviews, scoring interviews, and working with computer task data, and be responsible for conducting clinical diagnostic interviews, scoring interviews, and working with fMRI data The postdoc will work under the mentorship of Dr. Strauss to provide ongoing clinical supervision for assessments and help analyze and interpret task data, prepare results for publication, and present the subsequent material at conferences.</div> VPR-Owens Inst Behavioral Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496799 2026-07-29T15:42:56-04:00 2026-07-29T15:42:56-04:00 Student Worker-Safety Unit <div>This position is responsible for providing support to the Safety and Compliance program at the University of Georgia Veterinary Teaching Hospital.</div> VetMed-VTH Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477978 2026-04-21T18:16:49-04:00 2026-04-21T18:16:50-04:00 Senior Research Associate <div>The Senior Research Associate at the Analytical Services and Training Laboratory will be proficient in developing advanced MS techniques (MS/MS) for glycoproteins, oligosaccharides, and peptides in collaborative and time-sensitive projects. They will need to possess a strong background in carbohydrates and MS techniques, particularly on orbitraps, to tackle challenging analyses. Proficiency in isolating and purifying polysacchrides and glycoproteins from diverse sources, coupled with adeptness in writing, editing, and collaborating on manuscripts and reviews, is essential. Moreover, they will excel in training colleagues in structural characterization techniques and may contribute to teaching and organizing training courses as required. Flexibility to take on additional responsibilities as assigned is needed.</div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503824 2026-09-01T08:47:25-04:00 2026-09-01T08:47:25-04:00 Business Manager - Dept/Unit <div>This position has a high level of responsibility and aids the Director and Associate Director in daily operations of the Center for Applied Isotope Studies. The Business Manager is essential for maintaining the Center for Applied Isotope Studies’ compliance with all university, state, federal and USG/BOR regulations and functions. The Business Manager will be responsible for overseeing and coordinating all functions and personnel of the Business Office, including all aspects of financial management, sponsored projects, human resources, and employee relations.</div><div>Overall duties include but are not limited to: management of professional, fiscal and administrative work in planning, organizing, leading and controlling the fiscal, instructional, HR activities of the Center; project financial needs and oversee instructional budget, manage approved budget; prepare reports and provide information to the Director, supervise office staff, hire personnel and process paperwork for all new employees; serve as payroll representative for department; provide assistance to faculty and staff regarding interpretation and clarification of policies and procedures.</div> VPR-Ctr Applied Isotope Study https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500118 2026-08-14T10:25:15-04:00 2026-08-14T10:25:15-04:00 Payroll Coordinator <div>The Auxiliary Services Payroll Coordinator is responsible for assisting in overseeing the division of all payroll processes. These processes include, but are not limited to, the following: Payroll Reconciliation, Absence Management, Special Pay Processing, Payroll Validation, etc. This incumbent is responsible for establishing protocols and procedures to ensure the timely execution of each payroll process. The Auxiliary Payroll Coordinator reports and assists the Sr. Payroll Coordinator with the coordination of payroll activities with University Central Payroll Auxiliary Service Division employees, supervisors, and management on payroll issues, payroll funding, and budget updates. In coordination with the Auxiliary Services Human Resources department, this position works to streamline processes and improve efficiency in processing terminations, Administrative Leave, Invalid Funding, and Express Direct Retros. In addition to assisting with all payroll-related processes, this position is responsible for general ledger posting and reconciliation of payroll-related transactions.</div> Auxiliary Finance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478396 2026-04-22T17:19:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:23-04:00 White-tailed Deer Research Technicians <div>We are seeking one white-tailed deer research technician for participation in a deer research project funded by the Arkansas Game and Fish Commission. The project will investigate population-level impacts of Chronic Wasting Disease (CWD) of white-tailed deer in northern Newton and Searcy counties. The research team will consist of one research coordinator and four technicians. Technicians will gain extensive experience in fawn capturing and collaring with VHF collars, tracking fawns, investigating both adult and fawn mortalities and monthly monitoring and maintenance of camera traps. Captured deer will also receive ear tags and morphometric and biological tissue samples will be collected.<br><br>Because we are researching and working in areas with high concentrations of CWD prions, there will be precautions taken to minimize transmission of prions by field crews to different research sites.<br><br>This position will provide opportunity to network with local landowners, professionals from the University of Georgia, and staff from Arkansas Game and Fish Commission.<br><br>Chronic Wasting Disease Research in the Arkansas Ozarks -www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Mza6RP7uYc&amp;t=15s<br><br><br>Wild Science Webinar: March 2023 – CWD Research and Evaluating Florida Bass in Lake Ouachita - www.youtube.com/watch?v=jj0ujdTqhys<br>Apply by 04/05/24:<br><br><br>To apply, submit the following documents into a single PDF document and send to Lisa Jorge at arkansasdeerstudy@gmail.com.<br><br>Name your PDF file as “LastName_FirstName_CWD”. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. Incomplete applications, or applications not submitted as described may be rejected.<br><br>1. A one-page cover letter describing your experience and how it relates to this position as described above.<br>2. Resume/CV.<br>3. At least three professional references (be sure to include those from past ungulate work, if applicable).<br><br>Contact Person: Lisa Jorge<br>Contact email: Primary: arkansasdeerstudy@gmail.com alternate: LAB70208@uga.edu</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478831 2026-04-22T17:50:26-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:26-04:00 Greenhouse & Garden/Grounds Assistant <div>The responsibilities of the Greenhouse and Garden/Grounds Assistant involves general greenhouse work and maintenance activities such as watering, fertilizing, weeding, planting, cleaning, and plant propagation. Assistants work alongside the Greenhouse Manager to maintain and operate three production greenhouses and outdoor nursery gaining valuable hands-on experience.</div> PSO-State Botanic Garden of GA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502415 2026-08-25T10:12:50-04:00 2026-08-25T10:12:51-04:00 Haralson County Administrative Assistant <div>The County Extension Administrative Assistant position is a non-exempt professional staff role within UGA Cooperative Extension responsible for handling the many resources offered by the Extension office. A level of independent judgment is necessary to effectively carry out the duties of the job and the incumbent is expected to manage administrative duties by developing techniques and procedures as appropriate. This role works cooperatively with all Extension faculty and staff where applicable and is administratively responsible to the County Extension Coordinator.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478515 2026-04-22T17:24:37-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:38-04:00 Undergraduate Researcher in Soil Science <div>Candidate will be responsible for basic soil chemical, physical, and biological analyses and will be encouraged to work on their own research project. Candidate may be asked to occasionally work outside or in the laboratory environment, as well as work on data collection, curation, and analysis.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488665 2026-06-16T10:30:58-04:00 2026-06-16T10:30:59-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>The University of Georgia is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Postdoctoral Researcher to join a dynamic nutritional neuroscience research lab focused on understanding the molecular, cellular, and behavioral mechanisms of how nutrition impacts brain function and how the brain regulates eating behavior. The candidate will contribute to the direction of ongoing research, design and perform experiments, collect and analyze data, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, undergraduate and graduate students, write papers, attend scientific meetings, and write grants. This is an excellent opportunity for candidates interested in postdoctoral training in nutritional neuroscience research within a collaborative academic environment.</div> FACS-Nutritional Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478614 2026-04-22T17:33:27-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:27-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant (Ph.D.) - Dutta This will be a Ph.D. position starting Spring 2021 in the Department of Plant Pathology, College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences, The University of Georgia - Tifton campus. The position is based in Coastal Plain Experiment Station in GA. The successful candidate will be responsible for surveying commercial cole crops fields for the distribution of fungicide resistance among Alternaria sp. using traditional and molecular methods. Candidate should have completed a Master's Degree in Plant Pathology, and be interested in basic and applied research in Plant Pathology. Candidate will  have the opportunity to work in a multi-state and multi-disciplinary team of scientists with ample opportunities to interact directly with stakeholders. CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494821 2026-07-21T11:46:06-04:00 2026-07-21T11:46:06-04:00 Food Service Worker II (Late Night) <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work in the performance of advanced food service duties in dining halls or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for limited supervision over subordinate food service workers engaged in serving food and cleaning facilities for limited food preparation tasks and for related food service duties that are more advanced and responsible than the duties of Food Service Worker I. Employees of this class apply limited skills and knowledge that are acquired through experience. Duties include responsibility for instructing subordinate food service workers in dining hall techniques and methods; for maintaining high standards of cleanliness; and for assuring that patrons are served in a pleasant and courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477823 2026-04-21T17:57:59-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:00-04:00 LVT  - SA Specialty Services- Orthopedics <div>The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine teaching hospital is seeking a licensed veterinary technician to join our Orthopedics service. We strive to provide advanced veterinary medicine to our patients. The LVT in the Orthopedics service area works with small animal patients who are in the hospital from an emergent health issue, or planned visit. Duties expected will include diagnostic imaging (radiography, CT scanning), execute pre-, peri-, and post-operative care for surgical patients, monitor patients under anesthesia, monitoring, assist in maintaining surgical suite and equipment before, during and after surgery, provide proper physical restraint to allow for safe handling of patients, instruct and supervise students in proper clinical techniques to support patient care, keep patients cleaned and groomed, place and maintain IV catheters, administer and monitor patient diets as prescribed by the clinician, exercise patients as prescribed, collect or assist with the collection of the patient’s blood, urine, and tissue samples, properly submits patient’s blood, urine, and tissue samples for analysis, assist with and instruct students in performing proper physical examinations and diagnostic procedures, properly medicate patients as directed by the clinician, teach students proper patient restraint for safe handling of patients, serve in an advanced role in patient care and client communication, display a willingness to guide, mentor, and support faculty, residents, interns, and fellow team members with instruction.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Anim Spc Srvc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478753 2026-04-22T17:42:17-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:18-04:00 Temporary Technician (Peach) <div>The vector ecology group at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented candidate to support an applied research program focused on mosquito surveillance in agricultural and natural environments. This position centers on field sampling of mosquitoes in commercial pig barns and surrounding natural habitats, contributing to studies of vector ecology, pathogen transmission risk, and environmental drivers of mosquito abundance. The successful candidate will conduct routine and targeted mosquito collections using a variety of trapping methods, maintain accurate field records, and ensure proper handling, labeling, and transport of specimens. Work in pig barn environments necessitating comfort around livestock, adherence to strict biosecurity protocols, and willing to operate in warm, humid, and odor-intensive conditions. Sampling in natural habitats may involve variable terrain, evening or early morning collections, and occasional overnight trap deployments.<br>In addition to fieldwork, the candidate will assist with general laboratory duties, including specimen sorting and identification, sample preparation, chemical handling, equipment maintenance, inventory management, and data entry. Support for research logistics—such as coordinating field schedules, preparing supplies, maintaining sampling equipment, and assisting with regulatory compliance—will also be needed.<br><br></div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498428 2026-08-06T12:21:56-04:00 2026-08-06T12:21:56-04:00 PROGRAM SPECIALIST II <div>This full-time position will provide administrative support to the Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant team at the Program’s Brunswick facility. The position will also provide assistance in maintaining the facility and associated vehicles, vessels and grounds, as well as support ongoing extension, research and outreach programs as needed.</div> PSO-Marine Extension Service https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478123 2026-04-21T18:35:03-04:00 2026-04-21T18:35:03-04:00 Open Rank Clinical Track - SX IR 2026 <div>The Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery at the College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, invites applications for a clinical (non-tenure) track faculty position in veterinary soft tissue surgery and interventional radiology at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor.<br><br>The major responsibilities of this position will be to teach and provide service in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, teach pre-clinical didactic and laboratory courses in soft tissue surgery to veterinary students, to actively participate in the training of surgery and non-surgery house officers, and to build the interventional radiology service caseload. Proportionate assignments for each area are based on the interests of the candidate, faculty assignment, and the missions of the soft tissue surgery and interventional radiology programs and department.<br><br>The successful candidate will join a soft tissue surgery service with four full-time faculty members, six residents, and two dedicated technicians in support of the University of Georgia Veterinary Teaching Hospital, a 300,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility. The candidate in this position will spend approximately half of their clinical service time on one of two soft tissue surgery services and the other half of their time focused on interventional radiology cases. The UGA Cardiology and Internal Medicine services currently perform a variety of interventional radiology procedures; however, we are looking to expand our clinical offerings in this area.</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504304 2026-09-03T10:26:32-04:00 2026-09-03T10:26:32-04:00 IT Professional Assistant <div>Builds and maintains computer lab images for lab and staff computers. Ensures that the labs and client computers operate within established departmental policy and procedural guidelines. Develops and maintains EITS desktop standards and procedures. Provides client technical support on Windows and Apple hardware in addition to software products. Provides technical support on supported mobile devices. Contact the appropriate technicians with outstanding issues in a timely manner. Determines and maintains computer resources by established procedures performed on an as-needed basis, as well as on a day-to-day basis, such as software updates.</div> EITS-Client Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478588 2026-04-22T17:32:11-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:11-04:00 IP Summer Student Worker This position will perform general clerical duties that includes filing, editing, data entry, and event planning preparation. OGE-International Partnerships https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494078 2026-07-16T15:37:04-04:00 2026-08-11T14:37:23-04:00 Student Services Front Office Student Assistant <div>Provide front office assistance for the Rankin Smith, Sr. Student-Athlete Academic Center to include answering phones, filing, assisting student-athletes and walk-ins. Provide assistance as needed to any member of the full-time staff. Ensure compliance of NCAA, SEC and institutional rules and regulations pertaining to the area of Academic Services.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477756 2026-04-21T17:31:40-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:41-04:00 Cook I <div>Skilled cooking work in the preparation of foods for a cafeteria. Work involves the general preparation and cooking of a variety of foods, or the specialized preparations of meats and vegetables. Work involves responsibility of neatness and cleanliness in preparing food, and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Works under the supervision of a Cook 2 or Chef.</div> Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478713 2026-04-22T17:40:19-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:20-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>The Research Professional has duties to design develop, organize, and supervise the work on a major recombinant protein expression project in the lab employing bacterial and/or mammalian cell culture systems. The goals of this research project will provide large-scale protein production for enzyme structural and functional studies including design of mutations for protein engineering for improved protein stability and expression. The position entails establishing project goals, working directly with supervising faculty to design and implement new recombinant constructs, developing priorities among the large number of constructs, generation and large-scale production of recombinant DNAs, and supervising work of other research staff to accomplish these goals. Duties and expertise also include protein structural visualization and modeling, sequence/structural analysis for protein engineering, and development of high-throughput expression methods for analysis of engineered enzymatic functions. Work duties include close collaboration with senior faculty and working within a larger research group of postdoctoral researchers, research technicians, and undergraduate researchers to develop strategies for high quantity protein expression, and close interaction with investigators at other research sites for the design and generation of new constructs for collaborative studies. Additional roles involve supervision of research professionals, technicians and undergraduate researchers on executing protocols for protein expression in bacteria and mammalian cells, and training research technicians and undergraduate researchers on standard operating procedures. Direct supervision of the Research Professional by senior faculty is anticipated.<br><br></div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497679 2026-08-03T16:48:41-04:00 2026-08-03T16:48:41-04:00 NEPA Professional <div>Serves as an environmental protection professional with primary responsibility for supporting the installations National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA) Coordinator in performing a variety of environmental protection functions associated with the implementation of NEPA and related regulations and requirements.<br><br>The incumbent independently plans and carries out most duties without specific instructions or direction. The employee normally consults with the NEPA Coordinator and/or the supervisor only before proceeding with non-routine technical matters or unprecedented regulatory issues. Completed work is reviewed for technical soundness and compliance with regulatory requirements. The principal guidelines are NEPA, agency regulations; e.g., AR 200-2, and procedural instructions. The incumbent must also refer to a variety of other documents including technical manuals on other environmental protection programs, contracting procedures, and agency and installation administrative manuals. Incumbent will use some judgment in determining how guidelines should be interpreted and applied to specific situations.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478063 2026-04-21T18:29:27-04:00 2026-04-21T18:29:28-04:00 Assistant Professor: Insect Ecologist <div>The Department of Entomology at the University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track position (9-months) in insect ecology, to be based on the Athens campus at the Assistant Professor rank.&nbsp;<br><br>The position includes research (70%), teaching (25%) and service (5%). The appointee will be expected to build a nationally prominent, extramurally-funded research program that complements existing strengths in the Entomology Department, as well as contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring. We seek a teacher-scholar with a strong commitment to engaging students both in the classroom and through research mentorship at the undergraduate, M.S., and Ph.D. levels. Teaching loads are consistent with our high expectations for research. The successful candidate may teach courses in insect ecology, aquatic entomology, general entomology, insect natural history, and/or areas appropriate given their expertise and experience. In addition to strengthening and expanding the capacity of existing programs in the department, the research program is expected to be collaborative and multidisciplinary, including elements that solve important or emerging problems identified by appropriate stakeholders. Applicants are encouraged to consider how they can engage with departmental and college facilities, including the Georgia Museum of Natural History, the UGA Black Fly lab, and the CAES Research and Education Centers. This individual is also expected to be active in departmental and university service.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504158 2026-09-02T11:43:42-04:00 2026-09-02T11:43:43-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor <div>The Department Finance in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for one or more full-time tenure-track or tenured faculty positions at the assistant or associate professor level. The positions will begin in the fall semester of 2027, with an anticipated employment start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Finance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500516 2026-08-17T13:06:11-04:00 2026-08-20T10:21:38-04:00 Assistant Professor - Exercise Psychology <div>The Department of Kinesiology at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor in the area of Exercise Psychology to begin in Fall 2027. The Department seeks to hire a faculty member who will engage in high-quality research, instruction, and service.<br><br><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Develop and maintain a rigorous research program addressing important and novel exercise psychology-related problems</li><li>Seek extramural funding to support research</li><li>Provide high-quality instruction to undergraduate and/or graduate students</li><li>Mentor undergraduate and/or graduate students in research</li><li>Provide high-quality service to the University, state of Georgia, and the field of Kinesiology</li></ul> COE-Kinesiology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478417 2026-04-22T17:19:59-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:00-04:00 Temporary Painter - FMD Griffin Campus <div>This position is responsible for preparation and paint related work on Campus facilities including determining painting needs, color blending and matching and sequences of painting operations and method. Employee functions will include maintaining tool and equipment, paint stock and proper paint disposal. Assignments are received in writing and orally and work is performed under general direction from supervisor. Work is reviewed through inspection while in progress and upon completion. The position will be required to perform other functions related to the general activities in facilities operation and maintenance.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480048 2026-04-29T13:17:50-04:00 2026-04-29T13:17:51-04:00 Assistant Director, S-SARE Program <div>Assistant Director of the Southern Region Sustainable Agriculture Research and Education program: In addition to acting as the assistant to the director of the program in all matters, the position has the autonomous authority to manage three independent grant programs within the S-SARE portfolio.<br><br><strong><em>This is a grant-funded position with continued employment based on the needs of the project as well as available funding and satisfactory job performance and progress.</em></strong></div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478539 2026-04-22T17:26:01-04:00 2026-08-19T14:29:45-04:00 Math Tutor - Student Assistant Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490694 2026-06-29T16:44:14-04:00 2026-06-29T16:44:14-04:00 Fiscal Affairs Manager <div>The Fiscal Affairs Manager for the Office for Student Success and Achievement (OSSA) leads the office’s business operations and strategy and develops strategic solutions that support business success across the division. This individual directs the use and monitoring of a variety of complex financial accounts to ensure compliance and maintain balance throughout each account’s life cycle.</div><div>This individual supervises business office staff to ensure adherence to all UGA policies, procedures, and deadlines. This individual guides the creation, distribution, and analysis of financial reports for key stakeholders within OSSA and the Office of the Vice President for Instruction to support strategic growth and success.</div><div>This individual manages HR processes for the division office, including payroll processing, leave request approvals, time approval, and the creation of UGAJobs and OneUSG Connect transactions. This individual provides guidance to the Director on HR-related matters such as personnel changes, payroll, position funding, and performance evaluations.</div> VPI-Office for Student Success https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478633 2026-04-22T17:34:02-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:02-04:00 Temporary Field/Lab Research - Robacker <div>The position will work closely with faculty and technicians to assist in field, greenhouse, and laboratory experiments in horticulture and plant breeding.&nbsp; Attention to detail is critical.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496065 2026-07-27T13:15:08-04:00 2026-07-27T13:15:08-04:00 Plant Pathology Student Assistant-Chowdhury 2 <div>This is an entry-level student research worker position. The incumbent will work during the summer to aid the Cotton and Vegetable Crops Nematology team on research related activities. Responsibilities for the incumbent include but are not limited to watering greenhouse, extracting nematode from soil, enumerating nematode eggs, collecting soil samples from field, mixing soil samples, aiding in harvesting and planting of crops, and cleaning laboratory supplies. Depending on performance, experience and interest the incumbent will be given the opportunity to conduct research on plant-parasitic nematode of cotton and vegetable crops. Such research findings can then be presented by the incumbent at national and international conferences.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477865 2026-04-21T18:00:25-04:00 2026-04-21T18:00:25-04:00 Sous Chef <div>This position will be a highly skilled food preparation worker who will assist the chef in the preparation of a wide variety of meats, fish, starches, casseroles, breads, vegetables and desserts. Knowledge and skills in food quality, food safety and food preparation will be needed. A person in this position will work with very limited supervision and may lead other employees to complete assigned tasks.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503313 2026-08-27T17:09:51-04:00 2026-08-27T17:09:52-04:00 Administrative Specialist <div>This position provides executive-level support and is responsible for efficient and effective</div><div>management of the offices in the Department of Physics and Astronomy. Administrative duties include managing the Department Head’s and the Senior Associate Head’s correspondence and calendars, serving as a liaison with internal and external constituents, anticipating and addressing needs of the Department and Senior Associate Heads by using independent judgment. Responsibilities involve handling information that is sensitive, high-profile, and confidential in nature. Activities and decisions are highly complex and involve significant independent action and judgment while adhering to institutional policies.</div> Franklin-Physics & Astronomy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499490 2026-08-12T10:29:06-04:00 2026-08-12T10:29:07-04:00 Houseperson - Temporary <div>This position provides support for housekeepers and laundry personnel. Responsibilities include stocking housekeeping closets with linen and supplies, delivering linen and supplies to housekeepers, removing dirty linen and trash from housekeeper carts, and removing dirty linens and trash from hotel rooms. This position also assists with laundry responsibilities such as sorting, washing, drying, and folding linen and towels.</div> PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478375 2026-04-22T17:16:17-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:18-04:00 Ph.D. Graduate Research Assistant - Huang <div>The duties include conducting laboratory experiments under supervision, data analysis, report drafting, and laboratory management and maintenance.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478806 2026-04-22T17:46:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:48-04:00 Molecular Plant Nematology Lab Student Assistant – Mitchum Lab <div>The Molecular Plant Nematology Lab Assistant position will support laboratory and greenhouse research related to plant diseases and the biology of their causal agents under the direction of a faculty member and/or lab manager/post-docs/graduate students. Duties include, but are not limited to, participation in lab experimentation, collection and summary of data, in support of molecular plant-nematode interaction research activities; assisting with plant and/or pathogen care by watering of plants in greenhouses and growth chambers, including short periods on a rotational basis during assigned weekends; assisting with sample collection, media preparation, and other lab protocols; assisting with lab maintenance and chores, including dishwashing and autoclaving, stocking supplies, cleaning the lab, disposing of biohazardous materials.</div> CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504664 2026-09-04T16:04:43-04:00 2026-09-04T16:04:43-04:00 Permanent Residency and O-1 Advisor (II) <div>This position oversees employment‑based Permanent Residency (PR) sponsorships and selected nonimmigrant petitions, with a specialization in I‑140 immigrant petitions and O‑1 sponsorships. The incumbent assists foreign national employees and sponsoring departments with immigration procedures, ensuring all petitions, applications, and supporting documentation are prepared accurately and filed in a timely manner. The position establishes and maintains compliant immigration records, manages assigned program components, compiles reports, assists with budget tracking related to immigration cases, and monitors departmental projects related to lawful permanent residency and employment‑based sponsorships.</div> OGE-Immigration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501655 2026-08-20T13:59:44-04:00 2026-08-20T13:59:44-04:00 Van Operator (Partial Year) <div><strong>This is a benefits eligible, partial year position (August - May). Each selected candidate will sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.<br>&nbsp;<br></strong>Transport passengers with registered disabilities in an accessible van to and from various campus locations in accordance with applicable laws and department procedures. Assist passengers entering and exiting the vehicle as necessary. Inspect vehicle before, during, and after shift to ensure vehicle is in proper operating condition. Complete necessary paperwork, including timesheets and vehicle condition reports. Operates other vehicle equipment such as electronic AVL equipment and wheelchair ramps. Be trained to occasionally fill in in the front office answering phones and scheduling ADA pickups and drop-offs using TransLoc software. Be trained to occasionally drive library van route service between Athens and Atlanta. Occasional charters and special assignments.&nbsp; Drug and alcohol testing by the US Department of Transportation.</div> Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478497 2026-04-22T17:24:04-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:05-04:00 Deer Research Technician-Louisiana <div>The technician will be responsible for assisting with the following: capture of adult and juvenile white-tailed deer using various techniques, immobilization of captured animals, monitoring of animals via radio telemetry, and investigating related mortality events. The applicant will also assist in data collection and management. Further, the candidate will interact with state agency personnel and private landowners while working on various aspects of the project</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486660 2026-06-03T09:50:04-04:00 2026-06-03T09:50:05-04:00 Sous Chef <div>This position will be a highly skilled food preparation worker who will assist the chef in the preparation of a wide variety of meats, fish, starches, casseroles, breads, vegetables and desserts. Knowledge and skills in food quality, food safety and food preparation will be needed. A person in this position will work with very limited supervision and may lead other employees to complete assigned tasks.</div> Auxiliary Oglethorpe https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478163 2026-04-22T08:18:42-04:00 2026-04-22T08:18:43-04:00 College Adviser - Georgia College Advising Corps (GCAC) <div>The Georgia College Advising Corps (GCAC) recruits service-minded recent graduates to support low income, first-generation, and underrepresented students in accessing higher education. We seek individuals with a wide range of academic and professional experiences who are approachable, self-motivated, and deeply committed to expanding college access.<br><br>GCAC college advisers serve in public high schools across Georgia, working alongside school counseling staff to guide students through the college admissions process. Advisers help students identify best-fit colleges, complete applications, explore financial aid and scholarship opportunities, prepare for entrance exams, and develop informed postsecondary plans.<br><br>Final placement of advisers in schools is determined by program leadership based on overall progammatic need and best fit.<br><br>At the University of Georgia, GCAC advisers are part of the national College Advising Corps network, contributing to a broader movement focused on increasing college enrollment and success for students nationwide.</div> SRVPAA-Institute of Higher Ed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504330 2026-09-03T10:57:39-04:00 2026-09-03T10:57:39-04:00 Student Worker-Medical Equipment Assistant <div>Position will complete various tasks and projects throughout the Veterinary Teaching Hospital as assigned by the Medical Equipment Manager to include assisting with inventory management, repairs, and preventative maintenance of the Veterinary Teaching Hospital medical equipment.</div> VetMed-VTH Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501036 2026-08-18T16:34:54-04:00 2026-08-18T16:34:54-04:00 Assistant Research Scientist <div>The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy seeks an outstanding candidate for a full-time Assistant Research Scientist position to contribute to the College's expanding biomedical and translational research mission at the <strong>UGA Augusta Campus</strong>. This is a 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty appointment within the University of Georgia Research Scientist Track. The successful candidate will lead and support innovative research focused on the molecular, cellular, and physiological mechanisms underlying pulmonary diseases, including inflammatory, infectious, fibrotic, and chronic respiratory disorders.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Research Scientist will be responsible for designing and executing laboratory-based studies, developing novel scientific approaches, analyzing and interpreting complex datasets, and disseminating research findings through peer-reviewed publications and scientific presentations. Additional responsibilities include contributing to sponsored research programs through the preparation of grant proposals and progress reports, collaborating with faculty, research staff, students, and external partners, and providing mentorship and scientific guidance to research trainees.</div> Pharmacy-Clin & Admin Pharmacy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478462 2026-04-22T17:22:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:24-04:00 STUWK / Office Assistant GA 4H - Athens <div>This position provides general assistance with office/clerical work.</div> CAES-State 4-H https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/484141 2026-05-20T10:05:49-04:00 2026-05-20T10:05:50-04:00 Agricultural Specialist I <div>This position reports directly to the Swine Farm Manager in the Animal and Dairy Science Department (ADS) and ultimately to the Head of ADS. The principal duties of the position include, but are not limited to, 1) providing day-to-day operational support under the direction of the Swine Farm Manager and Sr. Farm Manager of swine operations. 2) direct involvement in feed preparation, facility maintenance and repairs. 3) equipment operation, maintenance and repair 4) working with faculty and farm staff to ensure that the research, teaching and extension missions are accomplished.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478568 2026-04-22T17:29:49-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:50-04:00 Post-Doctoral Research Associate The Laboratory of Archaeology at The University of Georgia anticipates being able to hire a Post-doctoral Research Fellow in Geographic Information Systems and Computer Modeling in Archaeology. This would be a three-year, 12-month, full-time position. The primary role of the individual will be to collaborate with the Laboratory Director and the Historic Preservation Division of the Georgia Department of Natural Resource on modeling and risk assessment for archaeological sites in Georgia. The ideal person for this position should have demonstratable skills using ArcGIS with regards to large-scale modeling, knowledge of geostatistical methods, a familiarity with state site file data, and the ability to write up process and procedures related to site file research. A familiarity with southeastern archaeology is a preferred, but persons who are trained in other regions are encouraged to apply. Franklin-Anthropology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492268 2026-07-09T12:23:20-04:00 2026-07-09T12:23:21-04:00 4-H McDuffie County AmeriCorps State Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting required impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members must comply with AmeriCorps requirements such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other required trainings.<br><br></div><div>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members are required to log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.<br><br></div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478667 2026-04-22T17:37:16-04:00 2026-04-22T17:37:16-04:00 Temporary Field/Lab Assistant - Czarnota <div>This position will assist faculty and staff with greenhouse, research and field plots as well as help with extension and teaching activities . This position will work both indoors and outdoors with minimum supervision. There will also be some work in a greenhouse environment. Duties may also include intermittent out-of-town travel to research plots. Computer experience with word processing, spreadsheet, and graphics software is a plus.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496893 2026-07-30T11:18:00-04:00 2026-07-30T11:18:01-04:00 Fayette County 4-H Program Assistant (PT) <div>This position conducts 5th-8th grade 4-H educational program in-classroom meetings, 9th-12th grade meetings, and a monthly senior 4-H meeting. It will also help 4-H’ers with project achievement and be responsible for weekend events and community service projects.<br>This is a fast-paced position, and activities each day will vary week to week and month to month. Indoor and outdoor activities are expected in this role.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477987 2026-04-21T18:24:48-04:00 2026-04-21T18:24:49-04:00 OPEN RANK Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Diagnostic Imaging <div>The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for two faculty positions in small animal diagnostic imaging at the rank of clinical (non-tenure) or tenure track/tenured assistant, associate, or full professor. To be considered for the tenure track or tenured faculty ranks, documented research productivity commensurate with rank and an interest in developing a research program is required. For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications.<br><br>The major responsibilities of this position are to teach and provide service in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, to teach pre-clinical didactic and laboratory courses in diagnostic imaging to veterinary students, to actively participate in the training of diagnostic imaging and other house officers, and to develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. Proportionate assignments for each area are based on the interests of the candidate, faculty assignment, and the missions of the Diagnostic Imaging program and the Department.<br><br>Successful candidates will join two full-time radiologists. Locum tenens support in ultrasound, and virtual locum tenens support of service and resident training with VetCT, will continue until all diagnostic imaging faculty positions are filled. Our team includes four residents (starting July 2022), eight skilled registered veterinary technicians (two VTS-DI), a veterinary assistant, a PRN MRI technologist, and a full-time diagnostic imaging systems administrator. The goal is to have five full-time radiologists. The service currently enjoys the following equipment: a Siemens Skyra 3.0 Tesla MRI magnet and Siemens Somatom Sensation 64 slice CT, both of which accommodate large and small animals; GE Logiq-S8, Canon Aplio i700 and Toshiba Xario; Canon fluoroscopy, Canon digital radiography (3 DR Rooms), Canon RadPro portable DR unit; a dedicated interventional radiology suite with OEC 9900 Elite mobile C-arm fluoroscopy; IS2 Research NuCamma SR 53cm x 39 cm Free Floater gamma camera (Mirage nuclear medicine software); integrated DICOM viewing and archival system (Hyland NilRead viewer and Mach 7 VNA); and MedQ RIS and Reporting software.<br><br>For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications.&nbsp;</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503832 2026-09-01T09:11:24-04:00 2026-09-01T09:11:25-04:00 Administrative Specialist <div>The Department Assistant for the Department of Public Administration and Policy in the School of Public and International Affairs is the primary point of contact for the Department and works independently to oversee general operations. In addition, the Department Assistant coordinates faculty recruitment<strong>,</strong>special events, and internal and external communications (social media). The Department Assistant prepares and initiates departmental business processes that flow to SPIA’s shared services business team. The Department Assistant reports directly to the Head of the Department of Public Administration and Policy.</div> SPIA-Public Admin & Policy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500134 2026-08-14T11:41:51-04:00 2026-08-14T11:41:51-04:00 Research Technician - McGregor <div>This position supports Dr. Cecilia McGregor’s cucurbit breeding and genetics program. The position will work closely with faculty, postdocs and graduate students to assist in field, greenhouse, and laboratory experiments in horticulture and plant breeding. Attention to detail is critical. <br><br><em>This is a limited-term appointment expected to end</em><strong><em> 2 years </em></strong><em>after the start date. Renewal or extension beyond the initial term is anticipated but not guaranteed and will depend on project needs, the availability of funding, and job performance. The position may be renewed on an annual basis, contingent upon continued grant support.</em></div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478400 2026-04-22T17:19:30-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:30-04:00 Temporary Laboratory Assistant - Huang <div>Incumbent on this position will work under the supervision of a PI to support research activities, including, preforming laboratory experiments, conducting data analysis, drafting research reports, laboratory management and maintenance, and other activities that the PI specify.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478837 2026-04-22T17:50:39-04:00 2026-09-01T11:03:44-04:00 Student Assistant (Dining Admin) <div>The Student Assistant (Dining Admin) will be responsible for assisting the Dining Services Administrative team with working the front desk, answering phones, assisting with various tasks and helping in the dining commons when necessary.</div> Auxiliary Dining Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502585 2026-08-25T15:00:51-04:00 2026-08-25T15:00:52-04:00 Brantley County 4-H  Agent <div>This position will provide educational programming in the County. This position will also provide management and oversight of the County 4-H Program in cooperation with other staff members. The County 4-H Program is robust and provides a wide variety of educational opportunities for youth. This position will work cooperatively with county 4-H staff and provide oversight, management, and support of the 4-H program. As necessary, deliver 4-H programming in a variety of settings including in-school, afterschool, and through participation in state and district events. This position utilizes the expertise of and works closely with advisory groups, community leaders, public officials and representatives of intended audiences to analyze data, identifies needs, and assists in developing educational programs.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and adult clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478519 2026-04-22T17:24:45-04:00 2026-08-26T10:04:37-04:00 Athletic Academic Mentor - Non-Student <div>Assist student-athletes in their academic endeavors by providing supplemental support.<br>This part-time position requires academic mentors to meet with student-athletes weekly during regularly scheduled sessions to foster academic independence and encourage self-regulated learning. Pay is $15 per 1-hour mentor session.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488743 2026-06-16T15:19:17-04:00 2026-08-31T13:10:18-04:00 Gopher Tortoise Survey - Seasonal Technician <div>This position will be largely ﬁeld-based to assist with surveys for gopher tortoises and indigo snakes), specifically line transect distance sampling and burrow scoping. We use pre-development data to project impacts and collaboratively develop plans for the avoidance or relocation of impacted species on industry lands (e.g., utility-scale solar, mineral surface mining) with project sponsors and natural resource agencies. We further work with project sponsors to develop and implement the local stewardship, habitat management and restoration, and staff/contractor education and awareness initiatives. We also conduct research on the post-translocation status of gopher tortoises, including vegetation assessments using transects and UAVs/drones in the recipient habitats. We use these data to engage adaptive management and process improvement for wildlife and habitat. Surveys will require weekly deployment to various sites in the coastal plain of Georgia, often involving overnight stays at a hotel while deployed or daily commutes to closer ﬁeld sites. Additionally, this position will involve office work, such as transferring and managing datasets, visualizing ﬁeld data and generating output in ArcGIS Pro, and assisting with reports and publications, as examples. This position will work alongside a group of researchers, usually deploying as part of 2-person survey crews. As part of onboarding, the technician will undergo speciﬁc task training with current project researchers regarding ﬁeld tasks as well as compliance with UGA and partner protocols, which includes but is not limited to vehicle safety, cybersecurity, animal use/IACUC certiﬁcation, and working with minors. Assistance with other grant-funded projects may be engaged as needed, but is not guaranteed as part of this position.</div> PSO-Marine Extension Service https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478617 2026-04-22T17:33:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:34-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate This position will organize and manage research tasks across several large-scale research studies focused on social determinants of health. The lab currently has several studies that are ongoing, including: (1) Annual studies focused on how stressful life experiences influence response to influenza vaccination; (2) an ongoing longitudinal study of African American families in rural Georgia; and (3) a new study of risk and resilience among African American families. Tasks will be distributed across the three projects, and day-to-day work will vary based on fluctuations in each study’s current needs. This person in this position will supervise the work of Research Assistants and coordinate with staff at the Clinical and Translational Research Unit at UGA to facilitate data collection. The postdoctoral associate is responsible for conducting data quality checks and addressing missing data before preparing data for analyses. The associate will assist with preparation of (1) all IRB materials throughout the duration of the project, (2) project updates as requested by the Principal Investigator, (3) annual progress reports for submission to the federal sponsor and private foundations.  The associate will analyze data and collaborate with their faculty mentor to prepare manuscripts for scientific review and publication. VPR-Center for Family Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494929 2026-07-21T15:44:14-04:00 2026-07-21T16:25:54-04:00 Associate Director, EPOMBA Alumni Engagement & Rankings <div>The Executive, Professional and Online EPOMBA Program office seeks an Associate Director of EPOMBA Alumni Engagement &amp; Rankings to lead a high-impact function at the intersection of alumni relations, data strategy, and global rankings performance. This role is responsible for building lifelong relationships with EPOMBA graduates while designing and executing a data-driven strategy that strengthens the school’s position in leading EPOMBA rankings (Financial Times, QS, U.S. News &amp; World Report, Bloomberg Businessweek).<br><br></div><div>This is a highly visible, cross-functional leadership role that connects alumni engagement directly to institutional reputation, requiring both strategic thinking and operational excellence.<br><br></div> Terry-Exec/Prof MBA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477825 2026-04-21T17:58:05-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:05-04:00 Licensed Veterinary Technician - Anesthesia <div>The primary purpose and function of the Licensed Veterinary Technician is to support veterinarians in ensuring quality veterinary care, advocating for pets, and educating clients. For Anesthesia, the LVT assists the senior veterinary and veterinary technician students with anesthetic management for a variety of surgical and diagnostic procedures. Performing and teaching competent catheter (venous, arterial, urinary) placement, regional anesthetic nerve blocks, and intubation skills in a variety of species. Ensuring the successful recovery of post anesthesia patients. Accurate maintenance of controlled drug log and anesthesia patient records. Maintenance and care of anesthesia related equipment. Stocking and maintenance of assigned crash cart.</div> VetMed-VTH Sm Animal Anesthes https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478762 2026-04-22T17:42:34-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:34-04:00 Experience UGA – Student Worker <div><em>Student workers with Experience UGA in the Mary Frances Early College of Education work with kindergarten children from elementary schools in the Clarke County School District using lesson plans designed to teach measuring and related concepts (tall/short, long/short, big/little). Student workers typically welcome children to the College, lead small groups through activities, and assist with their departure. Student workers are also responsible for setting up prior to the session and cleaning up afterward. Attending a training session and passing a background check to be completed prior to employment. </em><strong><em>Qualified student workers will be available to work on Friday mornings and will be scheduled on an as-needed basis, up to 24 hours per semester.</em></strong></div> COE-Academic Programs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498464 2026-08-06T13:11:36-04:00 2026-08-06T13:11:36-04:00 Veterinary Assistant -LA <div>This position is responsible for handling animal patients in the Large Animal Hospital. Handling/restraint of large animals includes multiple species: Primarily horses/cows, but may include sheep, pigs, goats and camelids. The handler is expected to be able to safely handle all temperaments of horses. This includes handling for lameness exams (jogging/lunging), procedures, standing surgeries, radiology/bone scan, neuro exams and stallion collection. Other duties include assisting LVT’s/Clinicians/Students/Client Support Coordinator in any capacity as needed for patient care, general housekeeping/stocking/stall maintenance, animal/sample transport, anesthetic induction/recovery, and ability to readily utilize Vetview/Cubex. In addition, maintaining tractors and associated equipment that are used to transport supplies and large animal patients throughout the large animal hospital complex, local farms, along with going to retrieve hay and feed.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478594 2026-04-22T17:32:22-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:22-04:00 Temporary Field/Greenhouse Assistant To assist in field preparation, maintenance, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494184 2026-07-17T11:14:11-04:00 2026-07-17T11:14:12-04:00 Student Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal <div>This position will give assistance to the senior veterinary technicians and veterinary staff on the care of ill or injured client-owned animals brought to the Veterinary Teaching Hospital in the hopes of recovery.</div> VetMed-VTH Sm Animal Intermed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477767 2026-04-21T17:32:02-04:00 2026-04-21T17:32:02-04:00 Construction Worker II <div>This advanced position within the Grounds Heavy Equipment division is responsible for supporting a wide range of construction and maintenance operations. The incumbent assists Concrete Masons with the forming and placement of concrete and serves as a spotter during excavation activities. Responsibilities include assisting with backfilling and grading for curb, sidewalk, storm sewer installations, and utility repairs, as well as verifying grade specifications for asphalt and concrete placement.<br><br></div><div>The employee operates a dump truck and demonstrates moderate proficiency in the operation of heavy equipment, including but not limited to skid steers, backhoes, mini excavators, and breakers. These skills are utilized in hauling operations and in support of various trade-related tasks.<br><br></div><div>Candidates who do not currently possess a Class B Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) will be required to complete the in-house Entry Level Driver Training (ELDT) program and obtain a CDL Learner’s Permit within six months of hire. During this period, operation will be limited to equipment not requiring a Class B CDL.<br><br></div><div>Additional responsibilities include proficiency in traffic control and providing support as needed across projects. The incumbent will perform other assigned duties as required and must report during inclement weather conditions to assist with snow and ice removal, as well as clearing downed trees.<br><br></div> FMD-Grounds-Construction https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478716 2026-04-22T17:40:25-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:25-04:00 Temporary Field/Summer Assistant - Vines <div>To assist in field preparation, maintenance, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497756 2026-08-04T11:28:44-04:00 2026-08-04T11:28:45-04:00 Part-Time Building Services Worker <div>The part-time Building Service Worker is a key member of the Facilities Maintenance department and reports to the Building Services Supervisor. The Building Services Worker performs manual work in a variety of cleaning and related duties in the University Health Center (UHC), including exam rooms, restrooms, conference rooms, and offices. The work of this position involves the performance of cleaning in an assigned building area. The primary responsibility of this position is the effective use of proper methods and materials in cleaning and caring for building areas and equipment. This individual works under close supervision and follows well established routines, procedures, and infection control standards.</div> UHC-Facilities Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478077 2026-04-21T18:30:56-04:00 2026-04-21T18:30:56-04:00 Lecturer <div>This is a nine-month, non-tenure track appointment, animal science lecturer (95% teaching) position in the Department of Animal and Dairy Science in collaboration with the Regenerative Bio Science Center, College of Agriculture and Environmental Sciences at the University of Georgia. The position will be located at the UGA Athens Campus.<br><br>The main responsibility of this position is teaching. Research and administrative duties are not required. The teaching assignment is flexible and will be determined in alignment with program needs, departmental priorities, available resources, and the professional interests and goals of both the Regenerative Bioscience program and the strengths of the selected candidate. This position will primarily teach within the RBIO undergraduate program, with additional opportunities to contribute to graduate-level instruction and course development. The successful candidate will play a key role in strengthening RBIO curriculum by teaching existing courses and developing new classes that align with their expertise and programmatic needs. This could include, but is not limited to, cell and gene therapies, tissue engineering, cell manufacturing, experiential laboratory courses, public service-oriented learning experiences, senior capstone course, or other relevant regenerative bioscience areas of focus. The faculty member is expected to advise and mentor students, enhance career readiness pathways, and foster meaningful industry or community partnerships.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504172 2026-09-02T12:13:45-04:00 2026-09-02T12:13:46-04:00 Transit Technician II <div>Troubleshoot, diagnose and repair defects on fleet vehicles. Perform maintenance on transit buses and other fleet vehicles in accordance with industry standards, safe practices and manufacturer's specifications.&nbsp; Applicants submit to drug and alcohol testing by the US Department of Transportation.</div> Auxiliary Transit Maint https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500541 2026-08-17T13:55:37-04:00 2026-08-17T13:55:38-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of International Affairs (IA) at the University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in the fall of 2027. We seek a scholar who is trained in the concepts, methods, and approaches used in the study of comparative politics.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The University of Georgia supports a culture of active learning in which students are active participants in the classroom and instructors utilize instructional practices that purposefully engage all students in the learning process.</div> SPIA-International Affairs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478421 2026-04-22T17:20:06-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:07-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant - Ortega <div>Temporary research assistant will be tasked to do: Autoclave biohazard waste, prepare microbiological media, perform PCR, maintain laboratory inventory and assist students in their research.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480446 2026-05-01T11:15:38-04:00 2026-07-10T10:37:32-04:00 Animal Caretaker <div>This work involves the cleaning and maintenance of patient facilities in the Vet Teaching Hospital. This includes:<br>1. Removing manure and soiled shavings/bedding in patient stalls and kennels.<br>2. Cleaning and disinfecting discharged patient stalls.<br>3. In specific areas of the hospital, floors are swept, vacuumed and hosed clean.<br>4. New patient stalls are prepared as directed by Lead Caretaker or Supervisor.<br>5. Various other facilities of the hospital in both large and small animal are also cleaned and maintained on a regular basis.<br>6. Assistance is also given to DVM’s, Technicians and Students where appropriate and requested.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478541 2026-04-22T17:26:04-04:00 2026-04-22T17:26:04-04:00 Oliveira-Hort PhD CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490715 2026-06-30T09:51:35-04:00 2026-06-30T11:59:07-04:00 Electronic & Continuing Resources Librarian <div>Reporting to the Assistant Director of Collections for Electronic Resources and Licensing, the Electronic &amp; Continuing Resources Librarian provides leadership and expertise in the acquisition, licensing, access management, and ongoing evaluation of electronic resources. This position plays a central role in negotiating and managing licenses for databases, electronic journals, e-books, data sets, and emerging digital content that support the University of Georgia’s research, teaching, and public service mission.<br><br>The Electronic &amp; Continuing Resources Librarian leads a unit of approximately 2 staff hiring, training, and managing performance. Working collaboratively across library units and with campus partners, the role ensures that electronic resources are licensed in ways that balance user access, fiscal responsibility, legal compliance, and strategic priorities such as open access, accessibility, and data-driven decision making. The incumbent contributes to library wide collection strategies, vendor relationships, and assessment initiatives, and serves as a key point of contact for license interpretation and use rights throughout the organization.<br><br>UGA librarians are non-tenured faculty members.&nbsp; UGA offers an attractive benefits program including a choice of health and retirement plans, dental plan, vision plan, tuition remission, paid relocation, 21 days annual leave, 12 days sick leave, and 13 paid holidays.</div> Libraries-Acquisitions Serials https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478635 2026-04-22T17:34:06-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:07-04:00 Student Research Assistant = van Iersel CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496375 2026-07-28T00:01:46-04:00 2026-07-28T00:01:47-04:00 Associate Director of Alumni & Industry Relations <div>This position is based in the UGA Odum School of Ecology and reports directly to the Director of Development. The Associate Director of Alumni &amp; Industry Relations promotes development through alumni relations, corporate and donor engagement, and event management, connecting stakeholders to the school’s priorities. The Associate Director will independently manage various special projects to expand partnerships, build relationships and increase school visibility. This position will also manage a stewardship portfolio of alumni and corporate donors with the goal of expanding development functions and institutional impact.</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477873 2026-04-21T18:00:44-04:00 2026-07-20T08:55:33-04:00 Project Nest Phlebotomist <div>The primary responsibility of the Phlebotomist is collecting and processing blood samples (e.g., centrifuging in the lab, performing aliquots on-site) as well as proper labeling and adherence to biosafety procedures. Phlebotomist may be asked to collect other physical measurements, such as blood pressure, height, weight, and hip/waist measures. Duties may include recording vital signs and medical histories, preparing patients for examination, and drawing blood. Ensures compliance with applicable policies and regulations.</div> VPR-Center for Family Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503328 2026-08-28T08:50:03-04:00 2026-08-28T08:50:03-04:00 Appling County Administratve Assistant <div>The County Extension Administrative Assistant is responsible for a variety of general office tasks. Work includes the performance of standardized office duties which involve using judgment based on knowledge gained through experience. Assignments that depart from established institutional or countyprocedures are approved by a supervisor, but employees will be expected to develop their own techniques and procedures. May coordinate functions with Extension staff and/or program assistants. This incumbent will work cooperatively with all agents and are administratively responsible to the County Extension Coordinator and District Extension Director.</div> CAES-Southeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499559 2026-08-12T12:46:30-04:00 2026-08-12T12:46:30-04:00 Sports Communication Student Worker <div>Assist with daily media relations and communications duties related to UGA’s 21-sport varsity athletic program. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Excel, PowerPoint, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe InDesign is beneficial. Basic sports writing skills and social media capability also required. Grady College or Sport Management majors preferred. Students will be assigned certain sports to assist with Game Day operations. Having a flexible schedule and working nights and weekends are required. Students will also assist with office/clerical operations of the Sports Communications department which includes answering phone calls, scanning documents, special projects and other duties as assigned.</div> Athletics-Sports Communication https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478378 2026-04-22T17:16:22-04:00 2026-06-04T12:11:17-04:00 Temporary Variety Testing Assistant - Mailhot <div>This is a part-time (up to 20 hours per week) position. The assistant will be working in the Variety Testing program, performing seed lab activities and sometimes field work. This position will report to Daniel Mailhot, Program Director.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478808 2026-04-22T17:46:51-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:51-04:00 Black Bear Hair Snare Technician <div>The University of Georgia's - South Georgia Bear Project (SGBP) is looking for highly motivated, detail-oriented, and self-sufficient individuals to join the summer hair snare survey crew. Work will be conducted on a combination of public and private properties across 11 counties in South Georgia (centered around the Okefenokee National Wildlife Refuge). Free shared housing and field vehicles will be provided. Technicians will be primarily responsible for constructing, repairing, and monitoring barbed wire hair snares, beginning in early May and extending to early August. Hair snare monitoring efforts are part of a multi-year research project tasked with assessing South Georgia's black bear population abundance and genetic diversity. Primary duties will include hair snare deployment, data entry, processing of field samples, and equipment maintenance. Ideal applicants will be comfortable operating 4x4 vehicles and UTVs over challenging terrain and can comfortably navigate with a handheld GPS unit. Applicants should be comfortable carrying 30 lb. backpacks, working in challenging conditions (high humidity/temperature, insects, tough topography, hazardous wildlife) in remote areas, and be able to navigate with provided field maps. Applicants must be willing to work flexible schedules. There will be opportunities for technicians to assist with bear captures given hair snare tasks have been completed. Experience hiking in remote areas, navigating small boats in shallow water, driving 4x4 vehicles, and working as a team towards a research goal is desired.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501716 2026-08-20T16:08:55-04:00 2026-08-20T16:08:56-04:00 Faculty Affairs Assistant II <div>The Office of Faculty Affairs, a unit within the Office of the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, provides support for faculty and oversight of faculty-related policies and procedures for the University of Georgia. The Faculty Affairs Assistant II supports the annual promotion and tenure (P&amp;T) process, faculty hiring processes, and faculty life cycle transactions. This role coordinates faculty affairs processes and activities in collaboration with senior team members, including P&amp;T preparation, faculty appointment actions, data management and review, and document tracking. The position works across multiple faculty processes and systems to ensure accuracy, timely completion of actions, and compliance with institutional policies, procedures, and established deadlines.</div> SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478499 2026-04-22T17:24:08-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:08-04:00 Temporary Grounds Assistant - FRS <div>This position will assist Field Research Services grounds crew with maintenance on the Griffin Campus. Work to include but not limited to planting, mowing grass, weed eating, edging, weeding, and maintaining flower beds.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486790 2026-06-03T16:42:21-04:00 2026-06-03T16:42:21-04:00 Food Service Worker (Part-Time Only) <div>This is NOT a benefits eligible position.<br><br>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens and retail locations. Work involves responsibility for preparing and serving foods, cleaning facilities, and providing customer service.</div> Auxiliary Dining Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502826 2026-08-26T11:40:17-04:00 2026-08-26T11:40:18-04:00 STRUCTURAL MAINTENANCE MANAGER This position directs the activities of the Off Campus Zone Shop. This position oversees 10-14 semi-skilled and skilled trade employees including HVAC technicians, plumbers, maintenance workers, electricians, carpenters, painters and skilled trades workers. This shop is responsible for responding to trouble calls in the buildings off of the campus. FMD-O&M-Off Campus Zone https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478771 2026-04-22T17:43:40-04:00 2026-04-22T17:43:41-04:00 Engineering Assistant <div>The Engineering Assistant works closely with the Facilities Engineer for University Housing. The primary purpose of the position is to assist in engineering projects as assigned. This position also assists in crisis management situations, and enforce university and departmental policies.</div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498511 2026-08-06T14:44:53-04:00 2026-08-06T14:44:54-04:00 4-H Cherokee County AmeriCorps Member, Part-time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting required impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members must comply with AmeriCorps requirements such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other required trainings.<br>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members are required to log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.</div> CAES-Northwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478199 2026-04-22T09:35:45-04:00 2026-05-04T12:05:32-04:00 Assistant Research Scientist - Trible <div>The Department of Entomology in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences seeks a full-time research-track faculty position (12-month appointment) at the assistant research scientist level. This twelve-month, non-tenure-track position will have research responsibilities focused on the ecology and evolution of globally invasive ant species. The position is budgeted at 95% research and 5% service. The position is renewable assuming satisfactory performance and funding. The successful candidate will use a wide range of techniques to better characterize the population biology of globally invasive ants. A particular focus will be on the genetic and ecological changes that distinguish native from invasive populations of these organisms, including establishing field populations within their source region and conducting baseline comparisons between invaded and intact populations within their invasive range (ie, in GA or the SE). While the research will be heavily aligned with existing research groups in the Department, the scope of this project requires an experienced researcher.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478791 2026-04-22T17:46:20-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:20-04:00 Student Assistant - CBIO 3800 Franklin-Cellular Biology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504477 2026-09-03T15:26:00-04:00 2026-09-03T15:26:00-04:00 HOUSEKEEPER <div>This position provides cleaning services primarily in hotel guest rooms. The housekeeper is responsible for responding to all guest requests appropriately, identifying and notifying appropriate parties of any maintenance issues, and maintaining accurate records of work performed and time spent. Housekeeper maintains their cart with the proper cleaning supplies, amenities, and linens. Housekeeper may be asked to work in other areas maintained by the housekeeping department (public areas, laundry, offices).</div> PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501203 2026-08-19T10:38:58-04:00 2026-08-19T10:38:58-04:00 Temporary Research Technician - Chen <div>The technician will evaluate the microbial load on various surfaces of modified blueberry machine harvesters and determine the antimicrobial activities of extracts from citrus wastes.</div> CAES-Food Science & Technology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478465 2026-04-22T17:22:28-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:29-04:00 Temporary Banquet Captain <div>At the Georgia Center, the Banquet Captain assists the banquet team in creating an optimal atmosphere for large events, conferences and meetings. Banquet Captains are responsible for event set-up, working and/or running events, helping direct banquet student and temporary staff for individual events, maintenance of basic equipment and cleaning, and the breakdown of meeting and banquet rooms according to department standards. Handling cash/credit cards may be required at times.</div> PSO-Cont Ed-Aux-Food Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/484450 2026-05-21T08:47:12-04:00 2026-05-21T08:47:12-04:00 Building Automation Specialist <div>This is highly skilled technical work involving operating, maintaining, and troubleshooting all building automated systems and components for campus high containment Biosafety Level 3 (BSL-3, ABSL-3, and ABSL-3Ag) facilities and laboratories. In addition, the Building Automation Specialist Technician will facilitate preventative and corrective maintenance on all mechanical systems, identify structural and mechanical repairs, assist with Annual Performance Verifications (APV), generate reports, escort contractors, assist with facility related alarms and facility emergency response, assist FMD with Veterinary Biosciences Facility and Riverbend South APV, including facility decontamination. This position will assist in writing and editing standard operating procedures as needed. This position will work closely with FMD and AHRC Administration to maintain compliance with regulatory bodies and achieve goals and objectives of the facility.&nbsp;</div> VetMed-Animal Health Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478570 2026-04-22T17:29:53-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:54-04:00 Summer Field Technician <div>This position will be responsible for performing routine fieldwork in crop research fields in the summer. This will involve caring for various species of plants (chiefly corn) in order to keep them healthy. The major responsibility early in the season will be weeding, while data collection will dominate later in the season.</div> CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492695 2026-07-10T16:02:05-04:00 2026-07-10T16:02:06-04:00 AI & Data Studio Coordinator <div>Under the direction of the Director of Open Scholarship and Data Services (OSDS) and in close coordination with the Director of Academic Engagement, the AI &amp; Data Studio Coordinator manages the UGA Libraries' AI &amp; Data Studio by providing essential operational and programmatic leadership. The AI &amp; Data Studio is — a dynamic, interdisciplinary space where students, faculty, and researchers come to explore AI tools, work with data, and engage with each other to enhance their knowledge and understanding.</div><div><br>The Coordinator supports public services and programming by overseeing the development, implementation, and ongoing management of the AI &amp; Data Studio, ensuring alignment with campus needs, coordinating outreach and educational events, and providing continuous support to enhance AI literacy and user engagement. Serves as the operational spine of the Studio, ensuring it functions as a coherent, welcoming, and well-run environment for everyone who walks through the door. Core responsibilities span space and logistics management, cross-program coordination, working collaboratively with Libraries Marketing &amp; Communications, and oversight of the AI Ambassadors peer support program.<br><br></div> Libraries-MAGIL https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/21482 2018-04-25T13:43:07-04:00 2018-04-25T13:43:08-04:00 NBE_Hourly (Medical Technologist IV) This individual in this position will perform, result, report and evaluate all diagnostic laboratory testing processed and performed at University Health Center independently, accurately and in a timely manner. UHC-Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478677 2026-04-22T17:38:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:38:48-04:00 Student Assistant -Veterinary Entomology <div>The student will assist the Veterinary Entomology Program in responding to pest complaints via phone, email, and mail. 4 - 6 hours a week</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497030 2026-07-30T16:02:18-04:00 2026-07-30T16:02:19-04:00 Development and Alumni Communications Professional <div>The Development and Alumni Communications Professional supports Franklin College of Arts and Sciences’ communications efforts related to development, alumni relations, donor engagement and college newsletters.<br><br></div><div>This position works as part of the Franklin College marketing and communications team and collaborates with Franklin Development and Alumni Relations, academic departments, school and institute communicators, central Development and Alumni Relations, central Marketing and Communications, and other university partners.</div><div>The position helps identify, develop and coordinate alumni, donor, faculty, student, research and department-level stories for use in development communications, alumni engagement, newsletters, websites, solicitations, event communications, stewardship materials and related college channels. The role requires strong writing and editing skills, sound editorial judgment, project coordination, attention to detail and the ability to adapt content for different audiences and purposes.<br><br></div><div>As the DAR communications point of contact within Franklin MarCom, this position participates in content planning discussions and helps recognize opportunities to use stories across multiple channels. For example, the position may identify that a research story could support an upcoming donor solicitation, that an alumni conversation could become a department web profile, or that a faculty or student achievement could be used in a newsletter, web story or advancement communication.<br><br></div><div>The position coordinates newsletter content and related workflows, drafts and edits alumni and donor communications, supports annual giving and stewardship communications, and helps ensure projects are accurate, timely, audience-appropriate and aligned with college and university standards.</div> Franklin-Deans Communications https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477990 2026-04-21T18:24:55-04:00 2026-04-21T18:24:55-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor <div>The Louise McBee Institute of Higher Education at the University of Georgia invites applications for an early or mid-career professor position (tenure-track at assistant or associate rank) to begin August 1, 2025.&nbsp;<br><br>The successful candidate will be expected to support student research interests on critical issues in higher education, teach core graduate-level courses, advise and mentor doctoral students in their studies and research, engage in national and international partnerships that enhance the opportunities of students, pursue an active program of funded research; actively and effectively pursue and achieve publication in appropriate scholarly venues; and participate fully in the ongoing academic and governance activities of the McBee Institute.</div> SRVPAA-Institute of Higher Ed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503868 2026-09-01T10:44:04-04:00 2026-09-01T10:44:04-04:00 HR Senior Recruiting Consultant <div>The UHR Talent &amp; Recruiting – Recruiter will contribute to the recruiting and sourcing initiatives of the Talent &amp; Recruiting department. This role involves acting as a liaison between University Human Resources (UHR) and leaders and candidates during the recruiting process. They will identify sourcing tools, assist with search projects and educate hiring managers on appropriate methods for hiring. The role will be engaged in all aspects of hiring – posting a position, sourcing candidates, advertising, interviewing and making an offer. They will be knowledgeable about the types of positions in the organization and be aware of the requirements for those positions. The role will be an advisor to hiring managers, bringing best practices to the hiring process. The recruiter will also work closely with other UHR teams to ensure compensation, benefits and other aspects of hiring are integrated into the process.</div> UHR-Wrkfrce Plan & Recr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500140 2026-08-14T11:54:51-04:00 2026-08-14T11:54:51-04:00 Administrative Associate II <div>As an employee of the Child Development Lab at the McPhaul Center, you are expected to demonstrate a high level of professionalism in the workplace. Professionalism encompasses a commitment to excellence, honesty, integrity, respect for others, dedication and responsibility. Overall, professionalism is both an attitude and a lifestyle for the workplace, from the way we answer the phone to the way we build relationships with children, parents, students, and co-workers. It is a set of standards and values we uphold everyday and it is demonstrated in the way we work, the care we give and the contributions we make to society through the quality care for children. It is the foundation upon which we establish dependability and communicate competence within our work environments.<br><br>This position involves the coordination and implementation of administrative services. Job responsibilities include but are not limited to processing hiring proposals and working within UGAJobs, assisting with financial and accounting paperwork and regular bills, bookkeeping/budgeting, typing/copying, and assisting in maintaining current and accurate files on students and personnel at the Child Development Lab. This position requires attendance at monthly staff meetings and assistance to faculty in the Houses in the event that their administrative assistants are not available or if someone needs assistance.</div> FACS-Child & Family Devel Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478402 2026-04-22T17:19:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:34-04:00 Laboratory assistant <div>The Shamblin lab seeks laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample processing and DNA extractions for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate students and the lab manager with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, skin, fin clips, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing for fish and wildlife species of conservation concern. This position will also assist in sample archiving and general laboratory maintenance.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478844 2026-04-22T17:51:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:51:43-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Principal Investigator Dr. Cai’s lab is mainly focused on the studies on 1) fatty acid mediated metabolism; 2) extracellular vesicles mediated delivery of gene editing machinery. Current projects are supported by grants from National Institutes of Health (NIH), Department of Defense, and American Institute for Cancer Research. This position will have the opportunity to develop a CRISPR delivery technology for treatment of various diseases by gene therapy.</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502618 2026-08-25T15:49:25-04:00 2026-08-25T15:49:25-04:00 Change Management Specialist <div>The Change Management Specialist supports organizational change initiatives by delivering training and engagement sessions and contributing to organizational development (OD) and change management efforts, particularly in support of ERP implementation. This role assists in conducting organizational assessments, supporting the development of OD and change plans, and contributing to the implementation of initiatives that enhance organizational effectiveness and adoption. The position may support program development, facilitate workshops, and analyze feedback and data to inform continuous improvement.<br><br></div><div>The ideal candidate has experience in facilitation, foundational knowledge of organizational development and change management, and the ability to support initiatives in a collaborative, fast-paced environment.<br><br></div><div>This is a time-limited position designed to provide additional capacity during a period of significant organizational change. <strong>This position has a limited term appointment which is expected to end December 2028. The position may be extended beyond the initial term, contingent upon continued funding.</strong><br><br></div> UHR-Learning & Development https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478521 2026-04-22T17:25:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:29-04:00 International Grant Program Support SU 22/23 #1 <div>This position will provide program assistance for the three international grants that are operating April through July 17, 2022. The position will provide assistance for the grants by arranging and picking up meals and supplies, providing clerical support, collecting receipts from participants, assist with logistic planning and facilitation as directed. This position will work 10 -12 hours per week throughout the summer.</div> OGE-International Partnerships https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/488849 2026-06-16T16:56:33-04:00 2026-06-16T16:56:34-04:00 Electrician III <div>Installs, maintains, and troubleshoots a variety of electrical equipment and systems. Also conducts preventive and general maintenance.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478619 2026-04-22T17:33:37-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:37-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research - J. Buck, Griffin Conduct laboratory and greenhouse work including making media, culturing fungi, extracting DNA, conducting CPR, thrashing seed, and collecting data. CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494988 2026-07-22T00:01:02-04:00 2026-07-22T00:01:03-04:00 Graduate Program Administrator <div>This incumbent serves as the Graduate Program Administrator for the Department of Workforce Education and Instructional Technology. The employee will assist the Director of Graduate Studies in implementing all services related to academic and student planning, support, monitoring, and development. Responsibilities will include graduate program administration, student services, and general departmental support. It involves a thorough knowledge of departmental, college, and UGA policies, university software platforms, and data systems. The incumbent will deal with complex issues and questions from students and faculty while maintaining and following university guidelines and procedures.</div> COE-Workforce Ed & Instr Tech https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477829 2026-04-21T17:58:13-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:14-04:00 Research Professional II <div>This incumbent will oversee day-to-day research experiments and diagnostic testing in the Shariat Lab. The lab studies the ecology of Salmonella in food animals and the environment by microbiological culture, molecular, and next-generation sequencing. The major duties involve Salmonella molecular diagnostics and research and the employee will be responsible for planning, conducting, and reporting diagnostic and research experiments and assisting trainees in the lab with ongoing projects. The employee will utilize good organizational and communication skills and adherence to good laboratory practices. Other duties include maintaining lab inventory and equipment, ensuring overall lab organization, and safety compliance.</div> VetMed-Poultry Diagnos & Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501815 2026-08-21T10:03:56-04:00 2026-08-21T10:03:57-04:00 Lecturer <div>The Department of Political Science at the University of Georgia invites applications for a Lecturer position to begin August 1, 2027. Lecturers teach eight courses per academic year, four courses in each academic term. They typically teach two or more sections of the same course each semester and/or in the same academic year. The allocation of effort at appointment will be 100% teaching. Instructional responsibilities for this position will focus on upper division undergraduate courses offered by the Department in political theory/political philosophy in areas that align with their academic interests.<br><br></div><div>Lecturers are valued members of the Department with opportunities to shape the curriculum and participate in faculty governance processes. They are eligible for professional-development support, travel funding, and summer teaching (including study abroad programs) when available.&nbsp;</div> SPIA-Political Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478503 2026-04-22T17:24:15-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:15-04:00 Wild Turkey Lab Assistants <div>Positions will process wild turkey gobbling data to determine whether selections identified by machine learning tools are gobbles or other sounds. Positions will also assist with processing images of wild turkeys for ongoing analyses.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487094 2026-06-05T09:36:31-04:00 2026-06-05T09:36:31-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate-Dutta <div>The Postdoctoral Researcher will investigate bacterial pathogens affecting vegetable crops—particularly cucurbits, onions, and brassicas—using comparative genomics, transcriptomics, and proteomics to identify virulence factors and develop practical diagnostic and resistance-screening tools. This role will evaluate how production practices, environmental conditions, and inoculum sources influence disease outbreaks, and assess cultural strategies that suppress pathogens while supporting beneficial microflora.</div><div>The researcher will also develop and optimize environmentally and economically sustainable disease management solutions. In addition to conducting independent and collaborative research, the incumbent will engage with industry stakeholders, contribute to student mentoring, and support grant development. Responsibilities include maintaining accurate research records, analyzing and synthesizing data, presenting findings at professional meetings, publishing scientific manuscripts, and assisting with routine bacterial disease diagnosis.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478598 2026-04-22T17:32:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:30-04:00 Temporary Field/Greenhouse Assistant To assist in field preparation, maintenance, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494332 2026-07-17T14:16:07-04:00 2026-07-17T14:16:08-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate AD <div>The Postdoctoral Associate will support a portfolio of externally funded research projects within the PIXL Lab, with a primary focus on data analysis, study design support, and dissemination of findings. The position emphasizes advanced methodological contributions across mixed methods research, including quantitative, qualitative, and computational approaches, applied to the design and evaluation of technology-based interventions (for example, AI and extended reality) for learning and health contexts.<br><br></div><div>The Postdoctoral Associate will contribute to the design and execution of research studies, oversee project workstreams, and supervise graduate student researchers. The role includes leading data analysis efforts, contributing to scholarly publications, and supporting the development of external grant proposals (for example, NSF, NIH, DoD). While the position supports ongoing projects rather than serving as a primary lead, it entails a high degree of independence in managing research activities and coordinating across multiple projects.</div> COE-Workforce Ed & Instr Tech https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477780 2026-04-21T17:34:08-04:00 2026-04-21T17:34:08-04:00 Forest Tech II <div>Assist with the daily land management and operations of properties owned and/or managed by the Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478719 2026-04-22T17:40:30-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:30-04:00 Temporary Technician (Beasley) <div>The main responsibilities will include trapping wild pigs, maintaining bait stations, and sampling wild pigs after helicopter removal operations. Other duties may include data management in excel and maintaining field equipment. Winter work will consist of conducting camera surveys as well as photo processing.<br><br></div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497817 2026-08-04T14:04:29-04:00 2026-08-19T11:27:24-04:00 Student Assistant - Yu <div>This position will assist faculty and staff with greenhouse, lab, and field work and routine lab maintenance, publications, newsletters, research projects and field plots.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478080 2026-04-21T18:31:04-04:00 2026-04-21T18:31:05-04:00 Associate or Full Professor <div>The Department of Food Science and Technology (FST) and Poultry Science (PS) at the University of Georgia (UGA) are recruiting for an Associate or Full Professor in Food Systems Innovation, which is expected to be supported by an endowment. To fill this role, we are seeking a highly motivated and creative individual to develop a Research and Extension program in the area of ingredients and food processing technologies related to meat and poultry products to enhance quality, processing efficiency, and value addition of meat and poultry products.<br><br>The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an externally funded Research and Extension program and establish an internationally recognized program in the area of ingredients and food processing technologies related to meat and poultry products relevant to the local, national, and international food industry sector. Specific responsibilities include (but are not limited to): (1) obtaining extramural funds to support Research and Extension programs, (2) establishing a strong record of scholarly activity and peer-reviewed publications, (3) directing graduate (PhD and MS degree) students and postdoctoral associates, and (4) developing an Extension program to complement the currently existing FST and PS Extension programs and meet identified needs of stakeholders. The Extension program will include, but is not limited to, ingredient functionality in product development, including the impact of ingredients on the sensory (organoleptic) attributes of finished products, as well as the application and optimization of marination strategies in poultry and meat products. The candidate will be expected to actively participate in service activities in FST, PS, CAES, and UGA, including global programs. The University of Georgia recognizes and supports interdisciplinary programs. As such, the incumbent will be encouraged to collaborate with other faculty members across the Colleges of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences, Engineering, and Family and Consumer Sciences, as well as other colleges.<br><br></div> CAES-Food Science & Technology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504191 2026-09-02T12:58:39-04:00 2026-09-02T12:58:39-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate AD-Rains <div>The Post-Doctoral Associate will coordinate, conduct, and publish original research to advance precision agriculture technologies, including farm application systems, weed management, cotton harvesting practices, and autonomous navigation of intelligent multi-purpose rovers. Responsibilities include designing and executing field and laboratory studies, developing and evaluating innovative technologies through computer programming, digital data analysis, and mechanical design and testing, and investigating peanut insect pests and their relationship to <em>Aspergillus</em> mold and aflatoxin contamination.<br><br>The successful candidate will analyze and interpret complex datasets, publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals, pursue extramural funding opportunities, collaborate with industry and research partners, and provide leadership and mentorship to graduate students and research personnel.<br><br><strong>This is a limited-term appointment expected to end 5 years after the start date. Renewal or extension beyond the initial term is anticipated but not guaranteed and will depend on project needs, the availability of funding, and job performance. The position may be renewed on an annual basis, contingent upon continued grant support.</strong></div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500633 2026-08-17T16:04:35-04:00 2026-08-17T16:04:35-04:00 Private Lands Engineer - IRIS (Kentucky) <div>The University of Georgia (UGA) is seeking applications for a <strong>Private Lands Engineer</strong> (Water Resources) to support implementation of the Working Lands for Wildlife (WLFW) Aquatics Connectivity Framework. This project is a collaboration between UGA and the USDA Natural Resources Conservation Service (NRCS) WLFW program. This position will serve as a key implementation lead and primary point of contact for the Regional WLFW Southern Waters Framework in Kentucky, will be responsible for developing and implementing multi agency and NRCS workshops within the state, will engage in regional coordination aligned with broader program goals, and will serve as a key engineering resource for Kentucky NRCS state leadership.<br><br></div><div>Through the Farm Bill, NRCS provides technical and financial assistance to farmers, ranchers, and forestland owners/managers who voluntarily undertake conservation practices on working lands. WLFW systematically targets conservation efforts to enhance wildlife habitat on agricultural landscapes while improving agricultural and forest productivity. Hellbenders face many threats from conventional agricultural practices that lead to loss of forested riparian habitat and degraded water quality from sedimentation and pollutants.<br><br>This high-level Staff position will be under the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS), at the College of Engineering’s School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering (ECAM). The successful incumbent(s) will join a multidisciplinary team of engineers, scientists and designers at the University of Georgia who are engaged in collaborations between IRIS and the USDA, other universities, and private sector partners. These projects are highly specialized due to the incorporation of natural infrastructure systems and nature-based solutions.<br><br>The successful incumbent will collaborate in an interdisciplinary environment and will lead, conceptualize and implement high-quality and high-impact engineering research and/or design projects through extensive knowledge and experience of environmental/civil engineering (or related discipline) for successful project delivery. <br><br>A successful applicant must be a licensed Professional Engineer in Kentucky or demonstrate sufficient experience and education to obtain licensure.<del><br></del><br><strong>This position will be based out of Kentucky, in the London area. Daily duties will be conducted remotely, in the NRCS field office, and on project sites throughout the area. </strong><br><br><strong>This is a grant-funded position. Continuation of employment is contingent upon the continuation of funding sources. </strong><br><br></div> ENGR-Resilient Infrast Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478423 2026-04-22T17:20:09-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:10-04:00 Transit Tech (Part Time Only) <div>Troubleshoot and conduct routine repairs to fleet vehicles. Perform limited maintenance repairs on transit buses within safety and manufacturer’s specifications.<br><br>Candidates should submit to drug and alcohol testing in accordance with USDOT regulations.</div> Auxiliary Transit Maint https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/481235 2026-05-05T16:23:18-04:00 2026-05-05T16:23:19-04:00 Temporary Technician (Bier) <div>This position is for a PhD-level aquatic macroinvertebrate researcher with extensive experience working on macroinvertebrate communities and water quality in the Savannah and Ogeechee Rivers during flood and drought conditions. The researcher will use these skills to evaluate previously collected data sets to understand differences in aquatic health with changing water levels in these rivers.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478547 2026-04-22T17:26:14-04:00 2026-04-22T17:26:14-04:00 Temporary Laboratory Technician - Adhikari CAES-Food Science & Technology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490851 2026-06-30T14:54:58-04:00 2026-06-30T14:54:58-04:00 Research Associate-Plant Pathology <div>The Research Associate position is housed in the Department of Plant Pathology at the University of Georgia’s Tifton Campus. The individual in this role will be expected to be an accomplished investigator to maintain a vigorous research program in the area of detection and understanding mechanism of fungicide resistance in Alternaria sp in brasssica, Colletotrichum sp, and Fusarium sp in cucurbits. The overall research goal is utilize techniques not limited to classical mycology, fungicide sensitivity assays, genomics and bioinformatics. The Research Associate will design and coordinate field and greenhouse experiment based assays to test hypotheses. In addition to conducting research, this position will work closely with key interdisciplinary teams across multiple states to evaluate the cultural practices that reduce Altermaria losses in broccoli. The successful candidate will assume a leadership role in data collection and analysis, as well as in the preparation of manuscripts for submission to peer-reviewed journals. Additionally, they will be expected to present research findings at local and national conferences and in the writing and preparing of grant proposals for submission.<br><br><strong><em>This is a limited-term position expected to end two years after the start date. Renewal or extension beyond the initial term is anticipated but not guaranteed and will depend on project needs, the availability of funding, and job performance. The position may be renewed on an annual basis, contingent upon continued grant support.</em></strong></div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478639 2026-04-22T17:34:13-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:14-04:00 Student Assistant - Altizer Lab <div>Student Assistant for Altizer Lab.</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496414 2026-07-28T09:46:06-04:00 2026-07-28T09:46:07-04:00 Farm Manager - UGA Grand Farm <div>The incumbent will be located at the University of Georgia Grand Farm in Perry, GA. Under the supervision of the Director of Operations, the position will be responsible for implementing research and demonstration trial protocols provided by the Director of Operations, Grand Farm partners, and CAES faculty. The Farm Manager will oversee the maintenance, repair, and security of the physical plant, farm equipment, fences, grounds, and landscaping. They will supervise and train full-time and part-time employees in the safe operation and use of equipment and pesticides. The Farm Manager will work closely with the Director of Operations to coordinate research and demonstration projects. The Farm Manager will work effectively with a wide variety of people in an effort to create an environment where partners and researchers have the opportunity to conduct successful research. The Farm Manager will keep detailed and accurate records of all farm-related activities.</div> CAES-Grand Farm https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477887 2026-04-21T18:04:06-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:07-04:00 LVT I - Cardiology <div>The Licensed Veterinary Technician in Cardiology will perform physical exams, technician appointments, patient restraint, patient sedation, intravenous catheterization, routine laboratory procedures, venipuncture, and indirect blood pressure. Obtain urine by expression, cystocentesis or catheterization. Administer treatments, drugs, fluids, and medications by oral, parenteral and injectable routes. Client communication in person and via phone or e-mail. Acquire diagnostic ECG tracings. Prepare and apply Holtor monitors and telemetry. Set up and assist with paracentesis, echocardiogram, electrocardiogram (ECG), interventional radiology procedures, electrocardioversion, oxygen cage, and surgical procedures. Review Holtor monitor tracings. Assist in euthanasia and emergency resuscitation procedures.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Anim Spc Srvc https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503408 2026-08-28T11:17:36-04:00 2026-08-28T11:17:37-04:00 Veterinary Assistant-LA-Field Services <div>Handling/restraint of large animals. (Primarily horses/cows, but may include sheep, pigs, goats and camelids). The assistant is needed to safely handle all temperaments of horses. This includes handling for lameness exams (jogging/lunging), procedures, standing surgeries, radiology/bone scan, neuro exams and stallion collection.<br><br>Other duties include assisting LVT’s/Clinicians/Students/Client Support Coordinator in any capacity as needed for patient care, general housekeeping/stocking/stall maintenance, animal/sample transport, anesthetic induction/recovery, and utilization of Vetview/Cubex.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499668 2026-08-12T15:48:17-04:00 2026-08-12T15:48:18-04:00 Executive Assistant <div>The Executive Assistant provides high-level administrative and operational support to the Dean and senior leadership team of the Victoria Kay Ivester School of Nursing. This position serves as a central point of coordination for executive operations by managing complex calendars, coordinating meetings and events, preparing correspondence and reports, supporting special projects, and facilitating communication among School leadership, faculty, staff, students, University offices, and external partners.<br><br></div><div>Working under the direction of the Chief of Staff and Communications Manager, the Executive Assistant exercises sound judgment, professionalism, and discretion while supporting the day-to-day operations of the Dean's Office. The position plays an integral role in ensuring the efficient operation of the School through exceptional organization, communication, and executive support.</div> SON-Administration https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478380 2026-04-22T17:16:26-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:26-04:00 Post Doc of Human Dimensions of Chronic Wasting Disease <div>This is a two-year position working on a study funded by the Georgia Department of Natural Resources that seeks to develop strategies for effective communication and cooperation with landowners, hunters, and other partners of GADNR to the minimize risk of Chronic Wasting Disease in Georgia’s white-tailed deer population. The specific research objectives are to determine perceptions, motivations, and preferences of landowners, hunters, and other partners of GADNR relative to white-tailed deer management in Georgia to minimize risks associated with CWD, and to differentiate strategies for communication and cooperation among stakeholder groups for implementation of management actions aimed at managing risks associated with CWD. The postdoctoral researcher will design and oversee the study in collaboration with Drs. D’Angelo and Boley. The methods for the study will likely include a large-scale survey of landowners and hunters with the use of discrete choice modeling to identify the most appropriate strategies to effectively engage different stakeholder groups. The postdoctoral researcher will be responsible for development of research questions, survey design, data collection, data analysis, and technical writing for preparation of scientific manuscripts. The postdoctoral researcher will be supervised by Drs. Gino D’Angelo and Dr. Bynum Boley at University of Georgia and will be expected to work closely with other research collaborators within the Georgia Department of Natural Resources.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478812 2026-04-22T17:46:58-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:58-04:00 Research Assistant <div>The student will work under the supervision of Dr. Tao Liu to conduct research and contribute to scholarly publications on AI applications using remote sensing data. The primary focus will be on developing and applying geospatial/remote sensing foundation models for land cover classification and monitoring key forest metrics.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478621 2026-04-22T17:33:40-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:41-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research - Leclerc <div>We are looking for some preferable an undergraduate student. One of the topics is in determining how much water is needed in pecan irrigation and in peanut. The successful applicant will be working with us learning how to program data loggers, install, calibrate, and troubleshoot instrumentation, and check data remotely for data quality. The projects are in Hawkinsville, Plains and Moultrie.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495101 2026-07-22T12:21:23-04:00 2026-07-22T12:21:23-04:00 Psychologist/Assistant Director of Clinical Training <div>The Assistant Director of Training is an essential member of the CAPS/Fontaine Center leadership team. Reporting to the Sr. Associate Director of Clinical Services and Training, this leadership position’s primary focus will be on the continued development and implementation of a strategic vision for, and oversight of, all the aspects of the various training programs offered at CAPS, including our American Psychological Association (APA) accredited doctoral internship program, and our Advanced Doctoral practicum and Social Work practicum programs.<br><br>In addition, this position will provide direct services to students and provide oversight of all supervision of our trainees in their various levels of training. In collaboration with other members of the CAPS/Fontaine Leadership team, this position ensures compliance with Joint Commission Standards; engages in multidisciplinary consultation teams; creatively develops cutting-edge training opportunities; and assists in monitoring client assignment and referral.</div> UHC-Counseling & Psych Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477834 2026-04-21T17:58:25-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:26-04:00 Research Professional <div>The Research Professional has duties to design develop, organize, and supervise the work on a major recombinant protein expression project in the lab employing bacterial or mammalian cell culture systems. The goals of this research project will provide large scale protein production for enzyme structural and functional studies. The position entails establishing project goals, working directly with supervising faculty to design and implement new recombinant constructs, developing priorities among the large number of constructs, generation and large scale production of recombinant DNAs, and supervising work of other research technicians to accomplish these goals. Work duties include close collaboration with senior faculty and working within a larger research group of postdoctoral researchers, research technicians, and undergraduate researchers to develop strategies for high quantity protein expression, and close interaction with investigators at other research sites for the design and generation of new constructs for collaborative studies. Additional roles involve supervision of research technicians and undergraduate researchers on preparation of plasmid DNAs from bacterial cultures, executing protocols for novel transfection strategies of mammalian cells, and training research technicians and undergraduate researchers on standard operating procedures. Direct supervision of the Research Professional by senior faculty is anticipated.<br><br></div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502962 2026-08-26T15:20:58-04:00 2026-08-26T15:20:58-04:00 Post Award Business Manager <div>Serves as a resource for PIs, Business Managers, and Grants Coordinators on all aspects of post-award sponsored projects management. Provides direct support to the Administrative Financial Director relating to all accounting processes to include research, report preparation, and collection of data. Provides support to other members of the Business Office team as needed.</div> VetMed-Business Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478780 2026-04-22T17:43:56-04:00 2026-04-22T17:43:57-04:00 Genetics Laboratory Assistant - Temp <div>The Shamblin lab seeks laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample processing, DNA extractions, and data calling for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate students and the lab manager with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, skin, fin clips, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing for fish and wildlife species of conservation concern. This position will also assist the PI with data calling with microsatellite and sequencing projects. Sample archiving and general laboratory maintenance are necessary.<em> Ideal candidates are available to work 30-40 hours weekly if not taking classes or 15-20 hours weekly if taking classes during the summer. Please list your summer availability in your cover letter.</em></div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498574 2026-08-06T16:25:40-04:00 2026-08-06T16:25:41-04:00 Student Assistant - SPW <div>This is technical work in performing routine as well as non-standardized laboratory testing. Assist with soil sample organization, sample grinding, sieving, weighing, cleaning glassware, and other miscellaneous duties.</div> CAES-Ag&Environmental Svcs Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478359 2026-04-22T17:14:41-04:00 2026-04-22T17:14:42-04:00 Student Assistant – Retail Dining Locations This is general work preparing and serving food as well as clerical work requiring processing financial transactions and handling cash and payment cards.\r\nRapid and accurate completion of transactions necessary to receiving and disbursing cash. Emphasis is placed on accuracy in handling cash as well as preparation and serving food. Accuracy of work is verified through the comparison of cash with receipt stubs, cash register receipts, or other controls. Work is performed according to established and well defined procedures.\r\nDuties include maintaining high standards of cleanliness and for assuring that patrons are served in a pleasant and courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained. Auxiliary Dining Retail Ops https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478793 2026-04-22T17:46:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:24-04:00 AHRC Student Employee Student will assist BioResources team in maintaining auxiliary spaces within the AHRC vivarium and 2nd floor auxiliary spaces. VetMed-Animal Health Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504486 2026-09-03T16:34:37-04:00 2026-09-03T16:34:38-04:00 Program Coordinator II <div>The Program Coordinator II supports the Defense Community Resilience Program (DCRP) through project coordination, operational support, stakeholder engagement, and administrative management. The position assists with planning and tracking project activities, coordinating internal and external partners, preparing reports and project materials, supporting proposal development, and monitoring project timelines and deliverables. The incumbent also supports outreach activities, events, and program evaluation efforts while assisting with division administrative and operational processes. The position serves as a key resource in maintaining project continuity and supporting the successful delivery of DCRP initiatives.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501219 2026-08-19T11:04:06-04:00 2026-08-19T11:04:06-04:00 Administrative Manager <div>The Administrative Manager manages the fiscal, business, human resources, facilities, and administrative operations of the Office of the Vice President for Public Service and Outreach (OVPPSO). Reporting to the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs, this position is responsible for coordinating day-to-day business operations, ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures, and serving as a primary administrative resource for OVPPSO employees.</div><div>The position also provides support to the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs by assisting with assigned division-wide reporting, information requests, recurring deadlines, strategic initiatives, special projects, and administrative process improvements across Public Service and Outreach.</div> PSO-VP Public Serv & Outreach https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478474 2026-04-22T17:22:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:44-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant - Dr. Kong CAES-Food Science & Technology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/485121 2026-05-26T08:39:05-04:00 2026-05-26T08:39:06-04:00 Assistant Professor of Legal Studies <div>The Insurance, Legal Studies and Real Estate Department in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. The position will begin fall semester of 2027, with an anticipated employment start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Insur, Legal, Real Est https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478572 2026-04-22T17:29:57-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:57-04:00 Temporary Technician This position will assist with an environmental monitoring progam that our Unit has recieved funding to complete. VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492877 2026-07-13T13:07:07-04:00 2026-07-13T13:07:07-04:00 Assistant Director for Residential Programs and Services <div>The Assistant Director for Residential Program and Services (RPS) manages the comprehensive operations for two to four residential areas housing more than 2,000 students. The Assistant Director is responsible for cultivating inclusive, engaging, and well-maintained residential communities that foster student learning and success. This position advances the department’s curricular approach to residential education and oversees major unit initiatives.<br><br></div><div>As a member of the RPS leadership team, the assistant director contributes to strategic planning, policy development, and assessment efforts, while collaborating with departmental, divisional, and university partners to enhance the residential experience. The position directly supervises two to five full-time staff and reports to an associate director for RPS.</div> Housing-Resident Progs & Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/29862 2018-08-07T13:57:16-04:00 2018-08-07T13:57:17-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Assoc The assigned responsibilities of the Postdoctoral Research Associate are predominantly research and/or scholarship but may combine these responsibilities with significant (no more than 50%) formal instructional responsibilities.\r\n\r\nThe appointment can be full time or limited term, and is viewed as preparatory for a full-time career in academia, industry, government, or the non-profit sector. Franklin-Biochemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478681 2026-04-22T17:38:54-04:00 2026-04-22T17:38:55-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Morkos <div>The Postdoctoral Researcher in Manufacturing and AI will be responsible for supporting the advancement of convergent research at the intersection of artificial intelligence and manufacturing. This position will play a key role in managing ongoing projects, ensuring timely progress, and contributing to the development of new initiatives in AI-driven manufacturing processes. The Post Doc will also mentor undergraduate and graduate students, guiding them through research methodologies and professional growth. Additionally, the candidate will collaborate on the development of proposals for external funding. The role requires a proactive approach to fostering innovation, exploring new research opportunities, and promoting collaboration across industry and academic partners to push the boundaries of AI applications in manufacturing.<br><br><strong>This Post-Doctoral position is an 18-month position that will end May, 2026.</strong></div> ENGR-Env Civil Agr & Mech https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497340 2026-07-31T14:46:54-04:00 2026-07-31T14:46:55-04:00 Vet Teaching Hospital Client Relationship Officer <div>The Client Relationship Officer owns the primary responsibility as the chief investigator of client complaints regarding services, charges and treatment while at the Vet Teaching Hospital(VTH). As the only Veterinary Teaching Hospital in the state of Georgia and with a combined caseload of over 36,000 cases, the VTH serves a wide network of referring DVM's for both small animal and large animal patients.</div><div>The Client Relationship Officer is authorized to exercise judgement regarding the path a complaint will go with hospital administration, clinical services, faculty, staff, and support teams to ensure clients are addressed promptly, professionally, and compassionately. This role will triage incoming complaints and inquiries, identifying the appropriate VTH personnel for follow-up and assist in facilitating resolutions that support both client satisfaction and hospital standards of care.</div><div>This position is also responsible for developing and maintaining a centralized tracking and reporting system for all client relations concerns and resolutions to help identify trends, recurring service issues, as well as data-driven decisions related to operational improvements and client experience initiatives. The Client Relationship Officer will regularly collaborate with hospital administration to provide reports, trend analysis, recommendations for improvement, and opportunities to enhance overall client satisfaction and communication workflow.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477992 2026-04-21T18:25:00-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:01-04:00 Public Service Faculty - Local Government Operations <div>The Carl Vinson Institute of Government at The University of Georgia invites applications for a Public Service Faculty position in the <strong>Government Services and Research Division / Local Government Unit</strong>.&nbsp; The position will be available <strong>February 1, 2025</strong> and carries rank in the public service faculty career ladder of the University.&nbsp;<br><br>Helping local governments operate in the most financially prudent and efficient manner is a priority of the Carl Vinson Institute of Government. This position will provide technical assistance and conduct studies to help government leaders make data informed decisions. To be successful in this position will require a mix of both qualitative and quantitative research methods to address the needs of the government being assisted. We are looking for an experienced professional who is eager to assist local government leaders through financial analysis, policy analysis, feasibility studies, benchmarking and best practice research. This position will also work with public works directors and other local government leaders who work every day to maintain the critical infrastructure in their city and county.<br><br>As a public service faculty member, this position will be part of one of the most trusted organizations in the state that provides objective research and analysis. This position is part of the Local Government Operations unit comprised of a team of faculty and staff. Public service faculty are responsible for understanding the needs of governments and developing and delivering programs and services to meet those needs.<br><br>As a public service faculty member, this position has an opportunity to serve governments across the state and also develop and share their expertise through training, webinars, writing reports, and making professional presentations. Occasional overnight travel is required of this position.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503897 2026-09-01T12:33:17-04:00 2026-09-01T12:33:17-04:00 Materials Handler I <div>Performs manual and clerical duties related to receiving, inspecting, and stocking: Receives shipments and checks for accuracy against purchase orders; Stocks inventory shelves by the appropriate hospital inventory numbers; Pulls inventory for various departments within the teaching hospital; Assist in the ordering, receiving, distributing and taking inventory of compressed gases for the hospital.</div> VetMed-VTH Warehouse https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500178 2026-08-14T12:52:36-04:00 2026-08-14T12:52:36-04:00 Relief Pharmacist <div>The purpose of the Relief Pharmacist is to provide coverage in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital Pharmacy for filling and approving prescriptions, and providing guidance to clinical and technical staff regarding effects of medications.</div> VetMed-VTH Pharmacy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478404 2026-04-22T17:19:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:37-04:00 Maintenance Assistant <div>The Maintenance Assistant performs semi-skilled tasks on the transit bus fleet at the University of Georgia. Duties include fueling Diesel buses, dispensing Diesel Exhaust Fluid (DEF), plugging in and monitoring electric buses, cleaning buses, and performing basic cleaning maintenance. Duties performed are primarily outside in surrounding compound or in bus yard with exposure to all weather types and conditions.</div> Auxiliary Transit Maint https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478912 2026-04-23T11:34:04-04:00 2026-04-23T11:34:05-04:00 Residential Building Services Worker <div>The primary function of this position is to execute a variety of cleaning tasks throughout residential communities housing 1,200 or more residents. This position also includes scheduled summer tasks, transitions and the cleaning of rotating camps, conferences and student orientation programs. The position performs duties necessary to uphold communication and customer service with a variety of peers, residents and other departmental stakeholders; performs periodic duties during weekend and holiday shifts and on-call operations to uphold the standards of care for a 24-hour, seven-day a week residential program. Must be available to work specified shift, with occasional additional shifts Saturday, Sunday, or after hours as needed.</div> Housing-Facilities-Build Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502723 2026-08-26T09:24:27-04:00 2026-08-26T09:24:28-04:00 Administrative Financial Director <div>The Administrative Financial Director oversees the J.W. Fanning Institute for Leadership Development’s (Fanning Institute) financial and human resources operations and provides guidance and support to the Director and senior leadership team. The position is responsible for budget planning and financial management, human resources processes, internal controls, compliance, and the effective administration of Institute resources. The position provides financial and administrative information, analysis, and recommendations to support informed decision-making.</div><div>The Administrative Financial Director serves as a primary liaison with central University offices and provides guidance and support to faculty and staff on financial, human resources, and administrative matters. The position promotes professional, responsive, and consistent administrative practices that contribute to a positive and productive work environment. The position also continuously evaluates and improves processes, systems, and workflows to strengthen efficiency, service, and continuity of operations. This position supervises the Business Manager II.</div> PSO-Fanning Inst Ldership Devl https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478523 2026-04-22T17:25:32-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:33-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research - Bahri <div>Conduct laboratory, greenhouse and field work including making media, culturing fungi, extracting DNA, conducting PCR, planting seed, and collecting data.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/489376 2026-06-23T08:27:39-04:00 2026-08-17T14:45:55-04:00 Class Checker - Student Assistant <div>As an Athletics Class Checker, your duties will include the following:<br>• Monitoring the daily attendance and promptness of a diverse group of student-athletes.<br>• Communicating regularly with Athletics Staff Members to ensure accountability<br>• Logging detailed reports to inform Academic Counselors/Staff of daily occurrences.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499730 2026-08-13T08:20:20-04:00 2026-08-13T08:20:21-04:00 Horticulturist–Garden Curator <div>Plan, plant, curate and manage the assigned areas at the State Botanical Garden of Georgia. Duties and responsibilities include planting design, selection, and acquisition of plant species and cultivars appropriate for this garden. The curator will work closely with the Director of Horticulture &amp; Grounds to ensure accurate plant accessioning, inventory and record keeping, make certain that plant labels and interpretive signs are correct and in place, and ensure that plazas, pathways, lighting, and architectural features are safe, clean and in good condition. The candidate will supervise part-time employees, students and volunteers. Engage in outreach activities to individuals, businesses, plant societies, botanical and horticultural organizations that might provide support or services. Contribute to the Garden’s newsletter and participate in various committees, educational programs, special events and other grounds/horticultural projects as needed. Work weekend or evening shift approximately six times a year.</div> PSO-State Botanic Garden of GA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478382 2026-04-22T17:16:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:30-04:00 Temporary Lab Assistant 2 - Plant Genetics <div>This position is needed to assist with sweet potato curation. Duties will include lab ware, making tissue culture media and other lab duties assigned.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478815 2026-04-22T17:49:50-04:00 2026-04-22T17:49:51-04:00 Garden & Grounds Assistant <div>The responsibilities of Garden and Grounds Assistants involve gardening and maintenance activities such as planting, weeding, mowing, and pruning. Assistants work alongside Garden Curators and Grounds Staff in maintaining formal gardens, trails, and natural areas gaining valuable hands-on experience.</div> PSO-State Botanic Garden of GA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501936 2026-08-21T14:08:18-04:00 2026-08-21T14:08:19-04:00 Georgia 4-H Foundation Development Officer-Athens <div>The Development Officer reports to the Executive Director of the Georgia 4-H Foundation. This employee will implement identified priorities and funding needs for the George 4-H Foundation in coordination with the State 4-H program. This highly responsible professional position has accountability for the implementation of the Georgia 4-H Foundation annual fund campaigns, special events as well as establishment of a portfolio of donors. Work is performed independently on the basis of a general assignment of the responsibilities and follows through the full continuity of the job to the final results. Frequent work on evenings and weekends is expected. A valid driver's license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official travel duty.<br>http://georgia4h.org/</div> CAES-State 4-H https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478505 2026-04-22T17:24:19-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:20-04:00 Temporary Lab Technician - Chavez <div>This position will work both indoors and outdoors assisting field and laboratory work for peach, blueberry and grape research projects. Fieldwork includes, but is not limited to, helping to plant, maintain, harvest, and process field studies. Work in the field and greenhouse will be done in hot conditions. Laboratory work includes, but is not limited to, processing samples, dissections, extraction, and others. Proficiency in Microsoft Office programs is desired, and Excel spreadsheet data entry is also needed. The position receives specific work instructions at the beginning of each new task and the work is closely supervised until the employee is capable of consistently performing the task.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487534 2026-06-08T15:32:19-04:00 2026-06-08T15:32:20-04:00 Senior Executive Process Consultant – Limited Term <div>The Senior Executive Process Consultant will serve as a senior member of the Process Team through the executive search process for senior level administration and faculty positions.&nbsp; Discretion and judgment will be crucial in this role as a key contributor and model for the team.&nbsp; As a senior member of the UGA Search Group, the role will assist in coaching, mentoring, and training members of the Process Team, share best practices, and provide organization and coordination in support of the executive search process.&nbsp; By maintaining a sound strategic search process strategy, and utilizing project management skills in the delivery of on-time communication, research, marketing, event planning and document management in the executive search process for the Institution, the Senior Executive Process Consultant will assist the office in filling key-contributor leadership positions. These top talent hires will have a major impact on the University.&nbsp; &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The Senior Executive Process Consultant serves as a key member of the Process Team and is responsible for producing an effective and respectable search process through high-level organization and project management of the executive search process. The Senior Executive Process Consultant will work on multiple searches at any given time and demonstrate independent initiative and resourcefulness in leading research efforts for prospective candidates, securing campus spaces for search meetings, communicating with key internal and external constituents, and focusing on the details that are the hallmark of the UGA Search Group.&nbsp; The position will maintain contact with senior level administrative leaders, senior staff, hiring authorities, search committee members, faculty, staff, and students in the facilitation of search events.&nbsp; This role will contribute to the development and execution of a strategic vision focused on continuous improvement and creative ways to leverage the team's expertise in support of our state's flagship institution.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;<br><strong>This position has a limited term appointment which is expected to end July 2028.&nbsp; The position may be extended beyond the initial term, contingent upon continued funding.&nbsp; </strong>&nbsp;<br><br></div> UHR-HR Search Group https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478602 2026-04-22T17:32:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:37-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate A person in this position will have two primary objectives: the first is to purify proteins from peripheral human blood and characterization using mass spectrometry. The second goal is to develop an in vitro expression system to test how protein modifications impact cell activation. The goal of these studies is to determine how cells in the human immune system modify antibody-binding receptors and define how these modifications impact cell activation.\r\n\r\nThis project is funded by the National Institutes of Health. The goal of this research is to characterize how a specific group of proteins, the Fc gamma receptors, are modified in the human body. Our laboratory has developed protocols to isolate proteins from primary human monocytes and natural killer cells that were isolated from apheresis and through negative selection. We have also determined that modification of the Fc gamma receptors affects antibody binding affinity in vitro. The goal of this position is to determine if receptor modifications impact cell activation. Franklin-Biochemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494488 2026-07-20T11:29:02-04:00 2026-07-20T11:29:03-04:00 Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor - Open Rank <div>The University of Georgia School of Law invites applications to fill one or more tenure-track or tenured positions at the rank of assistant professor, associate professor, or professor. The positions will begin in August 2027, with a possibility of a January 1, 2028, start date.&nbsp;<br><br>Our curricular priorities include professional responsibility, torts, and bankruptcy/secured transactions. Applications from candidates who can teach in more than one of the above-listed disciplines are especially welcome.</div> Law School-General https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477805 2026-04-21T17:50:27-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:28-04:00 Forest Health/Silviculture Technician This position is for 14 months and may be renewed for a longer period of time based on funding. \r\nThis individual will serve as the research technician for forest health, silviculture, and forest productivity work. The position provides support, both fieldwork and lab work, to the two Assistant Professors and one Professor. The successful candidate will be housed in Tifton at the UGA Research Center. Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478721 2026-04-22T17:40:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:33-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant (Beasley) VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497969 2026-08-05T08:07:17-04:00 2026-08-05T08:07:17-04:00 Senior Director of Development <div>The Senior Director of Development and Alumni Relations leads the overall operations and performance of the Franklin College of Arts &amp; Sciences Development and Alumni Relations teams. They are responsible for the planning and implementation of an integrated approach to development and alumni affairs, maximizing support for the College. They will serve as the chief development officer with responsibility for increasing philanthropic support and engagement for Franklin College.<br><br></div><div>The Senior Director of Development serves as a liaison between the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences and University Development. As Franklin’s chief development officer, this position is responsible for raising major ($50,000+) and principal gifts ($1,000,000+) to enable the unit to fulfill its mission and implement its programs and initiatives. In addition to major and principal gifts, the position is also responsible for providing strategy, leadership, direction, coordination, and management of all levels of giving for Franklin, including major giving, annual gifts, stewardship, and alumni relations.<br><br></div><div>To fulfill the college’s mission and implement its programs and initiatives, the Senior Director of Development works closely with the Dean to develop fundraising priorities, create a development plan, implement the plan, and secure major and principal gifts while also managing the development and alumni relations team. In this role, the employee is responsible for communication, collaboration, and coordination between Franklin and the University Development office, as well as creating productive partnerships with all other UGA school, college, and unit fundraising programs.<br><br></div><div>The University Development office sets four objectives for Senior Directors of Development: number of annual visits, number of major/principal gift proposals, unit fundraising goal and personal fundraising goal. Each of these goals is discussed with the director and customized for their specific unit on an annual basis. In addition, each director is required to attend applicable division and development meetings as well as an individual monthly strategy meeting at the University Development office with the Senior Director of Development for Constituent Programs.&nbsp;</div> DAR-College Relations https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478092 2026-04-21T18:31:33-04:00 2026-04-21T18:31:33-04:00 Assistant Professor in Comparative Disease Computation and Artificial Intelligence (Tenure Track) <div>The Department of Pathology in the College of Veterinary Medicine at the University of Georgia invites applications for a nine-month tenure track faculty position with a focus on AI. This position will be tenure track at the rank of Assistant Professor. <br><br>The selected candidate will be expected to establish a <strong>dynamic, externally funded research program</strong> and to contribute significantly to the Department’s research mission through <strong>collaborative efforts</strong> with other faculty. Areas of interest include AI-driven image analysis and computer vision for digital histopathology, integration of multimodal data (e.g., imaging and molecular ), AI-driven genomics and multi-omics analysis, and generative AI in disease modeling.<br><br>The successful applicant will join a team of 21 anatomic pathologists, 5 clinical pathologists, and 3 primary research faculty in addition to a motivated group of anatomic and clinical pathology residents, and graduate students. The Department is committed to excellence in teaching that spans undergraduate, professional, graduate, and resident programs. High quality diagnostic necropsy and surgical pathology services are provided to the Veterinary Teaching Hospital as well as to pet owners and food animal producers in the State of Georgia.</div> VetMed-Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504252 2026-09-02T16:14:14-04:00 2026-09-02T16:14:14-04:00 Lead Financial Aid Advisor, Client Services Provides leadership to and routinely assists Financial Aid Advisors and support staff in accomplishing their daily responsibilities. Serves as authority for satisfactory academic progress appeals and manages reports on potential changes in student eligibility. Advises students and parents regarding federal, state and institutional aid in an accurate and efficient manner, and assists with related financial aid application processes. Awards, cancels and revises financial aid awards based on office policies and procedures, and in compliance with applicable rules and regulations. Remains current on federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations, policies, and procedures. VPI-Student Financial Aid https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500636 2026-08-17T16:05:45-04:00 2026-08-17T16:05:46-04:00 Private Lands Engineer - IRIS (N. Carolina) <div>The University of Georgia (UGA) is seeking applications for a <strong>Private Lands Engineer</strong> (Water Resources) to support implementation of the Working Lands for Wildlife (WLFW) Aquatics Connectivity Framework. This project is a collaboration between UGA and the USDA Natural Resources Conservation Service (NRCS) WLFW program. This position will serve as a key implementation lead and primary point of contact for the Regional WLFW Southern Waters Framework in North Carolina, will be responsible for developing and implementing multi agency and NRCS workshops within the state, will engage in regional coordination aligned with broader program goals, and will serve as a key engineering resource for North Carolina NRCS state leadership.<br><br></div><div>Through the Farm Bill, NRCS provides technical and financial assistance to farmers, ranchers, and forestland owners/managers who voluntarily undertake conservation practices on working lands. WLFW systematically targets conservation efforts to enhance wildlife habitat on agricultural landscapes while improving agricultural and forest productivity. Hellbenders face many threats from conventional agricultural practices that lead to loss of forested riparian habitat and degraded water quality from sedimentation and pollutants.<br><br>This high-level Staff position will be under the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS), at the College of Engineering’s School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering (ECAM). The successful incumbent(s) will join a multidisciplinary team of engineers, scientists and designers at the University of Georgia who are engaged in collaborations between IRIS and the USDA, other universities, and private sector partners. These projects are highly specialized due to the incorporation of natural infrastructure systems and nature-based solutions.<br><br>The successful incumbent will collaborate in an interdisciplinary environment and will lead, conceptualize and implement high-quality and high-impact engineering research and/or design projects through extensive knowledge and experience of environmental/civil engineering (or related discipline) for successful project delivery. <br><br>A successful applicant must be a licensed Professional Engineer in North Carolina or demonstrate sufficient experience and education to obtain licensure.<del><br></del><br><strong>This position will be based out of North Carolina, in the Goldsboro area. Daily duties will be conducted remotely, in the NRCS field office, and on project sites throughout the area. </strong><br><br><strong>This is a grant-funded position. Continuation of employment is contingent upon the continuation of funding sources. </strong><br><br></div> ENGR-Resilient Infrast Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478428 2026-04-22T17:20:19-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:19-04:00 Lab/Field Student Assistant-9-Nankar <div>Selected applicant will provide assistance in greenhouse research activities including potting, planting, fertilizing, watering, weeding, pollinating, data collection, disease screening, and harvesting plants belonging to different breeding populations. Selected applicant will assist in keeping greenhouse space neat, orderly and weed free. Individual will provide assistance with basic field and laboratory research as requested including tissue sample collection, pollinations, basic data collection, disease screening, and setting up field studies including labeling and placing flags, stakes and markers. Individual will assist with basic lab protocols including molecular biology as requested and will be responsible for basic lab maintenance and chores including washing glassware, preparing simple solutions, preparing media, autoclaving supplies and waste, taking trash to dumpster, etc.to keep laboratory space neat, orderly and clean.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/481297 2026-05-06T09:06:03-04:00 2026-05-06T09:06:03-04:00 Poultry Health Specialist <div>The University of Georgia, College of Veterinary Medicine, Department of Population Health invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the field of Poultry Health. Responsibilities associated with this position include research (70%), teaching (20%), and service (10%). The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an independent extramurally funded research program with the aim of solving infectious disease problems in the poultry industry. Avenues of research that focus on the interactions between poultry management practices and disease are welcome. The selected faculty member will also be expected to teach in the undergraduate and graduate curriculums and to perform service activities in support of the University’s mission. It is expected that the successful candidate will collaborate with other faculty members in the Poultry Diagnostic and Research Center (PDRC), the College of Veterinary Medicine, and other Colleges and Centers at UGA to advance the field of poultry health.<br><br></div><div>Rank, salary, and terms of appointment will be dependent upon qualifications and experience of the applicant.</div> VetMed-Poultry Diagnos & Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478549 2026-04-22T17:26:18-04:00 2026-04-22T17:26:18-04:00 Parking Operations Student <div>Perform administrative and customer service related tasks for the Parking Services department to support in-office sales and operations. Apply standard business and customer service practices with professional guidance and supervision in a small business environment with advanced computer software, money handling procedures, and customer interactions on a large scale.</div> Auxiliary Parking Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491157 2026-07-02T09:03:49-04:00 2026-08-13T13:31:48-04:00 Student Operations Intern - Dining Services <div>This position supports UGA Dining Services via The FoodPro Office using FoodPro, the department’s primary software tool for dining menu management and financials. The intern will assist in maintaining accurate data integrity, reconciling invoices for Dining Services, and contributing to process improvement initiatives. This role provides hands-on experience in data management, system-based operations, and financial reconciliation within a large-scale university dining environment.<br><br></div> Auxiliary Central Storage https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478642 2026-04-22T17:34:18-04:00 2026-04-22T17:34:18-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate - Hallow <div>The responsibilities of this position will include developing and utilizing mathematical models of cardiovascular and renal physiology and pharmacology, working with industry sponsor to apply modeling to investigate open research questions, writing manuscripts and other scholarly works, mentoring graduate and undergraduate lab members.</div> ENGR-Chem Material & Biomed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496490 2026-07-28T13:52:30-04:00 2026-07-28T13:52:31-04:00 LAB ANIMAL TECH/CONTAINMENT <div>This is a high containment laboratory animal husbandry position at the Animal Health Research Center (AHRC), an AAALC accredited animal facility. This position will perform all aspects of high containment animal husbandry with various species of laboratory and agricultural animals in ABSL-2, ABSL-3, and ABSL3-Ag environments. Animal husbandry duties include, but are not limited to, daily health observations, feeding and watering animals, cleaning caging, receiving, identifying and transporting animals, and providing and monitoring environmental enrichment. The position may require veterinary technical assistance such as blood, tissue, weight, temperature and urine/fecal collections, administering prophylactic and/or terminal treatments and injections, and more. The incumbent will be expected to perform routine cleaning and sanitation duties such as decontaminating, cleaning, disinfecting and sterilizing cages, animal rooms, primary enclosures, ancillary areas, and equipment. Duties also include setting up and breaking down laboratories, operating large equipment like autoclaves, cage washers, biosafety cabinets, etc., providing some facility level training, perform minor preventative maintenance and facility monitoring, and maintaining important documentation (room logs, autoclave/cage washer logs, select agent tracking logs, etc.). The incumbent will be expected to perform all duties in various levels of personal protective equipment (PPE) when in active laboratories and adhere to strict standard operating procedures. Multiple daily showers are required as part of facility biocontainment policies. Participation in pre-study meetings, continuing education, and training classes is expected. This position will require federal approval to work in certain laboratories and requires rotating weekend and holiday work. Incumbent must participate in the UGA Occupational Health program.</div> VetMed-Animal Health Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477894 2026-04-21T18:04:24-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:24-04:00 Cook II <div>Supervises and participates in the work of preparing a large volume of meats, vegetables, and other foods. Consults with supervisor to determine best methods of preparation for individual food items. Assists in planning menus and devising means of using leftover foods. Prepares special foods for banquets and other occasions. Gives special attention to overall appearance of food prepared.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503524 2026-08-28T16:02:11-04:00 2026-08-28T16:02:12-04:00 Project Manager <div>The Project Manager oversees integrated projects from initiation through completion, leading cross-functional teams spanning integrated media, creative, and marketing. The Project Manager is responsible for project direction, facilitating kick-off and milestone meetings, and ensuring alignment with divisional priorities. This position works closely with the Assistant Vice President and Chief of Staff and the Senior Portfolio Manager to set checkpoints, allocate resources, and develop and execute integrated marketing and communications plans that achieve the division’s mission and strategic goals.</div><div><br></div> MarComm-VP Office https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478525 2026-04-22T17:25:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:36-04:00 Student Assistant - Ortega <div>Perform general laboratory tasks from media preparation, plating, general microbiological testing, autoclaving, disposal of laboratory material.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/489533 2026-06-23T13:55:02-04:00 2026-06-23T13:55:03-04:00 Caretaker - Detailed Cleaner <div>This work involves the cleaning and maintenance of patient facilities in the Vet Teaching Hospital. This position will follow a daily and weekly schedule and perform detailed tasks to include cleaning of service area floors including mopping, picking up laundry, stocking and distribution of food, cleaning drains, vacuuming, pressure washing, waste removal, using chemicals to disinfect equipment and surfaces, maintaining the appearance of concrete walkways of the outside barns using a backpack blower and pressure washer. This position picks up orders from a local company, replenishes gas in tractors, carts, and trucks used by the hospital, orders and stocks/distributes shavings with assistance from the lead caretaker. This position transports unowned animals brought to the hospital to the county animal shelter.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478623 2026-04-22T17:33:44-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:44-04:00 Kitchen KITCHEN UTILITY WORKER - COOK Position will assist with preparation and presentation of food for the Savannah Room, Courtyard Café, Training Table, and or Banquets (AM/PM). PSO-Cont Ed-Aux-Food Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495117 2026-07-22T12:43:09-04:00 2026-07-22T12:43:09-04:00 Director of Bar Passage <div>The University of Georgia School of Law Director of Bar Passage will provide strategic leadership for the School of Law’s bar success initiatives, working collaboratively with students, faculty, administrators, and external partners to promote strong bar examination outcomes and student success.<br><br></div><div>This position combines teaching and administration, with an allocation of effort of 40% instruction and 60% administration. The Director will oversee existing bar success programs, develop innovative initiatives to support student achievement, monitor developments related to the NextGen Bar Exam, and serve as the law school’s primary resource on bar passage trends, preparedness, and outcomes.</div> Law School-General https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477840 2026-04-21T17:58:39-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:39-04:00 LVT I - LA 24/7 Care <div>Provide nursing care to patients in the Large Animal Teaching Hospital. Licensed Veterinary Technicians work to fulfill the following within the course of caring for patients: taking vitals such as blood pressure, temperature, Collection of blood, urine by expression, cystocentesis or catheterization; collection and preparation of tissue, cellular, or microbiological samples by skin scraping, impressions; routine laboratory test procedures; radiology including settings, positioning, processing, and safety; intravenous and arterial catheterization; administration and application of treatments, drugs, fluids, medications and immunological agents by oral, parenteral and injectable routes; induction and maintenance of anesthesia; placement of intra-nasal, intra-gastric tubes; dental procedures; surgical assistance; resuscitative procedures; applications of splints and slings; application of appropriate wound dressings and external supportive care in severe wound and burn cases.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503079 2026-08-27T08:57:02-04:00 2026-08-27T08:57:03-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>Assistant Professor position in the Advertising &amp; PR department of Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication to teach a range of undergraduate and graduate courses across our curriculum, such as PR Ethics, Diversity and Leadership, PR Management, PR Campaigns, Integrated (Ad &amp; PR) Campaigns, Intro to Public Relations, and PR Foundations. Mentoring graduate students is expected.</div> Grady-Advertising & PR https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478785 2026-04-22T17:44:05-04:00 2026-04-22T17:44:06-04:00 Temporary Field/Summer Assistant 7 - Basinger <div>To assist with ongoing research taking place in the fields and laboratory.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498724 2026-08-07T15:29:41-04:00 2026-08-07T15:29:42-04:00 Director for Accreditation & Institutional Effectiveness <div>The Director for Accreditation and Institutional Effectiveness functions as the primary point of contact for campus on matters related to institutional accreditation by SACSCOC. The Director has primary responsibility for ensuring and documenting UGAs compliance with SACSCOC accreditation requirements. This includes communicating with campus regarding SACSCOC policies and procedures and working with campus leaders to develop and implement internal policies and procedures that ensure ongoing compliance. The Director oversees SACSCOC reporting requirements, including the fifth-year interim report, the decennial reaffirmation, annual reports, and substantive change notifications and approvals. The Director reports to the Chief of Staff to the Provost and supports UGA’s SACSCOC accreditation liaison.<br><br></div><div>In addition, the Director plays a key role in overseeing the University’s institutional effectiveness processes. This includes the University's strategic planning process, Academic Program Review, Support Unit Review, and Administrator Review processes. The Director also coordinates with campus offices responsible for other institutional effectiveness processes, such as unit evaluations and student learning outcomes assessment, to ensure that UGA meets SACSCOC expectations in these areas.<br><br></div><div>The Director will represent and promote accreditation and institutional effectiveness priorities by serving on University and University System of Georgia committees and task forces as applicable.</div> SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478364 2026-04-22T17:15:58-04:00 2026-04-22T17:15:58-04:00 Temporary Lab/Greenhouse Assistant - Raymer <div>To assist in field data collection, lab research, and greenhouse management of turfgrass.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478795 2026-04-22T17:46:27-04:00 2026-05-19T14:17:06-04:00 Equestrian - Building Services Work daily with horses at the UGA Equestrian barn and help to clean and maintain the area and animals. Athletics-Equestrian https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504500 2026-09-04T06:52:33-04:00 2026-09-04T06:52:34-04:00 BUILDING SERVICES WORKER, LEAD <div>The Building Services Worker Lead is a key position within Facilities Management Division’s Building Services unit. Reporting directly to a Manager, this position will be responsible for day to day management of custodial operations within an assigned building or collection of buildings. The Building Services Worker Lead directly supervises crews approximately 6 to 10 employees who are responsible for care, cleaning, and minor maintenance of campus building and fixtures. Responsible for communicating information and training material related to productivity, safety, and work performance. Provides guidance to Building Service Workers; verbally, written, and electronically, regarding personnel concerns, team performance, employee development, employee performance, overall work results, stakeholder experience and satisfaction. Works closely with other Building Service Worker Leads within Building Services and other shifts to ensure seamlessness of operations including work routines, equipment and supply recommendations and purchases. This is a working leadership position whereby the Lead will often have to perform the duties of their employees if they are short staffed. This position is considered Key and Essential and can be expected to be recalled 24/7 in an emergency situation.<br><br></div> FMD-Svcs-Blding Svcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501270 2026-08-19T13:13:21-04:00 2026-08-19T13:13:21-04:00 Assistant Director of Career Accelerators <div>Reporting to the Associate Director of Career Accelerators, this position leads the execution and daily operations of the Career Accelerator Initiative, managing the full lifecycle of student engagement from recruitment through completion. This role coordinates program delivery, student experience, and partner engagement while working closely with Career Center Consultants, Employer Relations, and the Mentor Program to ensure seamless implementation. The Assistant Director plays a key role in delivering group coaching, coordinating events, and driving participation through effective communication and outreach.</div> DAR-Career Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478477 2026-04-22T17:22:49-04:00 2026-04-22T17:22:50-04:00 Student Assistant- Tillman 2 <div>Collects stink bugs and bees at field sites using plant scouting and trapping techniques to monitor population dynamics and diversity of these insects in wildflowers, cotton, and other habitats. Washes collected bees to collect pollen for DNA studies and then pins the bees. Deploys and retrieves stink bugs egg masses in various stink bug host plants in these habitats. Maintains wildflower plots by mowing grass, de-weeding, and watering. Helps plant wildflowers in field plots. Responsible for general maintenance of vehicles (pumping gas and keeping clean) and field and laboratory tools and equipment.</div> CAES-Tifton Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/485841 2026-05-28T17:08:11-04:00 2026-05-28T17:08:12-04:00 Open Rank - Orthopedic Surgery <div>The Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery at the College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, invites applications for a clinical (non-tenure) track, tenure track, or tenured faculty position in small animal orthopedic surgery at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor.<br><br>The major responsibilities for this position are to teach and provide service in orthopedics in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, teach didactic and laboratory courses in orthopedics to veterinary students, actively participate in training of surgical residents, and to develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. Proportionate assignments for each area will be based on the interests of the candidate in conjunction with the missions of the Surgery program and the Department.<br><br>The service enjoys access to vanguard technology in diagnostic imaging, including a 64-slice CT scanner, 3.0 Tesla MRI, digital radiography, ultrasound, nuclear scintigraphy, and a dedicated interventional radiology suite. The Veterinary Teaching Hospital is a 300,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility opened in March 2015. Each specialty has its own dedicated rounds room. Faculty members’ offices and over 5,400 square feet of shared research space are located on the floor above the hospital.<br><br>The successful candidate will join two board-certified surgeons and technical staff. Faculty members enjoy a diverse caseload with ongoing clinical and benchtop research projects, extensive collaborations with other services, and opportunities to teach students and house officers. Laboratory space and core facilities are available to support basic and clinical research.<br><br>For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications.</div> VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478574 2026-04-22T17:30:00-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:01-04:00 Temporary Field/Greenhouse Assistant To assist in field preparation, maintenance, mowing, and greenhouse management of turfgrass research areas. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493179 2026-07-14T11:40:10-04:00 2026-07-14T11:40:11-04:00 Manager - Swimming & Diving Men’s Swimming and Diving is seeking a manager who is willing to work during the 2018-2019 Swimming and Diving Season. Typical Manager Duties include but are not limited to the following.\r\nKeep up with social media accounts (Twitter, Facebook, Instagram etc.)\r\nBe able to Film and process film of swim/dive meets.\r\nLift at least 50 pounds. Standing for periods of time is sometimes required while filming or working meets. \r\nPick-up/Drop-off Equipment and Laundry from the Equipment room as needed.\r\nHelp as needed with recruiting weekends i.e. set up, clean-up make sure supplies are in order for the weekend. \r\nAssist Coaches and staff as needed during practice times, meets, etc.\r\nBe able to travel to away meets and attend all home meets. Athletics-Mens Swim & Dive https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/34131 2018-10-17T16:18:47-04:00 2018-10-17T16:18:48-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research A temporary/lab research position is needed to work in the soybean research lab to take agronomic notes, collect data, and harvest soybean research plots in the field. This position will work in the seed lab to weigh and clean samples, thresh individual plants, and prepare seed for spring planting. CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478686 2026-04-22T17:39:03-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:04-04:00 Post-Doctoral Research <div>This position will isolate extracellular vesicles from cell culture media and characterize them. Dedicate time in lab research and analysis, and reporting data.<br>The fast pace of the grant necessitates someone who can dedicate there time to the lab research and the analysis and reporting of the data.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497439 2026-08-03T10:10:32-04:00 2026-08-03T10:10:33-04:00 Temporary Summer Residential Building Services Worker <div>This is a full-time, temporary <strong>summer</strong> position with University Housing. The primary function of this position is to perform a variety of cleaning and related duties in and around the residence hall. This person works in a community housing approximately 1,000 residents.</div> Housing-Facilities-Maintenance https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478001 2026-04-21T18:25:22-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:23-04:00 Louise McBee Distinguished Professor of Higher Education <div>The Louise McBee Institute of Higher Education at the University of Georgia invites applications from senior higher education scholars to fill the Louise McBee Distinguished Professorship in Higher Education with a starting date of August 1, 2026.<br><br></div><div>The professorship honors Dr. Louise McBee, who held multiple leadership positions at the University of Georgia before serving for over a decade as a champion for higher education in the Georgia legislature. As an administrator, she helped advance UGA’s academic and service missions; as a legislator, she played important roles in ensuring the future of the HOPE Scholarship and launching initiatives such as the Governor’s Teaching Fellows program.<br><br></div><div>We seek a scholar who will advance the multi-disciplinary character of the McBee Institute, add to the depth and breadth of our faculty, and undertake work that furthers our understandings of higher education.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will be expected to teach core graduate-level courses, advise and mentor doctoral students, pursue an active program of funded research, publish impactful scholarship, and participate in the ongoing academic and governance activities of the McBee Institute.</div> SRVPAA-Institute of Higher Ed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503957 2026-09-01T14:09:12-04:00 2026-09-01T14:09:12-04:00 FOOD SERVICE WORKER I (Partial Year) This is a benefits eligible, partial year position (9-11 months of the year) August 1st thru May 10th of each year. The selected candidate will sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date. **\r\n\r\nThis is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals. Auxiliary Snelling https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500207 2026-08-14T14:14:27-04:00 2026-08-14T14:14:27-04:00 Creative Video Intern <div>The University of Georgia Athletic Association is seeking a passionate and driven individual for a full-time post-graduate internship within the Creative Services team. This position offers hands-on experience producing high-impact video content that supports the UGA Athletics brand through storytelling, fan engagement, and recruiting efforts across digital and social platforms.<br><br></div><div>The ideal candidate is a visual storyteller who thrives in fast-paced environments, understands the college sports landscape, and is eager to contribute creatively within a collaborative team.<br><br></div> Athletics-Creative Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478407 2026-04-22T17:19:42-04:00 2026-05-11T11:28:43-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant - Ogden <div>The Research Assistant will help with all aspects of Dr. Ogden's CEA breeding program. This will involve a combination of greenhouse, lab, and field work with primary location at Bledsoe Research Farm in Williamson.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479117 2026-04-23T16:32:22-04:00 2026-07-23T15:17:49-04:00 Student Electronics Technician <div>The Student Electronics Technician will assist in the maintenance, troubleshooting, and installation of AVL (Automated Vehicle Location), video surveillance, and communication systems on UGA buses and transit vehicles. The position supports the daily technical operations by helping to ensure equipment is functional, accurate, and properly documented. The technician will work closely with the supervisor and team to support diagnostics, inventory, and repairs. Work is hands-on and may involve time in the shop and in the field.<br><br><em>All individuals selected for this position are required to undergo drug and alcohol testing in accordance with US Department of Transportation regulations.</em></div> Auxiliary Information Technolo https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502757 2026-08-26T10:07:23-04:00 2026-08-26T10:07:24-04:00 Behavioral Analyst II <div>This individual will provide direct behavior analytic services and support to individuals in school and clinic settings. This involves working with clients aged birth through adulthood who have developmental disabilities (or no disability) and who is being seen as a client for a reduction in severe problem behavior (i.e. behavior that is resulting in injury to themselves or others) or in skill acquisition of things like communication, toileting, and academic skills. They will operate in clinical, home, and school contexts. They will design, implement, and monitor treatment efficacy. This involves planning assessment procedures, training staff in assessment procedures, conducting assessment procedures, and analyzing data from the assessment. Communicating about the results of the assessment. Building treatment protocols based on assessment. Training staff and caregivers in treatment. Testing treatment. Conducting a follow-up of the intervention. Lead team meetings on client protocols. Consult with teachers, parents, and other therapists on appropriate behavior interventions.</div> COE-Autism&Behav Ed Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477902 2026-04-21T18:04:44-04:00 2026-04-21T18:04:44-04:00 Cook I (Partial Year) <div><strong>This is a benefits eligible, partial year position, 9-11 months of each year. The selected incumbent will be required to sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.</strong><br><br>Skilled cooking work in the preparation of foods for a cafeteria. Work involves the general preparation and cooking of a variety of foods, or the specialized preparations of meats and vegetables. Work involves responsibility of neatness and cleanliness in preparing food, and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Works under the supervision of a Cook 2 or Chef.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503581 2026-08-31T10:07:41-04:00 2026-08-31T10:07:41-04:00 Temporary Accountant <div>Involves the accurate and timely completion of reports and invoices and processing of awards and modifications under the terms of the various contracts, grants and agreements awarded to the university. The position will interpret, establish, and maintain award files and government documents pertaining to post-award administration of grants and contracts.</div> FD-SPA Post Award Accounting https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499770 2026-08-13T10:24:22-04:00 2026-08-13T10:24:23-04:00 Director of Skidaway Institute of Oceanography and Professor <div>The University of Georgia (UGA), a land-grant, sea-grant and space-grant university with statewide commitments and responsibilities, is Georgia's oldest, most comprehensive institution of higher education. UGA invites nominations and applications for the position of Director of the Skidaway Institute of Oceanography (Skidaway Institute) located on Skidaway Island near Savannah, Georgia. The Director will also be appointed as a tenured professor in the UGA Department of Marine Sciences, which includes faculty based at Skidaway Institute and on the main UGA campus in Athens.&nbsp;<br><br>Responsibilities of the Director:</div><ul><li>is the most senior administrator at Skidaway Institute and has overall responsibility for personnel, budgets, and facilities at Skidaway Institute;</li><li>models and fosters a climate of collegiality while providing the strategic and institutional vision for vigorous, collaborative research;</li><li>directly oversees the faculty in their research role, as well as the Director of Finance and Operations, Marine Superintendent, Public Relations/ Communications Coordinator, and an administrative assistant;</li><li>conducts or oversees annual evaluations of all Skidaway Institute staff and supports their professional development;</li><li>promotes and facilitates externally funded research at Skidaway Institute;</li><li>works collaboratively with the Department of Marine Sciences Head to recruit, mentor, and evaluate Skidaway Institute faculty;</li><li>works closely with the Department of Marine Sciences Head to integrate Skidaway Institute faculty into the Department’s strategic research, education, service, and outreach initiatives;</li><li>partners with UGA’s other coastal units, including the UGA Marine Institute on Sapelo Island, UGA Marine Extension and Georgia Sea Grant, to develop impactful initiatives consistent with their respective missions;</li><li>identifies and expands collaborative opportunities with other University System of Georgia institutions and UGA colleges and schools;</li><li>keeps the Office of Research, Department of Marine Sciences, and other stakeholders informed of Skidaway Institute initiatives and opportunities;</li><li>works closely with the UGA Office of Governmental Relations to elevate Skidaway Institute legislative priorities; and</li><li>represents Skidaway Institute in regional, national, and international organizations and venues.</li></ul><div><br>The Director, while first and foremost the administrator of the Institute and its functions, will be expected to remain active in research that advances the research and education missions of Skidaway Institute and the Department of Marine Sciences.<br><br>The Director reports to the Vice President for Research in their administrative role and to the Head of the Department of Marine Sciences in their faculty role.</div> VPR-Skidaway Inst Oceanography https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478385 2026-04-22T17:16:35-04:00 2026-05-01T16:35:36-04:00 Student Assistant - Gratzek <div>Temporary position will perform manual labor including food mixing, preparation, filling, cleaning and miscellaneous other tasks.</div> CAES-Food Prod Inno & Comm Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478820 2026-04-22T17:50:02-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:03-04:00 4-H Environmental Educator  - Student Assistant <div>This job is a temporary Environmental Educator at Georgia 4-H Centers.&nbsp; The primary responsibility is to independently lead K-12 grade students through multidisciplinary classes in an outdoor setting. Class subjects offered include life and earth science, ecology, team building, outdoor skills, and living history. Other responsibilities include animal care, maintenance of teaching areas and resources, facilities, grounds, and support of general operations of the facility.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501987 2026-08-21T15:56:48-04:00 2026-08-21T15:56:48-04:00 Program Operations Support Assistant <div>This position provides operational and programmatic support for statewide program initiatives for the Expanded Food and Nutrition Education Program (EFNEP). The incumbent coordinates trainings and program resources, supports purchasing and budget-related activities, maintains program accountability and reporting systems, and serves as a key communication liaison with county faculty and staff. The position assists with the implementation of program operations and ensures the timely flow of information, materials, and documentation necessary for effective statewide program delivery. Administrative functions are performed in support of program operations and represent a smaller portion of the overall responsibilities.</div> FACS-Community Food&Nutrit Ed https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478507 2026-04-22T17:24:23-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:23-04:00 Seasonal Animal Care and Environmental Education Assistant <div>The Seasonal Animal Care and Environmental Education Assistant position is a part-time role over the summer with a commitment of up to 10 hours per week. The primary responsibilities include animal care of live reptiles and amphibians and independently leading environmental education classes for K-12 grade students. Additional duties encompass general facility cleaning, light maintenance of grounds and trails, as well as various office and clerical tasks at the Mary Kahrs Warnell Forest Education Center in Guyton, GA (Effingham County).</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487652 2026-06-09T10:35:16-04:00 2026-06-09T10:35:17-04:00 Temporary Research Associate - Esseili <div>Ordering, maintaining chemical/reagent inventory, equipment maintenance, follow-up with companies and equipment repairs. Maintain cell culture for various cell lines, make cell culture plates and buffers for various projects, and perform limited experiments.</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478604 2026-04-22T17:32:40-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:41-04:00 Student Assistant Student assistant role to assist with peanut plant care in the greenhouse, harvesting seed, counting seed, and managing seed inventory. CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494785 2026-07-21T11:19:55-04:00 2026-07-21T11:19:55-04:00 FOOD SERVICE WORKER I This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals. Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477808 2026-04-21T17:50:34-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:35-04:00 Research Technician - Neuromuscular Diseases <div>This position will work with others on our team to develop treatments for neuromuscular diseases such as ALS (Lou Gehrig disease). We work on cell-based and gene therapies in cellular and mouse models. This position will be in a collaborative research environment.</div><div><br></div><div>This person will conduct detailed studies and have keen observational skills and eventually work independently. Knowledge and experiences in molecular genetics and cell culture. Responsibilities of the position will include maintaining lab safety regulations, laboratory instruments, and inventory, assisting with the purchase of lab supplies, and ensuring overall organization.</div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478724 2026-04-22T17:40:39-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:39-04:00 Forest Soil Fieldwork Temporary Technician <div>The Markewitz Forest Soils and Water laboratory is looking for two undergraduate students to assist with fieldwork in support of an upcoming scientific research effort. The work will involve travel to South and Central Georgia for the collection of plant material and soils over the course of one week of fieldwork.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498034 2026-08-05T10:07:02-04:00 2026-08-05T10:07:03-04:00 Laboratory Systems Administrator <div>This role is focused on providing exceptional desktop support, maintaining IT devices within a scientific laboratory environment, and performing systems administration tasks. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in IT support, excellent problem-solving skills, and the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, research-driven setting.<br><br>This position requires completion of specified certifications within the first two years of hire for employees who do not already possess them, with department support available.</div> VPR-Research IT https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478101 2026-04-21T18:31:54-04:00 2026-04-21T18:31:55-04:00 Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor <div>The Department of Clinical and Administrative Pharmacy is seeking an outstanding candidate to join our faculty and provide leadership in clinical practice, teaching, scholarly, and administrative activities. This is a full-time, non-tenure track position at the rank of clinical assistant, associate, or full professor. <strong>This position will be located in Albany, Georgia.</strong></div><div><br>The primary duties of the faculty member include didactic and experiential teaching of pharmacy students, development and maintenance of an active clinical practice site, participating in scholarship, and being actively engaged in citizenship to the college. This position will also have the administrative role of Extended Campus Coordinator (ECC) for the P3 Albany Extended Campus Site. The focus of the ECC is to contact, collaborate, communicate, and connect with issues germane to the specific P3 campus and related parties.</div> Pharmacy-Clin & Admin Pharmacy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504266 2026-09-02T17:36:48-04:00 2026-09-02T17:36:49-04:00 Career Consultant <div>The Career Consultant serves as the primary career services liaison to assigned colleges or schools at the University of Georgia. This role acts as a critical link between the Career Center and the college, serving as a resource for students, employers, and faculty on career planning, industry trends, and professional development. Internally, the Career Consultant advocates for the college’s career-related needs and serves as a key referral point for students and stakeholders. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Career Consultants provide comprehensive career coaching and programming support related to career exploration, job search strategies, skill development, experiential learning, graduate school preparation, and employment opportunities for program-specific undergraduate and graduate students. They develop industry connections relevant to students’ career interests and foster mentorship opportunities with UGA alumni. Additionally, they collaborate closely with faculty, academic advisors, and student services staff to integrate career development into the student experience. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Through open, honest, and respectful communication, all staff, supervisors, and colleagues of the Division of Development &amp; Alumni Relations are expected to interact with fairness, compassion, and decency. All employees will be held accountable for meeting the expectation of promoting a stable, productive, and healthy work environment. &nbsp;</div> DAR-Career Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500732 2026-08-18T09:40:52-04:00 2026-08-18T09:40:53-04:00 Director of Medical Education <div>The Director of Medical Education for the School of Medicine partners with the Associate Dean for Curriculum to provide oversight and supervisory leadership to MD program curricular operations, curriculum mapping, curriculum management, instructional design, educational technology integration, academic records coordination, and administrative support for the MD curriculum. The Director provides oversight and direct supervision to approximately 20 staff members and coordinators within the Office of Curriculum, who provide administrative and logistical support to curriculum operations and the Office of Curriculum. The Director supports compliance with LCME accreditation standards, continuous quality improvement, and curricular management and delivery under direction of the Associate Dean for Curriculum and in collaboration with the curricular assistant deans and directors, curricular academic leads, and teaching faculty.</div> SOM-UME https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478434 2026-04-22T17:20:26-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:27-04:00 Temporary Field/Lab Assistant - Buntin <div>Work involves 50% fieldwork and 50% work processing samples in the laboratory. Fieldwork includes but is not limited to helping to plant, maintain grain and forage crops as well as sampling field trials for insects and various plant measurements. Lab work includes but is not limited to sorting and inspecting plant samples for insects and other organisms and various other measurements. Some processing of samples may be needed. Data entry in Excel spreadsheets also is needed. Work will be mostly during hot conditions in the summer. Duties also may sometimes need out-of-town travel to research plots during the workday. The employee receives specific work instructions at the beginning of each new job and work is usually closely supervised; however, constant supervision is not necessary as many tasks are routine and repetitive and can be carried on without difficulty once they are learned.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/482768 2026-05-13T10:00:54-04:00 2026-05-13T10:00:55-04:00 Small Animal Emergency Front Desk <div>The primary responsibility for this position will be to assist the Emergency Critical Care team on setting appointments and receiving emergency patients during evenings, overnights, weekends, and holidays. The ECC Vet Asst. will assist clients in delivering their pets to the ECC team which may include lifting/restraining and transporting into the ER. This incumbent will also answer phones, set up appointments from local referring veterinarians, open patient charts in the hospital database system, and process payments for services.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478555 2026-04-22T17:29:25-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:26-04:00 Student Assistant - Golf Range/Carts <div>The role of the carts/range staff is to make sure clean golf carts are readily available to customers at all times, that customers always have plenty of golf balls to hit at the range, and that both the cart barn and driving range building are properly secured at the end of each day. In the event that a carts/range employee is asked to work a cash register, they are expected to do so within the established policies and procedures.</div> Auxiliary University Golf Cour https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491589 2026-07-06T13:40:26-04:00 2026-07-06T13:40:27-04:00 Greene County 4-H and Youth Development Agent <div>This position will be responsible for managing the 4-H &amp; Youth Development programming in Greene County by providing educational opportunities for youth in 4-H club meetings, coordinating local activities, and preparing youth for project and judging events.<br><br>This position requires frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official duty travel are required. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others including 4-H Youth and Adult Clientele is also a common and necessary function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants. http://extension.uga.edu/4h/ http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478646 2026-04-22T17:36:38-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:39-04:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>The White lab combines molecular genetics, evolutionary genetics, and genomics to investigate fundamental processes underlying sex chromosomes. The postdoc will have the opportunity to engage with multiple active research areas in the lab. There are projects underway to investigate the genetic and developmental mechanisms underlying male sex determination, with a particular emphasis on how these processes repeatedly evolve across species. In addition, the White lab is broadly interested in the mechanisms governing DNA repair and segregation of newly evolving sex chromosomes during meiosis. All projects use stickleback fish species as a model system. Threespine stickleback fish are a leading genetic model organism, with a well-assembled genome, including a fully assembled Y chromosome, and tools for efficient functional genetics.</div> Franklin-Genetics https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496605 2026-07-28T16:48:13-04:00 2026-07-28T16:48:14-04:00 4-H Marion/Schley Counties AmeriCorps Member, Part Time <div>The AmeriCorps State program is a federally funded grant providing U.S. citizens with the opportunity to serve in their own country. The Georgia 4-H AmeriCorps member provides 4-H programming directly to youth under the direction of the County Extension Agent. Supervision is also provided by the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator. This includes planning, implementation, and delivery of programming including in-school and after school club meetings, camp, and other 4-H programming delivered in the county as well as volunteer recruitment and transportation of youth. The member will also assist the AmeriCorps State Program Coordinator in collecting impact data by administering surveys to youth and entering data into provided spreadsheets. Members will comply with AmeriCorps guidelines such as quarterly reporting, monthly webinars, and other trainings.</div><div>This posting is for a half-time (part-time) AmeriCorps member serving for 12 months for the period of September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. Members will log a total of 900 hours, averaging 20 hours/week, depending on start date.<br><strong>Special Instructions to Applicants</strong> This is a National Service position funded through a grant from Georgia Serves (aka Georgia Commission on Service &amp; Volunteerism) and AmeriCorps, the federal agency. Please see the <a href=\"https://www.americorps.gov/\"><strong>AmeriCorps website</strong></a> for more information. Position availability is contingent upon continued availability of federal funds. This position is available September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. If additional funding becomes available, individuals may have the option to re-enroll for additional years of service if they meet the service hour requirement (900) and perform satisfactorily.</div><div>Federal regulations require a High School diploma or equivalent to apply. Additional education and experience are preferred but not required. The position requires a one-year commitment. This is a temporary national service position, not a traditional employment position.</div><div>Candidates are also required to apply in the My AmeriCorps portal. Please go to the <a href=\"https://my.americorps.gov/mp/login.do\"><strong>My AmeriCorps portal</strong></a>, click on Apply to Serve, and complete the four steps to Create Profile. After creating a profile, create an application and apply for the specific county position. For assistance, call the National Service Help Desk at 1-800-942-2677.</div><div>Benefits provided to half-time AmeriCorps members include modest monthly living allowance ($1,037.50/month), loan forbearance, and a Segal Education Award equivalent to half of the Pell Grant that may be used to pay educational costs at eligible post-secondary educational institutions as well as to repay qualified student loans. To qualify for the Segal Education Award of $3,697.50 the member must successfully log 900 service hours by August 31, 2027.</div><div>To serve in this position, applicants must be prepared to provide copies of the following documents: Proof of Citizenship (birth certificate or valid Passport), Social Security Card, Government Issued ID, Federal and State Tax Forms, High School Diploma or equivalent. Applicants must submit to a complete criminal history background check, including a finger-print based FBI check. Individuals convicted of murder or those on the sex offender registry or required to be on the sex offender registry are not eligible. The AmeriCorps member must comply with the Member Service Agreement (provided prior to service). You must possess a valid driver's license to be considered for this position.</div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478529 2026-04-22T17:25:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:44-04:00 Temporary Technician <div>Field and laboratory duties to support research in Peach laboratory</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490215 2026-06-25T18:29:19-04:00 2026-06-25T18:29:20-04:00 IT Technical Support Manager <div>This position will oversee and be responsible for the overall programmatic Information technology needs for the Savannah River Ecology Lab.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478625 2026-04-22T17:33:48-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:49-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate AD <div>Due to the varied nature of projects at BFF, the PostDoc will be required to operate in a variety of disciplines to execute fermentation projects for a major client. Outside of that work the Postdoc will focus on cell culture and protein purification process development. In addition, the candidate should have an understanding of molecular biology principles including gene cloning and strain development. The candidate will contribute to the development of new procedures that could eventually be services offered in the facility. This will require the ability to critically read and adapt procedures from the scientific literature, and accurately implement requested services.&nbsp;</div> Franklin-Biochemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495523 2026-07-23T14:54:19-04:00 2026-07-23T14:54:19-04:00 Academic Advisor <div>The primary responsibility of an Academic Advisor in the Office of Undergraduate Services in the Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication is to provide comprehensive academic guidance to an assigned caseload of 275-350 majors in Advertising, Entertainment and Media Studies, Journalism, and Public Relations. This role requires consistent communication with students and detailed record-keeping.<br><br></div><div>Core responsibilities include meeting regularly with students to offer accurate information about degree program requirements and course planning; maintaining advising notes and records; and developing a strong knowledge of academic regulations and student support resources. Advisors also provide orientation advising and program support for incoming first-year and transfer students.</div> Grady-Undergrad Studies https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477845 2026-04-21T17:58:50-04:00 2026-04-21T17:58:51-04:00 Limited Term Senior Research Associate (Caughy) <div>The individual will provide specialized support for two separate funded research projects. This includes tracking and troubleshooting participant incentives, creating R scripts for geocoding, and independently using R software to impute data files.<br><br><strong>This position is grant-funded and is expected to continue through 2029 (five years from the project’s start date in 2024). Extension beyond this period is contingent upon the availability of continued funding.</strong></div><div><br></div> VPR-Owens Inst Behavioral Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503095 2026-08-27T10:10:35-04:00 2026-08-27T10:10:35-04:00 Student Engagement and Retention Specialist Position <div>The Student Engagement and Retention Specialist Position is a central role that helps facilitate and promote student engagement and career readiness opportunities for Franklin College undergraduate students. Situated within the Office of Student Pathways/Engagement and Success, the Student Engagement and Retention Specialist Position works together with the (Student Pathways/Engagement and Success Coordinator) and the Senior Director for the Office of Student Academic Services to create and maintain systems that support student engagement opportunities and initiatives focused on retaining students in the Franklin College at UGA. This position would be a primary facilitator and contact for routing and tracking MOUs required for Franklin College internship experiences earning academic credit. The person in this role will work closely with academic departments and Internship and Career Coordinators in the college to broaden internship site access and troubleshoot MOU concerns with UGA General Counsel. The Student Engagement and Retention Specialist Position will work closely with partner offices across campus (e.g. Experiential Learning, Career Center, Pre-Professional Advising Office, etc.) to develop, support, and promote opportunities for Franklin College students.<br><br>This position is the primary contact for developing and maintaining engagement pages on the OSAS website A thorough knowledge of the following university data and reporting software is necessary: ARGOS, SAGE, Banner, and DegreeWorks, as well as Excel and the Microsoft Office Suite.</div> Franklin-Deans Academic Serv https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498907 2026-08-10T11:37:03-04:00 2026-08-10T11:37:03-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>This postdoctoral researcher position is essential to support multiple externally funded research projects focused on cancer immunotherapy and translational oncology. The position requires advanced expertise in tumor immunology, animal models of cancer, molecular and cellular biology, and high-dimensional data analysis. The postdoctoral researcher will play a leading role in the design, execution, and interpretation of preclinical studies evaluating novel immunotherapeutic and nanomedicine-based approaches for cancer treatment.<br><br>The individual will be responsible for coordinating and conducting complex in vivo and in vitro experiments, including therapeutic efficacy studies, immune profiling, sequencing-based analyses, and mechanistic investigations. The position is critical for maintaining project timelines, generating data required for sponsored research objectives, and disseminating findings through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations.<br><br>In addition, the postdoctoral researcher will provide scientific leadership within the laboratory by mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, assisting with experimental design and troubleshooting, and contributing to the preparation of manuscripts and research reports. The specialized training and independent research capabilities required for these responsibilities necessitate a postdoctoral-level appointment.</div> Franklin-Chemistry https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478366 2026-04-22T17:16:01-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:02-04:00 Student Assistant - Wurzburger Lab <div>Fieldwork: carrying 25 pounds, digging small holes. Lab work: standing to perform lab tasks such as grinding samples,</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478797 2026-04-22T17:46:31-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:31-04:00 Postdoctoral research associate <div>Position performs cutting-edge interdisciplinary research, aiming to investigate the pathological and therapeutic roles of extracellular vesicles in neuromuscular disease (Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, ALS) and shape efficient CRISPR-mediated gene therapy.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Leveraging methodologies from molecular biotechnology, cell biology, genetics, epigenetics, genomics, current research in Dr. Yao’s lab focus on <strong>1)</strong> Engineering extracellular vesicles as <em>in vivo</em> delivery shuttle to facilitate CRISPR-mediated gene therapy for neurological disorders; <strong>2)</strong> Uncovering the pathological and therapeutic roles of extracellular vesicles in ALS, using cellular (e.g. iPSCs) and mouse models to; <strong>3)</strong> Investigating Fibro-adipogenic progenitors (FAPs)-mediated muscle regeneration and reinnervation in response to denervation and other muscle damages.&nbsp;<br><br></div> CAES-Animal & Dairy Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504538 2026-09-04T09:46:22-04:00 2026-09-04T09:46:22-04:00 Graphic Designer <div>This position is responsible for assisting the Creative Services department's efforts in creating a digital identity strategy that includes graphic and motion graphic design, visual identity, digital and social media strategy. The Graphic Designer will fulfill requests from many different areas, including Athletic Communications, Marketing and Recruiting, while adhering to and assisting in the development of the programs' brand standards. Alongside the Assistant Athletic Director of Social Media and Digital Strategy, work to develop and implement a visual communication plan for the 21-sport Athletic department.</div> Athletics-Creative Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501310 2026-08-19T14:20:15-04:00 2026-08-19T14:20:15-04:00 Laboratory Technician I <div>The Laboratory Technician I will support research activities in the Huet Laboratory within the Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences. The laboratory investigates the organellar biology of apicomplexan parasites using molecular, cellular, genetic, and biochemical approaches. The incumbent will assist with daily laboratory operations, maintain cell culture systems, perform routine and specialized research procedures, prepare laboratory reagents and supplies, maintain accurate research records, provide guidance and support to junior researchers, and contribute to the overall success of ongoing research projects.</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478486 2026-04-22T17:23:05-04:00 2026-04-22T17:23:06-04:00 Temporary Service Worker Con't Ed - Cain <div>Room set-up and room clean up; office support such as copying, faxing, making conference disks, word-processing; managing storage space; supporting transportation need in our workshops; providing A-V support in some cases; and supporting our catering operation.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486036 2026-05-29T15:05:32-04:00 2026-05-29T15:05:33-04:00 Entomology Temporary Field Tech-Basu <div>The vegetable entomology research laboratory conducts investigation into how pest insects affect vegetable productivity in Georgia and how to best control these pests. Current tasks include maintaining insect (e.g., whitefly and diamondback moth) colonies, collecting and processing samples and entering data. Specific tasks include rapidly identifying and counting small insects under stereo microscope magnification, maintain plant food for insect colonies, plant seeds/seedlings for colonies and/or research tests, scout, and other duties related to entomological field research.</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478576 2026-04-22T17:30:05-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:05-04:00 Student Assistant Franklin-Psychology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493233 2026-07-14T13:19:01-04:00 2026-07-14T13:19:02-04:00 Business Consultant-Augusta <div>The University of Georgia Small Business Development Center seeks an experienced, results-driven management professional with strong business skills to serve the Augusta area as a <strong>Business Consultant</strong>.<br><br>A Small Business Development Center (SBDC) Business Consultant is a public service faculty position responsible for providing counseling and delivering programs to individuals, businesses, communities, organizations, and other public agencies in their assigned geographic territory. As a Business Consultant, you’ll work directly with business owners to provide expert guidance in areas such as financial analysis, business planning, marketing strategy, and operations management. You’ll also develop and lead educational programs tailored to the needs of the local business community.<br><br>This position is located in Augusta, Georgia. Multi-county travel is required.</div> PSO-Small Business Dev Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477479 2026-04-20T16:53:45-04:00 2026-04-20T16:53:45-04:00 Post Doctoral Research Associate <div>Join the <strong>Lance Wells Lab</strong> at the CCRC at UGA to investigate the pivotal role of <strong>O-GlcNAcylation</strong> in human health and disease. This research, supported by the <strong>Michael J. Fox Foundation (MJFF)</strong> and the <strong>NIH/NICHD</strong>, focuses on the molecular mechanisms of <strong>OGT-XLID</strong> (X-linked Intellectual Disability) and the emerging links between O-GlcNAc signaling and <strong>Parkinson’s Disease</strong>. We are looking for a creative scientist to push the boundaries of how we detect and quantify this dynamic modification in the brain.<br><br></div> VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478695 2026-04-22T17:39:20-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:20-04:00 Temporary Facilities Engineer Intern <div>This position will assist the Griffin Campus Facilities Management team with daily tasks and projects, have an opportunity to learn from professionals, gain practical experience, develop an understanding of how to manage and operate facilities, and work on meaningful projects that contribute to our mission.</div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497454 2026-08-03T10:44:04-04:00 2026-08-03T10:44:05-04:00 BUSINESS MANAGER II <div>The Business Manager for the UGA Gwinnett Campus manages professional, fiscal, and administrative processes for planning, organizing, leading, and controlling the unit’s fiscal and logistical activities. The position projects financial needs, oversees annual budget development, manages student activity and technology fee accounts and UGA Foundation funds, prepares monthly financial reports and annual budget analyses, and oversees P-cards for the campus. This position also manages key functions in HR, including payroll processing, leave tracking, and resolution of payroll issues. The Business Manager ensures the integrity and accuracy of all financial processes across the campus, maintains up-to-date policies and procedures, and responds to all audit requests. This person assists the Director of the Gwinnett Campus in obtaining, interpreting, and reporting data about campus enrollments, space usage, student recruitment and retention, and resource allocation. This is a professional position and requires a high level of knowledge, independent and sound decision-making, excellent communication skills, and a high degree of confidentiality. Supervision of support staff may be required.</div> VPI-Gwinnett Graduate Programs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478003 2026-04-21T18:25:27-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:28-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor - Fungal Biology/Mycology <div>The Department of Plant Pathology in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES) at the University of Georgia is recruiting for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor in Fungal Biology/Mycology with 70% research, 25% teaching, and 5% service appointment. This is an academic-year (9-month), tenure- track appointment located at the Athens Campus. The successful candidate will develop a dynamic, innovative, internationally recognized, and extramurally funded research program in basic fungal biology. Areas of interest include computational biology and comparative, population, or functional genomics, with the goal of understanding ecological or evolutionary patterns and processes of plant-pathogenic fungi. Research using novel and contemporary approaches into the molecular, ecological, or evolutionary aspects of pathogenic fungal–plant host interactions is also of interest. The position offers rich opportunities for collaborations with colleagues in the Department of Plant Pathology, the <a href=\"https://fungi.franklinresearch.uga.edu/\"><strong>Fungal Biology Group,</strong></a> the <a href=\"https://plantcenter.uga.edu/\"><strong>Plant Center,</strong></a> and the <a href=\"https://iob.uga.edu/\"><strong>Institute of Bioinformatics</strong></a>. There is an expectation of excellence in grantsmanship, timely communication of research findings via peer-reviewed journal articles, active participation in the mentoring of graduate students and postdoctoral scientists and contributing to a dynamic environment within the university. Initial instructional responsibilities will include teaching <em>Mycology</em>, a split-level graduate and undergraduate student course, and <em>Fungi, Friends and Foes</em>, a large lecture-format course on the impact of fungi on human civilization.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504041 2026-09-01T15:43:21-04:00 2026-09-01T15:43:22-04:00 E-resources Accounting Specialist <div>The E-resources Accounting Specialist assists with the acquisition, administration, and maintenance of the Libraries’ electronic and continuing resources, the continuity of access and discoverability of the Libraries' licensed and open access resources, as well as invoice processing, maintenance of statistics, account reconciliation, and works with various platforms to track financial data that informs collection management decisions. This position is a member of the Collections department, reporting to the Assistant Director of Collections for Acquisitions and Licensing and working at the direction of the Library Collections Professional and the Electronic and Continuing Resources Librarian.</div> Libraries-Acquisitions Serials https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500310 2026-08-14T17:53:53-04:00 2026-08-14T17:53:53-04:00 Academic Advisor II - Explore <div>This position is for an academic advisor who will serve in the Exploratory Center working with students who are Undecided/Exploring majors, primarily. As needed, they may also assist the office with a roster of Intended Business or Grady majors, particularly during New Student Orientation. This advisor will be responsible for advising and maintaining regular contact with a roster of students during the major exploration process, guiding them through use of appropriate resources and programs, responding to student communications, and referring to other campus units. This position will also be required to perform a combination of the following duties, based on the business needs of the office: office administrative tasks; office representation and liaison work with campus partners; advisor training and professional development leadership; and supplemental administrative tasks for Orientation. Because this individual will interact directly with Exploratory Center employees, advisees, and campus partners, they must demonstrate an appreciation for and a commitment to accommodating a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences in the course of their daily work. They must demonstrate a commitment to cultural competence and ongoing professional development in this area.</div> VPI-Advising Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478410 2026-04-22T17:19:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:48-04:00 MLC Classroom Support Student Worker VPI-Teaching & Learning Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479715 2026-04-28T10:33:18-04:00 2026-04-28T10:33:18-04:00 Client Care Team - Referral Coordinator Floater <div>Small Animal Client Services Floater is a dynamic role designed to support the seamless flow of the Small Animal Hospital Specialty Services. This position acts as the primary link between clients, referring veterinarians, and clinical staff. The successful candidate will remain highly adaptable, rotating among the admissions desk and client care team coordinator seats, managing referrals and appointments, and ensuring consistent, high-quality service across all small-animal departments. The “Floater” designation requires the ability to move between roles as daily needs dictate.</div> VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478651 2026-04-22T17:36:46-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:47-04:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>The Ye lab at the University of Georgia is a Human Genetics lab with a special interest in Human Nutrition. We strive to identify genetic variants that make each one of us unique in our nutritional requirements and risks of metabolic diseases. We aim for a future of Personalized Nutrition. Our research employs computational and experimental methodologies from Evolutionary and Quantitative Genomics, Molecular Genetics, and Nutritional Sciences. We are searching for a postdoc to work at the interface of Population Genetics and Quantitative Genetics, to study the role of Gene-Environment Interactions in human evolution and human complex traits. The postdoc will perform both empirical data analysis (ancient and modern DNA; large biobanks) and theoretical modeling.</div> Franklin-Genetics https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496646 2026-07-29T10:28:29-04:00 2026-07-29T10:28:30-04:00 Senior Content Producer <div>The Senior Content Producer helps WUGA-FM tell the stories that matter to the Athens and Northeast Georgia community and reports to the News Director. This position will be responsible for editorial and production planning for daily and weekly news programs, including topic selection, story ideas, and guest selection and booking. This position will develop a range of news, information, and entertainment consistent with the mission of public radio, the University of Georgia, and Georgia Public Broadcasting and work with full-time and part-time radio staff to assist in recording and editing and to ensure that the final product meets editorial, production, and technical standards. The Senior Content Producer will also produce stories for air in other parts of WUGA’s schedule and on daily newscasts, as well as initiate and maintain productive and mutually beneficial relationships with units at the University, Georgia Public Broadcasting, and communities within the station’s service area. The incumbent will work closely with the News Director and collaborate with the Program Director to identify opportunities to expand the reach, scope, and variety of WUGA News through compelling journalism, on-air hosting, special projects, and field reporting as needed.<br><br></div> MarComm-WUGA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477911 2026-04-21T18:05:04-04:00 2026-04-21T18:05:05-04:00 Cook I (Late Night) <div>Skilled cooking work in the preparation of food for a Dining Commons. Work involves the general preparation and cooking of a variety of foods, or the specialized preparation of meats and vegetables. Work involves responsibility of neatness and cleanliness in preparing food, and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Works under the supervision of a Cook 2 or Chef.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503608 2026-08-31T11:33:45-04:00 2026-08-31T11:33:46-04:00 Pharmacy Student Assistant <div>Support technical staff in ensuring quality veterinary care by assisting Pharmacy Technicians with compounding a wide variety of products for use in both client and research animals including chemotherapy drugs under the supervision of Pharmacists or Pharmacy Technician Supervisor. Utilizes extensive mathematical skills in the compounding and filling of prescriptions for wide variety of species and medications. Ensures proper disposal of expired medications, accurate billing to patient/client accounts, and filling the Cubex automated controlled medication supply machine.</div> VetMed-VTH Pharmacy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499802 2026-08-13T11:24:46-04:00 2026-08-13T11:24:47-04:00 FOOD SERVICE WORKER I This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals. Auxiliary Snelling https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478387 2026-04-22T17:16:39-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:39-04:00 Eastern Wild Turkey Research Technician <div>We are seeking one (1) technician to assist with a project focusing on wild turkey reproductive ecology. The project will specifically be focusing on chronology of turkey gobbling, turkey movements, space use, nesting, and brood rearing in relationship to hunting on the landscape. The role of the technician will be assisting with nest monitoring, radio-telemetry, habitat sampling, acoustic surveying, and data recording and processing. In order to accomplish these tasks, the technician will work both independently and as part of a small crew. The research will be conducted on the Savannah River Site in Aiken, South Carolina.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478824 2026-04-22T17:50:11-04:00 2026-06-12T15:21:22-04:00 class checker - Student <div>As an Athletics Class Checker, your duties will include the following:<br>• Monitoring the daily attendance and promptness of a wide range group of student-athletes.<br>• Communicating regularly with Athletics Staff Members to ensure accountability.<br>• Logging detailed reports to inform Academic Counselors/Staff of daily occurrences.</div> Athletics-Student Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502088 2026-08-24T10:44:26-04:00 2026-08-24T10:44:26-04:00 Agricultural Specialist- Poultry Research Complex <div>This incumbent is responsible for taking a hands-on role in operating and maintaining the UGA Poultry Research Complex; providing care for research animals in accordance with UGA Animal Use and Care guidelines; preparing animal rooms for experiments, assisting scientists with research as assigned, cleaning rooms, and facilities following experiments; providing maintenance and repair of facilities and grounds; and other duties as assigned by the Poultry Research Complex Manager.</div> CAES-Poultry Science https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478509 2026-04-22T17:24:26-04:00 2026-06-01T15:43:13-04:00 Part Time Grounds Keeper - Rock Eagle - Temporary <div>&nbsp;Job duties will include, but are not limited to:<br>Mowing grass with zero turn, stand up, walk-behind and push-type lawnmowers. Weed-eating turf edges, large areas, hillsides, and lake edges. Edging curbs, roads, sidewalks, and other areas. Trimming trees, bushes, hedges, and other landscaped areas. Picking up, grinding limbs, and working with a Brush Bandit chipper, or similar equipment. Hand stacking rip-rap stone and other type landscaping rock. Spreading pine straw, wheat straw, and grass seed. Lining and painting football fields. Knowledge of proper use of chainsaws and other related equipment. Will climb onto roofs (using a ladder) to blow off roofs and clean gutters on all buildings. Spraying chemicals to control weeds, insects, etc. Assist with center trash collection, building set up and breakdowns as needed.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487964 2026-06-10T14:17:58-04:00 2026-06-10T14:17:59-04:00 Director of Faculty and Leadership Development in Faculty Affairs <div>The Director of Faculty and Leadership Development in Faculty Affairs supports the professional development of faculty and administrators while advancing institution-wide initiatives and policies. The position reports to the Vice Provost for Academic and Community Engagement. The role includes managing personnel and budgets within the Faculty and Leadership Development area. The Director is responsible for researching, designing, delivering, and assessing development programs for faculty and academic leaders. These programs aim to enhance excellence at the University of Georgia. Current focus areas include faculty success planning, mentoring, leadership development, productivity, and engagement.<br><br>The Director also evaluates program effectiveness and assesses development needs across the institution. Collaboration with faculty and administrators is a key component of the role. The position involves working with multiple campus units, such as the Graduate School and the Center for Teaching and Learning. Additionally, the Director serves as a primary faculty support resource and develops communications for various audiences through email, web, and social media channels.<br><br>This is a non-tenure track or tenured faculty position. Candidates with academic credentials and qualifications that merit a tenured faculty appointment will be considered for tenure, which would be held within the appropriate academic department independently of their service as director. Internal applicants will retain their current rank and tenure status. External applicants and current staff with a master's degree who do not qualify for tenure on appointment will be appointed as a non-tenure track administrative faculty member.</div> SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478607 2026-04-22T17:32:46-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:47-04:00 Bus Operator (Student) <div>Safe operation of buses on campus routes and occasional charters. Complete paperwork associated with assignments. Follow written and verbal instructions as required by supervisory personnel. Occasional bus washing and other non-driving tasks are required from time to time. Applicants must submit to drug and alcohol testing as required by the US Department of Transportation.</div> Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494794 2026-07-21T11:26:47-04:00 2026-07-21T11:26:48-04:00 FOOD SERVICE WORKER I (Partial Year) <div><strong>This is a benefits eligible, partial year position 9-11 months of each year. The selected candidate will be expected to sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.<br></strong><br></div><div>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477810 2026-04-21T17:50:39-04:00 2026-04-21T17:50:39-04:00 Research Professional II <div>The position is responsible for conducting experimental duties in plant pathology, molecular biology, bioinformatics and metabolomics, and coordinating the daily operations of the laboratory, including but not limited to supervising laboratory safety compliance, maintaining instruments/equipment, and ordering supplies. Additional duties include training, supervising and assisting undergraduate and graduate students, laboratory assistants and visiting scholars in the performance of field and laboratory research tasks, as well as assisting the supervisor in administrative tasks.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478731 2026-04-22T17:40:51-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:51-04:00 Lead Instructor-Summer Academy at UGA (multiple subjects) <div>Summer Academy Lead Instructors are responsible for developing and leading academic-focused youth programs. Lead Instructors will develop an academically focused and engaging course in the subject area that will both teach and motivate the youth attending the program. They will coordinate in advance with the assistant instructor to ensure understanding of the course curriculum and the areas that the assistant instructor can lead. Instructors will comply with all guidelines of program staff, including providing requested planning information like room set up, supplies, and field trip support requests. During camp, they will teach the course with the aid of the assistant instructor; keeping the program staff informed of any issues with the courses or with students. Instructors will ensure proper supervision of students at all times in the classroom, moving between locations, and on field trips. All instructors must comply with UGA Programs and Activities Serving Minors policy requirements.<br>They will work up to 30 hours per week, typically for 1 work week.<br><br>Subjects Seeking Lead Instructors:<br>• Forensic Science: June 8-12<br>• Legal Studies: June 8-12<br>• Creative Writing (Plot &amp; Structure): June 8-12<br>• Creative Writing (Worldbuilding): June 22-26<br>• Creative Writing (2 topics): July 13-17</div><div>• Artificial Intelligence &amp; Coding: July 13-17<br>• Visual Storytelling &amp; Photojournalism: July 13-17</div> PSO-Cont Ed-GC Cont Education https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498068 2026-08-05T10:47:12-04:00 2026-08-05T10:47:12-04:00 PLUMBER <div>This is manual work at the journeyman level in the installation, maintenance, and repair of plumbing and heating systems. Work involves performance of skilled plumbing tasks in maintaining, repairing, and servicing a variety of fixtures and equipment. Routine maintenance, service, and repair work is performed independently. Assignments are normally received orally or through written work orders. Work is inspected on completion for conformity to instructions and quality of work.</div> FMD-O&M-Plumbing Shop https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478107 2026-04-21T18:34:24-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:25-04:00 Decatur County Ag & Natural Resources Agent <div>This area is known for its intense, high-quality agricultural production mostly due to the dedication and expertise of the growers and advisors available. This position will provide educational programming in the Agriculture and Natural Resources (ANR) area in Decatur County providing educational opportunities in production agriculture, horticulture, and natural resources to a wide variety of audiences utilizing multiple teaching methods. This position involves frequent night meetings, some weekend work, and attendance at out-of-county meetings. A valid driver’s license and access to a reliable private vehicle for official travel are needed. Reimbursement for business travel will be provided. Transportation of others, including 4-H youth and adult clientele, is also a common function of the job. 4-H competitions, overnight camps, and other events are conducted at district and state levels and necessitate travel and transport of participants.<br><br>http://extension.uga.edu/about/join/careers.cfm</div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504272 2026-09-03T08:18:44-04:00 2026-09-03T08:18:45-04:00 Photojournalist Assistant <div>The student photojournalist will work in the Office of Marketing and Communications (OMC) within the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences (CAES), supporting the creation of visual content that enhances storytelling across digital and print platforms. This position offers the opportunity to capture and curate engaging photography, assist with content repurposing and visual adaptations of previously published stories, and collaborate with writers and designers to develop multi-format stories for CAES Almanac, social media, the CAES website and other UGA communication platforms.<br><br></div><div>This role is ideal for a student interested in documentary-style photography, visual journalism, portraiture and strategic communication. The student photojournalist will also be trained in professional outreach and logistical planning to schedule shoots and interviews with faculty, staff and students across departments.<br><br>The ideal candidate is available to work 15 hours per week. Hours are flexible and can be structured around the student’s class schedule. The intern will report jointly to two members of the CAES OMC team for mentorship and supervision.<br><br><br></div> CAES-Comm & Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500790 2026-08-18T11:13:36-04:00 2026-08-18T11:13:37-04:00 Georgia 4-H Foundation - Executive Director <div>The Georgia 4-H Foundation Executive Director serves as both the manager and major fundraising/chief development officer of the Georgia 4-H Foundation. The position works under the direct supervision of the State 4-H Leader and the Georgia 4-H Foundation Board of Trustees and is responsible for providing strategy, leadership, direction, coordination, and management of all levels of giving for the Foundation, including major ($25K+), principal ($1M+), and capital gifts, annual funds, stewardship, special events, endowments, and estate designations, as well supervise the organization’s development and administrative staff. The Executive Director serves as the liaison between Georgia 4-H and University Development. This position also coordinates management and engagement of a Board of Trustees. To fulfill the unit’s mission and implement its programs and initiatives, the Executive Director works closely with the State 4-H Leader, the Georgia 4-H Foundation Board of Trustees executive committee, and the State 4-H faculty to develop fundraising priorities, create a development plan, implement the plan, and oversee and solicit all giving that supports the plan. In this role, the employee is responsible for communication, collaboration, and coordination between Georgia 4-H and the University Development office, as well as creating productive partnerships with all other UGA school, college, and unit fundraising programs.<br>The Executive Director is a member of the Georgia 4-H State Staff and is expected to attend monthly staff meetings, and the annual State Congress week. The Executive Director will also participate in any programmatic activity that also includes donor facing opportunities.</div> CAES-State 4-H https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478439 2026-04-22T17:20:36-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:37-04:00 Student Assistant - Continuing Ed Griffin <div>Room set-up and room clean up; office support such as copying, faxing, making conference disks, word-processing; managing storage space; supporting transportation need in our workshops; providing A-V support in some cases; and supporting our catering operation.<br><br></div> CAES-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483041 2026-05-14T08:23:26-04:00 2026-05-14T08:23:26-04:00 Putnam County Administrative Assistant <div>This vital position coordinates functions and operations with Extension staff and/or Program Assistants. It works cooperatively with all Agents and is administratively responsible to the County Extension Coordinator and District Extension Director. The County Extension Administrative Assistant will assist in managing the many resources offered by a county office. Coordinates and distributes time as needed for the satisfactory delivery of the county program.</div> CAES-Northeast District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478557 2026-04-22T17:29:29-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:30-04:00 Van Operator (Student) Transport passengers with registered disabilities in an accessible van to and from various campus locations in accordance with applicable laws and department procedures. Assist passengers entering and exiting the vehicle as necessary. Inspect vehicle before, during, and after shift to ensure vehicle is in proper operating condition. Complete necessary paperwork, including time sheets and vehicle condition reports. Operates other vehicle equipment such as electronic AVL equipment and wheelchair ramps. Auxiliary Transit Opera https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/491788 2026-07-07T10:54:09-04:00 2026-07-07T10:54:09-04:00 Auxiliary Student Videographer / Photographer <div>The Student Videographer / Photographer will be responsible for filming, producing, and editing video and photographic content for publication on the Auxiliary Services department websites and social media networks.</div> Auxiliary Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504090 2026-09-01T17:46:11-04:00 2026-09-01T17:46:11-04:00 GNSN Postdoctoral Research Assistant <div><strong><br>The State Botanical Garden of Georgia at the University of Georgia is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate to lead conservation genetics research supporting native plant restoration across the southeastern United States. This position is funded through a U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service Cooperative Agreement focused on strengthening the scientific foundation of native seed sourcing and restoration decision-making. This role will also collaborate with the University of Georgia Herbarium faculty and staff to complete lab work and research.<br></strong><br></div><div><strong><br>This role focuses on advancing genetic tools to inform seed transfer guidance, restoration planning, and long-term ecosystem resilience. The Postdoctoral Research Associate will design and implement research that evaluates population-level genetic variability across native plant species, ground-truth Provisional Seed Transfer Zones, and supports science-based recommendations for responsible plant material movement.<br></strong><br></div><div><strong><br>The position integrates field sampling, molecular laboratory research, bioinformatics, and applied restoration science. The successful candidate will lead publication development, mentor students, collaborate with federal and state partners, and contribute to grant development that expands the conservation genetics program. This role provides an opportunity to shape regional and national restoration strategies by ensuring genetically appropriate native plant materials are used in ecological recovery efforts.<br></strong><br></div> PSO-State Botanic Garden of GA https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500335 2026-08-17T08:30:04-04:00 2026-08-17T08:30:04-04:00 CSS- Student Associate- Shay 4 <div>The University of Georgia’s Grains Team is seeking candidates to provide part-time technical assistance for field research activities. Responsibilities include assisting with the establishment and management of field experiments, planting, spraying, harvesting crops, collecting and processing research data, and supporting other research operations as needed. This position involves assisting with small-plot and on-farm research trials at various locations throughout the state.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478412 2026-04-22T17:19:50-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:51-04:00 Student Assistant <div>This position will work with the Fountain Lab at the UGA Griffin Campus to assist in performing mycotoxin and postharvest pathogen research. The candidate will help with planting, maintenance, harvesting, sample collection, and processing for field and greenhouse-based corn and peanut experiments in Griffin and South Georgia. The candidate will also help with normal laboratory operations including cleaning, upkeep, media preparation, and basic lab procedures. The candidate will also be encouraged to develop an independent research project.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/479833 2026-04-28T14:53:42-04:00 2026-04-28T14:53:43-04:00 Part-time Food Service Worker - Rock Eagle <div>Work involves preparing and serving food and cleaning food service areas. Employees work under direct supervision, follow written and/or oral procedures and practices. Employee will implement these procedures, methods, and activities developed by others.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478531 2026-04-22T17:25:47-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:47-04:00 Federal Work Study - Lab Assistants <div>The Shamblin lab seeks laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample processing and DNA extractions for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate and undergraduate students with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, skin, fin clip, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing of fish and wildlife species of conservation concern.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490361 2026-06-26T14:12:29-04:00 2026-06-26T14:12:29-04:00 Client Care Team - Referral Coordinator First point of contact for veterinarians calling in referrals to the Veterinary Teaching Hospital (VTH). Ensures accurate and detailed medical history of each referred patient available to VTH specialists while operating a busy telephone system. Utilizes advanced knowledge of veterinary terminology to communicate referring veterinary diagnosis and coordinate consultation. Decisions are based upon VTH policies and practices. VetMed-VTH Admin Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478628 2026-04-22T17:33:53-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:54-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate AD - Mitchum 1 & 2 <div>This position seeks to understand the molecular basis of plant-nematode interactions, with an emphasis in nematode effector biology.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495602 2026-07-24T00:03:12-04:00 2026-07-24T00:03:13-04:00 Assistant Teacher <div>The assistant teacher works with the other members of the teaching team to create a positive, productive, professional environment for the children within their classroom. The responsibilities are determined by the job description and needs of the classroom, as identified by the lead teacher and/or administrators.</div> FACS-Child & Family Devel Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477852 2026-04-21T17:59:54-04:00 2026-04-21T17:59:55-04:00 Veterinary Assistant- SA 24/7 Care <div>This position will rovide animal care via feed, water, walk, transport, restrain, groom. Stocking of area and supplies, maintain clinical records, assure facility cleanliness., establish and maintain effective working relationships, and assist senior veterinary staff with animal care.</div> VetMed-VTH Small Animal Emerg https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503146 2026-08-27T12:13:30-04:00 2026-08-27T12:13:30-04:00 Annual Giving Coordinator <div>This position serves as the annual giving liaison for 3-4 assigned schools, colleges, and units and is responsible for developing and executing unit-specific and central annual giving strategies, providing regular reporting on key performance metrics, and ensuring best practices are utilized in all annual giving initiatives. This position plans and executes a full calendar of central direct mail campaigns annually, spanning large-scale institutional appeals and smaller, targeted solicitations. This role assists with special campaigns throughout the year that focus on increasing UGA’s alumni participation rate. This position is also responsible for managing the annual giving matching gift program including software management, reporting and analytics, and future state recommendations.</div> DAR-Annual Giving https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499207 2026-08-11T09:48:27-04:00 2026-08-11T09:48:27-04:00 Executive Director of the Georgia Center for Developmental Science <div><strong><em>This is an internal search restricted to current University of Georgia College of Family and Consumer Sciences faculty who hold tenure at the rank of Professor.</em></strong><br><br>The University of Georgia (UGA) invites applications and nominations for the position of Executive Director of the Georgia Center for Developmental Science (GCDS) in the College of Family and Consumer Sciences The Executive Director provides scientific and administrative leadership for a university-wide research hub advancing interdisciplinary inquiry, training, and community partnerships focused on child and adolescent development, behavioral health, and resilience. The Executive Director is responsible for setting strategic vision, building and sustaining the Center’s extramural funding portfolio, developing shared scientific infrastructure (including grant development, data science, neuroimaging, and biobehavioral resources), cultivating cross-college and inter-institutional collaborations, translating science into community and donor-facing partnerships, mentoring the next generation of developmental scientists, and elevating the visibility of GCDS on the UGA campus, throughout the state of Georgia, nationally, and internationally.</div> FACS-Fam & Cons Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478370 2026-04-22T17:16:08-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:09-04:00 Post-Doctoral Research Associate in Food Safety Virology <div>This post-doctoral research associate will conduct virology research intended to investigate ecology of foodborne viruses on produce and in Ag. water. Participate in the design, implementation, and evaluation of experiments to study foodborne viruses. Coordinate the work of students on the project and oversee final results. Analyze and evaluate research results. Prepare reports, presentations and manuscripts on the project.&nbsp;</div> CAES-Food Safety Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478799 2026-04-22T17:46:34-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:35-04:00 Temporary Field/Lab Assistant - Mergoum <div>Help with the planting and harvesting of the wheat breeding nursery in North and South Georgia. Will also help with the upkeep of six greenhouses and preparing of seed to be replanted in field. Overnight trips and working 8 hours in the heat of the summer. Lift 30lbs.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504621 2026-09-04T13:20:02-04:00 2026-09-04T13:20:02-04:00 Professor, Director of Choral Activities <div>The Hugh Hodgson School of Music at the University of Georgia (UGA) seeks a dynamic senior faculty member to contribute to teaching and creative activities in choral music, and leadership of the Choral Activities area as Director. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027.<br><br>Responsibilities:</div><ul><li>Serve as Artistic Director and primary conductor of the UGA Hodgson Singers, the School’s flagship choral ensemble, as well as the UGA Repertory Singers, the graduate recital choir, which functions both as a performance ensemble and as a master-class environment for graduate conducting students.</li><li>Provide leadership for the choral area at the University of Georgia’s Hugh Hodgson School of Music, which currently includes seven ensembles.&nbsp;</li><li>Work closely with other faculty, staff, and graduate student assistants in building upon one of the strongest choral traditions in the country.</li><li>Lead and develop the graduate MM and DMA programs in choral conducting through the instruction of conducting, literature, pedagogy, and/or related fields.&nbsp;</li><li>Recruit, advise, and mentor graduate conducting students.&nbsp;</li><li>Supervise graduate research and performances including capstone projects and research papers.</li><li>Engage with appropriate third parties in fulfillment of the university’s outreach mission, including:<ul><li>Interaction with educators and students in the state and region through educational outreach and recruitment activities such as on-campus student festivals and events, school visits, and conference presentations and performances.</li><li>Foster and engage in collaborations across the Hugh Hodgson School of Music, Franklin College, the University, and the broader professional and artistic community.</li></ul></li><li>Maintain and develop an active national/international reputation as a conductor, clinician, and pedagogue.</li><li>Join colleagues in advancing and refining the Hodgson School’s vision for inclusive and comprehensive music education in the 21st century.</li><li>Other duties and committee work as assigned.<br><br></li></ul> Franklin-School of Music https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501379 2026-08-19T15:49:44-04:00 2026-08-19T15:49:45-04:00 Limited Term Repository (Off-site) Stacks Specialist <div>The Repository Stacks Specialist is a temporary, 18-month position responsible to the Repository Coordinator for assisting with the general operations of the Library’s remote storage facility (Repository). This includes shelving and accessioning incoming material, pulling items for circulation, and scanning items for electronic delivery. In addition, the Stacks Specialist assists with the training and supervision of part-time student assistants.<br><br></div><div>Work will be performed in a warehouse environment with rolling staircases, ladders, pallet jacks, and scissor lifts. Work will primarily take place in the UGA Libraries off-campus storage facility known as the Repository, located in Athens, GA at the intersections of Whitehall Road and Milledge Avenue.<br><br><strong>This position has a limited term appointment which is expected to end 18 months after start date. The position may be extended beyond the initial term, contingent upon continued funding.&nbsp;</strong></div><div><br></div> Libraries-Special Collections https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478491 2026-04-22T17:23:54-04:00 2026-04-22T17:23:54-04:00 Graduate Research Assistant - PhD 48.9% (Parrott) Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486406 2026-06-02T10:05:08-04:00 2026-06-02T10:05:09-04:00 Director of the UGA Center for Continuing Education & Hotel <div>The University of Georgia (UGA) invites applications for the position of director of the University of Georgia Center for Continuing Education &amp; Hotel (Georgia Center). The University of Georgia, a land-grant and sea-grant institution, is an international leader in outreach programming and statewide engagement. As part of UGA’s outreach mission, the division of Public Service and Outreach (PSO) works to help create jobs and prosperity, develop the state’s leaders, and solve critical statewide challenges. More information can be found at: <a href=\"http://www.outreach.uga.edu\"><strong>www.outreach.uga.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div><strong>Position Overview</strong></div><div>The Director provides overall leadership of the Georgia Center, including administrative, budgetary, and programmatic operations, and supervision of faculty and staff. The Director will provide strategic leadership to advance the Georgia Center as a gateway to the University and as a hub for continuing and adult education. This includes leading a strategic vision that strengthens the Georgia Center’s role in lifelong learning, hospitality, and public engagement. The position reports to the Vice President for Public Service and Outreach and is a member of PSO’s senior leadership team.<br><br></div><div>The Director will also lead two complementary areas of focus: (1) advancing continuing education and lifelong learning opportunities for the state through conferences and non-credit courses, and (2) expanding student experiential learning with an academic partner: College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences’ Hospitality and Food Industry Management program. The successful candidate will work with the partner to grow student-focused programs and experiential learning opportunities, while also developing a clear vision for extending continuing education and adult learning through external partnerships that support statewide impact and align with the University’s public service mission.<br><br></div><div>This position requires a high level of hospitality leadership that is foundational to the success of the Georgia Center. The Director is responsible for ensuring excellence in service across operations and the learning environment, and for leading the development and expansion of student experiential learning grounded in real-world, service-oriented experiences. As a visible representative of both the Georgia Center and the University of Georgia, the Director is expected to uphold and advance a standard of service that reflects positively on the institution’s reputation and brand.<br><br></div><div>This is an administrative, non-tenure track <a href=\"https://outreach.uga.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Guidelines-for-Appointment-and-Promotion.pdf\"><strong>Senior Public Service Associate faculty appointment.</strong></a></div> UHR-HR Search Services https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478578 2026-04-22T17:30:08-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:08-04:00 Student Assistant Franklin-Psychology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493502 2026-07-15T09:25:31-04:00 2026-07-15T09:25:32-04:00 Sous-Chef, Rock Eagle 4-H Center <div>This position will be a highly skilled food preparation worker who will assist the chef in the preparation of a wide variety of meats, fish, starches, casseroles, breads, vegetables and desserts. A person in this position will work with very limited supervision and may lead other employees to complete assigned tasks. Knowledge and skills in food quality, food safety and food preparation. Work is performed under the immediate direction of the Executive Chef. This incumbent may also be responsible for administrative and supervisory work in food service management at the Rock Eagle Dining Hall in a Manager On Duty capacity. This position will work primarily evenings as the PM Sous Chef. There will be occasions when days are required as well as weekends and holidays.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477744 2026-04-21T17:31:15-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:16-04:00 FOOD SERVICE WORKER II This is manual and semi-skilled work in the performance of advanced food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves limited supervision over subordinate food service workers engaged in serving foods and cleaning facilities for limited food preparation tasks and for related food service duties that are more advanced and responsible than the duties of Food Service Worker I. Employees of this class apply skills and knowledge that are acquired through experience. Duties include instructing subordinate food service workers in dining hall techniques and methods; for maintaining high standards of cleanliness; and for assuring patrons are served in a courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained. Auxiliary Bolton https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478702 2026-04-22T17:39:32-04:00 2026-04-22T17:39:33-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant - Sun <div>Building robotic system for manufacturing applications or building 3D design and printing for ethical manufacturing.</div> ENGR-Env Civil Agr & Mech https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497474 2026-08-03T11:28:32-04:00 2026-08-03T11:28:33-04:00 Conservation Genetics Student Lab Assistant <div>The Shamblin lab seeks student laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample curation and processing, DNA extractions, and data calling for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate students, the lab manager, and PI with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, feather, skin, fin clips, eDNA filter, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing for fish and wildlife species to inform conservation and management. This position will also assist the PI with data calling with microsatellite and sequencing projects. Sample archiving and general laboratory maintenance are expected. Candidates available for a minimum of 10 hours weekly are preferred.</div> Warnell-Research https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478009 2026-04-21T18:25:42-04:00 2026-04-21T18:25:43-04:00 Associate or Full Professor <div>The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time tenure-track or tenured position at the level of Associate or Full Professor.&nbsp;<br><br>We seek highly motivated individuals who will:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Deliver high-quality education at the undergraduate and graduate levels.&nbsp;</li><li>Establish and maintain innovative, extramurally funded research programs that complement the Department’s existing strengths.&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br><strong>Research Areas of Interest</strong>&nbsp;</div><div>Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>AI/computational drug discovery&nbsp;</li><li>Computational or virtual drug screening&nbsp;</li><li>Chemical biology&nbsp;</li><li>Pharmacology&nbsp;</li><li>Immunology&nbsp;</li><li>Cancer biology&nbsp;</li><li>Drug formulation or drug delivery&nbsp;</li><li>Medicinal chemistry&nbsp;</li><li>Toxicology&nbsp;</li><li>Systems biology&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br>The Department offers a competitive salary, excellent laboratory space, and a generous start-up package to support the successful candidate’s research program.&nbsp;</div> Pharmacy-Pharm & Biomed Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478559 2026-04-22T17:29:33-04:00 2026-04-22T17:29:34-04:00 Parking Operations Student Perform administrative and customer service related tasks for the Parking Services department to support in-office sales and operations. Apply standard business and customer service practices with professional guidance and supervision in a small business environment with advanced computer software, money handling procedures, and customer interactions on a large scale Auxiliary Parking Admin https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/492020 2026-07-08T12:36:19-04:00 2026-08-21T11:41:29-04:00 Central Sterile Associate <div>This position will assist in the Central Sterile unit of the Veterinary Teaching Hospital to provide medical/surgical supplies to clinical staff for surgeries and procedures that occur on a daily basis.</div> VetMed-VTH Central Supply https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478653 2026-04-22T17:36:51-04:00 2026-04-22T17:36:51-04:00 Temp Lab/Rsch Student 11- Dutta <div>Position will provide greenhouse assistance to include potting, inoculating and watering plants. Individual will assist in keeping greenhouse space neat, orderly and weed free. Individual will provide assistance with basic lab research as requested to include collecting plant samples, inoculating plant samples, setting up field studies including labeling and placing flags, stakes and markers. Individual will assist with basic lab protocols as requested and will be responsible for basic lab maintenance and chores including washing glassware, preparing simple solutions, preparing media, autoclaving supplies and waste, taking trash to dumpster, etc.to keep laboratory space neat, orderly and clean.</div> CAES-Plant Pathology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496680 2026-07-29T11:03:33-04:00 2026-07-29T11:03:33-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor <div>The Department of Management Information Systems in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for one full-time tenure-track faculty position at the assistant or associate professor level. The position will begin fall semester 2027, with an anticipated employment start date of August 1, 2027.</div> Terry-Mgmt Information Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477937 2026-04-21T18:06:51-04:00 2026-04-21T18:06:52-04:00 Cook I - Rock Eagle <div>This is skilled cooking work in preparing foods for a dining hall and event spaces, requiring experience in large-volume cooking. Work may involve either the general preparation or cooking of a variety of foods or the specialized preparation of meats or vegetables. Work involves responsibility for neatness and cleanliness in preparing food and for adherence to prescribed schedules. Assignments are received verbally and from prepared menus, but employees exercise independence in the actual food preparation and working processes. General supervision is received from a superior who checks the work by observation of the results obtained.</div> CAES-Rock Eagle 4-H Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503687 2026-08-31T13:53:23-04:00 2026-08-31T13:53:24-04:00 Food Service Worker I <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work involving a variety of food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for serving foods, cleaning facilities, and in preparing serving line meals.</div> Auxiliary Oglethorpe https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500103 2026-08-14T09:27:50-04:00 2026-08-14T09:30:59-04:00 Student Assistant - JPC REC <div>This position will assist with any and all farm duties. It will also be responsible for mowing the grounds around the center and other landscaping duties as needed. Will assist in haymaking duties as needed.</div> CAES-Campbell Rsch & Ed Ctr https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478391 2026-04-22T17:16:45-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:46-04:00 Laboratory Assistant - Habteselassie <div>The position involves soil and water sample collection and analysis. It involves working in laboratory, greenhouse and field. General laboratory and greenhouse upkeep and maintenance is also part of the job.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478826 2026-04-22T17:50:15-04:00 2026-04-22T17:50:16-04:00 Data collection assistant <div>Two data collection assistants are needed to collect survey data from Kennesaw Mountain National Battlefield Park (KEMO) visitors between January 2024 and December 2024. The job will require 8-16 hours of work per month, with no more than 4 hours per shift. Days are flexible and will be determined with feedback from Dr. Kyle Woosnam.<br><br>Employees will work at KEMO and be positioned at varying locations depending on day of week and time of day to intercept visitors and ask them to complete an on-site questionnaire that should take no more than 10-12 minutes to complete. Individual will be responsible for securing completed questionnaires that will be periodically collected by Dr. Kyle Woosnam or one of his doctoral research assistants.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502342 2026-08-24T16:29:20-04:00 2026-09-03T09:48:23-04:00 Program Director of Couple & Family Therapy - Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor <div><strong><em>Please note that this position is only available to current College of Family and Consumer Sciences faculty.<br></em></strong><br></div><div>The College of Family and Consumer Sciences invites internal applications for the position of Program Director for the Master’s Program in Couple and Family Therapy program with a rank of <strong>Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor</strong> as non-tenure track, fiscal year position with a 50% teaching, 40% administration, 5% research, and 5% service appointment to begin November 1, 2026. <strong><br></strong><br></div><div>The Program Director will provide strategic leadership, administration, and oversight for the Couple and Family Therapy (CFT) Program while maintaining an active teaching role within the Department of Human Development and Family Science (HDFS). The Program Director will advance the quality, visibility, and reputation of the CFT master's program at the national and international levels; ensure compliance with Commission on Accreditation for Marriage and Family Therapy Education (COAMFTE) standards; and oversee curriculum, clinical training, program operations, facilities, services, and continuous quality improvement efforts. The position will serve as the primary liaison among the CFT Program, HDFS, COAMFTE, clinical partners, professional organizations, and community stakeholders, supporting student recruitment, admissions, orientation, practica, internships, and other experiential learning opportunities. The Program Director will collaborate with faculty, staff, community partners, and affiliated clinical programs to promote student success, maintain accreditation, strengthen professional partnerships, and advance the mission and strategic goals of the CFT Program.<br><br></div><div>As a core faculty member in the Couple and Family Therapy (CFT) master's program, the successful candidate will teach four undergraduate and/or graduate courses each academic year and provide classroom instruction, academic advising, mentorship, and supervision of applied and clinical learning experiences for students in the bachelor's, dual-degree (BS/MS), and master's programs. Teaching assignments may include courses within the Behavioral Health Science minor and the CFT master's program. The Program Director will ensure that curriculum, clinical training, and student learning experiences align with COAMFTE accreditation standards and disciplinary best practices.<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide strategic leadership and administrative oversight for the Couple and Family Therapy (CFT) Program.</li><li>Ensure compliance with COAMFTE standards and accreditation requirements, including annual reporting, self-study preparation, site visit coordination, policy development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement efforts.</li><li>Submits COAMFTE accreditation materials and oversees all reports to COAMFTE.</li><li>Lead curriculum planning, review, and development in collaboration with CFT faculty to maintain program quality and accreditation compliance</li><li>Oversee the clinical training program, including clinical experiences, supervision requirements, student evaluations, training documentation, and related program operations.</li><li>Coordinate program operations, including course scheduling, faculty engagement, strategic planning activities, and program-related meetings and retreats.</li><li>Coordinate graduate student recruitment, admissions, orientation, funding opportunities, assistantship assignments, and student success initiatives.</li><li>Develop and maintain partnerships with community agencies, clinical training sites, professional organizations, and other stakeholders to support practicum, internship, and applied learning opportunities.</li><li>Collaborate with the Love and Money Center and other clinical partners to support student training, policy development, clinic operations, and clinical education experiences.</li><li>Oversee student records, graduate outcomes assessment, liability and insurance requirements, supervision documentation, and accreditation-related reporting.</li><li>Coordinate practicum and internship placement processes, including training agreements, site relationships, student progress monitoring, and communication with site supervisors.</li><li>Develop and submit budget proposal to the Department Head for accreditation maintenance, CFT credentials, and professional development activities for CFT students (e.g., guest speakers).</li><li>Build collaborative relationships across the University, professional associations, and community organizations, while mentoring graduate students and supporting faculty development.</li><li>Serve as a core faculty member by teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, providing academic advising, mentorship, and clinical supervision, supporting student development across degree programs, and contributing to teaching, scholarship, and service activities that advance the discipline.</li><li>Participate in department, college, and university governance</li><li>Engage in AAMFT and other relevant professional organizations.</li><li>Support and develop opportunities for research collaboration, grants, contracts, and other externally funded initiatives that advance the mission of the program and department.</li></ul> FACS-Human Devel & Family Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478511 2026-04-22T17:24:30-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:30-04:00 Olympic Sports Nutrition Non-Student Worker <div>The Server will assist the Culinary Service Manager in executing front of house service for Georgia Olympic Sports. The employee will assist with the day-to-day operation of FOH. This person will need to follow proper cleaning and sanitation procedures as well as multitask. They will also be responsible for stocking front of house, which includes but is not limited to various fueling stations, food service lines, and tabletops.</div> Athletics-Olympic Nutrition https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/487987 2026-06-10T15:21:00-04:00 2026-06-10T15:21:00-04:00 Culinary Server for Georgia Football - NON-Student Assistant <div>The server will assist the Culinary Service Manager in executing front of the house service for Georgia Football. This person will need to follow proper cleaning and sanitation procedures as well as multitask. They will also be responsible for stocking front of house, which includes but is not limited to various fueling stations, food service lines and tabletops.<br><br></div> Athletics-Football Nutrition https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478610 2026-04-22T17:32:52-04:00 2026-04-22T17:32:52-04:00 Student Assistant Must be able to work independently, have excellent problem-solving skills, and good interpersonal and customer service skills. Duties will include data entry, providing reception and phone coverage,providing duplicates, handling fax and email communications. Helping staff with mailings, event planning, room set-up and clean-up, and other duties as needed. CAES-Asst Dean-Griffin Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494818 2026-07-21T11:43:34-04:00 2026-07-21T11:43:35-04:00 Food Service Worker II <div>This is manual and semi-skilled work in the performance of advanced food service duties in dining hall or cash operations kitchens. Work involves responsibility for limited supervision over subordinate food service workers engaged in serving foods and cleaning facilities for limited food preparation tasks and for related food service duties that are more advanced and responsible than the duties of Food Service Worker I. Employees of this class apply limited skills and knowledge that are acquired through experience. Duties include responsibility for instructing subordinate food service workers in dining hall techniques and methods; for maintaining high standards of cleanliness; and for assuring that patrons are served in a pleasant and courteous manner. Assignments are received in the form of specific oral and written instructions and are reviewed by inspection and observation of results obtained.</div> Auxiliary West Campus Dining https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477818 2026-04-21T17:57:49-04:00 2026-04-21T17:57:50-04:00 Research Coordinator - CAN Lab <div>This research coordinator position is within the Clinical Affective Neuroscience lab directed by Dr. Gregory Strauss. The research coordinator will be involved in the clinical aspects of the research program and coordinating day-to-day responsibilities for the research protocol.</div> VPR-Owens Inst Behavioral Rsch https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478744 2026-04-22T17:42:02-04:00 2026-04-22T17:42:02-04:00 Temporary Technician (Lance) <div>This is a technician position at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory (SREL). The incumbent(s) is/are responsible for assisting current University of Georgia graduate students with field and laboratory research. The technician will be assisting with research on amphibians and/or snakes, which will require trapping and handling in the field, setting up and maintaining mesocosm experiments, data collection/entry, and assisting with data management. The technician will also assist take a lead role in establishing an upland snake camera trapping project.</div> VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498138 2026-08-05T12:49:48-04:00 2026-08-05T12:49:49-04:00 Limited- Term Lecturer <div>The Department of Advertising and Public Relations at the University of Georgia’s Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication invites applications for a limited-term (2-year) lecturer position to begin in January 2027. This is primarily a teaching position with a 4/4 teaching load (12 credit hours per semester). Limited-term lecturers may be renewed annually for a maximum of two years. Any request for reappointment beyond the second year requires pre-approval by the Provost.<br><br>The primary responsibility for this position will be teaching core courses in public relations, such as Public Relations Communications, Crisis Communication, and Introduction to Public Relations, with the possibility of teaching other undergraduate core courses as needed. This hire will teach multiple sections of Public Relations Communications, the department’s required writing course. The course teaches students to communicate effectively across multiple platforms with an array of stakeholders and audiences at the local, national, and international levels.</div> Grady-Advertising & PR https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478116 2026-04-21T18:34:45-04:00 2026-04-21T18:34:46-04:00 Pesticide Safety Education Program (PSEP) <div>The Department of Entomology (https://ent.uga.edu) at the University of Georgia (UGA) invites applications for a full-time Public Service Assistant/Associate (non-tenure-track position, 12-months) to direct the Pesticide Use and Safety Program (https://psep.uga.edu/) for the state of Georgia. The position is budgeted at 95% Service 5% Research.&nbsp;<br><br>The Department of Entomology seeks highly qualified candidates to build interdisciplinary educational programs in pesticide use and safety and worker protection standards. The core responsibility of this position is to develop and deliver interdisciplinary programs by: 1) Serving as the state Pesticide Safety Educational Program (PSEP) coordinator which may entail involvement in grants that support this educational and service mission of the Department, 2) Developing, delivering and overseeing pesticide education and safety training, 3) Serving as departmental liaison to provide college- wide Pesticide Safety Training for graduate research assistants and staff in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences, 4) Developing, delivering and overseeing Worker Protection Standards Training, 5) Work with county agents and specialists to develop worker protection training modules and videos.<br><br>The incumbent will be required to travel independently across the state; therefore, comfort and proficiency in driving are essential for successful job performance.&nbsp;</div> CAES-Entomology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504287 2026-09-03T09:26:52-04:00 2026-09-03T09:26:53-04:00 Tift County EFNEP Program Assistant <div>This position is based in Tift County. This position is responsible for paraprofessional work with County Extension Agents in a Food and Nutrition Education program for limited resource clients. Work is performed under general supervision.</div> CAES-Southwest District CES https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500808 2026-08-18T11:29:53-04:00 2026-08-18T11:29:54-04:00 Cotton Research Technician- Tifton Campus <div>The Research Technician position will be under the Assistant Dean’s Office based at the University of Georgia Tifton Campus. At appointment, the person in this position will assist with research that focuses on all aspects of cotton production and improvement. The primary focus of current research projects is to support cotton breeding, germplasm development, cultivar evaluation, and agronomic programs and initiatives. This position will also provide assistance, as needed, to other research areas related to cotton improvement and production. This role will involve collaborating with and assisting researchers, graduate students, technicians, and student workers to achieve program objectives and support ongoing research activities.<br><br></div><div>General responsibilities include supporting field, greenhouse, and laboratory research activities for the cotton breeding program through the establishment, management, and evaluation of research trials. Duties include coordinating crop production activities such as planting, irrigation, fertilization, pest management, harvesting, and seed processing; collecting and managing research data; operating and maintaining research equipment and vehicles; coordinating with farm personnel and research staff; and assisting with the implementation of breeding, genetics, and germplasm evaluation projects. The position also involves maintaining accurate records, supporting inventory and land management activities, and ensuring compliance with applicable safety and operational procedures while contributing to the overall success of the cotton research program.</div> CAES-Tifton Campus https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478443 2026-04-22T17:20:43-04:00 2026-04-22T17:20:43-04:00 Auxiliary Summer Ambassador <div>The Auxiliary Summer Ambassador serves as a key representative of UGA Auxiliary Services, helping to educate first-year students, transfer students, and their supporters of its services and programs. Through summer orientation sessions, ambassadors provide essential information on Auxiliary Services, including the Bookstore, Dining Services, Golf Course, Transportation and Parking Services, and Vending Services.<br><br></div><div>In this role, ambassadors actively engage with orientation visitors, support new students in their transition to campus life, and assist with major orientation events such as the Resource Fair, Orientation Breakfast and Lunch, Breakout Sessions, Presentation Sessions, and more. Additional responsibilities may include leading tours, participating in promotional events, capturing photos and videos, and contributing to digital communications efforts as needed.<br><br></div><div>This position offers a unique opportunity to develop leadership, public speaking, and customer service skills while making a meaningful impact on the UGA community.<br><br></div> Auxiliary Marketing https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/483353 2026-05-15T09:36:26-04:00 2026-05-15T09:36:27-04:00 Senior Safety and Compliance Officer <div>The Senior Safety and Compliance Officer (SSCO) is a position of leadership with the responsibility of staff supervision and oversees all related programs in the Office of Research Safety-Chemical (ORSC). The ORSC resides within the Office of Research Safety (ORS) and is lead by the Senior Safety and Compliance Officer.<br><br></div><div>Oversight of all related chemical and laboratory safety programs, such as but not limited to, Laboratory Inspections, Support of the Research Safety Committee, CampusOptics Operations, Chemical Inventory, Lab Closings and Openings, Emergency Response, Maintenance of the Chemical Safety Manual, Website Information, development/updates of Safety Policy/Guidance Documents as well as serving on a variety of working groups involving: Environmental Safety Division, Facilities Management, Office of Emergency Preparedness, Office of University Architects, Office of Research Integrity, Campus Police and Athens Clarke County Fire and Life Safety.<br><br></div> VPR-Research Safety https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478707 2026-04-22T17:40:10-04:00 2026-04-22T17:40:10-04:00 Temporary Lab/Research Assistant (5) - Devos Lab <div>Conduct research experiments in the field, greenhouse and laboratory. General lab duties.</div> CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497485 2026-08-03T12:15:28-04:00 2026-08-03T12:15:28-04:00 Repository (Off-site) Services Coordinator <div>The Repository (Off-site) Services Coordinator is responsible to the Libraries High Density Storage Manager for performing a variety of tasks necessary for the efficient operation of the Libraries’ Repository Building. The Repository is a high density storage facility located off campus in which more than 1.2 million items are shelved by size utilizing the storage inventory management database CaiaSoft. This position requires a high level of collaboration with other Libraries Units including User Services, Cataloging, Facilities, Records Management, and Collections. This position is responsible for accessioning incoming materials, circulation of pieces for patrons and document delivery, space assessment, and maintaining accurate records in CaiaSoft. The role collaborates with the User Services Unit to manage and troubleshoot issues with scanning equipment for electronic document delivery. The Repository Services Coordinator supervises and trains full-time, non-exempt staff and student assistants.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Work will be performed in a warehouse environment with rolling staircases, ladders, pallet jacks, and scissor lifts. Work will primarily take place in the UGA Libraries off-campus storage facility known as the Repository, located in Athens, GA at the intersections of Whitehall Road and Milledge Avenue. Depending on need, the position may occasionally work from other library buildings, namely the Special Collections Libraries.<br><br></div> Libraries-Special Collections https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478023 2026-04-21T18:26:51-04:00 2026-04-21T18:26:52-04:00 Staff Psychologist <div>CAPS Psychologists are essential members of the CAPS Professional Staff, providing primary, secondary, and tertiary services to eligible members of the UGA community within CAPS' scope of service. These services include group therapy, individual therapy, crisis interventions, outreach, training, and consultation. Clinicians can also provide internal or external referrals as needed for optimal care. Services are delivered in accordance with UHC and CAPS policies and procedures. Clinicians follow professional and organizational standards for care and documentation. All are valued team members who participate in performance improvement initiatives and engage in team activities, such as required meetings and committees. As a thriving and growing training site, CAPS relies on all staff to contribute to the growth and development of trainees.</div> UHC-Counseling & Psych Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504102 2026-09-02T08:35:10-04:00 2026-09-02T08:35:10-04:00 Senior Assistant Director for Learning Technologies <div>The University of Georgia (UGA) seeks an organized and engaged leader to join the Center for Teaching and Learning (CTL) as Senior Assistant Director for Learning Technologies. This individual will have experience managing and/or providing support for a learning management or similar system, with an eye on effective use of that system by a broad set of users. The incumbent will provide leadership to a large group of learning technology support personnel across campus, while contributing their specific expertise to the work of the CTL.<br><br>The Assistant Director for Learning Technologies reports to the Senior Associate Director for Teaching and Learning, collaborates with a variety of campus partners, and benefits from UGA's participation in a multi-institution Learning Technology Consortium.</div> VPI-Teaching & Learning Center https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500378 2026-08-17T09:42:26-04:00 2026-08-17T09:42:26-04:00 Development and Stewardship Coordinator <div>This individual will support the Development and Alumni Relations efforts of the College of Family and Consumer Sciences by coordinating comprehensive donor relations and stewardship initiatives. Reporting to the Director of Development, this individual manages donor acknowledgement processes, organizes stewardship events, and ensures donor intent is upheld through accurate record-keeping and detailed briefings. This employee also provides administrative support to the development team, oversees gift processing and financial transactions, and assists with planning and logistics for donor and alumni engagement activities. Strong organizational and communication skills are essential, as the role involves managing confidential information, event coordination, and frequent interaction with donors and college leadership.</div> FACS-Fam & Cons Sci https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478414 2026-04-22T17:19:54-04:00 2026-04-22T17:19:54-04:00 Student Laboratory Assistant <div>The Shamblin lab seeks laboratory assistants for wildlife and fisheries sample processing and DNA extractions for population genetic analyses. This position will assist graduate students and the lab manager with sample tracking, processing of blood, eggshell, skin, fin clips, and swab samples, and DNA extractions for genotyping and sequencing for fish and wildlife species of conservation concern. This position will also assist in sample archiving and general laboratory maintenance.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480008 2026-04-29T10:51:12-04:00 2026-08-31T12:25:52-04:00 PGF Greenhouse Student Worker <div>Plant Growth Facilities student worker needed ASAP for weekday and weekend plant maintenance duties and other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Help with weekend watering duties in rotation with others.</div> CAES-Greenhouses https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478534 2026-04-22T17:25:52-04:00 2026-04-22T17:25:52-04:00 PMRC Forestry Technician II <div>Assist Plantation Management Research Cooperative (PMRC) field crew with a variety of different field work and data collection. This will entail measuring characteristics of pine and hardwood trees in the field, fertilization, and installation of research plots. Extensive travel required to visit research installations.</div> Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490464 2026-06-26T19:31:13-04:00 2026-06-26T19:31:14-04:00 Coordinator of Embedded Campus Programs/Psychologist (PY) <div>The Coordinator of Embedded Campus Programs is a senior clinician within Counseling and Psychiatric Services (CAPS) and reports to the Senior Director of CAPS and the Fontaine Center. This position is responsible for providing direct clinical services, including individual, group, and crisis counseling, as well as consultation, outreach, and supervision of trainees and staff. In addition to clinical responsibilities, this position leads the development and management of embedded counseling services in academic and campus units. This role collaborates with university stakeholders to enhance access to care, promote early intervention, and support student mental health and academic success. This is a 11-month position, off the month of June.<br><br></div><div><br></div> UHC-Counseling & Psych Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478630 2026-04-22T17:33:57-04:00 2026-04-22T17:33:57-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Schank Lab at the University of Georgia Department of Physiology and Pharmacology seeks to hire a postdoctoral associate. The position will be 100% research focused and the ideal candidate will have a Ph.D. in Neuroscience or a closely related field by the time that they begin this appointment. Research will focus on the comorbidity of alcoholism and depression, examining the neurokinin-1 receptor as a critical mediator of this relationship. Experimental techniques will include, but will not be limited to, behavioral pharmacology, molecular neuroscience, and neuroanatomical analysis. In addition to publishing scientific papers and presenting current data at scientific meetings, mentoring of junior graduate students and undergraduate researchers will also be a part of the expectations of this position.</div> VetMed-Physiology & Pharmacol https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495718 2026-07-24T14:07:05-04:00 2026-07-24T14:07:05-04:00 LA Financial Services/Auditing Coordinator <div>Serves as a member of the Vet Teaching large animal hospital’s front desk team with the primary responsibility being financial in nature. This includes cashiering, auditing, and taking deposits. This position ensures billing accuracy, verifies that all patient orders and product charges are complete, and helps support the Manager of Financial Services and the Director of Client Services in maintaining financial compliance and reporting accuracy. The coordinator assists with service contracts, estimates, and reconciliation of accounts while maintaining clear communication with clinicians, clients, and the hospital’s financial team. This position plays a vital role in capturing accurate revenue, maintaining transparency in billing, and supporting the financial health of the Veterinary Teaching Hospital’s Large Animal operations.</div> VetMed-VTH Patient Finan Srvcs https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477856 2026-04-21T18:00:03-04:00 2026-04-21T18:00:04-04:00 Farm Operations Professional I - Chavez (1) <div>This position directs the day-to-day management of farm operations, encompassing planting, irrigation, and harvesting to provide essential research support for the stone fruit and pecan research projects at the USDA-ARS Fruit and Tree Nut research Lab located at Byron, GA. The incumbent will manage the various phases of the research projects by performing largely independent farming duties within pecan and peach orchard settings. Key technical duties include the operation of farm tractors (greater than or equal to 50 horsepower) with associated implements/attachments and other heavy equipment, pesticide sprayer calibration and application, mowing, planting, and harvesting, and equipment repair. The role involves coordination and collaboration with faculty and project leaders on the design and implementation of field experiments. This position will modify and execute field experiments to maintain the uniform conditions of the research study. Specific technical management tasks involve scouting orchards for disease and pest issues, monitoring plant and soil nutrient levels, managing applications and pesticide planning, and maintaining and monitoring irrigation systems. The incumbent will be responsible for creating detailed schedules for planting, irrigation, spraying, fertilizing, pruning, training, and planting orchards. This position will assist in the hiring, training, and direct supervision of seasonal workers and staff, ensuring efficient execution of all farm and research-related tasks.<br><br>This is a grant-funded position with continued employment beyond 08/31/2026 based on the needs of the project as well as available funding and satisfactory job performance and progress.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503190 2026-08-27T14:29:14-04:00 2026-08-27T14:29:14-04:00 SPA - CONTRACT MANAGER <div>The SPA Contract Manager is responsible for the design and implementation of a cohesive and flexible contract team that supports faculty and research staff in their pursuit of externally funded sponsored projects. The Contract Manager will have excellent interpersonal and team building skills to promote a productive working relationship between our external sponsors, SPA staff and the research community. This position is ideal for an individual who has the vision and ability to encourage people to be innovative problem solvers while still maintain a highly compliant environment.</div> VPR-SPA Pre-Award https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/499394 2026-08-11T16:55:01-04:00 2026-08-11T16:55:02-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate- Sundaram <div><strong>The Sundaram Laboratory within the Precision One Health Initiative in the College of Veterinary Medicine at the University of Georgia is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to investigate the ecology of animal reservoirs and wildlife infectious disease outbreaks, and how these processes shape the emergence of zoonotic diseases in humans.</strong><br><br><strong>Research in the laboratory seeks to answer fundamental questions such as:</strong></div><ul><li>Which wildlife species serve as reservoirs for emerging pathogens?</li><li>What ecological conditions promote wildlife disease outbreaks?</li><li>Why do some wildlife outbreaks spill over into humans while others do not?</li><li>Can zoonotic outbreaks be anticipated from ecological patterns before human transmission occurs?</li></ul><div><br>The successful candidate will have the opportunity to pursue these and related questions while contributing to a growing research program integrating disease ecology, macroecology, epidemiology, machine learning, and spatial modeling. <br><br><strong>Research Responsibilities</strong>:The successful candidate will contribute to the following research activities: Develop and curate global databases of wildlife reservoirs, pathogen occurrence, and infectious disease outbreaks. Create, process, and integrate environmental, ecological, and socioeconomic GIS layers relevant to pathogen transmission and reservoir ecology. Conduct spatial, statistical, and machine learning analyses to identify ecological drivers of pathogen persistence, wildlife outbreaks, and zoonotic spillover. Develop predictive models linking wildlife disease dynamics with human zoonotic outbreaks. Publish findings in leading scientific journals.Projects span a broad range of pathogens and host systems, providing considerable flexibility for the successful candidate to pursue their own scientific interests while contributing to a larger research program focused on understanding and predicting zoonotic disease emergence. The position offers extensive opportunities to develop expertise in GIS, spatial statistics, machine learning, macroecology, and large-scale ecological databases. <br><br><strong>Funding is currently available for five years. The position will be based at the University of Georgia in Athens, Georgia, where the Principal Investigator is located.</strong> <br><br><strong>About the Laboratory:</strong> The successful candidate will be mentored by Dr. Mekala Sundaram, Assistant Professor in the Department of Infectious Diseases, College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, with a joint appointment at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory. Research in the Sundaram Laboratory integrates ecology, epidemiology, spatial analysis, machine learning, and statistical modeling to understand pathogen reservoirs, wildlife disease outbreaks, and zoonotic disease emergence. Current projects span wildlife reservoir forecasting, outbreak prediction, infectious disease ecology, and spatial epidemiology. More information can be found on mekalasundaram.com and on google scholar <a href=\"(https:/scholar.google.com/citations?user=dJm8OQQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en&amp;oi=ao).%20\"><strong>(https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=dJm8OQQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en&amp;oi=ao). </strong></a>Our laboratory values scientific curiosity, collaboration, independence, and mentorship. We strive to provide postdoctoral scholars with the freedom to develop their own research ideas while receiving close mentorship in publishing, grant writing, scientific communication, and career development. <br><br><strong>Application Instructions</strong></div><div>Applications should be submitted through the University of Georgia Jobs website.</div><div><strong>Applicants should upload:</strong></div><div>1. Cover letter (maximum two pages)</div><div>2. Curriculum vitae</div><div>3. Contact information for three professional references</div><div>4. One representative publication</div><div>Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div> VetMed-Precision One Health https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478372 2026-04-22T17:16:12-04:00 2026-04-22T17:16:12-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Resilient Infrastructure Systems <div>The College of Engineering wishes to appoint a Post-Doctoral Associate to work on grant funded research projects for a period of 1 year with additional employment dependent on the needs of the project. In this role they will work under the direct supervision of Dr. Brian Bledsoe, Professor and Director of the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS), at the College of Engineering’s School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural and Mechanical Engineering. The successful candidate will join a multidisciplinary team of scientists at the University of Georgia who are engaged in cooperative research projects in IRIS.</div> ENGR-Resilient Infrast Systems https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478803 2026-04-22T17:46:41-04:00 2026-04-22T17:46:42-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate - Song <div>The <a href=\"https://www.engr.uga.edu/\"><strong>College of Engineering at the University of Georgia</strong></a> is seeking to grow and diversify its programs through investments in researchers with expertise in advanced signal processing and artificial intelligence as it applies to the research and scholarship in Cyber-Physical Systems including but not limited to power and health systems.<br><br></div><div>The College invites applications for multiple postdoc positions in <strong>Advanced Signal Processing and Artificial Intelligence in Cyber-Physical Systems</strong>. These positions seek to identify highly qualified candidates with expertise at the intersection of data science and artificial intelligence with Cyber-Physical Systems and Security, in particular IoT, power and healthcare systems. We particularly look for strong candidates with fundamental and applied research on these two areas: (a) Advanced Signal Processing, (b) Deep Learning Interpretability and Domain Generalization. This position will be centered in the <strong>College of Engineering's </strong><a href=\"https://cps.uga.edu/\"><strong>Center for Cyber-Physical Systems (CCPS)</strong></a> and will be supervised by the Center Director.<br><br></div><div>This is a 1-year appointment (12 months).<br><br></div><div>This position will develop a vigorous, high-impact, externally funded research program; manage the CCPS’s outreach and proposal missions; effectively mentor undergraduate and graduate students; and contribute to the overall environment within the University.</div> ENGR-Electrical & Computer https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/504646 2026-09-04T14:32:00-04:00 2026-09-04T14:32:01-04:00 GLAD Program Coordinator <div>This position is responsible for coordinating the program and providing services for current/future partners and visiting scholars for the program. This position is also responsible for managing and monitoring program budget and expenses.</div> SPIA-Public Admin & Policy https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501516 2026-08-20T10:31:16-04:00 2026-08-20T10:31:16-04:00 Postdoc - van Rees <div>The postdoctoral associate will work under the mentorship of Dr. Charles van Rees (Odum School of Ecology) and in collaboration with graduate students in the WWL and other faculty at UGA on (1) spatial ecological research on the relationship between terrestrial birds, wetlands, and riparian habitats, and (2) biodiversity accounting for Nature-based Solutions projects. Specific responsibilities include (a) accessing, processing, managing, and analyzing large datasets including river flow data, remote sensing imagery, and spatially explicit biodiversity data (e.g., eBird, NEON), (b) testing ecological hypotheses through quantitative spatial analysis, including via machine learning and Bayesian approaches, (c) developing browser-based decision-making tools from existing frameworks and publicly available datasets, and (d) leveraging and training Artificial Intelligence (AI) agents to support decision-making tool functionality. The successful candidate will interface with collaborators at partner institutions, lead group meetings, and mentor one or more graduate students in each project capacity. The postdoc will present the project results at national conferences and will engage with other career development opportunities on and off campus, such as teaching and other professional development (grant management, etc.) workshops whenever suitable. In addition to a PhD degree in Ecology, Biology, or other related fields and a strong publication record, competitive candidates must have proven abilities to conduct statistical analyses using publicly available large datasets and to work as part of a scientific team. Especially competitive candidates will have familiarity either with the concepts of Nature-based Solutions, biodiversity accounting or net-gain, and the IUCN Global Standard or with the ecology of riparian birds, emergent aquatic insects, or river systems. Experience and proficiency in Python and/or Javascript is required, and experience working with and developing AI-enabled decision-making tools is welcome and encouraged. Strong written and verbal communication skills are required. The candidate will be based in the Water and Wildlife Lab in the Odum School of Ecology at the University of Georgia, and will also be an affiliate of the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems (IRIS; <a href=\"https://iris.uga.edu/)\"><strong>https://iris.uga.edu/)</strong></a> at UGA. The position will include retirement and health benefits. Interested candidates should apply online through UGA Jobs at <a href=\"https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/***\"><strong>https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/***</strong></a>. Any questions about the position should be directed to Dr. Charles van Rees (<a href=\"mailto:Charles.vanrees@uga.edu\"><strong>Charles.vanrees@uga.edu</strong></a>). Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The University of Georgia values diversity, and all qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. UGA is in Athens, GA, a vibrant mid-sized city renowned for its music scene, restaurants, and cultural opportunities</div> Ecology-Odum School of Ecology https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478494 2026-04-22T17:23:59-04:00 2026-04-22T17:24:00-04:00 Ruter Student Assistant #2 <div>The University of Georgia Department of Horticulture is seeking applicants as student workers with responsibility of operational management of field and container production of ornamental nursery crops along with supporting greenhouse and laboratory operations. Recruits will work to support an ornamental plant breeding program located at the Durham Horticulture Farm in Watkinsville, GA. The initial start date for this position is 3/1/2022 and continuation of the positions are contingent upon future funding.</div> CAES-Horticulture https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/486619 2026-06-02T16:42:43-04:00 2026-06-02T16:42:44-04:00 Business Operations Professional III <div>This Business Operations Professional serves as a strategic business partner to the Institute, providing comprehensive financial management of organizational accounts through a deep understanding of the Institute’s mission, operations, and the specific business needs of our divisions. This role applies advanced knowledge of financial accounting and public budgeting within the context of higher education and public service to support sound decision-making and operational effectiveness.<br><br>Acting as an internal consultant on fiscal affairs, financial management, and budget strategy, this position advises faculty, staff, and leadership on budgeting, budget management, and financial planning. Responsibilities include monitoring personal services and operating expenditures in relation to budgets and actuals, as well as overseeing sub-awards, contracts, and other outsourced services.<br><br>Using advanced financial expertise, the Business Operations Professional ensures all transactions comply with Institute of Government guidelines, University of Georgia policies, and Board of Regents policies. The role leads the development and production of complex financial reports and maintains accurate financial data and records within internal financial management systems (currently QuickBooks and related document management systems) to support transparency and informed decision-making.<br><br>The Business Operations Professional ensures proper administration of all related agreements, including compliance with applicable local, state, and federal laws. Regular financial analysis and reporting are conducted using internal systems, and accounts are routinely reconciled against university records to ensure accuracy and integrity.<br><br>Supporting business operations across multiple divisions, this position ensures financial coverage aligns with organizational priorities. The Business Operations Professional provides professional oversight of fiscal affairs, reinforces best practices in financial management, and serves as a trusted advisor and resource to faculty, staff, and Institute of Government leadership regarding financial operations and account management.<br><br>This position provides supervision of staff, including training, mentoring, and evaluating team members, as well as assigning and prioritizing work to ensure efficient operations and alignment with organizational goals, administrative requirements, and financial management standards.</div> PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478580 2026-04-22T17:30:12-04:00 2026-04-22T17:30:12-04:00 Temporary Lab/Summer Field Assistant To assist in breeding, harvesting, collecting data, and research. CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/493923 2026-07-16T12:15:05-04:00 2026-07-16T12:15:06-04:00 Student Veterinary Assistant - Large Animal <div>This position will assist the senior veterinary technicians and veterinary staff in the care of ill or injured client-owned animals brought to the Large Animal Hospital, with the goal of supporting their recovery.</div> VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477749 2026-04-21T17:31:26-04:00 2026-04-21T17:31:26-04:00 Bus Operator (Partial Year) <div><strong>This is a benefits eligible, partial year position. Each selected incumbent will sign a partial year agreement. Employees returning to work from designated partial-year leave periods are continued in the same position with no break in service and no change in the original hire date.</strong><br><br>Safe operation of buses on campus routes and occasional charters. Complete paperwork associated with assignments. Follow written and verbal instructions by supervisory personnel. Occasional bus washing and other non-driving tasks from time to time. Drug and alcohol testing by the US Department of Transportation.</div> Auxiliary Transit Opera"
