    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/502342": {
      "title": "University of Georgia | Program Director of Couple &amp; Family Therapy - Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Program Director of Couple &amp; Family Therapy - Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Program Director of Couple & Family Therapy - Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is an internal search restricted to current University of Georgia faculty. Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates should submit their materials by September 24, 2026. The application packet should include a cover letter detailing how the applicant’s credentials and experience meet the needs, responsibilities, and qualifications stated above; a current curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy for the CFT program; and contact information for three references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2777P Working Title Program Director of Couple & Family Therapy - Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor Department FACS-Human Devel & Family Sci About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The College of Family and Consumer Sciences, sixth largest at UGA in terms of undergraduate enrollment, is a student-centered college that emphasizes holistic student development and has grown rapidly in recent years to a current total enrollment of about 2,027 students. There are approximately 110 total faculty members in the College, where undergraduate and graduate degrees are offered in all areas of family and consumer sciences, as well as collaborative programs with other schools, colleges, centers, and institutes at the University. The College provides a comprehensive graduate program, offering master’s and doctoral degrees in all four departments with a current enrollment of about 250 graduate students. Administratively, the College is comprised of four academic departments (Financial Planning, Housing and Consumer Economics; Nutritional Sciences; Human Development and Family Science; and Textiles, Merchandising and Interiors) and houses the Georgia Center for Developmental Science as a College- and University-wide research hub. International opportunities are strongly supported in the College and the University. Programs of outreach and public service, including outstanding Cooperative Extension initiatives, extend the resources of the College and University to the general public and targeted audiences. Faculty in the College manage significant external grants and contracts for research and public service from NIH , USDA , DOD , NIMH , NIDA , DOE , CDC , and GEFA , among others. Additional information about the College of Family and Consumer Sciences is available at https://www.fcs.uga.edu/ . College/Unit/Department website Posting Type Internal (PEP) Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 11/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 08/24/2026 Job Closing Date 09/24/2026 Open until filled No Special Instructions to Applicants This is an internal search restricted to current University of Georgia faculty. Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates should submit their materials by September 24, 2026. The application packet should include a cover letter detailing how the applicant’s credentials and experience meet the needs, responsibilities, and qualifications stated above; a current curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy for the CFT program; and contact information for three references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate degree in HDFS or closely related field, Position Summary Please note that this position is only available to current College of Family and Consumer Sciences faculty. The College of Family and Consumer Sciences invites internal applications for the position of Program Director for the Master’s Program in Couple and Family Therapy program with a rank of Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor as non-tenure track, fiscal year position with a 50% teaching, 40% administration, 5% research, and 5% service appointment to begin November 1, 2026. The Program Director will provide strategic leadership, administration, and oversight for the Couple and Family Therapy ( CFT ) Program while maintaining an active teaching role within the Department of Human Development and Family Science ( HDFS ). The Program Director will advance the quality, visibility, and reputation of the CFT master’s program at the national and international levels; ensure compliance with Commission on Accreditation for Marriage and Family Therapy Education ( COAMFTE ) standards; and oversee curriculum, clinical training, program operations, facilities, services, and continuous quality improvement efforts. The position will serve as the primary liaison among the CFT Program, HDFS , COAMFTE , clinical partners, professional organizations, and community stakeholders, supporting student recruitment, admissions, orientation, practica, internships, and other experiential learning opportunities. The Program Director will collaborate with faculty, staff, community partners, and affiliated clinical programs to promote student success, maintain accreditation, strengthen professional partnerships, and advance the mission and strategic goals of the CFT Program. As a core faculty member in the Couple and Family Therapy ( CFT ) master’s program, the successful candidate will teach four undergraduate and/or graduate courses each academic year and provide classroom instruction, academic advising, mentorship, and supervision of applied and clinical learning experiences for students in the bachelor’s, dual-degree (BS/MS), and master’s programs. Teaching assignments may include courses within the Behavioral Health Science minor and the CFT master’s program. The Program Director will ensure that curriculum, clinical training, and student learning experiences align with COAMFTE accreditation standards and disciplinary best practices. Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership and administrative oversight for the Couple and Family Therapy ( CFT ) Program. Ensure compliance with COAMFTE standards and accreditation requirements, including annual reporting, self-study preparation, site visit coordination, policy development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement efforts. Submits COAMFTE accreditation materials and oversees all reports to COAMFTE . Lead curriculum planning, review, and development in collaboration with CFT faculty to maintain program quality and accreditation compliance Oversee the clinical training program, including clinical experiences, supervision requirements, student evaluations, training documentation, and related program operations. Coordinate program operations, including course scheduling, faculty engagement, strategic planning activities, and program-related meetings and retreats. Coordinate graduate student recruitment, admissions, orientation, funding opportunities, assistantship assignments, and student success initiatives. Develop and maintain partnerships with community agencies, clinical training sites, professional organizations, and other stakeholders to support practicum, internship, and applied learning opportunities. Collaborate with the Love and Money Center and other clinical partners to support student training, policy development, clinic operations, and clinical education experiences. Oversee student records, graduate outcomes assessment, liability and insurance requirements, supervision documentation, and accreditation-related reporting. Coordinate practicum and internship placement processes, including training agreements, site relationships, student progress monitoring, and communication with site supervisors. Develop and submit budget proposal to the Department Head for accreditation maintenance, CFT credentials, and professional development activities for CFT students (e.g., guest speakers). Build collaborative relationships across the University, professional associations, and community organizations, while mentoring graduate students and supporting faculty development. Serve as a core faculty member by teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, providing academic advising, mentorship, and clinical supervision, supporting student development across degree programs, and contributing to teaching, scholarship, and service activities that advance the discipline. Participate in department, college, and university governance Engage in AAMFT and other relevant professional organizations. Support and develop opportunities for research collaboration, grants, contracts, and other externally funded initiatives that advance the mission of the program and department. Additional Requirements Candidates must have a graduate degree (either MS or PhD) in couple/marriage and family therapy in addition to the earned doctorate in HDFS or closely related field. Currently licensed as marriage and family therapist ( LMFT ) in the state of Georgia, and obtained AAMFT -approved supervisor status. At least 5 years of post-doctoral experience in relational/system practice. At least 5 years’ experience of university-level teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate courses, including mentoring and supervising graduate students. For additional information about the criteria for appointment, please refer to the Guidelines for Clinical Faculty Appointment and Promotion. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Have attained AAMFT -approved supervisor designation. Qualifications consistent with appointment at the rank of Clinical Associate Professor under Guidelines for Clinical Faculty Appointment and Promotion. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Record of successful university-level teaching, clinical supervision, and mentorship of graduate students. Record of leadership in state professional organizations associated with Couple and Family Therapy. Record of leadership in accreditation processes. Knowledge of Georgia licensing laws and rules, knowledge of mental health needs and systems of delivery. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
