    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/496934": {
      "title": "University of Georgia | Associate Dean of College Operations",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Dean of College Operations Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Dean of College Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. YOU MUST HOLD A CURRENT FACULTY POSITION AT THE RANK OF PROFESSOR OR CLINICAL PROFESSOR IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARYMEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA TO APPLY TO THIS POSITION. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2766P Working Title Associate Dean of College Operations Department VetMed-Veterinary Medic Dean About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine, founded in 1946, is dedicated to training future veterinarians, providing services to animal owners and veterinarians, and conducting investigations to improve the health of animals as well as people. The college benefits pets and their owners, food-producing animals, and wildlife by offering the highest quality hospital and diagnostic laboratory services. Equipped with the most technologically advanced facilities located on a university campus, the college is dedicated to safeguarding public health by studying emerging infectious diseases that affect both animal and human health. The College of Veterinary Medicine values all members of the university community, recognizing that differences in experience and culture can only lead to a more well-rounded, accepting academic environment as embodied in our Principles of Community . College/Unit/Department website www.vet.uga.edu Posting Type Internal (PEP) Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 10/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 07/30/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants YOU MUST HOLD A CURRENT FACULTY POSITION AT THE RANK OF PROFESSOR OR CLINICAL PROFESSOR IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARYMEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA TO APPLY TO THIS POSITION . Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assoc/Asst Dean AC FLSA Faculty Rank Professor Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Tenured Minimum Qualifications A terminal degree or the foreign equivalent. Position Summary YOU MUST HOLD A CURRENT FACULTY POSITION AT THE RANK OF PROFESSOR OR CLINICAL PROFESSOR IN THE COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA TO APPLY TO THIS POSITION . The Associate Dean for College Operations ( ADCO ) reports directly to the Dean and oversees the comprehensive management of the college’s physical and technical infrastructure, including: facilities, information technology, and safety and compliance policies, designed to support and advance the CVM’s tripartite mission of teaching, service, and research. As a senior administrator, the ADCO serves as a strategic advisor to the Dean and other college leaders, bridges the gap between academic/clinical missions and university logistics, and ensures the college is compliant with all university, state, and federal regulations, as well as veterinary accreditation standards. Additional Requirements Required Education: A terminal degree or the foreign equivalent with an academic background and appropriate credentials to be a Full Professor in an academic department in the CVM . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Experience: Significant, progressive leadership in senior administration, preferably within an academic health center, veterinary college, or a highly regulated research and/or clinical environment is required . Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Operational Acumen: Demonstrated background managing complex physical footprints, capital projects, facilities logistics, or large-scale technical operations is required . Compliance Expertise: Deep familiarity with safety protocols, risk management, and state/federal regulatory compliance (e.g., AVMA COE , USDA , IACUC , or EHS guidelines) is required . Collaborative Leadership: Exceptional communication and conflict-resolution skills, with a proven ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, department chairs, university administrators, and external stakeholders is required . Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Infrastructure, Facilities & Capital Planning Space Allocation & Management: Partner with Department Chairs and the Associate Deans to strategically allocate and manage college space, including offices, instructional areas, and specialized research laboratories. Capital & Maintenance Projects: Coordinate directly with the Dean and the Facilities Planning Director on major maintenance projects, future capital project development, and long-term facility needs. Research & Instructional Support: Oversee research space logistics, lab setups, faculty move-ins, infrastructure upgrades, and the maintenance of modern classroom and conference room facilities. Institutional Liaison: Serve as the primary, senior-level liaison between individual CVM units and college/university facilities offices. Equipment Acquisition: Oversee major equipment acquisition workflows to ensure procurement aligns with facilities capabilities, safety standards, and institutional priorities. Percentage Of Time 34 Duties/Responsibilities Safety, Risk Management & Compliance Regulatory & Accreditation Compliance: Oversee CVM safety and compliance frameworks to ensure the college meets or exceeds all state, federal, and institutional regulations, as well as AVMA Council on Education ( COE ) accreditation standards. Biosafety & Biosecurity: Support the oversight of specialized veterinary environments (such as clinical teaching hospitals, BSL labs, and animal housing) and research environments (laboratories and shared equipment cores) to maintain rigorous biosafety, radiation safety, and controlled substance protocols. Emergency Preparedness: Lead the development, testing, and implementation of emergency preparedness plans and individual Unit Business Continuity Plans to protect human and animal populations. Percentage Of Time 33 Duties/Responsibilities Strategic Leadership, Policy & Technology Strategic Alignment: Ensure all programmatic operations and facility initiatives directly align with and advance the college’s overarching strategic plan. Policy & Governance: Lead the formal review, drafting, and implementation of updates to CVM bylaws and internal operating policies as needed. Technology & Systems Oversight: Provide administrative supervision for central Information Technology Services and specialized veterinary enterprise systems (e.g., VetView). Executive Support: Manage special projects assigned by the Dean and serve as the Dean’s formal delegate upon request. Percentage Of Time 33 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you currently hold a faculty position in the College of Veterinary Medicine at the University of Georgia? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
